cope\": \"epic/2380/t-8\",\n      \"role\": \"coder\",\n      \"budget\": \"45m\",\n      \"stopConditions\": [\n        \"tests green\",\n        \"budget elapsed\",\n        \"acceptance criteria met\"\n      ],\n      \"independentVerification\": \"QE / explore verifies story acceptance criteria\",\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"api change\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceEvidence\": [\n        \"story acceptance criteria verified\"\n      ],\n      \"tools\": [\n        \"git\"\n      ],\n      \"repairLimit\": \"2\",\n      \"escalationOwner\": \"delivery-lead\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"T-7\"\n      ],\n      \"contractDependency\": {\n        \"id\": \"ctx-api-contract\",\n        \"version\": \"v1.0.0\"\n      },\n      \"id\": \"T-8\",\n      \"repo\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Cancel Booking UI\",\n      \"acceptedInputVersions\": {\n        \"intent\": 1,\n        \"requirements\": 1,\n        \"design\": 1\n      },\n      \"branchScope\": \"epic/2380/t-9\",\n      \"role\": \"coder\",\n      \"budget\": \"45m\",\n      \"stopConditions\": [\n        \"tests green\",\n        \"budget elapsed\",\n        \"acceptance criteria met\"\n      ],\n      \"independentVerification\": \"QE / explore verifies story acceptance criteria\",\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"ui change\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceEvidence\": [\n        \"story acceptance criteria verified\"\n      ],\n      \"tools\": [\n        \"git\"\n      ],\n      \"repairLimit\": \"2\",\n      \"escalationOwner\": \"delivery-lead\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"T-8\"\n      ],\n      \"contractDependency\": {\n        \"id\": \"ctx-api-contract\",\n        \"version\": \"v1.0.0\"\n      },\n      \"id\": \"T-9\",\n      \"repo\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Event Bus Infrastructure\",\n      \"acceptedInputVersions\": {\n        \"intent\": 1,\n        \"requirements\": 1,\n        \"design\": 1\n      },\n      \"branchScope\": \"epic/2380/t-10\",\n      \"role\": \"coder\",\n      \"budget\": \"45m\",\n      \"stopConditions\": [\n        \"tests green\",\n        \"budget elapsed\",\n        \"acceptance criteria met\"\n      ],\n      \"independentVerification\": \"QE / explore verifies story acceptance criteria\",\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"api change\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceEvidence\": [\n        \"story acceptance criteria verified\"\n      ],\n      \"tools\": [\n        \"git\"\n      ],\n      \"repairLimit\": \"2\",\n      \"escalationOwner\": \"delivery-lead\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"T-8\"\n      ],\n      \"contractDependency\": {\n        \"id\": \"ctx-api-contract\",\n        \"version\": \"v1.0.0\"\n      },\n      \"id\": \"T-10\",\n      \"repo\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"WebSocket Push Infrastructure\",\n      \"acceptedInputVersions\": {\n        \"intent\": 1,\n        \"requirements\": 1,\n        \"design\": 1\n      },\n      \"branchScope\": \"epic/2380/t-11\",\n      \"role\": \"coder\",\n      \"budget\": \"45m\",\n      \"stopConditions\": [\n        \"tests green\",\n        \"budget elapsed\",\n        \"acceptance criteria met\"\n      ],\n      \"independentVerification\": \"QE / explore verifies story acceptance criteria\",\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"ui change\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceEvidence\": [\n        \"story acceptance criteria verified\"\n      ],\n      \"tools\": [\n        \"git\"\n      ],\n      \"repairLimit\": \"2\",\n      \"escalationOwner\": \"delivery-lead\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"T-10\"\n      ],\n      \"contractDependency\": {\n        \"id\": \"ctx-api-contract\",\n        \"version\": \"v1.0.0\"\n      },\n      \"id\": \"T-11\",\n      \"repo\": \"ui\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Real-Time Availability Updates in UI\",\n      \"acceptedInputVersions\": {\n        \"intent\": 1,\n        \"requirements\": 1,\n        \"design\": 1\n      },\n      \"branchScope\": \"epic/2380/t-12\",\n      \"role\": \"coder\",\n      \"budget\": \"45m\",\n      \"stopConditions\": [\n        \"tests green\",\n        \"budget elapsed\",\n        \"acceptance criteria met\"\n      ],\n      \"independentVerification\": \"QE / explore verifies story acceptance criteria\",\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"api change\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceEvidence\": [\n        \"story acceptance criteria verified\"\n      ],\n      \"tools\": [\n        \"git\"\n      ],\n      \"repairLimit\": \"2\",\n      \"escalationOwner\": \"delivery-lead\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"T-11\"\n      ],\n      \"contractDependency\": {\n        \"id\": \"ctx-api-contract\",\n        \"version\": \"v1.0.0\"\n      },\n      \"id\": \"T-12\",\n      \"repo\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Ship Operations Event Integration\",\n      \"acceptedInputVersions\": {\n        \"intent\": 1,\n        \"requirements\": 1,\n        \"design\": 1\n      },\n      \"branchScope\": \"epic/2380/t-13\",\n      \"role\": \"coder\",\n      \"budget\": \"45m\",\n      \"stopConditions\": [\n        \"tests green\",\n        \"budget elapsed\",\n        \"acceptance criteria met\"\n      ],\n      \"independentVerification\": \"QE / explore verifies story acceptance criteria\",\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"api change\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceEvidence\": [\n        \"story acceptance criteria verified\"\n      ],\n      \"tools\": [\n        \"git\"\n      ],\n      \"repairLimit\": \"2\",\n      \"escalationOwner\": \"delivery-lead\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"T-10\"\n      ],\n      \"contractDependency\": {\n        \"id\": \"ctx-api-contract\",\n        \"version\": \"v1.0.0\"\n      },\n      \"id\": \"T-13\",\n      \"repo\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Ship Cancellation Handling and Notification\",\n      \"acceptedInputVersions\": {\n        \"intent\": 1,\n        \"requirements\": 1,\n        \"design\": 1\n      },\n      \"branchScope\": \"epic/2380/t-14\",\n      \"role\": \"coder\",\n      \"budget\": \"45m\",\n      \"stopConditions\": [\n        \"tests green\",\n        \"budget elapsed\",\n        \"acceptance criteria met\"\n      ],\n      \"independentVerification\": \"QE / explore verifies story acceptance criteria\",\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"ui change\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceEvidence\": [\n        \"story acceptance criteria verified\"\n      ],\n      \"tools\": [\n        \"git\"\n      ],\n      \"repairLimit\": \"2\",\n      \"escalationOwner\": \"delivery-lead\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"T-13\",\n        \"T-11\"\n      ],\n      \"contractDependency\": {\n        \"id\": \"ctx-api-contract\",\n        \"version\": \"v1.0.0\"\n      },\n      \"id\": \"T-14\",\n      \"repo\": \"ui\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"qeOwner\": \"harness-qe\",\n  \"deliveryOwner\": \"harness-delivery\",\n  \"conflicts\": [],\n  \"status\": \"accepted\",\n  \"acceptedVersion\": 1,\n  \"acceptedBy\": \"Josh Clements\"\n}\n<!-- PLAN:END -->\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshclements518/gh-cc-test/issues/2380/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshclements518/gh-cc-test/issues/2380/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshclements518/gh-cc-test/issues/2376","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshclements518/gh-cc-test","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshclements518/gh-cc-test/issues/2376/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshclements518/gh-cc-test/issues/2376/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshclements518/gh-cc-test/issues/2376/events","html_url":"https://github.com/joshclements518/gh-cc-test/issues/2376","id":6174776986,"node_id":"I_kwDOUn8XWc8AAAABcAuemg","number":2376,"title":"[Epic 2376] character counter scheduling feature in the mobile app","user":{"login":"joshclements518","id":73498019,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNDk4MDE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73498019?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshclements518","html_url":"https://github.com/joshclements518","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshclements518/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshclements518/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshclements518/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshclements518/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshclements518/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshclements518/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshclements518/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshclements518/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshclements518/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12337220995,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUn8XWc8AAAAC31sNgw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshclements518/gh-cc-test/labels/human:needed","name":"human:needed","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12710119606,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUn8XWc8AAAAC9ZUItg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshclements518/gh-cc-test/labels/stage:plan:active","name":"stage:plan:active","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12734263547,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUn8XWc8AAAAC9wVw-w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshclements518/gh-cc-test/labels/intake:feature-request","name":"intake:feature-request","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":827,"created_at":"2026-11-03T02:04:49Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T18:17:20Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- stage-approvals -->\n| Stage | At | Approver | Session | Phrase |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| intent | 2026-11-03T02:33:08.403Z | Josh Clements · b626a055… | [join](https://aicp-cp-prod.blackriver-a051e806.westus2.azurecontainerapps.io/sessions/sdk-97e29772-9d2?k=fe2bd4cce93a4368bfaff27664106910) | policyVersion:1.0.0 |\n| requirements | 2026-11-03T02:47:00.583Z | Josh Clements · b626a055… | [join](https://aicp-cp-prod.blackriver-a051e806.westus2.azurecontainerapps.io/sessions/sdk-0c5b7dcd-11f?k=e7d3ec6f353b4c35bd819fdb7cfdee90) | [interview-draft] Write docs/requirements/issue-2376-prd.md now from this ledger. Human-facing outline first (scannab… |\n| design | 2026-11-03T03:10:41.148Z | Josh Clements · b626a055… | [join](https://aicp-cp-prod.blackriver-a051e806.westus2.azurecontainerapps.io/sessions/sdk-db839d08-510?k=59ee26fd55ce4c3d87b72084ac2106ee) | policyVersion:1.0.0 |\n<!-- /stage-approvals -->\n\n<!-- aicp-feature-request\n{\n  \"idempotencyKey\": \"1793671486804\",\n  \"text\": \"character counter scheduling feature in the mobile app\",\n  \"senderDisplayName\": \"Josh Clements\",\n  \"receivedAt\": \"2026-11-03T02:04:46.8367621Z\",\n  \"channelId\": \"19:NFdNe0N-Z6Hqqxra7ub1l6a2l6jwYl3URF9X5hOu9xM1@thread.tacv2\",\n  \"source\": \"teams\",\n  \"uiRepo\": \"joshclements518/gh-cc-test-ui\",\n  \"apiRepo\": \"joshclements518/gh-cc-test-api\"\n}\n-->\n\n## Feature request\n\ncharacter counter scheduling feature in the mobile app\n\nUI repo: joshclements518/gh-cc-test-ui\nAPI repo: joshclements518/gh-cc-test-api\n\n_Landed via `teams` · key `1793671486804` · 2026-11-03T02:04:46.8367621Z_\n\n---\n\n<!-- PRD:START -->\n# PRD — Character Encounter Scheduling\n\nEnable cruisers to browse and book character encounter meet-and-greets via the cruise ship mobile app.\n\n## Problem\n\n- Cruisers want to meet entertainment characters (Disney, Marvel, etc.) during their cruise but have no easy way to discover available encounters or reserve a spot\n- Character meet-and-greets fill up quickly; families miss out without advance booking\n- No visibility into which characters are available when and where on the ship\n\n## In Scope / Out Scope\n\n| In scope | Out of scope |\n|----------|--------------|\n| Browse available character encounters with sorting options | Push notifications or reminders for bookings |\n| View character details (name, photo, time, location, duration, spots available) | Check-in functionality at encounter time |\n| Book one encounter per cabin (whole cabin attends) | Waitlist or queue management |\n| View current booking in dedicated \"My Booking\" section | Multiple bookings per cabin |\n| Cancel booking anytime before encounter starts | Integration with photo packages or merchandise |\n| Rebook different encounter after cancellation | Individual per-person bookings within a cabin |\n| Handle ship-side cancellations with in-app notification | |\n| Sort encounters by time, character, or availability | |\n\n## Who / Systems\n\n**Personas:**\n- Cruiser (any guest aboard the ship; books on behalf of their cabin/family group)\n\n**Systems:**\n- Mobile app UI (`joshclements518/gh-cc-test-ui`)\n- Mobile app API (`joshclements518/gh-cc-test-api`)\n- Existing ship operations system (data source for character encounter schedules)\n\n## Flow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[Cruiser opens character encounters] --> B[Browse and sort encounter list]\n    B --> C{Cabin has existing booking?}\n    C -->|Yes| D[View in 'My Booking' section]\n    C -->|No| E[Select encounter from list]\n    D --> F{Want to cancel?}\n    F -->|Yes| G[Cancel booking]\n    F -->|No| H[Keep booking]\n    G --> E\n    E --> I{Spots available?}\n    I -->|Yes| J{Cabin already has booking?}\n    I -->|No| B\n    J -->|Yes| K[Show error message]\n    J -->|No| L[Book encounter]\n    K --> B\n    L --> M[Confirmation screen with details]\n    M --> N[Booking stored in 'My Booking']\n    \n    O[Ship cancels encounter] --> P[Clear booking]\n    P --> Q[Show in-app notification]\n```\n\n## User Stories\n\n1. As a cruiser, I want to browse available character encounters sorted by time, character, or availability, so that I can find the best option for my family.\n\n2. As a cruiser, I want to view detailed information about each encounter (character name, photo, time, location, duration, spots available), so that I can make an informed booking decision.\n\n3. As a cruiser, I want to book one character encounter for my entire cabin, so that my whole family can attend together.\n\n4. As a cruiser, I want to see a confirmation screen immediately after booking with all the details, so that I know my booking was successful.\n\n5. As a cruiser, I want to view my current booking in a dedicated \"My Booking\" section, so that I can easily find my encounter details later.\n\n6. As a cruiser, I want to cancel my booking anytime before the encounter starts, so that I have flexibility if plans change.\n\n7. As a cruiser, I want to book a different encounter after cancelling, so that I can still participate in a character meet-and-greet.\n\n8. As a cruiser, I want to see a clear error message if I try to book when my cabin already has a booking, so that I understand the one-booking limit.\n\n9. As a cruiser, I want to be notified in the app if the ship cancels my booked encounter, so that I know I need to make a new booking.\n\n## Decisions Captured\n\n- **Data source**: Character encounter schedules come from the existing ship operations system (integration required)\n- **Booking unit**: One booking per cabin/family group (not per individual person)\n- **Attendees**: When a cabin books, everyone in that cabin can attend the encounter together\n- **Capacity measurement**: Encounter capacity is measured by number of cabins, regardless of cabin size\n- **Booking window**: Cruisers can book anytime during the cruise, not restricted to same-day or advance windows\n- **Cancellation policy**: Cabins can cancel anytime before the encounter starts, no time restrictions\n- **Post-booking UX**: Show confirmation screen with booking details immediately after successful booking\n- **Booking access**: Dedicated \"My Booking\" section in the app to view current booking\n- **Duplicate booking handling**: Show error message if cabin attempts to book when they already have a booking\n- **List organization**: Encounter list supports multiple sort options: by time, by character, by availability\n- **Ship cancellation handling**: If ship cancels an encounter, clear the booking and show in-app notification to the cruiser\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] Cruisers can browse a list of available character encounters in the mobile app\n- [ ] Each encounter displays character name, photo, time, location on ship, duration, and available spots (cabin count)\n- [ ] Encounter list supports sorting by time, character, and availability\n- [ ] Cruisers can book one encounter per cabin when spots are available\n- [ ] Booking allows everyone in the cabin to attend together\n- [ ] System enforces one-booking-per-cabin limit\n- [ ] Attempting to book when cabin has existing booking shows clear error message\n- [ ] After successful booking, cruisers see confirmation screen with all encounter details\n- [ ] Cruisers can view their current booking in dedicated \"My Booking\" section\n- [ ] Cruisers can cancel their booking anytime before the encounter starts\n- [ ] After cancellation, cabin can book a different encounter\n- [ ] If ship cancels an encounter, booking is cleared and cruiser receives in-app notification\n- [ ] UI works on mobile app (iOS and Android)\n- [ ] Booking and cancellation updates are reflected in real-time availability counts\n- [ ] Integration with existing ship operations system retrieves encounter schedule data\n\n## Open Ambiguities\n\n> **Note:** Integration details with existing ship operations system\n> \n> While the data source is confirmed as the existing ship operations system, the specific integration mechanism (API endpoints, data refresh frequency, authentication) will be determined during the architecture stage.\n\n---\n\n```f07-requirements\n{\n  \"id\": \"REQ-2376\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"intentId\": \"INT-2376\",\n  \"intentVersion\": 1,\n  \"scope\": \"Enable cruisers to browse character encounter schedules, book one encounter per cabin (whole cabin attends), view booking details, cancel and rebook, with sorting options and ship cancellation handling via mobile app\",\n  \"rules\": [\n    \"One booking per cabin/family group maximum\",\n    \"Entire cabin can attend the booked encounter together\",\n    \"Capacity measured by number of cabins, not individual attendees\",\n    \"Cancellation allowed anytime before encounter starts\",\n    \"Booking allowed anytime during cruise\",\n    \"Duplicate booking attempts show error message\",\n    \"Ship cancellations clear booking and trigger in-app notification\"\n  ],\n  \"journeys\": [\n    \"Browse character encounters sorted by time, character, or availability\",\n    \"Select encounter and view details (character, time, location, duration, spots available)\",\n    \"Book encounter for cabin (all cabin members attend)\",\n    \"View confirmation screen with booking details\",\n    \"Access 'My Booking' section to view current booking\",\n    \"Cancel booking and rebook different encounter\",\n    \"Receive in-app notification if ship cancels encounter\"\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-1\",\n      \"text\": \"Encounter list displays all available encounters with character name, photo, time, location, duration, and cabin spots available\",\n      \"measurable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-2\",\n      \"text\": \"List supports sorting by time, character, and availability\",\n      \"measurable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-3\",\n      \"text\": \"Booking succeeds when cabin has no existing booking and spots are available\",\n      \"measurable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-4\",\n      \"text\": \"Booking attempt when cabin has existing booking shows error message\",\n      \"measurable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-5\",\n      \"text\": \"Confirmation screen displays after successful booking\",\n      \"measurable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-6\",\n      \"text\": \"My Booking section shows current encounter details\",\n      \"measurable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-7\",\n      \"text\": \"Cancellation succeeds anytime before encounter start time\",\n      \"measurable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-8\",\n      \"text\": \"After cancellation, cabin can book a different encounter\",\n      \"measurable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-9\",\n      \"text\": \"Ship-side cancellation clears booking and shows in-app notification\",\n      \"measurable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-10\",\n      \"text\": \"Availability updates in real-time after bookings and cancellations\",\n      \"measurable\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"testReferences\": [],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"status\": \"accepted\",\n  \"acceptedVersion\": 1,\n  \"acceptedBy\": \"Josh Clements\"\n}\n```\n<!-- PRD:END -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ARCHITECTURE-DECISIONS:START -->\n<!-- docs/adr/ADR-1-event-driven-architecture.md -->\n# ADR-1: Event-Driven Architecture for Character Encounters\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe character encounter scheduling feature requires:\n\n1. **Real-time availability updates** across all mobile clients when bookings/cancellations occur\n2. **Ship-side cancellation notifications** with < 1 second latency to affected cabins\n3. **High booking contention** during peak hours (families rushing to book popular characters)\n4. **Integration with ship operations system** that controls encounter schedules\n5. **Audit trail** for compliance and troubleshooting booking disputes\n6. **Scalability** to support 1000+ concurrent users per ship across multiple ships in the fleet\n\nThree architectural patterns were evaluated:\n- **REST + Polling**: Simple but 30-60s availability lag, high mobile battery drain\n- **REST + WebSocket**: Good real-time updates, moderate complexity\n- **Event-Driven**: Best real-time, scalability, and auditability, but highest complexity\n\n## Decision\n\nWe will implement an **event-driven architecture** using an event bus (Kafka, AWS SNS/SQS, or Azure Event Grid) as the central integration point.\n\n### Core Components\n\n1. **Event Bus**: Central message broker for all domain events\n2. **Mobile API**: REST endpoints + WebSocket service for real-time push\n3. **Sync Service**: Event consumer that maintains write model (PostgreSQL) and read model (Redis)\n4. **Push Service**: Event consumer that pushes updates to WebSocket clients\n5. **Notification Service**: Event consumer that sends push notifications for ship cancellations\n6. **Event Store**: Append-only log of all events for audit and replay\n\n### Event Types\n\n**Ship Operations:**\n- `encounter.created`: New character encounter scheduled\n- `encounter.updated`: Time, location, or capacity changed\n- `encounter.cancelled`: Ship-side cancellation\n\n**Bookings:**\n- `booking.created`: Cabin booked an encounter\n- `booking.cancelled`: Cabin cancelled their booking\n- `booking.cancelled.ship`: Ship cancelled encounter, booking cleared\n\n### Data Flow\n\n1. Ship operations system publishes events → Event bus\n2. Mobile API publishes booking events → Event bus\n3. Sync service consumes events → Updates DB and Redis read model\n4. Push service consumes events → Sends WebSocket messages to subscribed clients\n5. Notification service consumes events → Sends push notifications for cancellations\n\n## Consequences\n\n### Positive\n\n- **True real-time updates** (< 1s latency) for availability and cancellations\n- **Horizontal scalability**: Event consumers can scale independently\n- **Decoupled services**: Mobile API, sync, push, and notification services deploy independently\n- **Audit trail**: Event store provides complete history for compliance and replay\n- **Resilience**: Event bus provides durability; failed consumers can catch up via replay\n- **Future extensibility**: Analytics, reporting, and ML services can subscribe to events without API changes\n\n### Negative\n\n- **Complexity**: Requires event bus infrastructure, multiple services, distributed tracing\n- **Eventual consistency**: Read model (Redis) may lag write model (PostgreSQL) by milliseconds\n- **Longer implementation**: 5-6 weeks vs 2-3 weeks for REST + polling\n- **Operational overhead**: Must monitor event bus, consumer lag, and event replay\n- **Debugging difficulty**: Distributed transactions require correlation IDs and centralized logging\n\n### Mitigations\n\n- **Complexity**: Use managed event bus (AWS EventBridge, Azure Event Grid) to reduce operational burden\n- **Eventual consistency**: Acceptable for this domain (sub-second lag is not user-perceptible)\n- **Implementation time**: Phased rollout (MVP with REST + polling, migrate to events in v1.1)\n- **Debugging**: Implement OpenTelemetry for distributed tracing from day one\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### REST API + Client Polling\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- 30-60s availability lag creates race conditions (users book sold-out encounters)\n- High mobile battery drain from constant polling\n- High API load (all clients poll continuously)\n- Poor user experience for ship cancellations (5-15 minute notification delay)\n\n### REST API + WebSocket Push\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- Does not provide audit trail for compliance\n- Harder to scale horizontally (WebSocket server state management)\n- Tighter coupling between mobile API and ship operations system\n- Future analytics/reporting require querying production DB (no event log)\n\nHowever, **this was a close second choice**. If team lacks event-driven experience or timeline is constrained, this is the recommended fallback.\n\n## Supersedes\n\nNone (initial architecture decision)\n\n## Related ADRs\n\n- [ADR-2: CQRS Pattern for Availability Read Model](./ADR-2-cqrs-read-model.md)\n- [ADR-3: WebSocket Push for Real-Time Updates](./ADR-3-websocket-push.md)\n- [ADR-5: Ship Operations Integration via Event Bus](./ADR-5-ship-ops-integration.md)\n\n---\n\n```f07-design\n{\n  \"id\": \"DES-REQ-2376\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"requirementsId\": \"REQ-2376\",\n  \"requirementsAcceptedVersion\": 1,\n  \"covers\": {\n    \"interfaces\": \"{\\n  \\\"mobile_to_api\\\": {\\n    \\\"protocol\\\": \\\"HTTPS REST + WebSocket Secure (WSS)\\\",\\n    \\\"authentication\\\": \\\"JWT Bearer token\\\",\\n    \\\"endpoints\\\": [\\n      \\\"GET /encounters?sort=time|character|availability&date=YYYY-MM-DD\\\",\\n      \\\"POST /bookings {cabinId, encounterId}\\\",\\n      \\\"GET /bookings/cabin/:cabinId\\\",\\n      \\\"DELETE /bookings/:bookingId\\\",\\n      \\\"WebSocket wss://api.example.com/ws with subscribe/unsubscribe actions\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"data_format\\\": \\\"JSON\\\",\\n    \\\"rate_limits\\\": \\\"100 req/min per cabin, WebSocket: 1 connection per device\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"api_to_event_bus\\\": {\\n    \\\"protocol\\\": \\\"Event bus native protocol (Kafka, AMQP, or managed service SDK)\\\",\\n    \\\"events_published\\\": [\\n      \\\"booking.created\\\",\\n      \\\"booking.cancelled\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"payload_format\\\": \\\"JSON with schema version\\\",\\n    \\\"ordering\\\": \\\"Events for same encounterId maintain order (partition key = encounterId)\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"event_bus_to_consumers\\\": {\\n    \\\"consumers\\\": [\\n      \\\"Sync Service (writes DB/Redis)\\\",\\n      \\\"Push Service (WebSocket fanout)\\\",\\n      \\\"Notification Service (push notifications)\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"consumption_pattern\\\": \\\"At-least-once delivery with idempotency keys\\\",\\n    \\\"consumer_groups\\\": \\\"Each service has dedicated consumer group for parallel processing\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"ship_ops_to_event_bus\\\": {\\n    \\\"protocol\\\": \\\"Event bus publish or REST webhook adapter\\\",\\n    \\\"events_published\\\": [\\n      \\\"encounter.created\\\",\\n      \\\"encounter.updated\\\",\\n      \\\"encounter.cancelled\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"fallback\\\": \\\"If ship ops cannot publish events, build polling adapter service\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"api_to_data\\\": {\\n    \\\"write_db\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL (source of truth for bookings and encounters)\\\",\\n    \\\"read_cache\\\": \\\"Redis (CQRS read model for availability counts)\\\",\\n    \\\"event_log\\\": \\\"Event bus native persistence or dedicated event store (e.g., EventStore DB)\\\"\\n  }\\n}\",\n    \"dependencyImpacts\": \"{\\n  \\\"new_infrastructure\\\": [\\n    \\\"Event bus (Kafka cluster, AWS SNS/SQS, or Azure Event Grid)\\\",\\n    \\\"Redis cluster for read model (high availability, persistence enabled)\\\",\\n    \\\"PostgreSQL database for write model\\\",\\n    \\\"WebSocket service infrastructure (load balancer with sticky sessions or session affinity)\\\",\\n    \\\"Push notification gateway integration (Firebase Cloud Messaging, Apple Push Notification Service)\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"ship_operations_system\\\": {\\n    \\\"capability_required\\\": \\\"Publish events to event bus OR expose REST API for polling adapter\\\",\\n    \\\"data_required\\\": \\\"Character encounter schedules (character, time, location, capacity, status)\\\",\\n    \\\"authentication\\\": \\\"Mutual TLS or API key for event publishing\\\",\\n    \\\"change_impact\\\": \\\"If ship ops must modify their system to publish events, requires coordination with ship ops team\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"mobile_apps\\\": {\\n    \\\"sdk_additions\\\": [\\n      \\\"WebSocket client library (e.g., Socket.IO, native WebSocket)\\\",\\n      \\\"JWT token refresh logic\\\",\\n      \\\"Push notification registration and handling\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"state_management\\\": \\\"Local cache of encounter list and current booking for offline resilience\\\"\\n  }\\n}\",\n    \"testability\": \"{\\n  \\\"unit_tests\\\": {\\n    \\\"api\\\": \\\"Mock event bus publish calls, test booking validation logic\\\",\\n    \\\"sync_service\\\": \\\"Mock event consumption, verify DB/Redis updates\\\",\\n    \\\"push_service\\\": \\\"Mock WebSocket connections, verify message fanout\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"integration_tests\\\": {\\n    \\\"api_to_db\\\": \\\"Test booking creation flow with real PostgreSQL (testcontainers)\\\",\\n    \\\"event_flow\\\": \\\"Publish event to test event bus, verify consumers process correctly\\\",\\n    \\\"websocket\\\": \\\"Connect test client, subscribe to channel, verify push messages received\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"contract_tests\\\": {\\n    \\\"event_schemas\\\": \\\"Pact or JSON Schema validation for all event types\\\",\\n    \\\"rest_api\\\": \\\"OpenAPI spec with contract tests (Pact, Dredd)\\\",\\n    \\\"ship_ops_events\\\": \\\"Validate ship ops event payloads match schema\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"e2e_tests\\\": {\\n    \\\"booking_flow\\\": \\\"Mobile app books encounter \\\\u2192 verify DB updated, other clients receive push\\\",\\n    \\\"ship_cancellation\\\": \\\"Simulate ship ops cancellation event \\\\u2192 verify affected cabins notified\\\",\\n    \\\"race_condition\\\": \\\"Two clients book last spot simultaneously \\\\u2192 verify one succeeds, one fails\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"chaos_tests\\\": {\\n    \\\"event_bus_downtime\\\": \\\"Event bus unavailable \\\\u2192 API should queue events and retry\\\",\\n    \\\"consumer_lag\\\": \\\"Sync service behind by 10s \\\\u2192 verify read model eventually consistent\\\",\\n    \\\"websocket_disconnect\\\": \\\"Client disconnects \\\\u2192 verify reconnect and state reconciliation\\\"\\n  }\\n}\",\n    \"security\": \"{\\n  \\\"authentication\\\": {\\n    \\\"mobile_to_api\\\": \\\"JWT tokens issued by ship's identity provider, validated on every request\\\",\\n    \\\"token_expiry\\\": \\\"15-minute access tokens, 7-day refresh tokens\\\",\\n    \\\"cabin_authorization\\\": \\\"Token claims include cabinId, API verifies user can only manage their cabin's booking\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"data_protection\\\": {\\n    \\\"in_transit\\\": \\\"TLS 1.3 for all HTTPS and WSS connections, mTLS for ship ops integration\\\",\\n    \\\"at_rest\\\": \\\"Encrypted PostgreSQL volumes, Redis persistence encryption enabled\\\",\\n    \\\"pii_handling\\\": \\\"Cabin IDs and guest IDs are pseudonymous; no PII in event payloads\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"input_validation\\\": {\\n    \\\"api\\\": \\\"Validate all inputs against schema (cabinId format, encounterId exists, timestamp in future)\\\",\\n    \\\"event_consumers\\\": \\\"Validate event payloads against JSON schema before processing\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"rate_limiting\\\": {\\n    \\\"api\\\": \\\"100 requests/minute per cabin to prevent booking abuse\\\",\\n    \\\"websocket\\\": \\\"1 connection per device token, max 5 subscriptions per connection\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"audit\\\": {\\n    \\\"event_log\\\": \\\"Immutable append-only log of all bookings and cancellations\\\",\\n    \\\"retention\\\": \\\"7 years per maritime compliance requirements\\\",\\n    \\\"access_control\\\": \\\"Event log read-only except for append, admin access requires MFA\\\"\\n  }\\n}\",\n    \"operation\": \"{\\n  \\\"deployment\\\": {\\n    \\\"strategy\\\": \\\"Blue-green deployment for API and consumers (zero downtime)\\\",\\n    \\\"rollback\\\": \\\"Event consumers can replay events from offset in case of bad deployment\\\",\\n    \\\"database_migrations\\\": \\\"Use Flyway/Liquibase for versioned schema migrations\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"monitoring\\\": {\\n    \\\"metrics\\\": [\\n      \\\"Event bus consumer lag (alert if > 10 seconds)\\\",\\n      \\\"Booking API latency (p99 < 500ms)\\\",\\n      \\\"WebSocket connection count and message delivery rate\\\",\\n      \\\"Redis cache hit rate (target > 99%)\\\",\\n      \\\"PostgreSQL query performance\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"alerting\\\": [\\n      \\\"Consumer lag > 30 seconds \\\\u2192 page on-call\\\",\\n      \\\"Redis cache miss rate > 5% \\\\u2192 investigate\\\",\\n      \\\"API error rate > 1% \\\\u2192 alert\\\",\\n      \\\"Event bus unavailable \\\\u2192 immediate page\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"logging\\\": \\\"Structured JSON logs with correlation IDs (trace entire request flow across services)\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"disaster_recovery\\\": {\\n    \\\"event_log_backup\\\": \\\"Daily snapshots to object storage (S3, Azure Blob)\\\",\\n    \\\"database_backup\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL continuous archiving (PITR) with 30-day retention\\\",\\n    \\\"redis_backup\\\": \\\"Daily RDB snapshots, AOF persistence enabled\\\",\\n    \\\"recovery_time\\\": \\\"RTO: 1 hour, RPO: 15 minutes (event replay from last checkpoint)\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scaling\\\": {\\n    \\\"api\\\": \\\"Horizontal auto-scaling based on CPU (target 70%) and request rate\\\",\\n    \\\"event_consumers\\\": \\\"Add consumer instances to consumer group (Kafka partitions enable parallelism)\\\",\\n    \\\"redis\\\": \\\"Redis Cluster mode with sharding by encounterId\\\",\\n    \\\"websocket\\\": \\\"Sticky sessions via load balancer (session affinity by device token hash)\\\"\\n  }\\n}\",\n    \"ui\": \"{\\n  \\\"screens\\\": [\\n    \\\"Encounter List: Browse encounters with sort/filter, shows availability in real-time\\\",\\n    \\\"Encounter Detail: Character photo, time, location, duration, book button (disabled if cabin has booking)\\\",\\n    \\\"Booking Confirmation: Shows booked encounter details immediately after booking\\\",\\n    \\\"My Booking: Dedicated section showing current booking with cancel button\\\",\\n    \\\"Cancellation Alert: In-app alert when ship cancels encounter (triggered by WebSocket push)\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"real_time_updates\\\": {\\n    \\\"availability_changes\\\": \\\"Encounter list updates spot counts as other cabins book/cancel (via WebSocket)\\\",\\n    \\\"ship_cancellation\\\": \\\"My Booking section clears and shows alert when ship cancels\\\",\\n    \\\"offline_mode\\\": \\\"Show last-known state, queue booking requests for retry on reconnect\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"error_handling\\\": {\\n    \\\"duplicate_booking\\\": \\\"Show error: 'Your cabin already has a booking. Cancel it first to book a different encounter.'\\\",\\n    \\\"sold_out\\\": \\\"Show 'Sold out' badge, disable book button, offer 'Notify me if available' (future feature)\\\",\\n    \\\"network_error\\\": \\\"Show retry button, cache failed request for background retry\\\"\\n  }\\n}\",\n    \"api\": \"{\\n  \\\"rest_endpoints\\\": {\\n    \\\"list_encounters\\\": {\\n      \\\"method\\\": \\\"GET\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/encounters\\\",\\n      \\\"query_params\\\": [\\n        \\\"sort (time|character|availability)\\\",\\n        \\\"date (YYYY-MM-DD)\\\",\\n        \\\"limit\\\",\\n        \\\"offset\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"response\\\": \\\"Array of encounter objects with availableSpots from Redis cache\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"create_booking\\\": {\\n      \\\"method\\\": \\\"POST\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/bookings\\\",\\n      \\\"body\\\": {\\n        \\\"cabinId\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n        \\\"encounterId\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"response\\\": \\\"201 Created with booking object, 409 Conflict if duplicate or sold out\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"get_cabin_booking\\\": {\\n      \\\"method\\\": \\\"GET\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/bookings/cabin/:cabinId\\\",\\n      \\\"response\\\": \\\"200 OK with booking object, 404 Not Found if no active booking\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"cancel_booking\\\": {\\n      \\\"method\\\": \\\"DELETE\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/bookings/:bookingId\\\",\\n      \\\"response\\\": \\\"204 No Content on success, 403 Forbidden if encounter already started\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"websocket_protocol\\\": {\\n    \\\"connection\\\": \\\"wss://api.example.com/ws?token=<jwt>\\\",\\n    \\\"subscribe\\\": {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"subscribe\\\",\\n      \\\"channel\\\": \\\"encounter.availability.<encounterId>\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"unsubscribe\\\": {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"unsubscribe\\\",\\n      \\\"channel\\\": \\\"encounter.availability.<encounterId>\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"pushed_messages\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"encounter.availability\\\",\\n        \\\"encounterId\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n        \\\"availableSpots\\\": 5\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"cabin.booking.cancelled\\\",\\n        \\\"bookingId\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n        \\\"reason\\\": \\\"ship_cancelled\\\"\\n      }\\n    ]\\n  }\\n}\"\n  },\n  \"alternatives\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"event_bus_technology\",\n      \"summary\": \"Selected based on existing ship infrastructure: Kafka if available, otherwise AWS EventBridge or Azure Event Grid\",\n      \"accepted\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ship_ops_integration\",\n      \"summary\": \"If ship ops cannot publish events directly, build adapter service that polls ship ops REST API and publishes events to event bus\",\n      \"accepted\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"exceptions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"eventual_consistency\",\n      \"text\": \"Redis read model may lag PostgreSQL write model by < 1 second. Acceptable for this domain (booking conflicts handled via optimistic locking).\",\n      \"version\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"websocket_fallback\",\n      \"text\": \"If WebSocket connection fails, mobile app falls back to polling GET /encounters every 30 seconds until reconnected.\",\n      \"version\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"acceptedVersion\": null,\n  \"brownfield\": \"workspace\",\n  \"brownfieldSummary\": \"Workspace brownfield \\u2014 UI/API sample apps + ship-ops integration described in ADRs; F06 Neo4j graph not required for this design package.\",\n  \"rejectionReason\": null\n}\n```\n\n<!-- docs/adr/ADR-2-cqrs-read-model.md -->\n# ADR-2: CQRS Pattern for Availability Read Model\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe encounter list query (`GET /encounters`) must:\n\n1. Return availability counts for all encounters (50-100 encounters per day)\n2. Respond in < 200ms to avoid slow mobile app loading\n3. Handle high read traffic during peak hours (1000+ concurrent users)\n4. Stay consistent with booking writes (no stale availability data)\n\nTwo approaches were considered:\n\n**Direct database query:**\n- `SELECT encounter_id, capacity_cabins - COUNT(active_bookings) AS available FROM encounters JOIN bookings`\n- Simple, but slow (JOIN + COUNT on every request)\n- High PostgreSQL load during peak hours\n\n**CQRS with Redis cache (read model):**\n- Maintain `encounter:{id}:available` counters in Redis\n- Update counters atomically on booking/cancellation events\n- Read queries hit Redis (sub-millisecond latency)\n- Eventual consistency with PostgreSQL write model\n\n## Decision\n\nWe will implement a **CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation)** pattern with Redis as the read model for encounter availability.\n\n### Write Model (Command Side)\n\n**PostgreSQL** is the source of truth:\n- `encounters` table: Character, time, location, capacity\n- `bookings` table: Cabin bookings\n\nAll writes (bookings, cancellations, encounter updates) go through PostgreSQL.\n\n### Read Model (Query Side)\n\n**Redis** cache stores availability counts:\n- Key: `encounter:{encounterId}:available`\n- Value: Integer (remaining cabin spots)\n- TTL: None (persists until encounter starts or is cancelled)\n\n**Sync service** maintains read model:\n- Consumes `booking.created` → `DECR encounter:{id}:available`\n- Consumes `booking.cancelled` → `INCR encounter:{id}:available`\n- Consumes `encounter.created` → `SET encounter:{id}:available {capacity_cabins}`\n- Consumes `encounter.cancelled` → `DEL encounter:{id}:available`\n\n### Consistency Guarantees\n\n**Atomic decrement during booking:**\n```\nBEGIN TRANSACTION\n  available = DECR encounter:{id}:available\n  IF available < 0:\n    INCR encounter:{id}:available  // rollback\n    ABORT TRANSACTION\n  ELSE:\n    INSERT INTO bookings ...\n    COMMIT\nEND TRANSACTION\n```\n\n**Nightly reconciliation:**\n- Cron job at 3 AM compares Redis counters with PostgreSQL counts\n- Fixes any drift (e.g., Redis eviction, consumer lag)\n\n## Consequences\n\n### Positive\n\n- **Fast queries**: Redis reads are < 1ms (vs 50-100ms for PostgreSQL JOIN)\n- **Scalable**: Redis handles millions of reads/sec\n- **Reduced DB load**: PostgreSQL only handles writes (10-100x fewer than reads)\n- **Atomic operations**: `DECR`/`INCR` are atomic, prevent race conditions\n\n### Negative\n\n- **Eventual consistency**: Redis may lag PostgreSQL by milliseconds (event processing time)\n- **Cache invalidation complexity**: Must update Redis on every booking/cancellation event\n- **Persistence required**: Redis must persist to disk (RDB + AOF) to survive restarts\n- **Reconciliation needed**: Periodic job to fix Redis drift\n\n### Mitigations\n\n- **Eventual consistency**: Acceptable for this domain (sub-second lag is not user-perceptible)\n- **Cache invalidation**: Sync service handles all updates (single responsibility)\n- **Persistence**: Configure Redis with `appendonly yes` and `save 900 1`\n- **Reconciliation**: Automated nightly job with alerting on drift > 5%\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### Direct PostgreSQL Queries\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- Slow query performance (50-100ms with JOIN + COUNT)\n- High database load during peak hours\n- Difficult to scale reads horizontally (read replicas have replication lag)\n\n### Materialized View in PostgreSQL\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- Materialized view refresh is slow (locks table)\n- Still requires PostgreSQL for reads (doesn't reduce DB load)\n- Refresh frequency vs consistency tradeoff\n\n### Write-Through Cache (Redis + PostgreSQL)\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- Booking writes must update both Redis and PostgreSQL in transaction\n- Distributed transaction complexity (2PC or Saga pattern)\n- Harder to roll back on failure\n\n## Supersedes\n\nNone (initial data access pattern decision)\n\n## Related ADRs\n\n- [ADR-1: Event-Driven Architecture](./ADR-1-event-driven-architecture.md) — Events trigger read model updates\n- [ADR-4: One Booking Per Cabin Constraint](./ADR-4-one-booking-per-cabin.md) — Uses Redis for duplicate check\n\n<!-- docs/adr/ADR-3-websocket-push.md -->\n# ADR-3: WebSocket Push for Real-Time Updates\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe mobile app must show real-time availability updates when other cabins book or cancel encounters. Three delivery mechanisms were considered:\n\n1. **Client polling**: App polls `GET /encounters` every 30-60 seconds\n   - Simple, but 30-60s lag and high battery drain\n\n2. **WebSocket push**: Persistent bidirectional connection for instant updates\n   - Near-instant delivery (< 1s), moderate complexity\n\n3. **Server-Sent Events (SSE)**: Unidirectional server-to-client stream\n   - Good for read-only updates, but limited browser/library support on mobile\n\n## Decision\n\nWe will use **WebSocket (WSS)** for real-time push notifications to mobile clients.\n\n### Architecture\n\n**Push Service:**\n- Subscribes to event bus for `booking.created`, `booking.cancelled`, `encounter.cancelled` events\n- Maintains registry of active WebSocket connections (cabin ID → connection)\n- Publishes messages to subscribed clients via WebSocket\n\n**Mobile App:**\n- Establishes WebSocket connection on app launch: `wss://api.example.com/ws?token=<jwt>`\n- Subscribes to channels:\n  - `encounter.availability.{encounterId}` — Availability changes for viewed encounters\n  - `cabin.booking.{cabinId}` — Booking/cancellation for user's cabin\n- Receives JSON messages and updates UI in real-time\n\n**Connection Management:**\n- **Load balancer**: Sticky sessions (route by device token hash)\n- **Authentication**: JWT token in connection query params, validated on connect\n- **Heartbeat**: Client sends `ping` every 30s, server responds with `pong`\n- **Reconnect**: Exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, max 30s)\n- **Fallback**: If WebSocket fails, fall back to polling `GET /encounters` every 30s\n\n### Message Types\n\n**From client (subscribe):**\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"subscribe\",\n  \"channel\": \"encounter.availability.enc_789\"\n}\n```\n\n**From server (availability update):**\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"encounter.availability\",\n  \"encounterId\": \"enc_789\",\n  \"availableSpots\": 4,\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-03T14:35:22Z\"\n}\n```\n\n**From server (ship cancellation):**\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"cabin.booking.cancelled\",\n  \"bookingId\": \"bk_123\",\n  \"encounterId\": \"enc_789\",\n  \"reason\": \"ship_cancelled\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-03T14:30:00Z\"\n}\n```\n\n## Consequences\n\n### Positive\n\n- **Near-instant updates** (< 1s latency from event to UI)\n- **Lower mobile battery usage** vs polling (persistent connection, no repeated HTTP handshakes)\n- **Bidirectional**: Can add client-to-server events in future (e.g., typing indicators)\n- **Wide library support**: WebSocket libraries available for iOS (Starscream, SocketRocket) and Android (OkHttp)\n\n### Negative\n\n- **Connection management complexity**: Must handle disconnects, reconnects, network switches\n- **Load balancer configuration**: Requires sticky sessions or Redis-backed session store\n- **Infrastructure cost**: Persistent connections consume server memory (1-10KB per connection)\n- **Firewall issues**: Some corporate/ship networks block WebSocket (must fall back to polling)\n\n### Mitigations\n\n- **Connection management**: Use battle-tested WebSocket library (Socket.IO, Starscream)\n- **Load balancer**: Configure sticky sessions via AWS ALB, Azure App Gateway, or NGINX\n- **Infrastructure cost**: Acceptable for expected scale (5000 connections × 5KB = 25MB per server)\n- **Firewall issues**: Detect WebSocket failure, auto-fallback to polling\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### Client Polling\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- 30-60s lag is poor UX (users may book sold-out encounters)\n- High battery drain from repeated HTTP requests\n- High API load (all clients poll continuously)\n\n### Server-Sent Events (SSE)\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- Unidirectional (server → client only, no subscription management)\n- Poor mobile library support (requires EventSource polyfill)\n- Not widely used in mobile apps (less battle-tested than WebSocket)\n\nHowever, **SSE is a valid fallback** if WebSocket proves problematic in production. Can switch without changing event architecture.\n\n### Push Notifications Only\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- Push notifications are for background alerts, not real-time UI updates\n- Delivery is best-effort (may be delayed or dropped)\n- Cannot update UI while user is actively viewing encounter list\n\n**Push notifications are used in addition to WebSocket** for ship cancellations when app is backgrounded.\n\n## Supersedes\n\nNone (initial real-time delivery mechanism)\n\n## Related ADRs\n\n- [ADR-1: Event-Driven Architecture](./ADR-1-event-driven-architecture.md) — Push service consumes events\n- [ADR-5: Ship Operations Integration](./ADR-5-ship-ops-integration.md) — Ship cancellations pushed via WebSocket\n\n<!-- docs/adr/ADR-4-one-booking-per-cabin.md -->\n# ADR-4: One Booking Per Cabin Constraint\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nPer PRD requirements:\n- **Booking unit**: One booking per cabin/family group (not per individual person)\n- **Attendees**: When a cabin books, everyone in that cabin can attend together\n- **Constraint**: Cabin can have at most one active booking at any time\n- **Rebooking**: After cancellation, cabin can book a different encounter\n\nThis constraint must be enforced reliably, even under high concurrency (two users from same cabin attempting to book simultaneously).\n\n## Decision\n\nWe will enforce the one-booking-per-cabin constraint using a **unique database constraint** plus **check-before-write** in the API.\n\n### Database Schema\n\n**Unique partial index in PostgreSQL:**\n```sql\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_one_booking_per_cabin\nON bookings (cabin_id)\nWHERE status = 'active';\n```\n\nThis ensures:\n- Only one `active` booking per `cabin_id` (database-level guarantee)\n- Cancelled bookings (`status = 'cancelled_by_cabin'` or `'cancelled_by_ship'`) do not violate constraint\n- Race conditions are prevented at the database level (transaction serialization)\n\n### API Enforcement\n\n**Before creating booking:**\n```sql\nSELECT booking_id FROM bookings\nWHERE cabin_id = :cabinId AND status = 'active';\n```\n\nIf result is non-empty:\n- Return `409 Conflict` with error: `\"Cabin {cabinId} already has an active booking. Cancel it before booking a different encounter.\"`\n\nIf result is empty:\n- Proceed to insert booking (database will reject if race condition occurred)\n\n### Race Condition Handling\n\n**Scenario**: Two users from cabin 1234 attempt to book simultaneously.\n\n1. User A calls `POST /bookings` → API checks DB → No active booking\n2. User B calls `POST /bookings` → API checks DB → No active booking (A's booking not committed yet)\n3. User A's transaction inserts booking, commits → Success\n4. User B's transaction attempts insert → **Database constraint violation** → Transaction aborted\n5. API catches `UniqueViolationError`, returns `409 Conflict` to User B\n\n### Cancellation Flow\n\n**When cabin cancels their booking:**\n```sql\nUPDATE bookings\nSET status = 'cancelled_by_cabin', cancelled_at = NOW()\nWHERE booking_id = :bookingId AND cabin_id = :cabinId;\n```\n\nUnique constraint no longer applies (status != 'active'), cabin can book a different encounter.\n\n## Consequences\n\n### Positive\n\n- **Database-enforced consistency**: Constraint cannot be violated even if API logic fails\n- **Race condition safety**: Database handles concurrency via transaction isolation\n- **Clear error messages**: API can detect duplicate booking and return helpful error\n- **Rebooking support**: Cancelled bookings do not violate constraint\n\n### Negative\n\n- **Database dependency**: Constraint logic is in database schema (harder to test in isolation)\n- **Error handling**: Must catch database constraint violation and translate to API error\n- **Migration risk**: Adding unique index to existing table with duplicate data will fail (requires cleanup first)\n\n### Mitigations\n\n- **Database dependency**: Acceptable tradeoff (database is best place for data integrity)\n- **Error handling**: Standardize constraint violation → `409 Conflict` mapping in API error handler\n- **Migration risk**: N/A for new feature (no existing data), for future: cleanup script before index creation\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### Application-Level Lock (e.g., Redis Distributed Lock)\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- Requires Redis lock acquisition before booking (adds latency and complexity)\n- Lock must be held across database transaction (long-lived lock reduces concurrency)\n- Lock expiration and deadlock handling complexity\n- Database constraint is simpler and more reliable\n\n### Optimistic Locking with Version Number\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- Requires version column on `cabin` or `bookings` table\n- Client must retry on conflict (poor UX, multiple round-trips)\n- Does not prevent duplicate bookings, only detects them\n\n### No Constraint, Allow Duplicate Bookings\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- Violates PRD requirement (\"one booking per cabin\")\n- Would require periodic cleanup job to detect and fix duplicates\n- Unclear user experience if cabin has multiple bookings\n\n## Supersedes\n\nNone (initial constraint enforcement decision)\n\n## Related ADRs\n\n- [ADR-1: Event-Driven Architecture](./ADR-1-event-driven-architecture.md) — Bookings are written to DB and published as events\n- [ADR-2: CQRS Read Model](./ADR-2-cqrs-read-model.md) — Read model does not enforce constraint (write model does)\n\n<!-- docs/adr/ADR-5-ship-ops-integration.md -->\n# ADR-5: Ship Operations Integration via Event Bus\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nCharacter encounter schedules are managed by an external **ship operations system**. The mobile API must:\n\n1. Receive encounter schedules (character, time, location, capacity)\n2. Detect new encounters, schedule updates, and ship-side cancellations\n3. Update mobile app availability in near real-time (< 1 minute for schedule changes)\n\n**Integration constraint**: Per PRD, \"specific integration mechanism (API endpoints, data refresh frequency, authentication) will be determined during architecture stage.\"\n\n**Unknown**: Does ship operations system have a REST API? Can it push events? Or must we poll/batch sync?\n\nThree integration patterns were considered:\n\n1. **Event-driven**: Ship ops publishes events to event bus (ideal)\n2. **Webhook**: Ship ops sends HTTP POST to mobile API on changes (good)\n3. **Polling adapter**: Mobile API polls ship ops REST API every 5-15 minutes (fallback)\n\n## Decision\n\nWe will integrate via the **event bus**, with an **adapter service** as a fallback if the ship operations system cannot publish events directly.\n\n### Primary Pattern: Ship Ops Publishes Events\n\n**If ship operations system supports event publishing:**\n\nShip ops publishes to event bus:\n- `encounter.created` — New character encounter scheduled\n- `encounter.updated` — Time, location, or capacity changed\n- `encounter.cancelled` — Encounter cancelled by ship operations\n\n**Event payload example:**\n```json\n{\n  \"eventType\": \"encounter.created\",\n  \"encounterId\": \"enc_789\",\n  \"shipOpsId\": \"SHIP-MG-20261103-001\",\n  \"cruiseId\": \"cruise_123\",\n  \"character\": {\n    \"name\": \"Mickey Mouse\",\n    \"photoUrl\": \"https://cdn.example.com/characters/mickey.jpg\"\n  },\n  \"schedule\": {\n    \"startTime\": \"2026-11-03T15:00:00Z\",\n    \"durationMinutes\": 30,\n    \"locationCode\": \"DECK5-ATRIUM\",\n    \"locationName\": \"Deck 5 Atrium\"\n  },\n  \"capacity\": {\n    \"cabins\": 20\n  },\n  \"publishedAt\": \"2026-11-03T10:00:00Z\"\n}\n```\n\n**Sync service** consumes events:\n1. Validate event schema (JSON Schema validation)\n2. Write to `encounters` table (insert or update)\n3. Initialize Redis cache: `SET encounter:{id}:available {capacity_cabins}`\n4. For `encounter.cancelled`, clear bookings and notify affected cabins\n\n### Fallback Pattern: Polling Adapter\n\n**If ship operations system cannot publish events:**\n\nBuild **adapter service** that:\n1. Polls ship ops REST API every 5-15 minutes for encounter schedules\n2. Compares with local DB state to detect changes (diff algorithm)\n3. Publishes events to event bus on behalf of ship ops (`encounter.created`, `encounter.updated`, `encounter.cancelled`)\n4. Rest of system unchanged (sync service consumes events as usual)\n\n**Adapter service responsibilities:**\n- Authentication with ship ops API (API key, OAuth, or mutual TLS)\n- Retry logic for failed API calls\n- Change detection (compare fetched encounters with DB state)\n- Event publishing (identical payload format as primary pattern)\n\n### Authentication\n\n**Ship ops → Event bus (primary pattern):**\n- Mutual TLS or API key for event bus authentication\n- Event signature (HMAC) to verify authenticity\n\n**Adapter → Ship ops API (fallback pattern):**\n- API key, OAuth 2.0, or mutual TLS per ship ops system requirements\n- Store credentials in secret manager (AWS Secrets Manager, Azure Key Vault)\n\n## Consequences\n\n### Positive\n\n- **Flexible integration**: Works whether ship ops can push events or not\n- **Consistent architecture**: Adapter service hides ship ops integration complexity\n- **Future-proof**: When ship ops adds event support, remove adapter without changing rest of system\n- **Event-driven benefits**: Real-time updates, audit trail, decoupling (even with polling adapter)\n\n### Negative\n\n- **Adapter service complexity**: Requires change detection, retry logic, state tracking\n- **Polling lag**: If using adapter, 5-15 minute delay for ship cancellations (acceptable per PRD)\n- **Coordination required**: Must work with ship ops team to define integration contract\n\n### Mitigations\n\n- **Adapter complexity**: Use battle-tested change detection library (e.g., diff-json)\n- **Polling lag**: For urgent cancellations, ship ops can call webhook endpoint directly (bypass adapter)\n- **Coordination**: Define event schema first, ship ops implements when ready (adapter buys time)\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### Direct API Calls from Mobile API\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- Tight coupling between mobile API and ship ops system\n- No audit trail or event log for schedule changes\n- Harder to scale (every mobile API instance calls ship ops)\n- No buffer for ship ops downtime (mobile API fails if ship ops is down)\n\n### Database Replication from Ship Ops DB\n\n**Rejected** because:\n- Requires direct database access (security risk)\n- Schema coupling (ship ops DB schema changes break mobile API)\n- No change notifications (must poll or use triggers)\n\n### Webhook Receiver in Mobile API\n\n**Rejected as primary pattern** because:\n- Requires ship ops to implement webhook sending logic\n- Mobile API becomes tightly coupled to ship ops (must be online to receive)\n- No retry mechanism if mobile API is down during webhook delivery\n\nHowever, **webhook is a valid alternative to polling adapter**. If ship ops prefers webhooks over event bus, implement webhook receiver that publishes events to event bus.\n\n## Supersedes\n\nNone (initial ship ops integration decision)\n\n## Related ADRs\n\n- [ADR-1: Event-Driven Architecture](./ADR-1-event-driven-architecture.md) — Event bus is integration point\n- [ADR-2: CQRS Read Model](./ADR-2-cqrs-read-model.md) — Sync service updates read model from ship ops events\n\n## Open Questions\n\nTo be resolved during implementation:\n\n1. **Ship ops system capabilities**: Does it have a REST API? Can it publish events to event bus? Does it support webhooks?\n2. **Authentication mechanism**: API key, OAuth, mutual TLS, or other?\n3. **Data refresh frequency**: Real-time, hourly, daily?\n4. **Encounter schedule format**: JSON, XML, CSV, or other?\n5. **Historical data**: Must we backfill encounters from past cruises, or only future?\n\n**Recommendation**: Start with polling adapter (fallback pattern) to unblock mobile API development. Migrate to event-driven pattern when ship ops integration details are finalized.\n<!-- ARCHITECTURE-DECISIONS:END -->\n\n<!-- SYSTEM-OVERVIEW-ADDITIONS:START -->\n# System Context — Character Encounter Scheduling\n\nThis diagram shows the system landscape for the character encounter scheduling feature, including the new components and integrations.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n    Cruiser[\"Cruiser<br/>Mobile App User\"]\n    \n    subgraph Mobile[\"Mobile Applications (NEW)\"]\n        iOS[\"iOS App<br/>gh-cc-test-ui\"]\n        Android[\"Android App<br/>gh-cc-test-ui\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph API[\"Mobile API Layer (NEW)\"]\n        REST[\"REST API<br/>gh-cc-test-api\"]\n        WS[WebSocket Service]\n        Auth[Auth Service]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Events[\"Event Infrastructure (NEW)\"]\n        EB[\"Event Bus<br/>Kafka/SNS/EventGrid\"]\n        Sync[\"Sync Service<br/>Event Consumer\"]\n        Push[\"Push Service<br/>Event Consumer\"]\n        Notify[\"Notification Service<br/>Event Consumer\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Data[\"Data Layer (NEW)\"]\n        DB[\"(Booking DB<br/>PostgreSQL)\"]\n        ReadModel[\"(Read Model<br/>Redis)\"]\n        EventLog[\"(Event Store)\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph External[\"External Systems\"]\n        ShipOps[\"Ship Operations<br/>System\"]\n        PushGateway[\"Push Notification<br/>Gateway\"]\n    end\n    \n    Cruiser -->|Browse/Book| iOS\n    Cruiser -->|Browse/Book| Android\n    \n    iOS -->|HTTPS REST| REST\n    Android -->|HTTPS REST| REST\n    iOS -->|WSS| WS\n    Android -->|WSS| WS\n    \n    REST -->|Validate token| Auth\n    WS -->|Validate token| Auth\n    \n    REST -->|Read| ReadModel\n    REST -->|Write| DB\n    REST -->|Publish event| EB\n    \n    WS -->|Subscribe| EB\n    \n    ShipOps -->|Publish events| EB\n    \n    EB -->|Subscribe| Sync\n    EB -->|Subscribe| Push\n    EB -->|Subscribe| Notify\n    \n    Sync -->|Write| DB\n    Sync -->|Update| ReadModel\n    Sync -->|Append| EventLog\n    \n    Push -->|Send update| WS\n    Notify -->|Send| PushGateway\n    PushGateway -->|APNS/FCM| iOS\n    PushGateway -->|APNS/FCM| Android\n    \n    classDef added fill:#e1f5e1,stroke:#4caf50,stroke-width:2px\n    classDef external fill:#f5f5f5,stroke:#999,stroke-width:1px\n    \n    class Mobile,API,Events,Data added\n    class ShipOps,PushGateway external\n```\n\n## Components\n\n### New Components (This Epic)\n\n**Mobile Applications:**\n- iOS/Android apps with character encounter browsing and booking UI\n- WebSocket client for real-time availability updates\n- Local state management for offline resilience\n\n**Mobile API Layer:**\n- REST API: CRUD operations for bookings, encounter queries\n- WebSocket Service: Real-time push for availability and cancellations\n- Auth Service: Token validation (JWT)\n\n**Event Infrastructure:**\n- Event Bus: Central message broker (Kafka, AWS SNS/SQS, or Azure Event Grid)\n- Sync Service: Consumes events, updates DB and read model\n- Push Service: Consumes booking/cancellation events, pushes to WebSocket clients\n- Notification Service: Consumes events, sends push notifications for ship cancellations\n\n**Data Layer:**\n- Booking DB (PostgreSQL): Source of truth for bookings and encounters\n- Read Model (Redis): Materialized view of encounter availability (CQRS)\n- Event Store: Append-only log of all events for audit and replay\n\n### External Systems\n\n**Ship Operations System:**\n- Publishes encounter events (created, updated, cancelled)\n- Integration via event bus or adapter service\n\n**Push Notification Gateway:**\n- Existing infrastructure (Firebase Cloud Messaging, Apple Push Notification Service)\n\n## Key Interactions\n\n1. **Browse Encounters:** Mobile app → REST API → Read Model (Redis)\n2. **Book Encounter:** Mobile app → REST API → Booking DB + Publish event\n3. **Real-time Updates:** Event Bus → Push Service → WebSocket → Mobile app\n4. **Ship Cancellation:** Ship Ops → Event Bus → Sync + Notify → Mobile app (WebSocket + Push notification)\n<!-- SYSTEM-OVERVIEW-ADDITIONS:END -->\n\n<!-- DATA-MODEL-ADDITIONS:START -->\n# Data Model — Character Encounter Scheduling\n\nThis entity-relationship diagram shows the core domain model for character encounter bookings.\n\n```mermaid\nerDiagram\n    CRUISE {\n        string cruise_id PK\n        string ship_name\n        date departure_date\n        date return_date\n        string status\n    }\n    \n    CABIN {\n        string cabin_id PK\n        string cabin_number\n        string cruise_id FK\n        int occupancy_count\n        string primary_guest_id\n    }\n    \n    ENCOUNTER {\n        string encounter_id PK\n        string ship_ops_id \"External system ID\"\n        string cruise_id FK\n        string character_name\n        string character_photo_url\n        timestamp start_time\n        int duration_minutes\n        string location_code\n        string location_name\n        int capacity_cabins \"Max cabin count\"\n        string status \"scheduled, cancelled, completed\"\n        timestamp created_at_added\n        timestamp updated_at\n    }\n    \n    BOOKING {\n        string booking_id PK\n        string cabin_id FK\n        string encounter_id FK\n        string status \"active, cancelled_by_cabin, cancelled_by_ship\"\n        timestamp booked_at_added\n        timestamp cancelled_at\n        string cancellation_reason\n    }\n    \n    EVENT_LOG {\n        string event_id_added PK\n        string event_type_added \"encounter.created, booking.created, etc\"\n        string aggregate_id_added \"encounter_id or booking_id\"\n        jsonb payload_added\n        timestamp occurred_at_added\n        string source_service_added\n    }\n    \n    AVAILABILITY_CACHE {\n        string cache_key_added PK \"encounter:{encounter_id}:available\"\n        int available_cabins_added\n        timestamp last_updated_added\n    }\n    \n    CRUISE ||--o{ CABIN : \"has\"\n    CRUISE ||--o{ ENCOUNTER : \"schedules\"\n    CABIN ||--o| BOOKING : \"books one\"\n    ENCOUNTER ||--o{ BOOKING : \"has\"\n    ENCOUNTER ||--|| AVAILABILITY_CACHE : \"cached in\"\n    BOOKING ||--o{ EVENT_LOG : \"generates\"\n    ENCOUNTER ||--o{ EVENT_LOG : \"generates\"\n\n%% New entities and fields for this epic marked with _added suffix or comment\n```\n\n## Entity Descriptions\n\n### CRUISE\nRepresents a cruise voyage. Pre-existing entity (assumed to exist in ship systems).\n\n### CABIN\nRepresents a cabin/stateroom on the ship. Links to cruise. Pre-existing entity.\n\n- `occupancy_count`: Number of guests in the cabin (not used for capacity calculation per PRD)\n- `primary_guest_id`: Guest who can manage bookings via app\n\n### ENCOUNTER (NEW)\nRepresents a scheduled character meet-and-greet.\n\n- `ship_ops_id`: Foreign key to ship operations system (for sync/correlation)\n- `character_name`: Display name (e.g., \"Mickey Mouse\", \"Spider-Man\")\n- `character_photo_url`: URL to character image asset\n- `location_code`: Ship deck/room code (e.g., \"DECK5-ATRIUM\")\n- `capacity_cabins`: **Capacity measured by cabin count, not individual attendees** (per PRD)\n- `status`: Lifecycle state (scheduled → cancelled/completed)\n\n### BOOKING (NEW)\nRepresents a cabin's reservation for an encounter. **One booking per cabin maximum** (unique constraint on `cabin_id` where `status = 'active'`).\n\n- `status`:\n  - `active`: Current valid booking\n  - `cancelled_by_cabin`: Cruiser cancelled\n  - `cancelled_by_ship`: Ship operations cancelled the encounter\n- `cancellation_reason`: Free text or code (for ship cancellations)\n\n### EVENT_LOG (NEW)\nAppend-only event store for audit trail and event replay (event sourcing pattern).\n\n- `event_type`: Domain event name (e.g., `encounter.created`, `booking.created`, `booking.cancelled.ship`)\n- `aggregate_id`: ID of the affected entity (encounter or booking)\n- `payload`: Full event data as JSON\n- `source_service`: Which service published the event (for debugging)\n\n### AVAILABILITY_CACHE (NEW)\nRedis cache for fast availability lookups (CQRS read model).\n\n- `cache_key`: Format `encounter:{encounter_id}:available`\n- `available_cabins`: Real-time count of remaining spots\n- Atomically decremented on booking, incremented on cancellation\n- Rebuilt from DB on cache miss or nightly reconciliation\n\n## Key Constraints\n\n1. **One booking per cabin**: Unique index on `(cabin_id)` in `BOOKING` table where `status = 'active'`\n2. **Capacity enforcement**: `available_cabins` in cache never goes negative (atomic operations)\n3. **Booking window**: No time-based restrictions (per PRD, book anytime during cruise)\n4. **Cancellation allowed**: Until encounter `start_time` is reached\n\n## Data Flow\n\n1. **Encounter creation**: Ship ops publishes event → Sync service writes to `ENCOUNTER` table + Redis cache\n2. **Booking creation**: API writes to `BOOKING` table, decrements Redis cache, publishes event\n3. **Availability query**: API reads from `AVAILABILITY_CACHE` (sub-millisecond latency)\n4. **Ship cancellation**: Sync service updates `ENCOUNTER.status`, marks related `BOOKING` records as `cancelled_by_ship`\n<!-- DATA-MODEL-ADDITIONS:END -->\n\n<!-- SEQUENCE-ADDITIONS:START -->\n### docs/architecture/sequences/booking-flow.md\n\n# Sequence: Booking an Encounter\n\nThis sequence diagram shows the interaction flow when a cruiser books a character encounter, including real-time availability updates pushed to other users.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    actor User_A as User A<br/>(Cabin 1234)\n    actor User_B as User B<br/>(Cabin 5678)\n    participant Mobile_A as Mobile App A\n    participant Mobile_B as Mobile App B\n    participant REST as REST API\n    participant Auth as Auth Service\n    participant DB as Booking DB\n    participant Cache as Redis Cache\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n    participant Push as Push Service\n    participant WS as WebSocket Service\n    \n    Note over Mobile_A,Mobile_B: Both users viewing same encounter with 5 spots available\n    \n    User_A->>Mobile_A: Tap \"Book\" on encounter\n    Mobile_A->>REST: POST /bookings<br/>{cabinId: 1234, encounterId: enc_789}\n    REST->>Auth: Validate JWT token\n    Auth-->>REST: Token valid, cabin 1234\n    \n    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)\n        Note over REST,Cache: Booking transaction\n        REST->>DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION\n        REST->>DB: SELECT * FROM bookings<br/>WHERE cabin_id='1234' AND status='active'\n        DB-->>REST: No existing booking\n        REST->>Cache: DECR encounter:enc_789:available\n        Cache-->>REST: 4 (decremented from 5)\n        \n        alt Cache returned >= 0 (spot available)\n            REST->>DB: INSERT INTO bookings<br/>(booking_id, cabin_id, encounter_id, status, booked_at)\n            REST->>DB: COMMIT\n            DB-->>REST: Booking created: bk_abc123\n            \n            REST->>EventBus: Publish event:<br/>{\"type\": \"booking.created\", \"bookingId\": \"bk_abc123\",<br/>\"cabinId\": \"1234\", \"encounterId\": \"enc_789\"}\n            REST-->>Mobile_A: 201 Created<br/>{bookingId: \"bk_abc123\", confirmation: {...}}\n            Mobile_A->>User_A: Show confirmation screen\n            \n        else Cache returned < 0 (no spots)\n            REST->>Cache: INCR encounter:enc_789:available\n            REST->>DB: ROLLBACK\n            REST-->>Mobile_A: 409 Conflict<br/>{\"error\": \"No spots available\"}\n            Mobile_A->>User_A: Show \"Sold out\" message\n        end\n    end\n    \n    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)\n        Note over EventBus,Mobile_B: Real-time push to other users\n        EventBus->>Push: Event: booking.created<br/>encounterId: enc_789\n        Push->>WS: Broadcast to subscribers:<br/>channel \"encounter.availability.enc_789\"\n        WS->>Mobile_B: WebSocket message:<br/>{\"type\": \"encounter.availability\",<br/>\"encounterId\": \"enc_789\", \"availableSpots\": 4}\n        Mobile_B->>User_B: Update encounter list:<br/>5 spots → 4 spots (instant)\n    end\n    \n    Note over Mobile_A,Mobile_B: User A sees confirmation, User B sees updated availability in < 1 second\n```\n\n## Key Steps\n\n1. **Authorization**: API validates JWT token to confirm user has access to cabin 1234\n2. **Duplicate booking check**: Query for existing active booking by cabin\n3. **Optimistic locking**: Atomic Redis decrement reserves the spot\n4. **Database transaction**: Write booking record only if cache decrement succeeded\n5. **Event publishing**: Notify other services and clients of the booking\n6. **Real-time push**: WebSocket service broadcasts availability change to subscribed clients\n\n## Error Scenarios\n\n### User already has a booking\n- API returns `409 Conflict` with message: \"Cabin 1234 already has an active booking\"\n- User must cancel existing booking before rebooking\n\n### Race condition (two users book last spot simultaneously)\n- Both clients call API at same time\n- First to acquire Redis lock succeeds; second gets `availableSpots: -1` → transaction rolled back\n- Second user receives `409 Conflict: No spots available`\n\n### Ship operations cancels encounter during booking\n- API checks `encounter.status` before writing booking\n- If status is `cancelled`, return `410 Gone: Encounter cancelled by ship`\n\n### docs/architecture/sequences/ship-cancellation-flow.md\n\n# Sequence: Ship Cancels Encounter\n\nThis sequence diagram shows what happens when the ship operations system cancels a character encounter, including how affected cabins are notified.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    actor ShipOps as Ship Operations<br/>Staff\n    participant ShipSystem as Ship Ops<br/>System\n    participant EventBus as Event Bus\n    participant Sync as Sync Service\n    participant DB as Booking DB\n    participant Cache as Redis Cache\n    participant Notify as Notification<br/>Service\n    participant Push as Push Service\n    participant PushGateway as Push Notification<br/>Gateway\n    participant WS as WebSocket<br/>Service\n    participant Mobile as Mobile App<br/>(Affected cabins)\n    actor User as Cruiser\n    \n    ShipOps->>ShipSystem: Cancel encounter enc_789<br/>(Character unavailable)\n    \n    rect rgb(255, 245, 245)\n        Note over ShipSystem,EventBus: Ship operations publishes event\n        ShipSystem->>EventBus: Publish event:<br/>{\"type\": \"encounter.cancelled\",<br/>\"encounterId\": \"enc_789\",<br/>\"reason\": \"Character unavailable\",<br/>\"cancelledAt\": \"2026-11-03T14:30:00Z\"}\n    end\n    \n    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)\n        Note over EventBus,Cache: Sync service processes cancellation\n        EventBus->>Sync: Event: encounter.cancelled\n        Sync->>DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION\n        Sync->>DB: UPDATE encounters<br/>SET status='cancelled'<br/>WHERE encounter_id='enc_789'\n        Sync->>DB: SELECT booking_id, cabin_id<br/>FROM bookings<br/>WHERE encounter_id='enc_789' AND status='active'\n        DB-->>Sync: 12 affected bookings<br/>[{bk_1, cabin_101}, {bk_2, cabin_205}, ...]\n        \n        Sync->>DB: UPDATE bookings<br/>SET status='cancelled_by_ship',<br/>cancellation_reason='Character unavailable'<br/>WHERE encounter_id='enc_789' AND status='active'\n        Sync->>Cache: DEL encounter:enc_789:available\n        Sync->>DB: COMMIT\n        \n        Sync->>EventBus: Publish events (12x):<br/>{\"type\": \"booking.cancelled.ship\",<br/>\"bookingId\": \"bk_1\", \"cabinId\": \"cabin_101\",<br/>\"encounterId\": \"enc_789\", \"reason\": \"Character unavailable\"}\n    end\n    \n    par Notify affected cabins via push notification\n        rect rgb(255, 250, 240)\n            EventBus->>Notify: Event: booking.cancelled.ship (x12)\n            Notify->>DB: SELECT push_tokens<br/>FROM cabin_devices<br/>WHERE cabin_id IN (...)\n            DB-->>Notify: 18 device tokens<br/>(some cabins have multiple devices)\n            \n            loop For each device token\n                Notify->>PushGateway: Send push notification:<br/>\"Your Mickey Mouse meet-and-greet<br/>at 3pm has been cancelled\"\n                PushGateway->>Mobile: APNS/FCM push\n            end\n            Mobile->>User: Banner notification\n        end\n    and Push to connected WebSocket clients\n        rect rgb(240, 255, 240)\n            EventBus->>Push: Event: booking.cancelled.ship (x12)\n            Push->>WS: Publish to cabin channels:<br/>\"cabin.booking.cabin_101\", etc.\n            \n            alt Cabin is connected via WebSocket\n                WS->>Mobile: WebSocket message:<br/>{\"type\": \"booking.cancelled.ship\",<br/>\"encounterId\": \"enc_789\",<br/>\"reason\": \"Character unavailable\"}\n                Mobile->>User: In-app alert:<br/>\"Encounter cancelled by ship\"\n                Mobile->>Mobile: Clear \"My Booking\" section\n            else Cabin is offline\n                Note over WS,Mobile: Will see empty booking<br/>on next app open\n            end\n        end\n    end\n    \n    User->>Mobile: Open app to rebook\n    Mobile->>Mobile: \"My Booking\" shows empty\n    Note over Mobile,User: User can now browse and book a different encounter\n```\n\n## Key Steps\n\n1. **Event origin**: Ship operations staff marks encounter as cancelled in their system\n2. **Event publishing**: Ship ops system publishes `encounter.cancelled` event to event bus\n3. **Synchronous processing**: Sync service consumes event, updates DB in transaction\n4. **Cascade cancellation**: All active bookings for the encounter are marked `cancelled_by_ship`\n5. **Parallel notification**: Both push notifications and WebSocket messages sent to affected cabins\n6. **Graceful offline handling**: Offline users see empty \"My Booking\" when they reconnect\n\n## Notification Channels\n\n### Push Notification (via APNS/FCM)\n- **Pros**: Works when app is backgrounded or closed\n- **Delivery**: Best-effort (may be delayed or dropped)\n- **Content**: Short message with encounter details\n\n### WebSocket Message\n- **Pros**: Instant delivery for connected clients\n- **Delivery**: Guaranteed if client is connected\n- **Content**: Full event payload, app can update UI immediately\n\n### State reconciliation on reconnect\n- App fetches current booking state via `GET /bookings/cabin/:cabinId` on launch\n- If `My Booking` is empty but was previously set, show in-app alert\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n### Cabin has no registered devices\n- Push notification is skipped (no tokens)\n- User will see empty \"My Booking\" on next app open\n\n### Multiple users from same cabin are online\n- Each device receives push notification\n- Each WebSocket connection receives message\n- All see the same alert (idempotent)\n\n### User books different encounter immediately after cancellation\n- Cancellation clears the constraint\n- API allows new booking (one-per-cabin rule no longer violated)\n<!-- SEQUENCE-ADDITIONS:END -->\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshclements518/gh-cc-test/issues/2376/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshclements518/gh-cc-test/issues/2376/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/203592","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/203592/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/203592/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/203592/events","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/203592","id":6226309073,"node_id":"PR_kwDOA-j9z88AAAABNGfrww","number":203592,"title":"[MPS] Do not bind empty shape/strides for 0-dim iterators","user":{"login":"malfet","id":2453524,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NTM1MjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2453524?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/malfet","html_url":"https://github.com/malfet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malfet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malfet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malfet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malfet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malfet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malfet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malfet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malfet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malfet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":797012849,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3OTcwMTI4NDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/labels/in%20progress","name":"in progress","color":"FF8400","default":false,"description":"PR is being worked on by the author, until the automated review accepts it","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1301347167,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzAxMzQ3MTY3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/labels/triaged","name":"triaged","color":"006b75","default":false,"description":"This issue has been looked at a team member, and triaged and prioritized into an appropriate module","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1392590051,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzkyNTkwMDUx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/labels/open%20source","name":"open source","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":4164781683,"node_id":"LA_kwDOA-j9z874PYZz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/labels/release%20notes:%20mps","name":"release notes: mps","color":"1d76db","default":false,"description":"Release notes category","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":4417837777,"node_id":"LA_kwDOA-j9z88AAAABB1La0Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/labels/ciflow/mps","name":"ciflow/mps","color":"02EDA7","default":false,"description":"Run MPS tests (subset of trunk)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10078293082,"node_id":"LA_kwDOA-j9z88AAAACWLaMWg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/labels/bot-triaged","name":"bot-triaged","color":"0b8793","default":false,"description":"This is a label only to be used by the auto triage bot","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-05T15:32:58Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T18:16:58Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/pulls/203592","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/203592","diff_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/203592.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/203592.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Stack from [ghstack](https://github.com/ezyang/ghstack/tree/0.14.0) (oldest at bottom):\n* __->__ #203592\n\nA 0-dim TensorIterator has empty `shape()`/`strides()`, and passing them to `mtl_setBytes` issues a zero-length `setBytes` that leaves the buffer unbound. The kernels never read it (they loop over `ndim == 0` dims), but Metal validation requires every declared buffer to be bound. Two callers hit this: the binary `_strided_castout_` path, which is used for any `out=` dtype cast regardless of contiguity (e.g. `ne(x, 0, out=float)` inside `linalg.vector_norm(ord=0)` or `all(uint8, dim=())`), and `dispatch_index_kernel` for `take`/`put` with a 0-dim index.\n\nDescribe a 0-dim iterator as a 1-element 1-D one at both call sites, and turn a zero-length `mtl_setBytes` into an internal assert so new callers fail loudly rather than only under the validation layer.\n\nFixes `TestConsistencyMPS` `take`, `put`, `linalg_vector_norm`, `masked_norm`, `all` and `any` under `MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1 MTL_SHADER_VALIDATION=1`.\n\nTest Plan:\n```\nMTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1 MTL_SHADER_VALIDATION=1 python3 -m pytest test/test_mps.py -k \"TestConsistencyMPS and (take or put or linalg_vector_norm or masked_norm or _match_all_ or _match_any_)\"\npython3 -m pytest test/test_mps.py -n 4\n```\n\nThis PR was authored with the help of Claude Code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/203592/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/203592/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcplaya/home-ops/issues/415","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcplaya/home-ops","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcplaya/home-ops/issues/415/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcplaya/home-ops/issues/415/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcplaya/home-ops/issues/415/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dcplaya/home-ops/pull/415","id":4851898992,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQcfN3s7wAn3G","number":415,"title":"feat(deps): update dependency google-auth ( 2.55.1 ➔ 2.62.2 )","user":{"login":"renovate[bot]","id":29139614,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjkxMzk2MTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2740?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/renovate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9711743135,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQcfN3s8AAAACQt1wnw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcplaya/home-ops/labels/type/minor","name":"type/minor","color":"ff9800","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-10T04:05:12Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T18:16:34Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcplaya/home-ops/pulls/415","html_url":"https://github.com/dcplaya/home-ops/pull/415","diff_url":"https://github.com/dcplaya/home-ops/pull/415.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dcplaya/home-ops/pull/415.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Change | [Age](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) | [Confidence](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [google-auth](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/tree/main/packages/google-auth) ([source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python)) | `==2.55.1` → `==2.62.2` | ![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/pypi/google-auth/2.62.2?slim=true) | ![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/pypi/google-auth/2.55.1/2.62.2?slim=true) |\n\n---\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Some dependencies could not be looked up. Check the [Dependency Dashboard](../issues/1) for more information.\n\n---\n\n### Release Notes\n\n<details>\n<summary>googleapis/google-cloud-python (google-auth)</summary>\n\n### [`v2.62.2`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.62.2): google-auth: v2.62.2\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.62.1...google-auth-v2.62.2)\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- **auth:** prevent race conditions during mTLS cert rotation on 401 responses ([#&#8203;18168](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18168)) ([b86536f](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/b86536f91caa7ff2ea5a37b943444111959422c1))\n- **oauth2:** validate Firebase issuer/subject and warn on omitted audience in verify_firebase_token ([#&#8203;18777](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18777)) ([1851b9c](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/1851b9c3a57d7a5bc7c3da6a7ae89ddc0da0c72a))\n\n##### Documentation\n\n- **google-auth:** update requests intersphinx URL ([#&#8203;18978](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18978)) ([2b4575f](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/2b4575f36f1441792e51efb9394b636940ed539d))\n\n### [`v2.62.1`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.62.1): google-auth: v2.62.1\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.62.0...google-auth-v2.62.1)\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- **auth:** strip -fips suffix from AWS service name in SigV4 signing ([#&#8203;18920](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18920)) ([2e1899e](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/2e1899ed52a8c5adeb05422f48581124b4ab3fbe))\n- **auth:** use an unencrypted key for mTLS certificate rotation ([#&#8203;18709](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18709)) ([8166325](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/81663259c3743c6ab76005a5decb2b3628cfcc79))\n\n### [`v2.62.0`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.62.0): google-auth: v2.62.0\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.61.0...google-auth-v2.62.0)\n\n##### Features\n\n- **auth:** enable bound ID tokens by default on Cloud Run ([#&#8203;18635](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18635)) ([8b625c4](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/8b625c4927371992f4569962292299eced040047))\n\n### [`v2.61.0`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.61.0): google-auth: v2.61.0\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.60.0...google-auth-v2.61.0)\n\n##### Features\n\n- **auth:** support bound access and ID tokens for GKE ([#&#8203;18594](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18594)) ([9f5fd7b](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/9f5fd7bdf0707a17c363482b094ccd70a4358389))\n\n### [`v2.60.0`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.60.0): google-auth: v2.60.0\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.59.1...google-auth-v2.60.0)\n\n##### Features\n\n- **auth:** Support sync credentials in AsyncAuthorizedSession ([#&#8203;18542](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18542)) ([3799568](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/379956865248ebc40e5b851ede520056e65abcac))\n\n### [`v2.59.1`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.59.1): google-auth: v2.59.1\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.59.0...google-auth-v2.59.1)\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- **auth:** support mTLS in requests.Request for token refresh and impersonation ([#&#8203;18486](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18486)) ([590376d](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/590376df522bf5f89e0d23b956a85db61c4d48d7))\n\n### [`v2.59.0`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.59.0): google-auth: v2.59.0\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.58.1...google-auth-v2.59.0)\n\n##### Features\n\n- declare Python3.15 support ([05b0c34](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/05b0c342683b2b0e1b8dccd201ec86ec89612edc))\n\n### [`v2.58.1`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.58.1): google-auth: v2.58.1\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.58.0...google-auth-v2.58.1)\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- **auth:** allow mTLS retry when credentials raise NotImplementedError on refresh ([#&#8203;18349](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18349)) ([1665e68](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/1665e6867e0c5d7ea8e7857681efc3aae827d9b7))\n\n### [`v2.58.0`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.58.0): google-auth: v2.58.0\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.57.1...google-auth-v2.58.0)\n\n##### Features\n\n- \\[aiohttp] Add mTLS reconfiguration logic when certificate mismatch ([906ace7](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/906ace77a2a4cfe57954b3da727232e2fd481c22))\n- **auth:** \\[aiohttp] Add mTLS reconfiguration logic when certificate mismatch for existing credentials & Agent Identity workloads  ([#&#8203;18224](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18224)) ([906ace7](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/906ace77a2a4cfe57954b3da727232e2fd481c22))\n\n### [`v2.57.1`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.57.1): google-auth: v2.57.1\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.57.0...google-auth-v2.57.1)\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- **auth:** parse hostname for mTLS and PSC endpoint certificate rotation ([#&#8203;18147](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18147)) ([#&#8203;18201](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18201)) ([b18bb4c](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/b18bb4cb749d2dd10d0e2f7d8505460d305e54fc))\n\n### [`v2.57.0`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.57.0): google-auth: v2.57.0\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.56.3...google-auth-v2.57.0)\n\n##### Features\n\n- **auth:** add deprecation warning for grpcio < 1.83.0 (PQC support) ([#&#8203;18070](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google