(\\) > as written | 1/171&nbsp;(1%) | 0/171&nbsp;(0%)&nbsp;🟢 |\n| Code Delegation Via Ethereum Type 4 Transaction Tests > <span title='testDelegationWithMultipleAccountsAndNotEnoughGasForLazyCreation()'>testDelegationWithMultipleAccountsAndNotEnoughGasForLazyCrea…</span> > as written | 1/171&nbsp;(1%) | 0/171&nbsp;(0%)&nbsp;🟢 |\n| Code Delegation Via Ethereum Type 4 Transaction Tests > testMultipleCodeDelegationsSetViaEthCall\\(\\) > as written | 1/171&nbsp;(1%) | 0/171&nbsp;(0%)&nbsp;🟢 |\n| ScheduleEvmTraceTest > immediatelySignedScheduleTracesStorageWrites\\(\\) > as written | 1/34&nbsp;(3%) | 0/34&nbsp;(0%)&nbsp;🟢 |\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>:test-clients:hapiTestStateThrottling</b> (6)</summary><br>\n\n| Test | Failures | Flakiness |\n|---|--:|--:|\n| LogValidationTest > logsContainNoUnexpectedProblems\\(\\) > as written | 7/183&nbsp;(4%) | 23/183&nbsp;(13%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n| StreamValidationTest > streamsAreValid\\(\\) > as written | 7/183&nbsp;(4%) | 23/183&nbsp;(13%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n| SteadyStateThrottlingTest > checkContractCallsTps\\(\\) > ThrottlesContractCallsAsExpected as written | 7/194&nbsp;(4%) | 23/194&nbsp;(12%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n| SteadyStateThrottlingTest > checkCryptoCreatesTps\\(\\) > ThrottlesCryptoCreatesAsExpected as written | 7/194&nbsp;(4%) | 23/194&nbsp;(12%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n| SteadyStateThrottlingTest > checkFungibleMintsTps\\(\\) > ThrottlesFungibleMintsAsExpected as written | 7/194&nbsp;(4%) | 23/194&nbsp;(12%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n| SteadyStateThrottlingTest > restoreDevLimits\\(\\) > as written | 7/194&nbsp;(4%) | 23/194&nbsp;(12%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>:test-clients:hapiTestTimeConsuming</b> (2)</summary><br>\n\n| Test | Failures | Flakiness |\n|---|--:|--:|\n| ConcurrentSubprocessValidationTest > validateLogsAndStreams\\(\\) > as written | 7/185&nbsp;(4%) | 23/185&nbsp;(13%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n| EthereumSuite > <span title='ethereumCreateWithInlineInitcodeRecordsChildCreateWithoutInitcodeSource()'>ethereumCreateWithInlineInitcodeRecordsChildCreateWithoutIni…</span> > as written | 1/72&nbsp;(2%) | 1/72&nbsp;(2%)&nbsp;🟡 |\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>:test-clients:hapiTestTimeConsumingSerial</b> (1)</summary><br>\n\n| Test | Failures | Flakiness |\n|---|--:|--:|\n| StreamValidationTest > streamsAreValid\\(\\) > as written | 7/176&nbsp;(4%) | 23/176&nbsp;(14%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>:test-clients:hapiTestToken</b> (1)</summary><br>\n\n| Test | Failures | Flakiness |\n|---|--:|--:|\n| ConcurrentSubprocessValidationTest > validateLogsAndStreams\\(\\) > as written | 7/185&nbsp;(4%) | 23/185&nbsp;(13%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>:test-clients:hapiTestTokenSerial</b> (1)</summary><br>\n\n| Test | Failures | Flakiness |\n|---|--:|--:|\n| StreamValidationTest > streamsAreValid\\(\\) > as written | 7/179&nbsp;(4%) | 23/179&nbsp;(13%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>:test-clients:hapiTestWraps</b> (3)</summary><br>\n\n| Test | Failures | Flakiness |\n|---|--:|--:|\n| StreamValidationTest > streamsAreValid\\(\\) > as written | 1/126&nbsp;(1%) | 29/126&nbsp;(24%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n| LogValidationTest > logsContainNoUnexpectedProblems\\(\\) > as written | 1/126&nbsp;(1%) | 26/126&nbsp;(21%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n| WrapsHandoffsTest > genesisAndIncrementalWrapsProofsConstructed\\(\\) > as written | 1/132&nbsp;(1%) | 26/132&nbsp;(20%)&nbsp;🔴 |\n</details></details>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary><b>⚪ Branch <code>feature/updateTokenKeysMisleadingSuccess</code></b></summary><br>\n<details open>\n<summary>&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Branch and pull request builds (includes only tests with flaky results)</b></summary><br>\n:tada: No flaky tests detected!\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Branch builds (includes tests with flaky or failed results)</b></summary><br>\n:tada: No flaky tests detected!\n</details>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary><b>⚪ Branch <code>release/0.78</code></b></summary><br>\n<details open>\n<summary>&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Branch and pull request builds (includes only tests with flaky results)</b></summary><br>\n:tada: No flaky tests detected!\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Branch builds (includes tests with flaky or failed results)</b></summary><br>\n:tada: No flaky tests detected!\n</details>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary><b>⚪ Branch <code>release/0.79</code></b></summary><br>\n<details open>\n<summary>&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Branch and pull request builds (includes only tests with flaky results)</b></summary><br>\n:tada: No flaky tests detected!\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Branch builds (includes tests with flaky or failed results)</b></summary><br>\n:tada: No flaky tests detected!\n</details>\n</details>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hiero-ledger/hiero-consensus-node/issues/26709/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hiero-ledger/hiero-consensus-node/issues/26709/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vlemutov/portable-context/issues/3","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vlemutov/portable-context","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vlemutov/portable-context/issues/3/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vlemutov/portable-context/issues/3/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vlemutov/portable-context/issues/3/events","html_url":"https://github.com/vlemutov/portable-context/pull/3","id":6304210348,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVfMxqc8AAAABOEYFVQ","number":3,"title":"Prepare 1.0: HTTPS/OAuth, recovery and automatic mTLS renewal","user":{"login":"vlemutov","id":225960532,"node_id":"U_kgDODXfiVA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225960532?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlemutov","html_url":"https://github.com/vlemutov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlemutov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlemutov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlemutov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlemutov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlemutov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlemutov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlemutov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlemutov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vlemutov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T09:38:23Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T18:13:27Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vlemutov/portable-context/pulls/3","html_url":"https://github.com/vlemutov/portable-context/pull/3","diff_url":"https://github.com/vlemutov/portable-context/pull/3.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/vlemutov/portable-context/pull/3.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Portable Context gains owner-authenticated HTTPS access while memory stays on the owner VM. A stateless Cloud.ru edge forwards over mTLS; the MCP server validates owner-bound OAuth tokens and operation permissions.\n\nIdentity backups use a separate encrypted restic repository. Recovery creates fresh identity/signing keys and rejects historical access/refresh tokens and cookies. The installer privately hands off an offline recovery kit. A disposable full-installation recovery restores messages, originals and wiki, switches systemd services, obtains new consent and verifies new HTTPS writes.\n\nThe VM renews transport certificates automatically, starting 30 days before expiry. Durable stages overlap trust, observe the actually served Cloud.ru revision, drain existing requests, then retire old trust. Lost cloud replies and controller crashes resume the same generation. The ten-minute timer survives SSH logout; concurrent controllers cannot race. The SSH installer preserves deployment identity and pending rotations without exposing credentials.\n\nSafe finite diagnostics separate public edge, mTLS transport, MCP metadata and OAuth challenge from independent VM probes. Traces retain only bounded status/timing and allowlisted revision/failure headers: no response bodies, credentials or raw exceptions. VM TLS probes verify exact issued leaves during overlap, avoiding same-subject historical CA ambiguity without disabling TLS verification. Tests reject unrelated, wrong-host and retired certificates.\n\nValidation: a full local run passed 223 tests (one Linux-only skip), followed by six focused diagnostic tests and 19 actual-Caddy gateway tests after subsequent fixes. The exact-leaf overlap test also passed on Linux. Current code CI (399c4f5) has passed Windows/Linux mTLS, Linux OAuth recovery and all 16 controller-interruption points; Ubuntu Python 3.11–3.13 and ARM64, Windows Python 3.11/3.12, SSH install on both Linux architectures and Terraform on Windows/Linux/Intel macOS passed. Remaining matrix jobs are pending, not claimed passed. An earlier Intel macOS failure exposed a test fixture whose five-second client timeout preceded the proxy dial timeout; the current fixture explicitly terminates the synthetic TLS connection.\n\nLive Cloud.ru repeat kept min/max 0/1, CPU 0.1 and memory 256 MiB. Renewal completed after an actual controller exit immediately after PATCH, reused the generation, and preserved OAuth workspace counts. The real timer is active/enabled and returns not_due. Public monitoring recorded 4,234 requests: one HTTP 504 at the first revision handoff and two public TLS-handshake failures after completion. The corrected independent VM probe recorded 1,255 checks without failure, including both late public TLS failures. The first 504 lacks simultaneous VM coverage because the initial monitor failed to start; that dependency bug is fixed. Original traces also retain 178 false VM TLS verification failures from the prior CA-bundle implementation, separately from corrected results. No trace records were dropped. Provider system logs returned only previous-day events.\n\nUninterrupted public access has NOT passed: the first 504 remains unexplained, and the later handshake failures do not distinguish the client/VPN path from the provider endpoint. Warm instances remain disabled and are not an established fix. Next diagnostic step: a second public observer on an independent network and current provider ingress/revision events. Memory mutations are never automatically replayed to conceal failures. See docs/certificate-renewal.md for timestamps and coverage limits.\n\nDraft, not the public 1.0 release. Remaining gates include public continuity, coordinated fresh HTTPS/OAuth installer/update/replacement-VM recovery, actual cross-client capture/files/wiki journey and OAuth compatibility, manual passkey recovery enrollment, consistent release versions, onboarding and pinned artifacts.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vlemutov/portable-context/issues/3/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vlemutov/portable-context/issues/3/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/issues/54","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/issues/54/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/issues/54/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/issues/54/events","html_url":"https://github.com/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/issues/54","id":6124999643,"node_id":"I_kwDOPHfPVc8AAAABbRQT2w","number":54,"title":"P0 GO blocker: deploy and audit independent monotonic finalized-checkpoint witnesses","user":{"login":"the-code-learner","id":142033899,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHdD6w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142033899?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-code-learner","html_url":"https://github.com/the-code-learner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-code-learner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-code-learner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-code-learner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-code-learner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-code-learner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-code-learner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-code-learner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-code-learner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-code-learner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":42,"created_at":"2026-10-30T18:41:41Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T18:12:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Public mainnet gate: still NO-GO\n\nPR #53 merged the **verifier** for canonical checkpoint bundles signed by a >2/3 Ed25519 witness key supermajority and QC-certified observer replay. This issue tracks the missing, genuinely **independent external witness service**. Static signature checking does NOT establish freshness, independence, uptime, correct upstream validation or rollback-resistant custody.\n\n### Minimum acceptance\n- [ ] Publish independently reviewed witness key ceremony and pinned public key fingerprints; minimum 4 distinct witness keys under at least 3 independent operators/infrastructure providers, with operator attestations that keys are independently controlled.\n- [ ] Implement signed checkpoint production by each witness **only after local native genesis, validator-chain/QC and finality verification**, never merely echoing a single trusted RPC. Run each witness on a separate host/backup and access-control domain.\n- [ ] Implement monotonic per-network finalized (height, canonical header hash) store backed by non-rollbackable hardware or independently authenticated append-only remote witness storage. Reject signing lower heights or a conflicting hash at the same height across crashes, host migrations and restore drills.\n- [ ] Add authenticated publication, signed witness key rotation/revocation with versioned policy, bound trust roots, explicit equivocation handling, witness expiry/freshness SLA and external observer fail-closed behavior for stale/missing publication. Do not use local clock alone as evidence of consensus finality.\n- [ ] Reproduce live 3-of-4 valid attestation and independently observe the correct QC-certified ancestor in v2 observer. Negative tests: two different height hashes, stale signed checkpoint/replayed bundle, forged or missing signature, compromised single signer, 1–2 witness outages, operator key rotation, genuine old backups and network partitions.\n- [ ] Record >=3 independent infrastructure operators and multi-host execution artifacts (logs, exact SHAs/config/versions, QC roots, failure injections, clock and network conditions). Independent third-party security review of witness key custody, authenticity and monotonic counter; documented fixes and sign-off.\n- [ ] Threat-model witness trust separation from consensus validator threshold. NO release eligibility simply because a witness threshold has signed a value.\n\n### Current state\nVerifier support: [PR #53](https://github.com/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/pull/53). Native local history/QC replay, manually operator-pinned ancestor and separately stored fsynced high-water ledger are available; the high-water file **itself** remains rollbackable. No deployed witness committee, independently measured monotonicity or production audits were demonstrated in the PR.\n\nParent release blocker: #42. Do not mark public mainnet GO until all independently demonstrated acceptance criteria pass, including separate validator-signing custody, historical committee changes, distributed Byzantine testing and runtime security.\n\n### 2026-11-10 — PR #151 merged: multi-operator witness HTTPS provisioning guard\n- Protected squash merge [#151](https://github.com/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/pull/151) on `main` `69960a95a8cea7f76d9d2e396e8b2e23c6886b8f` from exact PR head `584528159125f50db58e38e00d3580651bdb54df`.\n- Five exact-head PR workflows COMPLETED/SUCCESS: CI `42837849469`, V2 Lab `42837849648`, Dependency Lock `42837849486`, Devnet Gate `42837849203`, Security Regression `42837849334`.\n- New opt-in `NewProvisionedMultiOperatorHTTPSWitnessFloor` requires 3–8 distinct inventoried operator IDs/DNS hosts, 4–16 unique independently pinned public witness keys, strict HTTPS source validation and signed >2/3 floor agreement. Negative regressions cover invalid/duplicated endpoint/operator inventory, source outage, conflict, monotonic rollback and cancellation. See `docs/witness-https-operator-provisioning.md`.\n- Three postmerge `main` push workflows for exact merge SHA independently verified COMPLETED/SUCCESS: CI `42838497452`, V2 Lab `42838498805`, Security Regression `42838497226`.\n- **No acceptance checkbox closed.** Distinct labels/DNS are NOT proof of distinct infrastructure ownership/custody; no production HSM globally nonrollbackable reserve+sign, signed freshness, real distributed partition/restart evidence or third-party audit. Public mainnet remains **NO-GO** under #42/#54/#55.\n\n\n### 2026-11-10 — PR #152 signed inventory integrated; PR #153 aggregate deadline in review\n- [PR #152](https://github.com/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/pull/152) protected squash merged `main` SHA `a6a0e1b9732b324d9a5a48d28e41c730d2104db2`, PR head `f09df538491e759c06bc6eb7b3e41f5967cdc181`, all five exact-head PR gates SUCCESS after a real 180-second wait. Postmerge main SHA matched, all three push checks COMPLETED/SUCCESS: CI `42840790940`, V2 Lab `42840790928`, Security Regression `42840791308`, then a separate real 180-second wait.\n- #152 adds 3–8 out-of-band pinned operator inventory Ed25519 attestations, binds operator key/ID/HTTPS URL/NetworkID/validator root/pinned roster revision, prohibits operator inventory key reuse as quorum witness key. This is signed-claim provenance, **not** proof of independent legal ownership or infrastructure.\n- [Draft PR #153](https://github.com/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/pull/153) introduces one aggregate 5-second timeout for all sequential provisioned HTTPS origins, preserving shorter caller context and fail-closed verification, with deterministic cancellation regression and dedicated race CI. Initial workflow edits produced failed syntax runs on early heads; the YAML was reconstructed from known-good `main` and a single additional regression step. Current exact PR head `cf7d30dc80f0597eff08a32f29bb02879a48adb7` has 5 workflows launched (CI `42842932195`, Lab `42842932250`, Dependency `42842932185`, Devnet `42842932262`, Security `42842932201`); Dependency SUCCESS but remaining gates were IN PROGRESS at this update. PR #153 protected squash **MERGED** to main commit `cc87eb00236883fa9e9e5d48d051cf1bb4824a99` from final PR head `cf7d30dc80f0597eff08a32f29bb02879a48adb7` after real 180-second wait. Five exact-head PR gates completed SUCCESS: CI `42842932195`, Lab `42842932250`, Dependency `42842932185`, Devnet `42842932262`, Security `42842932201`. Three postmerge main push workflows independently rechecked on exact unchanged main SHA after a second real 180-second interval, all COMPLETED/SUCCESS: CI `42843836260`, Lab `42843836144`, Security Regression `42843836316`. All five exact PR-head gates and 3/3 postmerge push workflows succeeded. This does **not** satisfy independent witness custody/deployment, freshness, multi-host recovery or audit acceptance: #42/#54/#55 remain OPEN and public mainnet remains NO-GO. No deployment/audit acceptance criteria met; NO-GO.\n- #42/#54/#55 remain OPEN: no independent multi-host custody/recovery, signed freshness, globally nonrollbackable signer/HSM, or external audit. Public mainnet NO-GO.\n\n\n### 2026-11-10 — PR #154 draft: reject compressed witness HTTP representation\n- [Draft PR #154](https://github.com/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/pull/154), exact head `1f1f57ff6b5a1a11d67c583115a1748f245573fd` based on main `cc87eb00236883fa9e9e5d48d051cf1bb4824a99`. This changes the HTTPS witness floor source to disable automatic gzip negotiation/decompression and reject any HTTP `Content-Encoding` other than absent or single explicit identity, including ambiguous duplicate headers. Negative TLS test cases for gzip, brotli, duplicate headers; canonical uncompressed floor remains allowed. No quorum, BFT, custody or signed freshness change.\n- Five exact-head workflows launched: CI `42849770111`, Lab `42849769971`, Lock `42849770106` (SUCCESS), Devnet `42849769981`, Security `42849770375`; other four **still in progress** at this update. **Do not merge/claim green without 5/5 exact-head complete success plus postmerge push verification**.\n- #42/#54/#55 acceptance remains OPEN; external multi-host operators, nonrollbackable remote HSM and independent security audit not yet evidenced. Public mainnet remains NO-GO.\n\n- **PR #154 CI correction (2026-11-10):** initial head `1f1f57ff6b5a1a11d67c583115a1748f245573fd` failed Lab `42849769971` and CI `42849770111`: `TestHTTPWitnessFloorRejectsUntrustedURLAndResponses` incorrectly asserted that a separately injected `httptest` TLS client's default transport would not negotiate gzip. The production constructor does disable gzip, but that fixture doesn't use it. Removed the incorrect injected-client assertion, retained production `transport.DisableCompression` check and negative gzip/br/duplicate response-header checks. New exact PR head `75ecb5231ae22642a3bc3e22a5b97298e00da718` with fresh five workflows CI `42850150073`, Lab `42850149906`, Lock `42850149760`, Devnet `42850149862`, Security `42850149840` IN PROGRESS. Protected squash PR #154 now MERGED from corrected final PR head `75ecb5231ae22642a3bc3e22a5b97298e00da718` to main `0b545559a7282226375c59e2138cfcf1253ce85e`, after an actual 180s wait; exact-head 5/5 COMPLETED/SUCCESS: CI `42850150073`, Lab `42850149906`, Lock `42850149760`, Devnet `42850149862`, Security `42850149840`. Three postmerge push workflows verified COMPLETED/SUCCESS on unchanged exact main SHA after separate real 180-second sleep (2026-11-10 16:04:15Z to 16:07:15Z): CI `42850822798`, Lab `42850822693`, Security `42850822738`. Full 5/5 exact PR-head and 3/3 postmerge push gates SUCCESS. Mainnet NO-GO; no independent operators/HSM/audits.\n\n\n### 2026-11-10 — Draft PR #156: context-preserving certified witness minimum\n- [PR #156](https://github.com/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/pull/156), head `c88557149a0027c1aebeed74461ffdc15ee5a39e`, base main `0b545559a7282226375c59e2138cfcf1253ce85e`, **draft/unmerged**. `CertifiedWitnessFloorMinimum` previously only exposed a background-context legacy read and could drop a caller's signing/recovery deadline when wrapping a context-aware HTTPS multi-source floor. New context method propagates cancellation, rejects nil/already cancelled context before reading and rejects even late legacy sync responses after caller cancellation; minimum height/hash/network/root comparison stays unchanged. Dedicated race-repeated cancellation, deadline and valid-response regressions included in V2 Security Regression.\n- Five exact-head PR CI workflows pending at this update; NOT green, no merge. This does not prove independently operated witness keys, signed freshness, nonrollbackable remote HSM reserve/sign, or multi-host adversarial recovery. Mainnet #42/#54/#55 remain OPEN and NO-GO.\n\n\n### 2026-11-10 — P0 certified minimum context merge, P1 PR base refresh\n- PR #156 (`c88557149a0027c1aebeed74461ffdc15ee5a39e`) **5/5 exact-head CI completed/SUCCESS** after actual >=180s cumulative waiting, then protected expected-head squash **MERGED** as main `dfc839cab6edbf1c8a1e3ccde9b731af210f7c16`. CI `42855380398`, Lab `42855380601`, Lock `42855380274`, Devnet `42855380488`, Security `42855380672` all green. After an independent real 180-second sleep, all three exact postmerge main push workflows completed SUCCESS on unchanged `dfc839cab6edbf1c8a1e3ccde9b731af210f7c16`: CI `42856075093`, Lab `42856074969`, Security `42856075139`. P0 PR #156 is integrated 5/5+3/3 green, but no real multi-host HSM/audit or public mainnet GO. Change preserves caller cancellation through `CertifiedWitnessFloorMinimum`, with late legacy answer fail-closed and race tests.\n- Parallel P1 PR #155 was 5/5 successful on **old main** but had become stale after #156, so it was closed UNMERGED as superseded; [draft PR #157](https://github.com/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/pull/157) recreates the bounded 1 MiB peer status JSON fix on new protected main, head `76c490a4f71e6fb06c35837091f2148df50f2b57`, and requires its own 5 exact-head gate checks. No liveness root-cause, TPS or public mainnet GO claim.\n\n\n### 2026-11-10 — Draft PR #158: aggregate timeout for legacy operator-separated HTTPS floor\n[PR #158](https://github.com/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/pull/158) at exact head `67b18c8d42d903f979b90654ee6899207a0482b4`, base main `e2065e0ab3302d1d1aebd4d11bac62846d37cb04`, draft. `NewOperatorSeparatedWitnessFloor` previously read 2–8 independently pinned HTTPS origins sequentially with each source allowed five seconds, without a shared budget. It now sets one aggregate five-second `readTimeout` on the existing multi-source verifier; caller shorter deadlines still win and incomplete reads fail closed. Deterministic cancellation regression with three sources, blocked second, no third read/high-water advancement; dedicated Security Regression race test `-count=10`. Legacy 2-origin configuration remains *not production operator-independence proof*, strict 3+ attested path preferred. Initial head `67b18c8d42d903f979b90654ee6899207a0482b4` CI **FAILED** (run `42863561780`), unrelated `TestLabSevenValidatorsLastProposerNeedsFollowingSweepForQuorum` under busy CI; runner logged validator0 missing own vote after two manual sweeps while inherited automatic 1-second round timer advanced round. New PR head `505281a32df1cc6f86d0b5c4b50e95fcc6f5c056` also fixes ONLY this synthetic lab sweep-order test by disabling its unrelated automatic round timer, without modifying production timeout, the unchanged 5-second lab finality cap or separate 8-second proposer rotation liveness tests; adds full state diagnostics. Five exact-final-head PR workflows ALL COMPLETED/SUCCESS after repeated real 180s waiting and SHA check: CI `42864231107`, Lab `42864231166`, Lock `42864231182`, Devnet `42864232356`, Security Regression `42864231103`. Protected squash merge #158 SUCCESS from head `505281a32df1cc6f86d0b5c4b50e95fcc6f5c056` to main `f83b34d1695a029241f56860511ac3c08a4ded5d`. After independent real 180-second postmerge wait and exact-main-SHA recheck, all THREE push workflows COMPLETED/SUCCESS on main `f83b34d1695a029241f56860511ac3c08a4ded5d`: CI `42865155824`, V2 Lab `42865156292`, Security Regression `42865155585`. All 5 exact-head PR gates and 3/3 postmerge push gates GREEN. This software hardening is not evidence of physical operator independence, globally monotonic remote HSM reserve/sign, multi-host Byzantine recovery or external audit; mainnet NO-GO. NO external operator attestation or HSM/deployment/audit proof; mainnet NO-GO. Do NOT merge until all five exact-head completed SUCCESS, real sleep180, expected SHA protected squash, postmerge 3/3 and new sleep180. No mainnet GO: independent HSM and audit not fulfilled.\n\n\n### 2026-11-10 — PR #159 draft: custody HTTPS/mTLS attestations must use identity encoding\n- [PR #159](https://github.com/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/pull/159) head `431274d6d9eebe0bf293819bfe02c892a02cb8ae` based on main `f83b34d1695a029241f56860511ac3c08a4ded5d`. Both default and mutual-TLS custody HTTP clients now disable Go auto gzip negotiation/decompression; the reserve-and-sign response rejects any Content-Encoding other than absent or one explicit `identity` before its 4096-byte canonical JSON check. Negative end-to-end tests cover gzip, brotli and duplicate headers; positive explicit identity; dedicated `-race -count=5` Security Regression step. Ed25519 attestation, challenge, durable reserve/signing, network/root checks and consensus untouched.\n- Five exact PR-head runs completed SUCCESS after a REAL 180s sleep (18:03:48Z–18:06:48Z) and unchanged SHA / main recheck: CI `42871042673`, Lab `42871042848`, Dependency Lock `42871042984`, Devnet Gate `42871042624`, Security `42871042798`. Protected expected-head squash PR #159 MERGED from `431274d6d9eebe0bf293819bfe02c892a02cb8ae` to main `0bcadf10d26eeaffc9937fb652cd11eec966435d`. After separate REAL 180s postmerge sleep from 18:07:39Z to 18:10:39Z and exact unchanged main SHA verification, all three main push workflows COMPLETED/SUCCESS: CI `42871952344`, V2 Lab `42871952388`, Security Regression `42871952565`. Full 5/5 exact PR-head and 3/3 postmerge push gates GREEN. Mainnet still NO-GO pending independently operated witness custody, nonrollbackable HSM, signed freshness, multi-host fault tests, external audit. Mainnet still NO-GO. This is software boundary hardening only; no independent HSM operator/physical witness proof, signed freshness or audit. #42/#54/#55 remain OPEN and mainnet NO-GO.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/issues/54/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-code-learner/Zephyr-Chain/issues/54/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/querdian-dev/querdian/issues/60","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/querdian-dev/querdian","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/querdian-dev/querdian/issues/60/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/querdian-dev/querdian/issues/60/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/querdian-dev/querdian/issues/60/events","html_url":"https://github.com/querdian-dev/querdian/pull/60","id":6264275110,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVJAHQc8AAAABNkwPKA","number":60,"title":"feat(agent): add the spoke agent (T6.6)","user":{"login":"querdian-meeseeks","id":353045425,"node_id":"U_kgDOFQsLsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/353045425?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/querdian-meeseeks","html_url":"https://github.com/querdian-meeseeks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/querdian-meeseeks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/querdian-meeseeks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/querdian-meeseeks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/querdian-meeseeks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/querdian-meeseeks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/querdian-meeseeks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/querdian-meeseeks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/querdian-meeseeks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/querdian-meeseeks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12975284541,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVJAHQc8AAAADBWMhPQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/querdian-dev/querdian/labels/agent:review-requested","name":"agent:review-requested","color":"D93F0B","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12975339980,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVJAHQc8AAAADBWP5zA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/querdian-dev/querdian/labels/agent:review-passed","name":"agent:review-passed","color":"E6ECE6","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-07T21:17:16Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T18:18:18Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/querdian-dev/querdian/pulls/60","html_url":"https://github.com/querdian-dev/querdian/pull/60","diff_url":"https://github.com/querdian-dev/querdian/pull/60.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/querdian-dev/querdian/pull/60.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What and why\n\nThis pull request implements task T6.6 of milestone M6 (PLAN §18.5 and §18.6 rule 2): the spoke agent, as the subcommand `querdian agent`.\n\n**Base:** `agent/mc-t6.5-receiver`. Merge the T6.5 pull request first.\n\n- **Read before each sync:** the agent lists both policy kinds and the namespaces directly from the spoke API server, with no cache. If a read fails, or if it is not complete, the agent sends nothing, so `lastSyncTime` is not renewed. It sends nothing before the first complete read.\n- **Sync:** a digest at each heartbeat (default one minute), and the full state at once on `fullStateRequired`. Retry with backoff of at most one minute on `409`, `429`, network errors and read failures.\n- **mTLS client:** TLS 1.3, the receiver is verified against the CA file, no redirects. The cert, the key and the CA are read again before each request, so a rotation needs no restart.\n- **Status write-back:** a `Ready` condition with `observedGeneration` on each spoke object. A status never moves back to an older generation.\n- **Leader election** with a Lease, so one agent sends at a time.\n- **RBAC:** the package comment gives the minimum. An envtest shows that the agent works with only these rules and cannot change a policy spec.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests added or updated (unit; `test/e2e` if backend behaviour is involved). Envtests and unit tests for each T6.6 item, including an agent that loses its API server after a good sync, retries on `409` and `429`, cert reload, and a leader takeover.\n- [x] `make lint test-race` green; `make generate manifests` has no diff\n- [x] No new dependency outside the licence allowlist (`make licenses`). `go-logr/logr` and `k8s.io/klog/v2` move from indirect to direct.\n- [ ] Docs updated (`docs/`, `CHANGELOG.md` if user-visible). T6.7.\n- [x] Commits are signed off (`git commit -s`)\n- [x] Clean-room rule respected (no Loki/Tempo/janus source consulted; see CONTRIBUTING.md)\n\nThe implementation agent ran the `reviewer` subagent and fixed its blocking finding.\n\n**Open question:** the agent writes the condition type `Ready` on spoke objects. If a local Querdian also runs on the spoke, both write `Ready`, and the status changes again and again. Today the package comment says that the two must not run together.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/querdian-dev/querdian/issues/60/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/querdian-dev/querdian/issues/60/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openOMSI-org/openOMSI/issues/3863","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openOMSI-org/openOMSI","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openOMSI-org/openOMSI/issues/3863/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openOMSI-org/openOMSI/issues/3863/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openOMSI-org/openOMSI/issues/3863/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openOMSI-org/openOMSI/pull/3863","id":6311459832,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUu_qfc8AAAABOKNHzw","number":3863,"title":"feat(render): Apple MetalFX temporal upscaling on macOS","user":{"login":"realmaitreal","id":152312877,"node_id":"U_kgDOCRQcLQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152312877?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmaitreal","html_url":"https://github.com/realmaitreal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmaitreal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmaitreal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmaitreal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmaitreal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmaitreal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmaitreal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmaitreal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmaitreal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmaitreal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-10T16:46:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T18:09:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openOMSI-org/openOMSI/pulls/3863","html_url":"https://github.com/openOMSI-org/openOMSI/pull/3863","diff_url":"https://github.com/openOMSI-org/openOMSI/pull/3863.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/openOMSI-org/openOMSI/pull/3863.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What changes for the player?\nOn a Mac with Apple silicon (macOS 13 or newer), Settings → Graphics → Upscaling offers **Apple MetalFX**, with the same quality levels as NVIDIA DLSS and AMD FSR 3 on Windows: the picture is drawn smaller and brought up to the window with the help of the last frames, in place of the anti-aliasing and the render scale, from the next start. It is part of macOS, so there is nothing to install. Closes #3812.\n\n## How to test\nmacOS test build, a Mac with Apple silicon, any map and bus. Settings → Graphics → Upscaling: Apple MetalFX, Upscaling quality: Quality, start the game anew.\n- `game.log` says `MetalFX upscaling: Apple's temporal scaler, up to ...x on this Mac`, `metalfx upscaling (quality) running on ...` and `MetalFX upscaling: WxH to WxH`.\n- With `MTL_HUD_ENABLED=1` (Metal's own overlay) the HUD shows a MetalFX section: Scaling Temporal, input and target sizes.\n- Look at fine lines (fences, lamp posts, wires), the cab's displays and gauges behind their glass, and rain on the windscreen: sharp, no ghosting behind moving vehicles.\n- Ultra performance: where the Mac's MetalFX scales up less than 3x, the log says `this Mac's MetalFX does ...x at most; drawing at ...`.\n- An Intel Mac, or macOS 11/12: MetalFX is not in the list.\nThe full list is in `docs/UPSCALING_TESTS.md`, section \"Apple MetalFX (macOS)\".\n\n## Screenshots\nSame place in St-Servan, 2940x1846 window, 1:1 crops: top left the standard upscaler at 1470x923, top right MetalFX Performance at 1470x923, bottom left the standard upscaler at 1720x1080 (the game's largest size), bottom right MetalFX Quality at 1961x1231.\n\n<img width=\"1620\" height=\"860\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a2654531-d273-4114-a94f-a8740b8d9f86\" />\n\n## What does this change, and why?\nA third temporal upscaler beside DLSS and FSR 3, `TemporalUpscaler::MetalFx` (`upscaler=metalfx`), in `crates/omsi-render/src/temporal/metalfx.rs`. It mirrors `fidelityfx::Upscaler`: it takes the same `Inputs` and `FrameConstants` (jittered picture, reversed depth, motion vectors, the glass mask) and gives back the same sRGB-encoded picture, so everything in `temporal/frame.rs` that prepares the frame is reused unchanged.\n- MetalFX's `MTLFXTemporalScaler` runs on wgpu's own Metal device and queue (`as_hal`), its work committed on wgpu's queue right after the scene's. wgpu is not changed.\n- The framework is opened at run time (`dlopen`) and its classes called by name with `objc2`, as the game still starts on macOS 11 and 12. The objc2 crates are the ones wgpu-hal already uses: Cargo.lock gains no new crate.\n- The render size is clamped to `supportedInputContentMaxScaleForDevice` (3x on an M2), the reactive mask is used where the descriptor has it (macOS 14.4+), and FSR 3's weaker glass mask is shared, as MetalFX reads its mask the same way.\n- Jitter and motion: the motion vectors already follow MetalFX's convention (pixels, pointing back, y down, see the header's example). The jitter's sign was measured with a GPU test (`metalfx_settles_on_the_full_sized_picture`): a still picture settles at 0.29 from the full-sized one against 0.66 for the stretched one; with the jitter negated on one or both axes 0.39 to 0.62.\n- Offered by `omsi_cfg::upscaler_files` without any file beside the game; the in-game menu, the web launcher and the SwiftUI launcher list it (the latter now builds its list from `temporal_upscalers`, and shows the quality and hides MSAA/render scale like the web page).\n\nWorth reading first: `temporal/metalfx.rs`, then the `Runtime::MetalFx` arms in `temporal/frame.rs`.\n\n## What could break?\nOnly players who choose MetalFX, on a Mac. The other upscalers and platforms go through the same code as before; `upscaler_device::usable` was reworded per upscaler. Not tested: macOS 13 to 14.3 (no reactive mask), an Intel Mac (not offered), iOS (not offered), HDR, a triple screen (MetalFX is not used there, as with DLSS/FSR 3), driving in motion over a long time.\n\n## Performance\nApple M2 (16 GB), macOS 27.2, St-Servan at 13:19, PDO C2 standing at the start in the driver's view, no AI traffic, window 2940x1846, vsync off and no frame cap, fixed render scale (`OMSI_FIXED_SCALE=1`), SSAO and shadows on. Frame rates are the game's per-minute status lines once loading had settled (4 to 5 minutes each).\n\n| Upscaler | Drawn at | Frame rate |\n|---|---|---|\n| Standard (Catmull-Rom), 2x MSAA | 1470x923 | 26 to 27 fps |\n| **MetalFX Performance** | 1470x923 | **28 to 29 fps** |\n| Standard, 2x MSAA, render scale 100 % | 1720x1080 | 20 fps |\n| **MetalFX Quality** | 1961x1231 | **18 fps** |\n\nThe template's columns (this branch, the current release, 0.2.30) are not filled in: the table above compares the upscalers on this branch. Nothing changes for the other choices.\n\n## Checklist\n- [ ] `cargo test --workspace` and `cargo build --release` pass (`cargo build --release` and the changed crates' tests pass on macOS, among them the upscaler GPU tests with `--ignored`; the workspace run is in progress)\n- [x] The pull request contains a single change\n- [x] Before/after screenshots are in the description if anything changes on screen\n- [ ] A new feature has its performance table filled in (this branch, the current release, 0.2.30) (see above: the upscalers compared on this branch)\n- [x] New or changed interface texts are in `crates/omsi-app/locales/app.yml`, in every language I can\n- [x] Online play, saves, settings and mods made for the previous release still work, or the description says what changes\n- [x] No original OMSI 2 content and no file of a megabyte or more in the commits\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openOMSI-org/openOMSI/issues/3863/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openOMSI-org/openOMSI/issues/3863/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openemr/openemr-devops/issues/931","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openemr/openemr-devops","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openemr/openemr-devops/issues/931/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openemr/openemr-devops/issues/931/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openemr/openemr-devops/issues/931/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openemr/openemr-devops/pull/931","id":6293257381,"node_id":"PR_kwDOBhb1Wc8AAAABN7qvKQ","number":931,"title":"feat(k8s): zero-downtime cert rotation across the mTLS stack (closes #912)","user":{"login":"bradymiller","id":278968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3ODk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/278968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradymiller","html_url":"https://github.com/bradymiller","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradymiller/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradymiller/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradymiller/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradymiller/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradymiller/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradymiller/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradymiller/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradymiller/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradymiller/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-11-09T19:35:23Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T18:08:43Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openemr/openemr-devops/pulls/931","html_url":"https://github.com/openemr/openemr-devops/pull/931","diff_url":"https://github.com/openemr/openemr-devops/pull/931.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/openemr/openemr-devops/pull/931.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Closes #912.\n\n## Summary\n\nWeekly certificate rotation across the entire mTLS stack — MariaDB, Redis, Sentinel, NFS server + stunnel-client, phpMyAdmin, OpenEMR's own client certs — with **zero user-visible downtime and zero committed-transaction loss**. Replaces the previous 10-year cert durations (adopted defensively because pods had no reload path) with a 168h / 48h renewBefore cycle that's exercised ~every 5 days per leaf cert.\n\n## Why\n\nEvery cert-manager-managed certificate in this stack carried `duration: 87660h` (10 years) with `renewBefore: 360h` (15 days). The 10-year pin existed because **pods didn't reload the certs when cert-manager rotated them** — a rotation updated the referenced Secret, but the running processes (mariadb, redis, stunnel, apache/openemr PHP) continued to use whatever certs they parsed at startup. Shortening cert durations to industry-standard values therefore required solving the reload problem first.\n\nDoing that honestly required solving a second problem too: on the hand-rolled mysql stack, the `mysql` Service was headless and selected only `mysql-sts-0` (the primary) via pod-name selector — so a rolling restart of mysql-sts produced a **mandatory ~10-30s read-and-write outage** every rotation cycle. Rotating certs every 5 days that way would be a net negative. So the PR scope expanded to include a MariaDB HA layer that owns primary-failover orchestration end-to-end.\n\n## What's in the stack\n\n### Install path (`kub-up` + `kub-up.bat`)\n\nThree new install blocks after cert-manager, each with the same 5-attempt (bash) / 3-attempt (CMD) linear-backoff retry as the cert-manager block so a transient `github.com` 504 doesn't nuke the stack bring-up:\n\n1. **[stakater/reloader](https://github.com/stakater/Reloader)** `v1.4.23` — watches Secrets named in a `secret.reloader.stakater.com/reload` annotation and rolls the referencing workload on UPDATE.\n2. **[MariaDB Operator](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator)** `26.10.2` (CRDs + operator + cert-controller + webhook from `manifests.min.yaml`, a single self-contained apply).\n3. (cert-manager + reloader + MariaDB Operator sequence completes before any Certificate resources are issued or any workload is applied.)\n\n### MariaDB cluster → declarative via `MariaDB` CRD\n\n`kubernetes/mysql/mariadb.yaml` (new) replaces the hand-rolled mysql StatefulSet + configmap + Service + two cert-manager Certificates:\n\n- `spec.replicas: 2`\n- `spec.replication.enabled: true` + `primary.autoFailover: true`\n- `spec.replication.semiSyncEnabled: true` + `semiSyncWaitPoint: AfterSync` — primary blocks commit until replica has ACKed the binlog write, so transactions committed on the old primary are durable at the new primary before the switchover. No in-flight-transaction loss window.\n- `spec.tls.enabled: true` + `serverCertIssuerRef: ca-issuer` — operator issues its own server cert via the shared cert-manager Issuer. Same trust chain as the rest of the stack.\n- Three Services generated: `mysql` (headless, both pods), `mysql-primary` (writable), `mysql-secondary` (read-only replica). openemr + phpmyadmin env switched from `mysql` → `mysql-primary`.\n\n### Cert durations shortened\n\nAll leaf certs: `duration: 87660h` (10y) → **`168h` (7d)**, `renewBefore: 360h` (15d) → **`48h` (2d)**. Rotation cadence: every ~5 days per cert. CA cert (`ca-key-pair`) stays at 10y — CA rotation requires trust-chain overlap choreography (both old + new CA trusted simultaneously) that's out of scope.\n\n### openemr default Deployment → `RollingUpdate`\n\n`strategy: Recreate` → `strategy: RollingUpdate` with `maxSurge: 1, maxUnavailable: 0`. The previous Recreate was conservative — openemr's SWARM_MODE leader-election handles multi-replica concurrent boot safely (the gocryptfs example has shipped `replicas: 3` + `RollingUpdate` since day one, CI validates every PR). Flipping removes the biggest user-visible outage on any rotation cycle.\n\n### Reload path per workload\n\n| Workload | Reload mechanism | Secret(s) watched |\n|---|---|---|\n| `mysql` MariaDB cluster | **MariaDB Operator cert-controller** | operator-managed (`mysql-server-cert`) |\n| `redis` StatefulSet | stakater/reloader | `redis-certs` |\n| `sentinel` StatefulSet | stakater/reloader | `sentinel-certs` |\n| `openemr` Deployment (default + LUKS + gocryptfs variants) | stakater/reloader | `mysql-openemr-client-certs`, `redis-openemr-client-certs` |\n| `phpmyadmin` Deployment | stakater/reloader | `phpmyadmin-server-certs`, `mysql-phpmyadmin-client-certs` |\n| `nfs-server` Deployment | stakater/reloader | `nfs-server-certs` |\n| `nfs-stunnel-client` DaemonSet | stakater/reloader | `nfs-client-certs` |\n\nMariaDB Operator owns the mysql reload path because a correct mysql rollout requires more than \"roll the pods\": promote the replica to primary BEFORE terminating the current primary, fence the demoted pod, switch `mysql-primary` Service endpoints, bring the replaced pod back as the new replica. Reloader can only trigger a rolling restart — not failover.\n\n## Data-plane impact during rotation\n\n| Workload | Rotation shape | Downtime |\n|---|---|---|\n| MariaDB cluster | Operator-orchestrated failover (promote → fence → endpoint switch) with semi-sync AfterSync durability | **Sub-second reconnect, no data loss.** CI asserts zero FAIL probes through the rotation window. |\n| redis + sentinel | Sentinel re-elects primary (configured `down-after-milliseconds: 5000`) | ~5s + reconnect. In-flight sessions can drop (openemr tolerates via re-login). |\n| nfs-server | Single-replica Recreate; csi-driver-nfs reconnects via stunnel-client | ~5-10s NFS I/O blip |\n| nfs-stunnel-client DaemonSet | Per-node staggered roll | ~5-10s NFS blip per node, non-simultaneous |\n| phpmyadmin | Single-replica Recreate | ~5-10s 503 for active admin sessions |\n| openemr default | `RollingUpdate` with `maxSurge: 1, maxUnavailable: 0` | **~0s user-visible.** At least `replicas - 1` pods Ready throughout. |\n| openemr LUKS example | Must stay `Recreate` (ext4-in-LUKS is single-writer) | Single-pod cutover; brief outage. Operators who need zero-downtime openemr should use the default or gocryptfs examples. |\n| openemr gocryptfs example | Already `RollingUpdate` (gocryptfs `-sharedstorage` supports concurrent mounts) | ~0s |\n\n## CI validation — closed-loop proof\n\nNew top-level step in `.github/workflows/test-kubernetes.yml`: **\"Verify cert rotation triggers workload reload and preserves data plane\"**. End-to-end:\n\n1. Install `cmctl` v2.6.2 (cert-manager CLI).\n2. Discover the operator-managed server Certificate via jq label/name query.\n3. Record pre-rotation state: Secret fingerprint, StatefulSet `observedGeneration`.\n4. Start a 1 Hz mTLS probe from openemr → `mysql-primary` in the background (each iteration retries up to 3× over ~3s to absorb kube-proxy endpoint-sync microjitter).\n5. Wait for the probe to establish a successful baseline.\n6. `cmctl renew <server-cert>` to trigger cert-manager re-issue.\n7. Assert the Secret fingerprint changes.\n8. Assert the operator rolls its StatefulSet (observedGeneration advances).\n9. Assert `kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready mariadb/mysql` returns Ready (operator considers replication re-established + semi-sync re-connected).\n10. Stop the probe; demand **zero FAIL iterations** across the rotation window.\n11. Post-rotation openemr → mysql-primary mTLS smoke to confirm new cert is actually in use.\n\nLatest CI run (commit `84c6fdca5`): all green, including this step. The operator rolled the StatefulSet from generation 1 → 2 in 17 seconds; probe recorded 0 FAIL across the full window.\n\n## Files touched (high level)\n\n- `kubernetes/kub-up` + `kub-up.bat` — three install blocks for cert-manager/reloader/MariaDB Operator\n- `kubernetes/mysql/mariadb.yaml` (new) + deletions of `statefulset.yaml`, `configmap.yaml`, `service.yaml`, and the two operator-replaced certs (`certs/mysql.yaml`, `certs/mysql-replication.yaml`)\n- 10 leaf Certificates: duration/renewBefore shortened\n- 7 workloads annotated with `secret.reloader.stakater.com/reload`\n- `kubernetes/openemr/deployment.yaml` + both encryption-at-rest Deployments: `MYSQL_HOST: mysql` → `mysql-primary`, init container probe switched to match\n- `kubernetes/openemr/deployment.yaml` strategy: `Recreate` → `RollingUpdate`\n- `.github/workflows/test-kubernetes.yml` + `test-kubernetes-luks.yml` + `test-kubernetes-gocryptfs.yml`: cert rotation test added + mysql-sts refs rewritten for operator topology + `.github/actions/kubernetes-stack-up/action.yml` waits on `mariadb/mysql` Ready\n- `kubernetes/README.md`: `Certificate reload mechanism` section rewritten end to end; Overview + `kubectl get all` sample + scale instructions updated to reflect operator topology\n- LUKS example README: stale \"gocryptfs not shipped\" refs updated to point at the shipped sibling\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- **CA rotation**: `ca-key-pair` stays at 10y. Rotating a CA invalidates every issued cert + every trusted-CA list downstream peers hold; needs trust-chain overlap. cert-manager supports `trust-manager` for this; wiring it is a separate initiative.\n- **Multi-cluster MariaDB** (operator supports cross-cluster replication for DR). Out of scope.\n- **Redis async-replication durability**: semi-sync equivalent for Redis isn't configured; brief session loss is possible on Redis primary failover. openemr tolerates via user re-login; documented in the data-plane impact table.\n\n## Related\n\n- #910 — introduced the current 10y cert durations for the NFS pair, flagged this gap\n- #915 (LUKS) + #923 (gocryptfs) — encryption-at-rest examples; both openemr Deployments rewired for the new mysql-primary target\n- #913 — per-pod identity + namespace isolation (next in the #910 followup series)\n\n🤖 Assisted by [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openemr/openemr-devops/issues/931/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openemr/openemr-devops/issues/931/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boykopovar/AnyPS5/issues/11587","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boykopovar/AnyPS5","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boykopovar/AnyPS5/issues/11587/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boykopovar/AnyPS5/issues/11587/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boykopovar/AnyPS5/issues/11587/events","html_url":"https://github.com/boykopovar/AnyPS5/pull/11587","id":6048769778,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTs_xqs8AAAABK4XX6A","number":11587,"title":"perf(agc): destroy deferred MoltenVK objects when the queue is already idle","user":{"login":"imellag","id":118837721,"node_id":"U_kgDOBxVR2Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118837721?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imellag","html_url":"https://github.com/imellag","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imellag/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imellag/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imellag/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imellag/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imellag/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imellag/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imellag/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imellag/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imellag/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12429579047,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTs_xqs8AAAAC5NxTJw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boykopovar/AnyPS5/labels/needs%20rebase","name":"needs rebase","color":"b60205","default":false,"description":"Conflicts with main, rebase needed","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12432801526,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTs_xqs8AAAAC5Q1-9g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boykopovar/AnyPS5/labels/docs","name":"docs","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12432802489,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTs_xqs8AAAAC5Q2CuQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boykopovar/AnyPS5/labels/agc","name":"agc","color":"1d76db","default":false,"description":"libSceAgc*","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12743148713,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTs_xqs8AAAAC940EqQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boykopovar/AnyPS5/labels/perf","name":"perf","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Performance change","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"oneandonlydean","id":158058829,"node_id":"U_kgDOCWvJTQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158058829?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean","html_url":"https://github.com/oneandonlydean","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:48:17Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T18:07:29Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"oneandonlydean","id":158058829,"node_id":"U_kgDOCWvJTQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158058829?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean","html_url":"https://github.com/oneandonlydean","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oneandonlydean/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boykopovar/AnyPS5/pulls/11587","html_url":"https://github.com/boykopovar/AnyPS5/pull/11587","diff_url":"https://github.com/boykopovar/AnyPS5/pull/11587.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/boykopovar/AnyPS5/pull/11587.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"### What\n\nOn MoltenVK, #10062 destroys released buffers and device memory only while the graphics queue is idle (KhronosGroup/MoltenVK#2876). Before every recorder or command batch submission it drains the queue once 512 objects wait or the oldest has waited 100 ms. A title that releases buffers all the time reaches the 100 ms bound about ten times a second, and each `vkQueueWaitIdle` stops the queue worker until the GPU has finished everything queued. That cost was not measured in #10062.\n\nWith this change the recorder also passes whether every batch it has submitted has completed: its timeline semaphore against its submission count, read with `vkGetSemaphoreCounterValueKHR`, without waiting. When they have, and the oldest deferred object has waited 30 ms, the drain runs at once. It still calls `vkQueueWaitIdle`, so the guarantee #2876 needs is unchanged, but the queue is already idle. A title whose GPU finishes a frame before the next one starts now drains about once a frame, between frames.\n- The 512-object and 100 ms bounds stay as they were, for a queue that never goes idle and for `CommandBatch` submissions.\n- Only MoltenVK defers destruction. On other drivers the deferred list is empty, so the recorder only adds one `DeferredObjects` lookup per submission.\n- Why 30 ms: with 8 ms the idle drains also ran mid-frame, whenever the GPU caught up between small batches. Each one is a GPU round trip in MoltenVK's `waitIdle` (an empty command buffer committed and waited for), and Planet of Lana lost about 2% against no deferral. With 30 ms it is about 1%.\n- `agc_deferred_destruction` covers three new cases:\n  - an idle queue with objects younger than 30 ms: no drain;\n  - a busy queue at 31 ms: no drain;\n  - an idle queue at 31 ms: the queue wait, then the buffer.\n- The debt entry describes the new rule.\n\n### Tested\n**Current `main` (2026-10-27), clean commits.** Base `9f6232f229eb` is `main` `3fea2a937b` plus the 8 macOS PRs listed on #1 (fork branch `bench/main-boot-1027`); the change `87853364575c` is the base plus this commit (`bench/dd-pr`). `main` now has #11142, which removed most buffer creations, so the drains this PR avoids are rare there: the base committer spends 0.1 ms per frame in `Recorder.Submit`, not 3.5 ms.\n- Lana, alternating 120 s runs with mimalloc, fps from 85 s: base 30.31, 30.63; this PR 30.48, 30.69.\n- `trace_digest`, 95:10: base 302 presents, p50 32.9 / p90 34.9 / p99 44.5 / max 53.0 ms; this PR 306 presents, p50 32.6 / p90 34.6 / p99 37.7 / max 42.5 ms.\n- `agc_deferred_destruction` and `agc_buffer_pool` pass 3 of 3.\n\nThe runs below are from the earlier base (`main` `035ac96edd` with the macOS PRs), before #11142.\n\nmacOS 27.0.1, Apple M4 Pro, MoltenVK 1.4.2 (Vulkan SDK 1.4.363.0), x86-64 Release under Rosetta 2. `main` does not build and run on macOS, so this ran on `main` `035ac96edd` + #10366 #10552 #7631 #7804 #11249 #10669 #10540 #11447 #11047 #11048 #10876 #9263 and a local patch that loads `libvulkan.1.dylib`, without and with this commit. Every run had mimalloc injected with `DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES` (as #11130 does on request), and the same shader cache.\n\n**Planet of Lana (PPSA19450)**, New Game into the village, 120 s runs, alternated, fps from 85 s:\n\n| | runs (fps) | Driver.Packet | frame p90 / p99 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `main` (#10062 as merged) | 28.33, 28.49, 28.36, 24.52 | 24.0-25.4 ms | 45 / 50 ms |\n| this PR | 29.38, 29.12 | 21.0-21.3 ms | 35.5 / 39-41 ms |\n| `APS5_NO_DEFERRED_DESTRUCTION=1` | 29.64, 29.78, 29.82, 29.55, 29.58, 29.59 | 21.3-21.7 ms | |\n\n`tools/trace_digest.py` on the `APS5_TRACE_SUMMARY_EVERY=10` summaries, gameplay intervals (attached):\n- `main`: 70-110 s, 277-284 presents per 10 s, p50 33.7-34.7, p90 44.8-45.9, p99 49.2-54.5 ms, largest phase Driver.Packet 23.9-24.4 ms per frame\n- this PR: 60-100 s, 291-294 presents per 10 s, p50 33.8-34.1, p90 35.4-35.8, p99 39.0-48.5 ms, largest phase Driver.Packet 20.9-21.1 ms per frame\n\nSummary lines of the attached traces (`APS5_TRACE_SECONDS=95:10 APS5_TRACE_EVENTS=1048576`, window 95-105 s; the change build is marked dirty because the 30 ms constant was edited before the commit, its code equals this head apart from the debt text and the test):\n\n`main`:\n```json\n{\"commit\":\"c930034b60a8\",\"dirty\":false,\"env\":{\"APS5_ASYNC_PIPELINES\":\"1\",\"APS5_NO_PAD_INPUT\":\"1\",\"APS5_PAD_INPUT_FILE\":\"<path>\",\"APS5_TRACE_DIR\":\"<path>\",\"APS5_TRACE_EVENTS\":\"1048576\",\"APS5_TRACE_SECONDS\":\"95:10\",\"APS5_VIDEOOUT_TELEMETRY_DIR\":\"<path>\"},\"gpu\":\"Apple M4 Pro\",\"driver\":\"MoltenVK 1.4.2\",\"os\":\"Darwin 27.0.0\",\"cpu\":\"VirtualApple @ 2.50GHz\",\"cpu_threads\":12,\"memory_mib\":24576,\"title_id\":\"PPSA19450\",\"title\":\"Planet of Lana\",\"content_version\":\"01.010.000\",\"resolution\":\"3840x2160\",\"window\":{\"spec\":\"seconds 95:10\",\"first_present\":3968,\"ms\":10041.083},\"presents\":287,\"frame_ms\":{\"p50\":33.333,\"p90\":44.751,\"p99\":48.517,\"max\":51.355},\"gpu_busy_ms_per_present\":21.749,\"worker_busy_pct\":{\"queue worker 0x0\":69.718},\"top_phases_ms_per_frame\":{\"Driver.Packet\":23.883,\"Driver.Packet.draw\":18.592,\"Driver.Draw\":18.431,\"Graphics.Draw\":15.645,\"Graphics.Draw.draw_and_resource_release\":12.029,\"VideoOut.Flip\":10.065,\"Driver.Present\":9.268,\"VideoOut.Flip.present\":9.258},\"trace_dropped\":false,\"trace\":\"aps5-trace-c930034b60a8-41812.json.gz\"}\n```\nThis PR:\n```json\n{\"commit\":\"33dbe48a8e0d\",\"dirty\":true,\"env\":{\"APS5_ASYNC_PIPELINES\":\"1\",\"APS5_NO_PAD_INPUT\":\"1\",\"APS5_PAD_INPUT_FILE\":\"<path>\",\"APS5_TRACE_DIR\":\"<path>\",\"APS5_TRACE_EVENTS\":\"1048576\",\"APS5_TRACE_SECONDS\":\"95:10\",\"APS5_VIDEOOUT_TELEMETRY_DIR\":\"<path>\"},\"gpu\":\"Apple M4 Pro\",\"driver\":\"MoltenVK 1.4.2\",\"os\":\"Darwin 27.0.0\",\"cpu\":\"VirtualApple @ 2.50GHz\",\"cpu_threads\":12,\"memory_mib\":24576,\"title_id\":\"PPSA19450\",\"title\":\"Planet of Lana\",\"content_version\":\"01.010.000\",\"resolution\":\"3840x2160\",\"window\":{\"spec\":\"seconds 95:10\",\"first_present\":4015,\"ms\":10013.230},\"presents\":294,\"frame_ms\":{\"p50\":33.789,\"p90\":35.790,\"p99\":39.741,\"max\":41.878},\"gpu_busy_ms_per_present\":24.335,\"worker_busy_pct\":{\"queue worker 0x0\":62.869},\"top_phases_ms_per_frame\":{\"Driver.Packet\":20.976,\"Driver.Packet.draw\":16.603,\"Driver.Draw\":16.448,\"Graphics.Draw\":15.388,\"VideoOut.Flip\":12.220,\"Graphics.Draw.draw_and_resource_release\":11.782,\"Driver.Present\":11.413,\"VideoOut.Flip.present\":11.383},\"trace_dropped\":false,\"trace\":\"aps5-trace-33dbe48a8e0d-45115.json.gz\"}\n```\n\n**Stray (PPSA02100)**, the title #10062 was written for, 180 s runs pressing cross into the game, `MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1`, a MoltenVK without residency sets (where #2876 still crashes without the deferral):\n- `APS5_NO_DEFERRED_DESTRUCTION=1`: segmentation fault after about 30 s (status 139), so #2876 still reproduces on this setup.\n- `main`: 3 of 3 runs reach 180 s, no device loss, no Metal assertion.\n- This PR: 5 runs, no device loss and no Metal assertion in any. 4 reach 180 s. In the fifth the game stopped presenting after about 71 s, waiting on a `WAIT_REG_MEM` (the AGC wait diagnostic printed). The same diagnostic appears in 5 of 12 Stray runs on 2026-10-24 without this change, so I don't attribute it to this PR.\n- Stray's frame rate is the same in both: 2.8-3.2 fps with the Metal debug layer.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `agc_deferred_destruction` and `agc_buffer_pool` pass with `ANYPS5_REQUIRE_VULKAN=1 ANYPS5_NO_SHADER_CACHE=1 VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS=VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation`: no `VUID-` line, no \"was not found but was requested by env var VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS\". `agc_deferred_destruction` uses a mock device.\n- `tools/check_conventions.py --base upstream/main` passes.\n- `tools/pr_overlap.py` finds no conflicting lines. It could not compare the open pull requests that conflict with `main`; of those, #5609 also edits `Recorder.cpp`.\n\nNot tested: Linux and Windows (the path only runs on MoltenVK), GCC.\n\n### Checklist\n<!-- Rules behind each item: https://github.com/boykopovar/AnyPS5/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md -->\n- [x] Based on current `main`; no other open PR implements the same functions\n- [x] One topic per PR; follow-ups go in a new PR\n- [x] No comments in code except [technical debt](https://github.com/boykopovar/AnyPS5/blob/main/docs/dev/CONVENTIONS.md)\n- [x] Unimplemented paths throw (`NotImplemented_nid_no_patch`); silent stubs are listed under Silent stubs in their library's [technical debt](https://github.com/boykopovar/AnyPS5/tree/main/docs/dev/debt) file\n- [x] No notes, investigation `.md` files or images added to the repository (attach them to this PR)\n- [x] New third-party code is a submodule built from source\n- [x] Generic behaviour, not specific to one title\n- [x] Depends on: none\n- [x] Fixes: none\n- [x] Unblocks: none\n- [x] GPUs tested: Apple M4 Pro, MoltenVK 1.4.2 (Vulkan SDK 1.4.363.0), macOS 27.0.1\n- [x] AI-assisted: yes\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boykopovar/AnyPS5/issues/11587/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boykopovar/AnyPS5/issues/11587/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dnmitev/stralforsmcp/issues/2","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dnmitev/stralforsmcp","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dnmitev/stralforsmcp/issues/2/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dnmitev/stralforsmcp/issues/2/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dnmitev/stralforsmcp/issues/2/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dnmitev/stralforsmcp/pull/2","id":6310520089,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVoW5fc8AAAABOJckOA","number":2,"title":"Phase 1: Stralfors client library (mTLS, tokens, typed operations, write guard)","user":{"login":"dnmitev","id":5481670,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODE2NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5481670?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnmitev","html_url":"https://github.com/dnmitev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnmitev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnmitev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnmitev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnmitev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnmitev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnmitev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnmitev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnmitev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnmitev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-11-10T15:55:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T18:02:30Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T18:02:11Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dnmitev/stralforsmcp/pulls/2","html_url":"https://github.com/dnmitev/stralforsmcp/pull/2","diff_url":"https://github.com/dnmitev/stralforsmcp/pull/2.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dnmitev/stralforsmcp/pull/2.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T18:02:11Z"},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds a typed Stralfors Output Management API client library (`src/stralfors/`) and an opt-in live script.\n\n- Config and credential profiles from environment variables and secret files; secrets are non-enumerable and redacted in every string form.\n- undici mTLS agent per profile; OIDC client-credentials token source with a per-profile cache, single-flight refresh and exactly one re-auth on 401.\n- Typed operations (apiinfo, v1 health, channels, templates, rules, document example, validate dry run) with lenient zod schemas; double-encoded JSON bodies are unwrapped.\n- Error model: fixed messages, never upstream text or identifiers; raw fault data stays non-enumerable. Validation faults become structured `violations`.\n- pino allowlist logging with a canary leak test over logs and every error form.\n- Deny-by-default write guard on the parsed request URL: prod allows reads plus an opt-in validate dry run (`test=true` only); test allows reads plus the dry run unless writes are enabled; prod refuses `STRALFORS_ALLOW_WRITE=true` at config load.\n- `npm run live:channels` (not part of CI) prints the token scope summary and channel lists per agreement label, never an identifier.\n- CI: the denylist scan now also covers commit author/committer names, emails and messages of the whole history.\n\n## Testing\n\n- 199 tests, Node 24 and 26; coverage 97 / 92 / 97 / 99 (statements / branches / functions / lines).\n- Tests run against an in-process mTLS server with a runtime-generated CA (`openssl`) and synthetic fixtures.\n- Principal review: no critical, high or medium findings open; confidence is posted as `review/confidence` once CI has run on this head commit.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Mutation testing (Stryker) follows in the next plan of this phase.\n- Not included: MCP server, tools, retries beyond the single 401 re-auth, `requiredScope` metadata.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_011zTgbScZW4rhy8Y25hgv18\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added a Stralfors API client with configuration, authentication, invoice validation, and structured error handling.\n  * Added a command to report available channels for configured profiles.\n  * Added mutation-score reporting to CI summaries.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Documented client setup, environment settings, live API checks, terminology, and architectural decisions.\n* **Tests**\n  * Added coverage for client behavior, security safeguards, error handling, channel reporting, and mutation scores.\n* **Chores**\n  * Updated the automated review workflow to include review triage and a final review before maintainer merge.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dnmitev/stralforsmcp/issues/2/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dnmitev/stralforsmcp/issues/2/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/issues/22","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/issues/22/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/issues/22/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/issues/22/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Mistribe/Nid/issues/22","id":6260229824,"node_id":"I_kwDOVmSS_88AAAABdSOGwA","number":22,"title":"Documents: OCR and hybrid full-text and vector search inside documents","user":{"login":"Oleexo","id":3015008,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMTUwMDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3015008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oleexo","html_url":"https://github.com/Oleexo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oleexo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oleexo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oleexo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oleexo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oleexo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oleexo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oleexo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oleexo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Oleexo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12994335380,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVmSS_88AAAADBoXSlA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12994341649,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVmSS_88AAAADBoXrEQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/labels/pdf","name":"pdf","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Import ou rattachement de documents PDF","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12994341736,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVmSS_88AAAADBoXraA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/labels/Extra%20Large","name":"Extra Large","color":"e99695","default":false,"description":"Estimate: several areas or stages, a spec and several PRs","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12994341740,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVmSS_88AAAADBoXrbA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/labels/web","name":"web","color":"1d76db","default":false,"description":"Area: the web app (web/)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12994341741,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVmSS_88AAAADBoXrbQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/labels/mcp","name":"mcp","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Area: the assistant's MCP tools","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12994341743,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVmSS_88AAAADBoXrbw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/labels/backend","name":"backend","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Area: the .NET API and modules (src/)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12994341745,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVmSS_88AAAADBoXrcQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/labels/infra","name":"infra","color":"6e7781","default":false,"description":"Area: deployment, images and CI (deploy/, .github/)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":13024397332,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVmSS_88AAAADCFCIFA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/labels/module:documents","name":"module:documents","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"Module: documents and attachments (src/Documents)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-07T14:32:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:58:52Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\nA document can only be found by its name, role, year or links (`GET /api/v1/documents?q=…` searches metadata). Nothing reads what is inside it: « the boiler invoice », « the 2024 property tax amount » or « the clause on early repayment fees » cannot be found unless the file name says so. Scanned PDFs and photos have no text layer at all, so even a full-text index would miss them.\n\n## Proposal\n\nExtract the text of every document, OCR it when it has no text layer, and search it with a hybrid full-text + vector index.\n\n**Text extraction and OCR — first ingestion worker**\n- When a document is uploaded (and once for the documents already stored), Nid queues a `document-text` job.\n- The job runs on an ingestion worker registered as an agent (see « Worker agents » below): no database, no API key, no credential that opens Nid; it receives the file with the job and returns the text per page.\n- PDF text layer first; OCR (Tesseract, `fra` + `eng`) only for pages without one and for images. An `.eml` gives its body text.\n- The job contract lives in `contracts/jobs/document-text/v1/{input,output}.schema.json`; the API validates the output before storing it (risk AI-2 in `docs/security/risk-register.md`).\n- The text is stored per document and page, marked with its source (text layer or OCR) so the UI can say when it was read by OCR.\n\n**Worker agents — several workers, possibly outside the network**\n\nWorkers are agents an adult registers in Nid, so a household can run several and place them anywhere: on the same host, on another machine of the LAN, or in the cloud while Nid stays self-hosted behind a home network.\n\n- **Nid calls the worker, never the reverse.** A worker may be unable to reach Nid (Nid on an internal network, no inbound port), so the pull model of `docs/architecture.md` §9.3 (`claim` long-poll, `heartbeat`, `complete`) becomes a push model: Nid sends the job with its input and the file, then polls the worker for status and result. Leases, retries and `dead` stay on Nid's side. Nid reaches the worker through `SafeHttpClient`, the worker's host added to the allow-list at registration. One protocol for every worker, local ones included; §9.3 is updated accordingly.\n- **Registration.** On first start a worker generates its key pair and prints a one-time pairing code and its key fingerprint. An adult enters the worker's URL and the code in the settings; Nid shows the fingerprint to confirm, then both sides pin each other's public key. Each worker gets a name, its declared capabilities (job types and contract versions), its placement (`local` or `remote`), an optional `safe` tag and a status (online, last seen, version, current load). A worker can be disabled, its keys rotated, or revoked; revoking takes effect on the next call.\n- **`safe` tag.** An adult can tag a worker `safe`, whatever its placement (a remote worker on a machine the household trusts, for example). Only a `safe` worker receives documents marked local-only, payslips included; setting or removing the tag is audited and applies to the next dispatch.\n- **Routing.** Nid picks among the enabled workers that support the job type and version and are allowed to see the document, preferring local ones, then the least loaded; a worker that fails or stops answering has its job handed to another. When no eligible worker exists, the job stays queued and the jobs page says why.\n- **Transport security.**\n  - Mutual TLS 1.3 only, with the certificates pinned at registration (no public CA trusted, no fallback to plain HTTP or to an unpinned certificate).\n  - On top of TLS, every request and response is signed with the sender's key (HTTP Message Signatures, RFC 9421) with a timestamp and a nonce, rejected outside a short window or on reuse (no replay).\n  - The job input and the file are also encrypted end to end to the worker's key, and the result to Nid's key (HPKE or JWE), so a reverse proxy or load balancer terminating TLS in front of a cloud worker sees nothing.\n  - Nid verifies the result's signature, then its schema (risk AI-2), before storing anything; limits on size, duration and number of pages per job.\n  - Nid's private key is stored encrypted like the provider API keys (`llm-providers.md`); the worker's key never leaves the worker.\n- **Data policy.** A remote worker sees the document in clear while it reads it: encryption protects the transport, not the host. A remote worker therefore counts as leaving the premises, with the same rules as a cloud LLM provider: an adult's opt-in for the household. Documents marked local-only, payslips included (`llm-providers.md` §2.7), go only to workers tagged `safe`. `llm-providers.md` §2.7 is updated: a payslip may now leave the host, but only for a `safe` worker. The worker is stateless: it deletes the input once the result is fetched, and an unfetched result after a short TTL.\n- **Audit.** Every dispatch is recorded (job, document, worker, time, outcome) and shown on the jobs page; registering, rotating or revoking a worker is audited.\n- `docs/security/risk-register.md` and `docs/security/ai-ingestion.md` gain the worker-agent risks: impersonated worker, interception, stolen worker key, compromised remote host.\n\n**Index**\n- Postgres moves to an image with pgvector (`pgvector/pgvector:pg16` or equivalent) in `deploy/`, the Aspire AppHost and Testcontainers; backup and restore are checked with it.\n- Text is split into chunks (a few hundred tokens, overlapping, page kept). Each chunk gets a `tsvector` (French configuration) and an embedding (`vector`, HNSW index).\n- Embeddings are computed through the LLM gateway (`docs/ingestion/llm-providers.md` §9): **local Ollama by default**; an adult can switch the household to a cloud provider profile, with the existing opt-in, eligibility and consent rules. The model name and dimension are stored with each embedding; changing model re-embeds in the background.\n- Payslips stay local whatever the household chose (`llm-providers.md` §2.7).\n\n**Search**\n- One server query fuses full-text rank and vector similarity (reciprocal rank fusion), filtered in SQL by the reader's rights, and returns documents with the best matching snippet and its page.\n- Exposed in three places:\n  - **Documents page**: the existing search field also searches content, results show a highlighted snippet and the page; filters and paging unchanged (Nid-archive#420 rules).\n  - **MCP**: a `search_documents` tool returning document ids, snippets and pages, so the assistant can then call `read_document`.\n  - **Global search** (command palette): a « Documents » group with the top matches.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Uploading a PDF with a text layer, a scanned PDF and a JPEG photo produces stored text for each, the scan and photo through OCR\n- [ ] Existing documents are processed once by a backfill, without blocking start-up\n- [ ] The worker holds no database credentials and nothing that opens Nid; a malformed worker output is rejected\n- [ ] Two workers registered at once both receive jobs; stopping one hands its job to the other\n- [ ] A worker that cannot open any connection to Nid (outbound blocked) still processes jobs, Nid calling it\n- [ ] Registration pins the keys after an adult confirms the fingerprint; a worker with another certificate or key, an unsigned or replayed request, or a revoked worker is refused\n- [ ] A TLS-terminating proxy in front of a worker sees neither the file nor the text (end-to-end encryption)\n- [ ] A payslip or a local-only document is only sent to a worker tagged `safe`; with no `safe` worker available it stays queued with the reason shown\n- [ ] No document is sent to a remote worker before an adult's opt-in\n- [ ] Searching a word that only appears inside a scanned document finds it on the Documents page, with its snippet and page\n- [ ] Searching by meaning (« facture chaudière » for a document titled « Facture 2025-118 ») finds it; searching an exact reference number finds it too\n- [ ] A person never gets a snippet from a document they cannot read (web, MCP and global search)\n- [ ] Embeddings are local by default; switching to a cloud provider needs an adult's opt-in, and payslips are never sent\n- [ ] `search_documents` MCP tool and the global search group return the same results as the API\n- [ ] Postgres with pgvector runs in dev (Aspire), tests (Testcontainers) and `deploy/`, and a backup restores with the index\n- [ ] Deleting a document deletes its text, chunks and embeddings\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Turning extracted text into proposals (amounts, dates): the ingestion pipeline of stage 4\n- Generated answers over the documents (RAG chat); this issue only finds passages\n- OCR by a vision model; Tesseract only for now\n- Handwriting and languages other than French and English\n- Automatic discovery of workers on the network; a worker is always registered by an adult\n\n## Estimate\n\nExtra Large: worker agents and job pipeline, database image and index, API, MCP and web, in several PRs (suggested split: 1. worker agent protocol (push, registration, mTLS, signatures, encryption) + settings screen; 2. pgvector image + text storage + OCR job; 3. chunks, embeddings and gateway; 4. search API + Documents page; 5. MCP tool + global search).\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/issues/22/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mistribe/Nid/issues/22/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rest-mail/rest-mail-server/issues/1869","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rest-mail/rest-mail-server","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rest-mail/rest-mail-server/issues/1869/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rest-mail/rest-mail-server/issues/1869/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rest-mail/rest-mail-server/issues/1869/events","html_url":"https://github.com/rest-mail/rest-mail-server/issues/1869","id":6200139621,"node_id":"I_kwDOSPYs788AAAABcY6fZQ","number":1869,"title":"Open PR repair plan: strict oldest-first order","user":{"login":"christhomas","id":827996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNzk5Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/827996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/christhomas","html_url":"https://github.com/christhomas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christhomas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christhomas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christhomas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christhomas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christhomas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christhomas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christhomas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christhomas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christhomas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12942751101,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSPYs788AAAADA3K1fQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rest-mail/rest-mail-server/labels/claimed:macbook","name":"claimed:macbook","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Being worked by the MacBook issue loop","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":263,"created_at":"2026-11-04T09:28:59Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:54:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Tracking the analysis of every open PR (162 at 2026-11-04 09:30 UTC), oldest first, to build one strictly ordered plan for repairing and landing them.\n\nRule (owner, 2026-11-04): PRs land in creation order. Older PRs are the closest match to main; newer PRs may redesign what older ones built, so a newer PR is always adapted to what older ones left behind, never the reverse. Stacks land bottom-up.\n\nEach analysis comment covers one block of PRs and, per PR: what it changes, its base and stack position, CI state and the real cause of any failure, conflicts with main, overlap with older open PRs (same files or same objects), whether it is superseded or obsolete, whether it needs an owner decision, and the proposed repair action and order.\n\nBlocks: #1544–#1687, #1689–#1739, #1740–#1807, #1808–#1867.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rest-mail/rest-mail-server/issues/1869/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rest-mail/rest-mail-server/issues/1869/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FOGProject/fog-node/issues/189","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FOGProject/fog-node","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FOGProject/fog-node/issues/189/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FOGProject/fog-node/issues/189/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FOGProject/fog-node/issues/189/events","html_url":"https://github.com/FOGProject/fog-node/pull/189","id":6312286509,"node_id":"PR_kwDOD1wEVs8AAAABOK3n-Q","number":189,"title":"feat(agent): serve fog-agent over mTLS (listener, principal, renew, poll)","user":{"login":"mastacontrola","id":7305838,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMDU4Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7305838?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mastacontrola","html_url":"https://github.com/mastacontrola","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mastacontrola/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mastacontrola/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mastacontrola/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mastacontrola/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mastacontrola/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mastacontrola/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mastacontrola/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mastacontrola/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mastacontrola/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T17:34:01Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:53:36Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T17:53:35Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FOGProject/fog-node/pulls/189","html_url":"https://github.com/FOGProject/fog-node/pull/189","diff_url":"https://github.com/FOGProject/fog-node/pull/189.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/FOGProject/fog-node/pull/189.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T17:53:34Z"},"body":"## What\n\nAn enrolled fog-agent now proves itself on every request with its client certificate, renews it, and polls. It does this against fog-node exactly as it does against FOG 1.6, with the same agent binary. Brief: `2026-11-10-agent-mtls`. Wire reference: the 1.6 enrollment contract, sections 1.3, 1.5, 1.6, 4.4 and 5.\n\n- **Agent listener** (`api/hooks/agent-tls`): fog-node's own HTTPS listener on `custom.agentTlsPort` (default 8443; `0` turns it off). It serves the same Express app as port 1337.\n  - It requests a client certificate but never requires one.\n  - It sends the agent CA and the root as the acceptable CA list, which Go needs before it will send its certificate.\n  - A busy port or missing PKI logs one warning, and fog-node keeps running without the listener.\n  - At lift it makes or renews only the server certificate. It never creates or rotates an agent CA, which would orphan every enrolled agent. That stays with `npm run setup`.\n- **`agentPrincipal` policy:** verifies the leaf against the agent CA and the root in code, checks the dates of the whole chain and checks clientAuth, as 1.6 `openssl_x509_checkpurpose` does. A failure gets the 1.6 `401 {reason}` bodies. A plain-HTTP request is never an agent.\n- **`POST /agent/v1/renew`:** the 1.6 statuses and bodies. It writes the 1.6 `agent.enroll` audit row \"certificate renewed to …, key …\" (authSource `agent`).\n- **`POST /agent/v1/poll`:** the minimal 1.6 answer. `poll_interval` is an integer (`(int)` in 1.6; the Go agent declares `int`). `server_time` is ISO 8601, as 1.6 `format('c')` sends it. It writes no audit row (1.6 has none).\n- Sessions are off for `/agent/v1/`, so polls create no Redis sessions.\n- The installer asks for the port and the server certificate SANs. `docs/install.md` has an \"Agent port\" section.\n- `ensurePki` moved to `api/lib/agent-pki-files.js`, so runtime code no longer requires `tools/`.\n\n## Test\n\n- `npm test`: 421 passing. The new tests are `test/integration/agent-mtls.test.js`, `test/hooks/agent-tls.test.js` (including the lift/lower races and the missing-PKI path) and the server-certificate tests. Each was made to fail with its fix removed.\n- `npm run test:ui` and `npm run test:install`: green.\n- `openssl s_client`: the chain verifies against `root.pem`, and the acceptable client CA names are \"FOG Agent CA\" and \"FOG Server CA\".\n\n## The real fog-agent, end to end\n\n<details><summary>Commands and verbatim log excerpts (enroll, poll, renew, interval, re-enroll)</summary>\n\n# Real fog-agent end to end against feat/agent-mtls\n\nRun on 2026-11-10 against the current uncommitted tree in ~/fog-node-mtls,\nafter the server_time change and the lift-time ensureServerCert change.\nAgent: ~/fog-agent/bin/fog-agent. The database is the worktree's dev database (config/local.js).\n\nEvery block below headed `<file>.log` is copied from that file in\n<lab>/e2e/. Each line is verbatim. A line left out is\nnamed in the text above its block. The previous run is in `prev-run/`.\n\n## Setup\n\n    cd ~/fog-node-mtls\n    sails_port=1350 sails_custom__agentTlsPort=18443 sails_hooks__grunt=false nohup node app.js > $E/server.log 2>&1 &\n\n    E=<lab>/e2e\n    A=~/fog-agent/bin/fog-agent\n    ROOT=~/fog-node-mtls/pki/root.pem\n    D=$E/agent       # the agent --dir, new for this run\n    H=$E/admin.js    # signs a JWT in-process with the config secret and calls the admin API on 127.0.0.1:1350; prints no secret or token\n\nBefore the run, `node $H setting get` printed `null`: FOG_CLIENT_CHECKIN_TIME did not exist.\nAfter the lift, the pki folder held only the seven base files, with no timestamped file:\nthe lift made no agent CA and did not re-issue the server certificate.\n\n## (a) enroll: pending, then issued after an admin approve\n\n    $A enroll --server https://127.0.0.1:18443 --ca $ROOT --dir $D --once > $E/enroll1.log 2>&1    # exit 0\n\nenroll1.log:\n```\ngenerated a new key for this machine's identity\npending approval on the server (unknown-host); waiting\n{\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"reason\": \"unknown-host\",\n  \"retry_after\": 300\n}\n```\n\n    node $H pending > $E/pending.log 2>&1\n    node $H approve > $E/approve.log 2>&1\n\npending.log:\n```\n[{\"id\":\"6af353029e0787e4760ca178\",\"hostID\":\"6af353029e0787e4760ca179\",\"hostname\":\"<host>\",\"reason\":\"unknown-host\"}]\n```\n\napprove.log:\n```\napprove 200 {\n  \"id\": \"6af353029e0787e4760ca178\",\n  \"hostID\": \"6af353029e0787e4760ca179\",\n  \"state\": \"issued\"\n}\n```\n\n    $A enroll --server https://127.0.0.1:18443 --ca $ROOT --dir $D --once > $E/enroll2.log 2>&1    # exit 0\n\nenroll2.log (the `certificate_pem` line, a public certificate chain, is left out for length):\n```\nenrolled as host 254, certificate valid until 2027-11-10 17:23:14\n{\n  \"status\": \"issued\",\n  \"host_id\": 254,\n  \"not_after\": \"2027-11-10 17:23:14\"\n}\n```\n\n## (b) one clean poll; server_time matches +00:00\n\n    $A run --dir $D --once > $E/poll1.log 2>&1    # exit 0\n\npoll1.log:\n```\nfacts: sending inventory=true software=2849 directory=true printers=1 network=6\nhost 254 (<host>), server capabilities: []\n{\n  \"directory_hold\": false,\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"protocol\": 1,\n  \"host\": {\n    \"id\": 254,\n    \"name\": \"<host>\"\n  },\n  \"revision\": \"\",\n  \"poll_interval\": 60,\n  \"server_time\": \"2026-11-10T17:23:18+00:00\",\n  \"state\": {\n    \"revision\": \"\",\n    \"capabilities\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n\nChecks on the logs:\n\n    grep -ciE \"401|decode|revision moved|no state|error\" poll1.log poll-905.log    # poll1.log:0, poll-905.log:0\n    grep -E '\"server_time\": \"[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}\\+00:00\"' poll1.log poll-905.log    # one match in each\n    grep -niE \"error|warn|404|500\" server.log    # no match\n\n## (c) renew, and its audit row\n\n    $A renew --dir $D > $E/renew.log 2>&1    # exit 0\n    node $H audit > $E/audit.log 2>&1\n\nrenew.log:\n```\ncertificate renewed, valid until 2027-11-10 17:23:18\n{\n  \"enrolled\": true,\n  \"host_id\": 254\n}\n```\n\naudit.log (this run's row; the second line of the file, a row from the previous run, is left out):\n```\n{\"type\":\"agent.enroll\",\"text\":\"certificate renewed to 2027-11-10 17:23:18, key cb02ef337caf0205\",\"authSource\":\"agent\",\"createdBy\":\"(system)\",\"subjectLabel\":\"<host>\",\"renderable\":true,\"outcome\":\"allowed\"}\n```\n\n## (e) FOG_CLIENT_CHECKIN_TIME = \"90.5\" gives poll_interval 90\n\n    node $H setting 90.5 > $E/setting-set.log 2>&1\n    $A run --dir $D --once > $E/poll-905.log 2>&1    # exit 0\n    node $H setting unset > $E/setting-unset.log 2>&1\n    node $H setting get > $E/setting-get.log 2>&1\n\nsetting-set.log:\n```\nset 90.5 inserted\n```\n\npoll-905.log:\n```\nhost 254 (<host>), server capabilities: []\n{\n  \"directory_hold\": false,\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"protocol\": 1,\n  \"host\": {\n    \"id\": 254,\n    \"name\": \"<host>\"\n  },\n  \"revision\": \"\",\n  \"poll_interval\": 90,\n  \"server_time\": \"2026-11-10T17:23:28+00:00\",\n  \"state\": {\n    \"revision\": \"\",\n    \"capabilities\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n\nsetting-unset.log:\n```\nremoved 1\n```\n\nsetting-get.log:\n```\nnull\n```\n\n## (d) host deleted: the next poll re-enrolls\n\n    node $H delete-host > $E/delete-host.log 2>&1\n    $A run --dir $D --once > $E/poll-deleted.log 2>&1    # exit 1 (--once stops after the message)\n\ndelete-host.log:\n```\ndelete host <host> 200\n```\n\npoll-deleted.log:\n```\nserver no longer recognizes this certificate; enrolling again\nfog-agent: server does not recognize this agent's certificate\n```\n\n## Cleanup\n\n    kill $(cat $E/server.pid)    # then: nothing listens on 1350 or 18443\n    node $E/cleanup.js > $E/cleanup.log 2>&1\n\ncleanup.log:\n```\nenrollment rows removed 1 ; hosts named <host> left 0\n```\n\nThe Setting is absent again, as it was before the run (setting-get.log). The audit\nrows and the `agentId` counter stay, because the trail is append-only.\n\nA grep for a PEM private-key header gives 0 for every log in this folder and for this file.\nThe words token and secret appear only in two Sails route names in server.log and in the\ndescription of admin.js above, never with a value.\n\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FOGProject/fog-node/issues/189/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FOGProject/fog-node/issues/189/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/issues/16","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taotao1024/prometheus2.53","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/issues/16/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/issues/16/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/issues/16/events","html_url":"https://github.com/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/pull/16","id":6312611254,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVpqWjc8AAAABOLIS1Q","number":16,"title":"Bump github.com/influxdata/influxdb from 1.11.5 to 1.13.2 in /documentation/examples/remote_storage","user":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":13030812363,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVpqWjc8AAAADCLJqyw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/labels/dependencies","name":"dependencies","color":"0366d6","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update a dependency file","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":13030820449,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVpqWjc8AAAADCLKKYQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/labels/go","name":"go","color":"16e2e2","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update go code","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T17:53:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:53:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/pulls/16","html_url":"https://github.com/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/pull/16","diff_url":"https://github.com/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/pull/16.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/pull/16.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Bumps [github.com/influxdata/influxdb](https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb) from 1.11.5 to 1.13.2.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb/releases\">github.com/influxdata/influxdb's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.13.2</h2>\n<p>Please see <a href=\"https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb/v1/about_the_project/release-notes/#v1132\">https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb/v1/about_the_project/release-notes/#v1132</a> for official release notes.</p>\n<h2>Bug fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Resolve unimplemented interface member (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27715\">#27715</a>) in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27716\">influxdata/influxdb#27716</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Maintenance</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update go version to 1.26.10 in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27730\">influxdata/influxdb#27730</a></li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>OSS BINARY FILES</th>\n<th>SHA256</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://dl.influxdata.com/influxdb/releases/v1.13.2/influxdb-1.13.2_linux_amd64.tar.gz\">influxdb-1.13.2_linux_amd64.tar.gz</a></td>\n<td>4b1254ebcef8361baab2e0e4313e7e2821d56bea34bc0d5a63c0c2312cdd41c1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://dl.influxdata.com/influxdb/releases/v1.13.2/influxdb-1.13.2_linux_arm64.tar.gz\">influxdb-1.13.2_linux_arm64.tar.gz</a></td>\n<td>5f334b94cb02c20a063698f25155171013f61f9c6c7deb07e83b825247413f69</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://dl.influxdata.com/influxdb/releases/v1.13.2/influxdb-1.13.2_darwin_amd64.tar.gz\">influxdb-1.13.2_darwin_amd64.tar.gz</a></td>\n<td>f54909cb3f3960f49023309b30bf91a5bdd4ce7f037dbeff7a3363d71da19e5d</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://dl.influxdata.com/influxdb/releases/v1.13.2/influxdb-1.13.2-windows_amd64.zip\">influxdb-1.13.2-windows_amd64.zip</a></td>\n<td>5e61905d8a50d1775ae329183a1c2b4f798abd6328b812a7bf27870ae2fe87bb</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>OSS UBUNTU AND DEBIAN PACKAGE FILES</th>\n<th>SHA256</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://dl.influxdata.com/influxdb/releases/v1.13.2/influxdb_1.13.2-1_amd64.deb\">influxdb_1.13.2-1_amd64.deb</a></td>\n<td>c072144aa2aed112c0ae46a099b9e3677ac5d0c8b17abba8699d3bad5b3d603e</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://dl.influxdata.com/influxdb/releases/v1.13.2/influxdb_1.13.2-1_arm64.deb\">influxdb_1.13.2-1_arm64.deb</a></td>\n<td>d25674a563084400f34761945e810b2aa4f3ed8dd586a264705257dc0e950b31</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>OSS REDHAT &amp; CENTOS PACKAGE FILES</th>\n<th>SHA256</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://dl.influxdata.com/influxdb/releases/v1.13.2/influxdb-1.13.2.aarch64.rpm\">influxdb-1.13.2.aarch64.rpm</a></td>\n<td>c69b796e2c8f6ef6b1df7e5de99a5abe797b2903875b229b7c534e129e1a946d</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://dl.influxdata.com/influxdb/releases/v1.13.2/influxdb-1.13.2.x86_64.rpm\">influxdb-1.13.2.x86_64.rpm</a></td>\n<td>8241f6c01459648467caca61353487400fc5ec9e472b4f677955245fb2639445</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>v1.13.1</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>mTLS support</strong>: Add mutual TLS (mTLS) authentication for the HTTP, OpenTSDB, and subscriber services, including certificate reload on <code>SIGHUP</code> and separate client and server certificate configuration. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27534\">#27534</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27543\">#27543</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>Adaptive TSI cache sizing</strong>: The <a href=\"https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb/v1/administration/config/#series-id-set-cache-size\"><code>series-id-set-cache-size</code></a> cache can now grow and shrink itself between a configurable floor and ceiling based on the measured query hit rate, instead of staying at one fixed size. Configure it with the new <a href=\"https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb/v1/administration/config/#series-id-set-cache-max-size\"><code>series-id-set-cache-max-size</code></a>, <a href=\"https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb/v1/administration/config/#series-id-set-cache-target-hit-rate\"><code>series-id-set-cache-target-hit-rate</code></a>, and <a href=\"https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb/v1/administration/config/#series-id-set-cache-shrink-conservatism\"><code>series-id-set-cache-shrink-conservatism</code></a> settings. Monitor it through the new <code>tsi1_cache</code> <code>SHOW STATS</code> measurement. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27480\">#27480</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27552\">#27552</a>)</li>\n<li><strong><code>hardening-enabled</code></strong>: Add a <code>hardening-enabled</code> configuration option that restricts Flux HTTP requests to public addresses, mitigating server-side request forgery (SSRF). Disabled by default to preserve existing behavior. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27488\">#27488</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>Backup compression</strong>: Add a <code>-gzipCompressionLevel</code> flag to <code>influxd backup</code> for trading compression ratio against speed. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27293\">#27293</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>Broader config value formats</strong>: Size and duration configuration settings now accept a wider range of human-readable input formats, while remaining compatible with all previously accepted values. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27376\">#27376</a>)</li>\n<li><strong><a href=\"https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb/v1/query_language/explore-schema/#show-measurements\"><code>SHOW MEASUREMENTS</code></a></strong>: Support partial results when some shards are unavailable. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27443\">#27443</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>Operational visibility</strong>: Failed and slow queries, per-user query and <a href=\"https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb/v1/administration/config/#user-write-bytes-enabled\">write byte statistics</a> (opt-in), the remote host and user in query logs, compaction planning statistics, continuous query diagnostics, and TSM file-store merge metrics are now available through <code>SHOW STATS</code>, <code>/debug/vars</code>, and <code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code>. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27536\">#27536</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27547\">#27547</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27188\">#27188</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27528\">#27528</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/26981\">#26981</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27523\">#27523</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/26874\">#26874</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/26615\">#26615</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/26624\">#26624</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixed a potential deadlock and reduced lock contention between compactions and hot query reads in the TSM file store by splitting its single lock into separate fast and slow paths. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27501\">#27501</a>)</li>\n<li>Corrected several TSI compaction-planning and lock-contention issues. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27146\">#27146</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27123\">#27123</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/26649\">#26649</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/26647\">#26647</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/26432\">#26432</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixed authorizer leakage in <code>SHOW</code> queries. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/pull/27196\">#27196</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Notes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>This is identical code to InfluxDB OSS v1.13.0. Only the version number has changed.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb/commit/64ccba8d279e45a625d6b94873209de7335ba6e5\"><code>64ccba8</code></a> chore(go): Update go version to 1.26.10 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27730\">#27730</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb/commit/34efc1a7201a8096c81cb41c539861cfe97478d8\"><code>34efc1a</code></a> fix(influx_tools): Resolve unimplemented interface member (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27715\">#27715</a>) (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27716\">#27716</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb/commit/f130d738b652ac64b8ad923d5d751b0b5914c9ae\"><code>f130d73</code></a> chore(ci): add republish workflow for re-publishing a release tag (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27611\">#27611</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb/commit/f0281924ae2d2865dd1b981320d795a5e246639e\"><code>f028192</code></a> ci: push release artifacts to Cloudflare R2 instead of AWS S3 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27595\">#27595</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb/commit/e30b5b226075dfe3cbb64ffb17062e0548028921\"><code>e30b5b2</code></a> feat: Update go to 1.26.5 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27564\">#27564</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb/commit/4dd554f1df3a0bc03ae8099efb73962f61deb350\"><code>4dd554f</code></a> chore: bump golang.org/x/crypto and golang.org/x/net in 1.x (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27561\">#27561</a>) (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27562\">#27562</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb/commit/3d4d4afce490b9ce5996769c9f76f946bf290b4b\"><code>3d4d4af</code></a> fix: permit small TSI series caches to grow (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27552\">#27552</a>) (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27555\">#27555</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb/commit/798e8bfc4e8013d2b3b6a950fd7e542e1183cf63\"><code>798e8bf</code></a> feat: add per-user write byte statistics (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27547\">#27547</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb/commit/05622b2e022c7e42137240e582a3be051696f8c2\"><code>05622b2</code></a> feat: add --hardening-enabled option to limit flux/pkger HTTP requests (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27488\">#27488</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb/commit/4bb28843ea873be919d4343f18af42d237a94e91\"><code>4bb2884</code></a> feat: support separate client TLS certificates (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/influxdata/influxdb/issues/27543\">#27543</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/influxdata/influxdb/compare/v1.11.5...v1.13.2\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=github.com/influxdata/influxdb&package-manager=go_modules&previous-version=1.11.5&new-version=1.13.2)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/issues/16/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/taotao1024/prometheus2.53/issues/16/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albidev/hermes-mission-control/issues/127","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albidev/hermes-mission-control","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albidev/hermes-mission-control/issues/127/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albidev/hermes-mission-control/issues/127/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albidev/hermes-mission-control/issues/127/events","html_url":"https://github.com/albidev/hermes-mission-control/pull/127","id":6003837507,"node_id":"PR_kwDOR14J4M8AAAABKU1LUw","number":127,"title":"feat(rooms): invite-only federated rooms — owner side (MVP)","user":{"login":"albidev","id":22292011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjkyMDEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22292011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev","html_url":"https://github.com/albidev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"albidev","id":22292011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjkyMDEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22292011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev","html_url":"https://github.com/albidev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-23T19:03:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:47:39Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"albidev","id":22292011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjkyMDEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22292011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev","html_url":"https://github.com/albidev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/albidev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albidev/hermes-mission-control/pulls/127","html_url":"https://github.com/albidev/hermes-mission-control/pull/127","diff_url":"https://github.com/albidev/hermes-mission-control/pull/127.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/albidev/hermes-mission-control/pull/127.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Invite-only Rooms — owner side (MVP)\n\nFederated group rooms where the owner invites a paired peer, both sides consent, and the\nroom is activated exactly once. **Everything is off by default**: without\n`MISSION_CONTROL_ROOM_INVITES_CONFIG` the routes answer 404 like a missing path and the UI\nentry point stays hidden.\n\n### What is in here\n| Commit | Scope |\n|---|---|\n| `b9e1004`, `6e3b315`, `c73398e` | Network spike checkpoint (relay, connector, lab gates S1/S2/F1) and local invite consent |\n| `cff7647` P1 | Service boundary: lobby store, invite tokens, consent, fixed roster |\n| `6c87b25` P2a | Owner HTTP routes (`/api/local/room-invites/*`): auth before gate, 403 cross-origin, no URL/fingerprint/grant from the browser, `expected_binding` required on host decisions |\n| `79d4c0e` P2b | Joining-owner operations, material mint, once-only activation, lab hardening (schema guard, diagnostic allowlist, teardown) |\n| `0c59d08` | Re-pin native lab checkpoint after rebase |\n| `0e8246d` P3a | Owner invite panel in the group chat drawer (create lobby, issue/revoke, approve/reject, activate) |\n| `de44a3b` R7 | Lab `TargetMint` delegates to the product material mint (single implementation) |\n| `cfcf494` | Drain-deadline test slack (was failing under host load) |\n| `5bb9713` | Invite entry shown only when the owner routes answer |\n| `363a230` | CI: pinned public Hermes core on `PYTHONPATH` for the server step + optional `server/requirements-rooms.txt` |\n| `1e5587c`, `760b054` | Server suite made portable: MVP.1 baseline vendored as fixtures; real-lab parity test skips unless the lab is provisioned |\n\n### Not in here (follow-ups)\n- **P3b** — invitee-side UI to receive an invite and give consent.\n- **P2c** — orphaned-room reconciliation.\n- Lab `JoiningOwner` / `OnceActivation` stay lab-only (porting needs a legacy-binding migration and a product activation journal).\n\n### Verification (local, on the final tree)\n- Server suite: 337 tests OK (1 skip), both with `HERMES_PROFILE` unset and named, 0 ResourceWarning.\n- Spike suite: 208 OK (6 skip), 0 ResourceWarning.\n- Native lab gates: full suite, p2-p4, s2g, s2e, f1 green; source unchanged during the run, no listening ports left, Hermes core untouched.\n- Frontend: typecheck 0, `test:frontend` 112/112 files, build 0.\n- CI (GitHub): `tests` 328 OK, `server/tests` 337 OK (2 skip: the pre-existing one + the lab-only parity proof).\n- Every package reviewed independently; RED proven on copies for each fix.\n\nHermes core is not modified.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albidev/hermes-mission-control/issues/127/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/albidev/hermes-mission-control/issues/127/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeremyhahn/go-trusted-platform/issues/1576","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeremyhahn/go-trusted-platform","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeremyhahn/go-trusted-platform/issu