scriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebrandon1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebrandon1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebrandon1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebrandon1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sebrandon1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T16:38:15Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:23:20Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T17:23:16Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sebrandon1/tls-compliance-operator/pulls/688","html_url":"https://github.com/sebrandon1/tls-compliance-operator/pull/688","diff_url":"https://github.com/sebrandon1/tls-compliance-operator/pull/688.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/sebrandon1/tls-compliance-operator/pull/688.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T17:23:16Z"},"body":"## Summary\n\nFixes the deterministic nightly e2e failure and makes every Ginkgo block assert the conditions that make its scenario meaningful, instead of \"resource exists\" or exit-code-only checks.\n\nNightly run [42787685391](https://github.com/sebrandon1/tls-compliance-operator/actions/runs/42787685391) failed both Kubernetes and OpenShift jobs on all three attempts:\n\n```\nManager Per-Target Scan Configuration [target-scan-config]\n  [FAILED] Timed out after 120s. Expected <string>: (empty) not to be empty\n```\n\nRoot cause: `Run-Once Mode`'s `BeforeAll` runs `make undeploy` and never restores the operator. `Per-Target Scan Configuration` is declared immediately after it and depends on the suite-level deployment from `Manager.BeforeAll`, so `.status.reportName` never populated. Nightly is the only run that executes the whole suite in one cluster; PR CI runs one label per cluster, which masked it.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Operator lifecycle is now order-independent\n\n- `ensureManagerDeployed()` — idempotent: ensures namespace + CRD + Deployment, adds only missing fast-scan args in one patch, waits for rollout and `readyReplicas==1`.\n- `undeployManager()` — undeploys and waits for the Deployment and manager pods to disappear, so a local `bin/manager` cannot race a stale instance.\n- `buildManagerBinary()`, `managerArgPatch()`, `ensureManagerArgs()`, `parseManagerArgs()` — shared helpers replacing duplicated logic.\n- Wiring: `Manager.BeforeAll`, `ICI Integration.BeforeAll` and `Per-Target Scan Configuration.BeforeAll` call `ensureManagerDeployed()`; `Run-Once`, `Listening Port Discovery` and `Dry-Run Discovery` call `undeployManager()`. The previous spec comment that \"a report matters here, not the exit\" is gone; the target spec now explicitly re-ensures the operator.\n- Fast-scan args gained `--retry-backoff=1s`, because `Closed`/`Unreachable` are transient and the first check of an idle port otherwise spends minutes in backoff before `status.checkCount` is recorded.\n\n### Every block asserts vital state\n\nTyped helpers replace JSONPath substring checks: `listReports`, `findReports`, `getReport`, `getTarget`, `waitForCheckedReport` (matching source identity + `checkCount>=1` + `Available=True`), `expectCondition`, `reportEventExists` (scoped by `involvedObject.name`), `metricValue` (exact label set), `podIPs`, `tlsReportNames`.\n\n| Block | Assertions added |\n|---|---|\n| Manager | `readyReplicas==1`, pod `Running`, fast-scan args present |\n| Service detection | exact `Service/default/<name>:<port>` report with a completed check (the 443 spec previously passed if *any* report existed) |\n| ExternalName | identity + `Unreachable` + `lastError` contains `reserved address blocked` |\n| Pod / hostNetwork | identity, port, host in `podIPs`, `Closed`; hostNetwork report also matches `sourceName` and the `host-network=true` label |\n| Ingress / Target | full identity; Target additionally `Unreachable` + reserved-address error, `Ready=True/ScanComplete`, `reportName` matches |\n| Compliance validation | TLS version matrix, cipher grade A/B, forward secrecy, cert fingerprint/ECDSA/notAfter/days, `TLSCompliant`, `CertificateValid`, `Available`, `nextScanAt > lastCheckAt`; STARTTLS same identity/status; mTLS asserts the check ran; expiry asserts `0 <= days <= 1`, `isExpired=false`, `CertificateValid=False/Expiring` and a scoped `CertificateExpiring` event |\n| ML-KEM | `quantumReady`, `TLSCompliant`, `PQCCompliant` (True/PQCReady vs False/TLS13Capable) |\n| Non-TLS ignored | a canary HTTPS report proves scanning is active; exact-identity absence for the negative resources |\n| scan-all-ports | negative baseline before the flag, report on port 3000 with pod IP + `Closed`, report removed after pod deletion, flag removal via `removeManagerArg` |\n| PlaintextHTTP | status, no certificate, no `CertificateValid` condition |\n| Cleanup | completed report captured before deletion; exact-identity absence after |\n| Plugin | CSV header equals `export.CSVHeader` and rows match a typed snapshot; JSON unmarshals to `[]export.JSONReport` with values and sort order checked; Markdown header/row values; summary numeric totals computed from the snapshot; ETA relation `nextScanAt ≈ lastSeenAt + 30s`; uses `buildPlugin()` instead of `/tmp` |\n| Namespace filter | target `Ready/reportName`; rescan proves `checkCount` and `lastCheckAt` advance (not just annotation consumption); exact per-endpoint metric values for `version_support`, `forward_secrecy`, `pqc_readiness`, `cipher_grade`; deterministic TLS 1.3 fixture; `time.Sleep` replaced with polling |\n| Retry stall | `nextScanAt` advances and status stays `Closed` |\n| Run-once | JUnit decoded: case count/name format/class names; JSON rows well-formed; namespace filter only emits `ns/default ` cases; leftover report absent; `--fail-on-non-compliant` positive and a new negative case (exit 1); deterministic Pod fixture in `default` because Service discovery is event-driven and can lag the one-shot exit |\n| Per-target scan | typed target/report identity, `Ready=ScanComplete`, `tls10/11/ssl30=false`, 15m interval and not the 30s global |\n| Port discovery | manager exit path documented, pod declares no ports, report for 9443 with pod IP and `Available` |\n| Dry-run | strict endpoint line format, at least one endpoint, no reports created |\n| ICI | `ensureManagerDeployed()`; digest-label format; `waitForCheckedReport` before asserting field presence/absence; per-container `imageCertificationInfo` fields; CRD actually absent in the negative case |\n\n### Behavior-preserving cleanup\n\nDuplicated `deployTestServer`/`createTestService`/`waitForPodRunning` collapsed into `deployTestServerIn`/`createTestServiceIn`/`waitForPodRunningIn`/`deletePodAndService`; single `agnhostImage` constant; plugin builds use `buildPlugin()`; `countTLSReports` moved to helpers next to `tlsReportNames`.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- [x] `gofmt`, `go vet -tags=e2e ./test/e2e/`, `make lint` (0 issues)\n- [x] `make test`, `make security`\n- [x] Local Kind, `run-once || target-scan-config` (the exact nightly failure) — passes\n- [x] Every modified label individually and in grouped runs\n- [x] `run-once || target-scan-config || port-discovery || dry-run` — 9/9\n- [x] Full suite: 43 passed / 0 failed / 4 skipped (hostNetwork on Kind; ICI without `ICI_REPO`)\n- [ ] CI green (pending: GitHub Actions PR-triggered workflows were delayed by the 2026-11-10 incident)\n\n## Follow-ups surfaced (not changed here)\n\n- TLS 1.3 defers client-certificate rejection to the first application read, so an mTLS endpoint can report `Compliant`/`Unreachable` rather than `MutualTLSRequired`.\n- `--run-once` lists Pods synchronously but Service/Ingress discovery is controller-driven, so a one-shot scan can omit them depending on reconcile timing.\n- `nextScanAt` is anchored to `lastSeenAt`, which is not advanced by scans, so it ages into the past until the next status update.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sebrandon1/tls-compliance-operator/issues/688/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sebrandon1/tls-compliance-operator/issues/688/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NeverWe1come/KMIPKit/issues/168","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NeverWe1come/KMIPKit","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NeverWe1come/KMIPKit/issues/168/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NeverWe1come/KMIPKit/issues/168/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NeverWe1come/KMIPKit/issues/168/events","html_url":"https://github.com/NeverWe1come/KMIPKit/pull/168","id":6306789441,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU6dXVs8AAAABOGccpg","number":168,"title":"KMIPKIT-0090 Preserve FFI client protocol version","user":{"login":"NeverWe1come","id":111150798,"node_id":"U_kgDOBqAGzg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111150798?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NeverWe1come","html_url":"https://github.com/NeverWe1come","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NeverWe1come/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NeverWe1come/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NeverWe1come/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NeverWe1come/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NeverWe1come/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NeverWe1come/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NeverWe1come/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NeverWe1come/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NeverWe1come/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-10T12:27:47Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:20:32Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T17:20:32Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NeverWe1come/KMIPKit/pulls/168","html_url":"https://github.com/NeverWe1come/KMIPKit/pull/168","diff_url":"https://github.com/NeverWe1come/KMIPKit/pull/168.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/NeverWe1come/KMIPKit/pull/168.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T17:20:32Z"},"body":"## Summary\n\n- Preserve the configured KMIP protocol version when `kmipkit_client_create` constructs its internal Rust client configuration.\n- Add an mTLS regression that selects KMIP 2.0 through the C ABI and verifies the emitted Message Header.\n- Add the scoped specification, traceability, and changelog entry.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Red: without the fix, the controlled peer observed KMIP minor version 1 after the C caller selected 2.0.\n- Green: the targeted mTLS regression passes and observes minor version 0.\n- `cargo +1.94 fmt --all -- --check`\n- `cargo +1.94 clippy -p kmipkit-ffi --all-targets --features coverage-c-consumer -- -D warnings`\n- `cargo +1.94 test -p kmipkit-ffi --features coverage-c-consumer` (471 unit, 50 C API integration, and 1 operation parity tests pass)\n- `git diff --check`\n\n## Review state\n\nThis PR remains a draft with `[WIP]` until its complete CI passes. It is not approved or merged.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NeverWe1come/KMIPKit/issues/168/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NeverWe1come/KMIPKit/issues/168/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nginx/kubernetes-ingress/issues/8305","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nginx/