IVE — 2026-11-02 (LLP-first):** ALL NFL/NBA/NHL Pick'em, game-winner and daily team/event research insights must be surfaced **through LLP_TEAM_BETTING_ENGINE's governed team/event intelligence contract**, not a parallel competing predictor. The Pick'em project is a downstream contest/output consumer; LLP is the team/event model and synthesis owner. Reuse existing team-event and Daily full-slate paths; do not route player/scalar props into LLP or bypass V17 terminal governance.\n\n### Cross-market intelligence fusion — mandatory upstream/downstream contract\n- **Shared per-game context:** same canonical sport, official event ID, start time, participants, pregame snapshot and exact timestamped team/roster, injury, rest, starting QB/goalie and pace/script context where applicable. An insight generated here must be available as traceable, immutable, read-only **context** to LLP; it must never directly modify a certified fitted probability.\n- **Winner/moneyline and upset:** use LLP's existing controlling sport-specific team/event model and governed favorite/underdog upset-alert interpretation. Record predicted side, actual/model role, calibrated p/bounds and model receipt only if genuinely certified. NFL weekly Pick'em consumes this receipt; it does not produce an independent probability model.\n- **Spreads/puck lines/run lines:** separate fitted scoring-margin distribution and exact signed line/side, including push rules. A winner prediction is *not* a cover prediction. Current uncertified sports stay shadow/research and cannot qualify.\n- **Game total Over/Under and team totals:** treat as separate **team/event** market families within LLP intelligence scope, distinct from WOW player/scalar props. Exact numeric line, market basis and event-ending rules; require independently fitted/calibrated game/team scoring distribution, p_over, p_under, p_push (when line allows), uncertainty and governed certification. Until a real route/model is verified, show `RESEARCH_ONLY` / `MODEL_UNAVAILABLE`, not a manufactured Full Model. NHL total-goals challengers are currently research only; do not promote based on existence.\n- **Combined view, not probability averaging:** produce one event-level output bundle with per-market, per-sport source receipt/status, uncertainty, material injury/goalie changes, matchup insights, disagreement/correlation diagnostics and shared market context. It may compare theses and explain disagreements, but **cannot average or derive probabilities between incompatible markets** or let research override fitted sport-specific outputs.\n- **Integrity:** immutable kickoff/tipoff-time receipts, freshness and exact event mapping, fail-closed missing input; no postgame hindsight leakage. Full slate stays visible even when particular markets fail. Keep independently measured accuracy/calibration for winner, spread and totals (graded against their own exact settlement basis).\n- **Authority:** Controlling engine `LLP_TEAM_BETTING_ENGINE`; single authoritative specialist per *event + market family + side/line*; `V17_TERMINAL_REDUCER` sole terminal authority; `can_execute=false`. Shared market/value/portfolio governance remains separate. **No trading, order placement or automatic Pick'em submission.**\n- **Release:** Patch LLP canonical instruction/source/API contract and its read-only intake, regression-test missing/non-certified inputs and cross-market identity/line mismatches; review on isolated PR. Do not claim the live LLP Custom GPT or backend was updated until separately verified post-merge/deploy/editor sync.\n\n> **Owner scope extension — 2026-11-02:** This is now the umbrella for **NFL + NBA + NHL game-winner intelligence**. The original NFL-only charter and weekly pool rules below remain binding for NFL; they do **not** imply NBA/NHL pool entries or tiebreakers. Use the existing NBA model implementation issue #1950 and NHL issue #1952, governed by #2020 and #1562. Do not create competing fitted models, scoring owners, or release gates.\n\n## NBA + NHL daily intelligence — V1 additive contract\n\n**Objective:** Give GH complete current-day **full-game winner** boards and immutable pregame/postgame diagnostics for NBA and NHL. Start with game winners (not props, spreads, regulation-only NHL results, or bets). NBA full-game includes overtime; NHL full-game includes overtime/shootouts. Existing NFL weekly Pick'em sheet, tiebreaker and scheduled tasks stay separate.\n\n1. **Slate-first, full coverage.** Use sport-authoritative/current event manifest, exact event IDs, game dates and start times in America/Chicago, late cancellations and postponements; reconcile discovered/countable/started/completed/postponed games. A game without a model score remains visible with typed missing status.\n2. **Specialist-only predictions.** NBA: existing fitted NBA team/event owner #1950. NHL: existing NHL full-game winner owner #1952. Require exact sport/event/outcome, verified source timestamps before start, model ID/hash, certified calibrated p and its uncertainty bound, and immutable pregame receipt. *Never* convert a research candidate, uncalibrated simulation, sportsbook line, public consensus or narrative into `Full Model`. If any required evidence is absent show `PROVISIONAL_NO_CERTIFIED_PROBABILITY` (no numeric model confidence), retaining context-only notes separately.\n3. **Daily board fields:** sport | local date/time | official event ID | away/home | full-game winner pick or HOLD | prediction class (CERTIFIED_FITTED / PROVISIONAL / NO_PICK) | calibrated probability and bound *only when certified* | starting-goalie/availability status (NHL), confirmed/probable rotation/injuries (NBA) | freshness | pregame receipt/hash | late material status change | settlement status.\n4. **Independent grading.** Freeze picks before each event's start. Grade only officially FINAL (NHL including OT/SO); publish correct/graded, missing model coverage, expected correct, Brier, log loss, calibration by confidence range and separate NBA/NHL accuracy. Compare champion vs shadow challengers with forward-out-of-sample evidence; do not backfill post-lock data into historical pregame knowledge.\n5. **Source changes & updates.** Injury/lineup/goalie status must be timestamped. Material changes before start produce a newly versioned pregame receipt; keep prior versions immutable. After start, prohibit re-scoring as pregame.\n6. **Pool strategy optional.** If GH later provides NBA/NHL contest rules, entry/share data and tiebreaker semantics, add a *separate* pool-equity shadow. Without that evidence, do not infer a pool, opponent picks, or a tiebreaker.\n7. **Operational boundary.** Reuse V17 team-event source/identity, specialists, existing Daily stage and grading/QA patterns. No new provider spend by default; escalate missing free data as an explicit gap. SIRT independent acceptance and exact live SHA/readback are required for production-capable labels. `V17_TERMINAL_REDUCER` alone controls terminal status; `can_execute=false`; no wagers or automatic entries.\n\n**V1 acceptance:** (a) verified full daily slate in both sports; (b) complete read-only board that preserves every event and explicit model-hold statuses; (c) NBA/NHL each produce genuine certified fitted results *only when individually certified*; (d) frozen per-event card, independently official-settled accuracy report and pregame receipt; (e) no regression to NFL weekly card or existing model/QA ownership. Missing certification means *board V1 can be usable while model coverage is pending*.\n\n### Linked existing engineering work\n- **NBA full-game pregame fit/registration** #1950; existing #1511/#1512/#1695 components and QA remain the owners.\n- **NHL full-game fit + goalie preflight** #1952, #1349; existing candidate research never auto-promotes.\n- **Cross-sport restoration status** #2020; authoritative V17 release and capability acceptance #1562.\n- **NFL pool/cardy/accuracy** remains governed below; the NFL-only milestones below are unchanged.\n\n---\n\n# WOW Pick'em Intelligence — Project Hub\n**Project type:** Dedicated NFL Pick'em product/workstream within WOW V17 (not a replacement for the WOW fitted NFL specialist or a separate betting engine).\n**Created:** 2026-10-25\n**Mission (user priority, October 25):** Improve NFL game-winner **prediction accuracy, calibration, reliability and full-slate coverage**. Audit misses, establish actionable root causes with frozen pregame evidence, and validate improvements against untouched holdouts. Pool standings and first-place equity are secondary; never lead with them in routine reports.\n\n## Non-negotiable reporting hierarchy\n\n1. **Accuracy:** settled correct/total for all scheduled games, with fitted-model coverage and missing/provisional games shown separately; compare the frozen GH card only when available.\n2. **Miss review:** list each missed game, original fitted probability and bounds, evidence genuinely available before kickoff, and whether the loss indicates a correctable model/input failure or ordinary variance. Postgame storylines are hypotheses, not historical pregame evidence.\n3. **Model reliability:** expected correct, Brier/log loss, calibration buckets with honest sample counts, confidence intervals and multiweek patterns.\n4. **Improvement:** smallest testable fix or challenger, timestamp-safe replay, counterexamples, untouched holdout, independent scientific review and governed promotion only if evidence supports it.\n5. **Pool standings/tiebreakers:** optional, lower priority unless specifically asked.\n\n## Product contract\n- `PREGAME_MODEL`: route all NFL win probabilities through the controlling fitted/calibrated V17 NFL event specialist. Require immutable model receipt, kickoff time, official event identity, calibrated probability/bounds, and exact row terminal. Fail closed on missing capability; never substitute bookmaker odds, opponent vote shares, narratives or intuition as governed model probability.\n- `POOL_INTELLIGENCE`: collect only authorized pre-lock-visible selections/ownership and source timestamps; distinguish all-visible sample vs actual opponent-only cards; verify league lock rules, roster completeness, payout and tiebreaker semantics. Use sampled ownership only as *research assumptions* until validated.\n- `PICK_SHEET`: generate a clearly labeled user-ready printable NFL weekly pick sheet with all games, GH signature when requested, team sides, and a tiebreaker that is **not already used** in the currently connected weekly Google Sheet. Never modify the source sheet without explicit user instruction. Mark unsupported picks as provisional, not Full Model.\n- `WEEKLY_EQUITY`: keep incumbent `MAX_EXPECTED_CORRECT` separate from `POOL_WIN_EQUITY_SHADOW` / proposed `MAX_WEEKLY_WIN_EQUITY`; measure expected correct, sole-first, tied-first and tiebreaker impacts with truthful assumptions and conservative uncertainty. No strategy promotion without authentic discovery/untouched holdout and independent certification.\n- `POSTMORTEM`: lead with all-game predictions, errors, fitted-model coverage, expected correct, Brier/log loss, calibration, and pregame evidence-based root-cause hypotheses; keep GH's prepared vs verified submitted card, standings and variance separate.\n- `RELIABILITY`: same fixed issue -> reproduce -> minimal repair -> exact-head tests -> independent QA -> approved release -> production readback; avoid repetitive blocker/checkpoint escalations. Retain SIRT independent review and `can_execute=false`. Never place a wager or edit user entries automatically.\n\n## Canonical existing work (no duplicate ownership)\n| Area | Current source of record |\n|---|---|\n| Pick'em equity research, leakage proof, tie grading | PR #1680 and research issue #1708 |\n| Pre-lock opponent/ownership evidence and prospective holdout | #1703 |\n| Automated full-week official result scoring/delivery | #1530 |\n| Independent end-to-end Pick'em QA/accuracy | #1521 |\n| Week 6 real-world postmortem | #1852 |\n| NFL tiebreaker total-points specialist history | #1090 (closed; validate current production capability before reuse) |\n| Original winner-probability objective spec | #1116 (closed/not-planned; **do not claim delivered**) |\n| Base MAX_EXPECTED_CORRECT optimizer | #1073 (closed; verify current production route rather than assume) |\n\n## Milestones / acceptance\n- [ ] **M1 — Project boundary:** single charter; one product hub; links to existing issues/PRs; explicit status matrix.\n- [ ] **M2 — Weekly data contract:** canonical NFL game manifest and kickoff times, connected pool sheet, exact opponent visibility and pool rules, frozen snapshots and no hindsight leakage, row identity and tiebreaker uniqueness check.\n- [ ] **M3 — Usable weekly card:** all eligible games accounted, immutable fitted specialist predictions where available, typed source gaps where missing, no fabricated model probabilities, user-ready image/PDF with GH name and non-duplicated tiebreaker; independent provenance/readback.\n- [ ] **M4 — Accuracy evidence:** independent full-week settled predictions and per-game error taxonomy; calibrated Brier/log loss, model coverage, multiweek reliability and freeze-before-kickoff receipts. Pool-equity PR #1680 remains secondary research requiring genuine independent review.\n- [ ] **M5 — Accuracy improvement loop:** each miss investigated without hindsight; compare smallest challenger to unchanged fitted champion across discovery, counterexamples and untouched holdout. Report measured hit-rate and calibration gains or honest no-improvement, keeping strategy separate.\n- [ ] **M6 — Verified release:** independent QA/Release and actual live route/deployed SHA acceptance, no direct trading/execution.\n- [ ] **M7 — Operational ownership:** reuse existing NFL Pick'em Engineering Build daily task for actionable work and finished receipts; do not create duplicate scheduled agents.\n\n## Known evidence / caution\n- Oct 22 Week 7 Google Sheet was privately snapshotted before first kickoff: 14 games and 6 *visible* participant rows. This is **not** proof of six total pool entries, opponent-only entries, per-person submission time, or a complete 14-event fitted NFL prediction package. Preserve raw names/picks privately, not in this public issue.\n- PR #1680 is research-only and was open/unmerged at last review; independently verify all status claims fresh.\n- The Week 7 GH sheet with unique 47 tiebreaker was previously prepared as a user artifact; do not assume 47 remains unique in future weeks.\n- Metrics and improvement targets are aspirations, never guaranteed winners.\n\n## Roles\n**Owner / product:** GH. **Probability:** controlling WOW NFL fitted specialist. **Pool strategy:** downstream Pick'em research. **Engineering/AMRT:** build/fix. **SIRT / Independent QA / Release:** evaluate and verify without self-approval. **Terminal authority:** V17_TERMINAL_REDUCER. `can_execute=false`.\n\n## Status language\n`PROJECT_HUB_CREATED` does NOT imply `MODEL_CERTIFIED`, `RESEARCH_ACCEPTED`, `MERGED`, `DEPLOYED`, or `PICKEM_OPTIMIZER_PRODUCTION_READY`.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gregoryharper84-ship-it/WOW-Dashboard/issues/2076/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gregoryharper84-ship-it/WOW-Dashboard/issues/2076/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2171","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2171/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2171/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2171/events","html_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2171","id":6306306530,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAABOGDtFg","number":2171,"title":"DM_NVN_SHLOAD_LITE=1: shader loads take the argument buffer length from the reflection instead of an argument encoder, so the prefetch queues stop holding Metal's compiler cache lock at a scene load (default off)","user":{"login":"uncraftablexd","id":352372032,"node_id":"U_kgDOFQDFQA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/352372032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd","html_url":"https://github.com/uncraftablexd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12938277381,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy5yBQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/docs","name":"docs","color":"0075ca","default":false,"description":"Documentation","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12938278094,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy50zg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/nvn","name":"nvn","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"NVN on Metal and its tests (dm/gfx/nvn, dm/gfx/tests)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12962853499,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADBKVyew","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/game:%200400486024DEC000","name":"game: 0400486024DEC000","color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"A game","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-10T11:57:03Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:14:22Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/pulls/2171","html_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2171","diff_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2171.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2171.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"### What\n`DM_NVN_SHLOAD_LITE=1` (off by default): `shader_load` takes a shader's argument buffer length from its reflection json (8 bytes per argument ID) and makes no argument encoder.\n\nChanges:\n- `encode_args_` encodes whenever `arg_len` is set; it no longer needs an encoder object.\n- The pulling, shadow-input, alpha and logic side libraries skip the encoder length check.\n- With the switch unset, nothing changes.\n\n### Why\nThe encoder is only a consistency check. `o->ae` is used for nothing but `encodedLength`. `shader_load` already dies when that differs from `8 × (max argument ID + 1)`, the number the reflection gives.\n\nMaking an encoder is not free, though. `newArgumentEncoderWithBufferIndex` → `reflectionWithOptions` → `compileFunctionRequestInternal(reflectionOnly)` takes Metal's compiler file-system cache lock (`MTLCompilerFSCache::getElementImpl`, which also SHA-256s the element while holding it).\n\nAt a scene load, the shader prefetch queues (`dm.nvn.pso-bg` ×5, `mtl_prog_prefetch → shader_load`) held that lock. The replay thread's own pipeline and driver-program builds inside the same submission wait on the same lock.\n\npread, decompression and the rest of a library load are plain CPU outside the lock. The reflection request is the only part that takes it.\n\n### Numbers\nThe Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time (`0400486024DEC000`, v131072), Apple M4 Pro, title → gameplay load, on our integration host with this change. Route: a scripted walk through the load, cut 15 s into gameplay; base n = 5, lite n = 4.\n\n| | base | lite |\n|---|---|---|\n| prefetch queues' samples in `MTLCompilerFSCache::getElementImpl` (one 14 s sample) | 2,228 | 0 |\n| prefetch queues' CPU in that sample | 15.3 s | 10.6 s (−31 %) |\n| replay thread's samples in that lock (`rp_begin_ex`) | 28 | 0 |\n| load frame, wall / submit CPU (mean) | 445 / 193 ms | 392 / 180 ms |\n| load frame wall, range | 409–490 ms | 343–413 ms |\n\n- **What it fixes:** the lock contention. The load-frame gain is modest and the ranges overlap.\n- **What the load frame's remaining time was:**\n  - CPU texture deswizzles;\n  - upload-slot waits;\n  - time not running on a loaded machine (load averages 22–86 during the runs).\n\n**Side finding.** One lite run crashed at boot in `AGX createVertexProgramVariant` (`dispatch_group_leave`). The same crash also appears in three earlier runs without this change (the #342 family, PR #2079), so it is not attributed to this change.\n\n### How tested\n`make -C dm/gfx/tests GAME=0400486024DEC000 check_t_shload_lite` (`MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1`): 12 checks, 0 failed.\n\nThe test loads a vertex and a fragment shader with three bindings (constant buffer, storage buffer, texture), with and without the switch. Checks:\n- the old path makes an encoder, the lite path makes none;\n- both give the same length, which is the encoder's (24 bytes);\n- the vertex shader's `layer_out` from the reflection is unchanged;\n- `encode_args_`'s gate is open for a lite shader with bindings.\n\n**Fails without:** the test does not build on main (`g_shload_lite`).\n\nThe test runs on the GPU. It was run under our machine's GPU lock with Metal API validation on.\n\nLocal CI (`ci_local.sh --full`, merge with main ab41d6a17): no new failures. The jobs that fail are the ones main fails on its own: lint-c (t_mip_extent, t_pso_archive) and tool-tests (test_tree_tar).\n\n### Port notes\nOur branch also made only vertex libraries scan their bytes for `render_target_array_index`. That part is left out here: main takes `layer_out` from the reflection json and never scans a library.\n\nOur follow-up fix for that scan (the prewarm's vertex library) is left out for the same reason.\n\n### Reference\n- [Shader loads holding Metal's compiler cache lock at a scene load](docs/reference/shaders.md#shader-loads-holding-metals-compiler-cache-lock-at-a-scene-load), with its symptom index line.\n- Ocarina of Time's Found-on line.\n- The `docs/env_switches.tsv` row.\n\n### Risk\nUnder the switch, a side library whose argument layout drifted from its base library is no longer refused by the length check. All of them are built from the same reflection.\n\n### Regression\n`scripts/regress.py impact origin/main..HEAD` picks 3 games, all **affected** through `nvn_mtl.m` (`shader_load`, `encode_args_`, `pull_load`, the alpha and logic side libraries):\n\n| game | status | why |\n|---|---|---|\n| The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild `01007EF00011E000` | affected | switch off by default: `shader_load` and the side-library checks run as before; `encode_args_`'s gate is the same with an encoder |\n| Pokémon Scarlet `0100A3D008C5C000` | affected | the same |\n| The Legend of Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom `0100F2C0115B6000` | affected | the same |\n| Hades `0100535012974000` | not affected | |\n\n- None of the three were run (no data).\n- With the switch unset, the only change on their path is `encode_args_`'s gate: `!ae && !arg_len` instead of `!ae`. That is the same whenever an encoder exists, because `arg_len` is then its length.\n- 151 profiles have no usage manifest.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2171/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2171/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation/issues/4045","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation/issues/4045/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation/issues/4045/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation/issues/4045/events","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation/pull/4045","id":6186565468,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOa4Yns8AAAABMmfAww","number":4045,"title":"feat(k8s-cache): optional TLS and mutual TLS for the cache connection","user":{"login":"sainad2222","id":44405294,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NDA1Mjk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44405294?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sainad2222","html_url":"https://github.com/sainad2222","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sainad2222/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sainad2222/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sainad2222/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sainad2222/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sainad2222/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sainad2222/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sainad2222/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sainad2222/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sainad2222/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-11-03T16:15:19Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:12:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation/pulls/4045","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation/pull/4045","diff_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation/pull/4045.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation/pull/4045.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds optional TLS and mutual TLS between OBI and the k8s-cache. Plaintext still stays default.\r\n\r\n- k8s-cache now needs `tls.cert_file`, `tls.key_file`, and `tls.client_ca_file` to require client certs. Can also be as `OTEL_EBPF_K8S_CACHE_TLS_*` env vars. Validated when config loads\r\n- OBI needs `enrichers.kubernetes.metadata_cache.tls` in config v2 only (`ca_file`, plus `cert_file`/`key_file` for mTLS)\r\n\r\nI followed how peer metadata does TLS. I named it `tls` to match `peer_metadata.tls`, happy to rename. The commits are split so each one can be reviewed on its own.\r\n\r\n## Rationale\r\n\r\nThe cache sends cluster metadata to anyone who can reach port 50055, and NetworkPolicy doesn't help much when OBI runs with hostNetwork.\r\n\r\n## How to review\r\n\r\nOther than going commit by commit, you can also start with `pkg/kube/kubecache/tls.go`, which has all the TLS logic. Then the few lines in `kubecache/service/service.go` and `kube/cache_svc_client.go` where it's used. The config v2 part is in `internal/config/`. Everything else is tests, docs and regenerated fixtures (`migration-v2.yaml`, the defaults reference). \r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\nAlong with UTs passing, I added kind run results here\r\n\r\n<details><summary>kind run</summary>\r\n\r\n    client: plaintext    -> rejected (server preface: EOF), no metadata\r\n    client: TLS, no cert -> rejected (tls: certificate required), no metadata\r\n    client: rogue cert   -> rejected (tls: certificate required), no metadata\r\n    client: mTLS         -> service at 10.96.0.1 = \"kubernetes\" in \"default\"\r\n    TLS off (default)    -> service at 10.96.0.1 = \"kubernetes\" in \"default\"\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## Related issue or discussion\r\n\r\nFixes #1881\r\n\r\nAI disclosure: I used Claude Code to help write the code and tests, then reviewed and tested all of it myself.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read and followed the contributing guidelines\r\n- [ ] Features documentation / support matrix (not needed, k8s-cache isn't covered there)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation/issues/4045/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation/issues/4045/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2176","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2176/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2176/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2176/events","html_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2176","id":6306807859,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAABOGdY3g","number":2176,"title":"Specialized Metal 4 pipelines keep their base's sample count (and other fixed state) in their descriptor","user":{"login":"uncraftablexd","id":352372032,"node_id":"U_kgDOFQDFQA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/352372032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd","html_url":"https://github.com/uncraftablexd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12938277381,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy5yBQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/docs","name":"docs","color":"0075ca","default":false,"description":"Documentation","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12938278094,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy50zg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/nvn","name":"nvn","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"NVN on Metal and its tests (dm/gfx/nvn, dm/gfx/tests)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T12:28:58Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:11:15Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/pulls/2176","html_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2176","diff_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2176.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2176.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What\n\n`pso_build_ex` specializes a base pipeline (colour state left open) with the descriptor from `newRenderPipelineDescriptorForSpecialization`. Before the colour state, it now sets four fields from the draw's pipeline descriptor (`pso_spec_fixed`, `nvn_mtl.m`):\n- the raster sample count;\n- alpha to coverage;\n- the input primitive class;\n- the vertex amplification count, when above 1.\n\nThere is no switch. Pipeline keys, prewarm rows, the archive and the shader chain do not change.\n\n## Why\n\nWith `MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1`, a draw in a multisampled pass stops the host at its pipeline bind:\n\n```\n-[MTL4DebugRenderCommandEncoder setRenderPipelineState:]: failed assertion `Render Command Encoder Set Render Pipeline State Validation\nThe color sample count (4) does not match the renderPipelineState's color sample count (1)\nThe raster sample count (4) does not match the renderPipelineState's raster sample count (1)'\n```\n\nThe pipeline key, the pass and the guest's state are all right. NVN rasterizes at the render target's sample count. The host's key takes the attachments' count (`g_pass.samples`), and the base is built with it.\n\nThe problem is the specialization descriptor. `newRenderPipelineDescriptorForSpecialization` returns the colour state open and every other field at its default, whatever the base was built with. Small test programs (Apple M4 Pro, macOS 26.6.2) give:\n\n| base built with | specialization descriptor returns |\n|---|---|\n| 4 samples | 1 |\n| alpha to coverage enabled | disabled |\n| triangle input primitive class | unspecified |\n| amplification 2 | 1 |\n\nThe specialized pipeline is described by that descriptor, so the debug layer reads a 4x pipeline as 1-sample.\n\nOn the GPU nothing changes, measured both ways with the same programs:\n- A 4x base specialized with the defaults still leaves partly covered pixels on a triangle's edge (28 full and 8 partial of 64 pixels, the same with the field set).\n- An alpha-to-coverage base specialized with the defaults still gives half coverage for alpha 0.5 (mean 128 of 255, the same with the field set).\n\nSo this fixes what validation sees, not the picture. Without it, no game with a multisampled pass can run under API validation past its first such draw.\n\n## How tested\n\nApple M4 Pro, macOS 26.6.2.\n\n- `make -C dm/gfx/tests GAME=0100E95004038000 check_t_pso_msaa` (new) uses the production pass setup (`rp_begin_ex`), pipeline lookup (`pso_get_`) and specialization. It covers:\n  - a 4x depth-only pass;\n  - a 4x colour and depth pass, also with alpha to coverage;\n  - a 1x pass.\n\n  Each pipeline is bound and drawn under `MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1`. It must read as the pass's sample count and keep the draw's alpha to coverage. This runs through both pipeline compilers and with the encoding thread on: Metal 4 29 checks, MTLDevice 21 checks, Metal 4 with the encoding thread 29 checks; 0 failed.\n- **Fails without:** the same test built without the change.\n  - Both Metal 4 runs fail \"the pipeline reads as the pass's sample count\", then abort at the bind with the assertion above (exit 134, 2 of 2).\n  - The MTLDevice run passes either way: it builds pipelines whole, with no base and no specialization.\n- `dm/tools/tests/test_docs.py`: OK (new reference entry, symptom index regenerated).\n- **Local CI** (`ci_local --quick`): tool-tests, gfx-tests-build and cpu-gfx pass. lint-c reports `nvn_mtl.m` NullDereference 12 against a baseline of 9; main's `nvn_mtl.m` gives 12 too, and none is on a changed line.\n\n## Reference\n\n`docs/reference/rendering.md`: new entry \"A specialized Metal 4 pipeline keeps its base's fixed state in its descriptor\". `docs/agents/symptoms.md` regenerated.\n\n## Regression\n\n`scripts/regress.py impact origin/main..pso-spec-state`:\n\n| game | status | why |\n|---|---|---|\n| The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild `01007EF00011E000` | broad (`api:nvn`) | `nvn_mtl.m` |\n| Pokémon Scarlet `0100A3D008C5C000` | broad (`api:nvn`) | the same |\n| The Legend of Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom `0100F2C0115B6000` | broad (`api:nvn`) | the same |\n| Hades `0100535012974000` | not affected | |\n\nThese three were not run. Every Metal 4 pipeline that is specialized from a base now carries the base's fixed fields in its descriptor. The GPU state is the base's either way (above), so no picture or timing change is expected.\n\nPRAGMATA and Ocarina of Time were run on integration hosts carrying the same change:\n- **PRAGMATA, abort-mode API validation:** it got through gameplay load (where it used to abort, at about 25 s) to the cabin. It ran 128 s to its time limit with no assertion.\n- **PRAGMATA, 2 interleaved pairs without validation**, 4x pass window, base / with the change:\n  - pair 1: 55.5 / 57.1 fps, GPU p50 16.57 / 17.22 ms (the with-change run had a shorter window, 435 frames);\n  - pair 2: 55.1 / 55.2 fps, GPU p50 16.49 / 16.25 ms.\n- **PRAGMATA burst frames:** flicker 0 in all runs; mean luma 62.6-62.7 and edge energy 10.84-11.03 in every run.\n- 0 faults, 0 GPU events.\n- **Ocarina of Time** (title, cold pipeline archive): 1,726 specializations, 0 pipeline failures, 60 fps p50, no reports.\n\n## Where the bug sits (NVN vs host)\n\nThe guest is not at fault. At the failing binds (a diagnostic logging each bind's pipeline and pass sample counts, PRAGMATA):\n- The passes are depth-only: no colour target, NVN depth texture with 4 samples (`NVN_TEXTURE_TARGET_2D_MULTISAMPLE`).\n- The multisample state the host holds is all 0: samples, raster samples (no target-independent rasterization), alpha to coverage, coverage modulation and coverage to colour.\n- The fragment shaders read no sample ID or mask (reflection `raster.sample_mask` 0). One writes depth from a texture; two are depth-only.\n\nNVN rasterizes at the target's sample count, and the host's pipeline key did the same (4). Neither a misread NVN field nor a missing Metal feature: the Metal 4 specialization call needs the base's fixed state again in its descriptor.\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2176/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2147","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2147/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2147/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2147/events","html_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2147","id":6304400638,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAABOEhvog","number":2147,"title":"MetalFX's Metal 4 scalers run under Metal validation: a fence of their own","user":{"login":"uncraftablexd","id":352372032,"node_id":"U_kgDOFQDFQA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/352372032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd","html_url":"https://github.com/uncraftablexd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12938277381,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy5yBQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/docs","name":"docs","color":"0075ca","default":false,"description":"Documentation","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12938278094,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy50zg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/nvn","name":"nvn","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"NVN on Metal and its tests (dm/gfx/nvn, dm/gfx/tests)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T09:50:56Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:11:12Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/pulls/2147","html_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2147","diff_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2147.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2147.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What\n\nEach MetalFX Metal 4 scaler the host makes gets an `MTLFence` of its own (`mfx_fenced`, `nvn_mtl.m`). This covers the DLSS temporal scaler (`dlss_scaler_for`), the game's upscaler (`up_mfx_scaler_for`) and the present's spatial scaler (`fx_encode`). No switch.\n\n## Why\n\nWith `MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1` the host aborts at its first MetalFX scale:\n\n```\nMetal4FXTemporalScalingEffectV4.mm:561: failed assertion `_outputTextureBarrierStages not set'\nMetal4FXSpatialScalingEffectV1.mm:316: failed assertion `_outputTextureBarrierStages not set'\n```\n\nPRAGMATA (DLSS on MetalFX) stops about 20 s into a boot, so no PRAGMATA run can use API validation. The tests worked around it: `check_t_dlss_mfx` ran without validation, and `check_t_upscaler_mfx` ran validation only with the swap off.\n\n- The scaler classes (`_M4FXTemporalScalingEffectV4`, `_MTL4FXSpatialScalingEffectEFFECT_NAME_V1`) have only a getter for `outputTextureBarrierStages`. The SDK headers do not declare it, and there is no setter.\n- The public `fence` property (\"an optional fence that you provide to synchronize your app's untracked resources\") satisfies the check. A standalone 960x540 → 1920x1080 encode passes validation with a fence and asserts without one, for both the temporal and the spatial scaler.\n- MetalFX waits for the fence and updates it, so each scaler's encodes stay in order. The host's barriers before the scale (the queue barrier before MetalFX's encoders) and after it (each later encoder's queue barrier) still order it against the frame's work and do not change.\n\n## How tested\n\nApple M4 Pro, macOS 26.6.2, SDK 27.2.\n\n- `make -C dm/gfx/tests GAME=040074A01BF12000 check_t_dlss_mfx check_t_upscaler_mfx check_t_present_crop`: every run now uses `MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1`. With and without the encoding thread, and the present snap on and off: 7 / 91 / 12 / 112 checks, 0 failed.\n- **Fails without:** the same binaries built without the fence abort with the assertion above (exit 134) in all 6 runs: `t_dlss_mfx` with the encoding thread off and on, `t_upscaler_mfx` with `DM_UPSCALER=metalfx` (off and on), and `t_present_crop` (off and on).\n- `dm/tools/tests/test_docs.py`: OK (new reference entry and symptom line).\n- PRAGMATA `0400C76024710000` boot with `MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1` on an integration host carrying the same commit: see \"PRAGMATA\" below.\n\n## Reference\n\n`docs/reference/rendering.md`: new entry \"MetalFX's Metal 4 scalers under Metal validation\"; the upscaler entry's check line now points to it. `docs/agents/symptoms.md` regenerated.\n\n## Regression\n\n`scripts/regress.py impact origin/main..mfx-fence` picks 3 games, all **affected** only through the broad `api:nvn` rule (`nvn_mtl.m`):\n\n| game | status | why |\n|---|---|---|\n| The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild `01007EF00011E000` | affected | only with `DM_PRESENT_UPSCALE=metalfx` (off by default): the present's spatial scaler gets the fence |\n| Pokémon Scarlet `0100A3D008C5C000` | affected | the same |\n| The Legend of Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom `0100F2C0115B6000` | affected | the same |\n| Hades `0100535012974000` | not affected | |\n\nThese three were not run (no data). A game reaches the new code only when it uses MetalFX: NVN2's DLSS (PRAGMATA, Fire Emblem Fortune's Weave), `DM_UPSCALER=metalfx` (Donkey Kong Bananza, Splatoon Raiders) or `DM_PRESENT_UPSCALE=metalfx`. PRAGMATA was run (below).\n\n## PRAGMATA\n\n`0400C76024710000`, integration host carrying the same commit (`prag_r11memlive5_async_mfx_host`), `MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1`:\n- **Before:** aborts at the first DLSS evaluation, about 20 s in (2 of 2 boots).\n- **After:** no MetalFX assertion. With `MTL_DEBUG_LAYER_ERROR_MODE=nslog` the boot reaches gameplay and logs 4096 MetalFX evaluations, with no `_outputTextureBarrierStages` line.\n- **Another error, not this change's:** in abort mode the game now stops later, at about 25 s, on a different error that exists before this change (`setRenderPipelineState`: a sample-count-1 pipeline in a 4x pass; 11k per run in nslog mode). It is left to its own PR.\n- Without validation: 4 boots, 0 faults, flicker 0.\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2147/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2147/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2221","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2221/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2221/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2221/events","html_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2221","id":6311886112,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAABOKi8Hg","number":2221,"title":"Pipeline archive: a run that ends during its prewarm keeps the pipelines it compiled (prewarm timer flush with backoff, a larger SIGTERM budget)","user":{"login":"uncraftablexd","id":352372032,"node_id":"U_kgDOFQDFQA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/352372032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd","html_url":"https://github.com/uncraftablexd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uncraftablexd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12938277381,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy5yBQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/docs","name":"docs","color":"0075ca","default":false,"description":"Documentation","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12938278094,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy50zg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/nvn","name":"nvn","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"NVN on Metal and its tests (dm/gfx/nvn, dm/gfx/tests)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12938280714,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy5_Cg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/host","name":"host","color":"1d76db","default":false,"description":"The Horizon host: SVCs, services, threads, memory (dm/host)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T17:10:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:11:06Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/pulls/2221","html_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2221","diff_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2221.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2221.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"\n## Problem\n\nA start compiles the same bases again every time, and area loads stall on them. The last lines of each run say one of:\n\n- `pipeline archive at exit: 425 pipelines not written yet, not all written in time: those left are built again at the next start (968 ms)`\n- `[RED] graceful exit not done in 1.5 seconds, exiting at once`, with no archive line at all.\n\nSince #1879, the timer's flushes wait for the prewarm's end, so a period is written only when it is full (`ARCH_PERIOD_MAX`, 2,000) or at exit. Ocarina of Time's prewarm (31,663 lines after the first frame, on 5 workers) outlives a play session, so everything the session compiled waits for the exit. There are two failure modes:\n\n1. **Exit budget too small.** The graceful exit (`SIGTERM`, `hle_lifecycle.c`) gives the archive what is left of 1.5 s. A write takes seconds: 1.8–4 s per 900 bases on Macs, and up to 74 s for a period of 436 bases + 1,241 compute pipelines on Ocarina of Time.\n2. **No write at all.** When a draw is still compiling its pipeline, `dm_gfx_suspend` waits on that draw, and the 1.5 s fallback calls `_exit` before any write. A harness or watchdog that stops a run for \"no new frame\" sends `SIGTERM` at exactly that moment.\n\n## Change\n\n- **Prewarm timer flush.** In `arch_hand_over`, during a prewarm that is not compacting, a timer flush hands the period over once it is `DM_PSO_ARCH_WARM_FLUSH_MS` old (default 60000; `0` restores today's behaviour).\n  - Each later flush waits twice as long, at most 16 times as long (60 s, 120 s, … 16 min). A cold start therefore adds about one file per doubling, not one per 10 s (the 80 files of #1747).\n  - While captures wait, the timer looks again every 10 s.\n  - During a compaction nothing changes: the recaptured bases still go into as few files as they can.\n- **Graceful exit** (`hle_lifecycle.c`):\n  - The archive starts writing first (`dm_gfx_quit_begin`), before the drain.\n  - The archive gets `DM_EXIT_ARCH_MS` beyond the 1.5 s: 8000 on the Mac, 3000 on iOS (iOS ends an app about 5 s after its termination callback).\n  - If graphics are not suspended within 1.5 s, the fallback now waits for the archive's write within the same deadline, then exits.\n  - A hard deadline at 1.5 s plus the budget plus 0.5 s ends the process whatever happens.\n- **Log.** `mtl_arch_save` logs the write's start and how many pipelines are left.\n- **Leftovers of a cut-short write.** A file is still written as `.tmp` and renamed after its index, and a start still removes an index whose file never came. A start now also removes a `.mtl4a.tmp`. Before, a write that a kill cut short left its `.tmp` in the folder for good, and the longer exit budget makes a cut-short write more likely. The existing files stay valid either way.\n- **One exit.** The drain finishing just as the 1.5 s fallback fires could run the exit's last step twice. It now runs once (`exit_finish`). The hard deadline still ends the process if the first is stuck.\n- **Switches.** `DM_PSO_ARCH_WARM_FLUSH_MS` and `DM_EXIT_ARCH_MS` have rows in `docs/env_switches.tsv`.\n\n## Tests\n\n`test_pso_archive.py` gets four new cases, each run in fresh processes:\n\n| Case | With the change | Without it (int-r13 731efbb47 binary) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Five new bases in a prewarm, the timer's flush with `DM_PSO_ARCH_WARM_FLUSH_MS=300`, then `_exit` | one file; the next start takes all 5 and compiles none | no file, all 5 compiled again |\n| `SIGTERM` in a prewarm | one file, all 5 taken at the next start | passes: with 5 bases, the old 1.3 s is enough (the case is coverage, not fail-without) |\n| `SIGTERM` while a draw holds the graphics layer (`dm_gfx_enter` with no leave) | one file, all 5 taken at the next start | the 1.5 s fallback exits with no file |\n| A torn write's `.tmp` and an index without its file, beside a file that is not an archive | the leftovers are removed, the bad file is skipped, all 5 bases come from the good file | the `.tmp` stays (main removed only the index); the rest passes |\n\nResults (M4 Pro, macOS 26.6, `MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1`, 2026-11-10, on main): `t_pso_archive` 338 checks, 0 failed; `test_pso_archive.py` 10 tests OK in 11.6 s. Without the change (measured on our fork's binary), the timer-flush and stuck-draw cases fail with `0 != 1 : seed` (no file written).\n\n`t_pso_archive` links `hle_lifecycle.c` for the `SIGTERM` cases. The existing cold-start, cut-short and quit cases are unchanged; the default 60 s flush is never reached in them.\n\nReference entry: [A run that ends in its prewarm loses what it compiled](docs/reference/rendering.md#a-run-that-ends-in-its-prewarm-loses-what-it-compiled), plus the archive paragraph in `docs/development.md`.\n\n## Measured\n\nOn Ocarina of Time, M4 Pro, macOS 26.6, on our fork (translator chain `2f445c6b122f`, not main), warm-up runs of five areas (walkcam route, each ended by `SIGTERM`), each starting from the archive the one before left:\n\n| | before (r13w2/r13w3, oot_r13_host) | after (r13w4, with this change) |\n|---|---|---|\n| writes during play | none (the prewarm runs the whole session) | one per run at about 60 s: e.g. `00152-713.mtl4a` (138 bases, 448 compute, 127 task / mesh), `00153-1677`, `00155-447`, `00157-358`, `00159-52` |\n| at exit | `425 pipelines not written yet, not all written in time (968 ms)`; Kakariko: `graceful exit not done in 1.5 seconds`, no write | written in 0.5–6.0 s: 522 (Hyrule Field, 6.0 s), 209 (Kakariko, 3.9 s), 71, 28 |\n| prepare before the first frame (10,534 lines) | 3.8–4.0 s (r13w2, four areas) | 1.4–4.4 s (Zora 1.39, Kokiri 1.48, Kakariko 1.65, fog 2.26, Hyrule Field 4.42) |\n\nNot yet covered: the first (fog) run of the series still ended with 1,378 pipelines not written in its 9.3 s, because its 60 s write (713 pipelines, 20 s) was followed by a second period that the backoff (next flush at 120 s) did not reach before the run ended, and compute-heavy periods take tens of seconds to write. A few pipelines (0–8) captured after the exit's hand-over stay unwritten.\n\nBefore the change, the warm-up runs of 2026-11-10 (same chain) all ended with 400–500 bases not written. The next runs compiled 57–167 bases, missed the archive 57–256 times, and stalled for more than 20 s at the Hyrule Field, Zora's Domain and Kakariko loads.\n\n## Regression\n\n`scripts/regress.py impact` names three games:\n\n- The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild, Pokémon Scarlet and The Legend of Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom are affected. They use the pipeline archive, and BotW and TotK also use the prepare step.\n- Hades is not affected.\n- 153 profiles have no usage manifest.\n\nNone of those three games was run for this PR. What changes for them:\n\n- **More run files.** A prewarm longer than 60 s writes up to about log2(prewarm / 60 s) more run files, since the default backoff caps it at about one per doubling. More files bring the next tier compaction (`PSO_ARCH_COMPACT`) closer by that many.\n- **Longer exit.** A `SIGTERM` exit with unwritten captures can now take up to 9.5 s instead of 1.5 s. An `oe::ExecuteProgram` hand-off goes through the same exit, so it waits the same way.\n\n`DM_PSO_ARCH_WARM_FLUSH_MS=0` and `DM_EXIT_ARCH_MS=0` restore the old timings (the archive then gets what is left of 1.3 s, as before).\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2221/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2221/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bingjiang0611/scry/issues/52","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bingjiang0611/scry","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bingjiang0611/scry/issues/52/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bingjiang0611/scry/issues/52/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bingjiang0611/scry/issues/52/events","html_url":"https://github.com/bingjiang0611/scry/pull/52","id":6288202954,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfUhNc8AAAABN3lXJA","number":52,"title":"fix(remote): reliable, faster iOS remote connection","user":{"login":"bingjiang0611","id":307659028,"node_id":"U_kgDOElaBFA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/307659028?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingjiang0611","html_url":"https://github.com/bingjiang0611","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingjiang0611/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingjiang0611/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingjiang0611/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingjiang0611/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingjiang0611/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingjiang0611/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingjiang0611/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingjiang0611/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingjiang0611/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12898603253,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTfUhNc8AAAADANEQ9Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bingjiang0611/scry/labels/size:XXL","name":"size:XXL","color":"b60205","default":false,"description":"1,000+ effective changed lines (test files excluded in mixed PRs).","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12898604042,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTfUhNc8AAAADANEUCg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bingjiang0611/scry/labels/vouch:trusted","name":"vouch:trusted","color":"1f883d","default":false,"description":"PR author is trusted by repo permissions or the VOUCHED list.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":9,"created_at":"2026-11-09T14:39:47Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:10:20Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bingjiang0611/scry/pulls/52","html_url":"https://github.com/bingjiang0611/scry/pull/52","diff_url":"https://github.com/bingjiang0611/scry/pull/52.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/bingjiang0611/scry/pull/52.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## 问题\n\niOS 远程连接经常失败、加载慢、不稳定。代码分析定位到以下原因：\n\n- Relay 不知道 Mac 的 leg 是否还活着，而且优先选最旧的。Mac 睡眠或断网后，手机会被接到死 leg 上，连等 3×8 秒握手超时。\n- 手机有 4 条独立隧道，每条约 2 秒冷握手；空闲 20 秒就关闭，形成\"冷启动悬崖\"。\n- 网络切换时全部断开重连；没有心跳；流式输出靠长轮询，每批多付一个往返。\n- 首页会话列表每次全量分页遍历；历史记录不压缩；同一 Wi-Fi 下也要绕 Cloudflare。\n\n## 改动与范围\n\n详见 `docs/remote-network-measurement.md`。\n\n- **Relay（Worker/DO）**：根据心跳选证据最新的 leg；没有存活 leg 时以 `4001 host_offline` 快速拒绝（只有 10 s 内有 host leg 活动时才先等 600 ms 宽限）；忙时最多等 2 秒补位；`RELAY_LOCATION_HINT`；新增可自托管的 `ws-relay-server.mjs` 与无凭据的 `relay-path-probe.mjs`。\n- **Mac host**：每条 leg 心跳，唤醒后重建（锁屏解锁只替换空闲 leg）；新增 `ping` 和能力声明；按请求 id 复用连接；`watchStream` 推送；局域网直连监听（47820 端口，`SCRY_REMOTE_LAN=0` 关闭；不广播 VPN/隧道/虚拟网卡与 /32 地址）；会话列表 `known` 未变化时短路；历史 deflate 压缩。\n- **iOS 传输层**：按能力协商切换到复用模式，4 条隧道变 2 条；前台保活；切网先探测再决定是否重建；`4001` 不重试，任一 lane 收到即返回；`mux_busy` 退避重试而不是停止观察；推送流超时会通知主机停止；只在当前网络确认过的直连地址才进打开路径，其余后台升级；Network.framework（swift-nio-transport-services 1.28.0）；记录每条隧道的分阶段耗时。\n- **iOS App**：前后台驱动保活；推送优先、不支持时退回长轮询；会话列表缓存复用；历史解压并按原文哈希校验；离线文案；DEBUG `-netBench` 测量入口（不挂载主界面，含离线探测）。\n- **本机验证工具**：`experiments/remote-g0/verify/`（`local-verify.sh` 分阶段执行、`summarize.mjs` 自动判定规则 R1–R7、`redact.mjs` 在提交前脱敏），三轮真机结果在 `docs/handoff/ios-remote-verification/results/`。\n- **个人标识脱敏**：从 `main` 继承的 25 个文档/测试文件里的账户名、Apple ID、签名团队 ID 和设备 UDID 改为占位值（只改这些字面值）。\n\n旧手机、旧 Mac、旧 relay 都能混用，各自退回原有行为（兼容矩阵见文档 §2）。\n\n## 方向批准与风险边界\n\n- 这是一个大改动。用户在会话中要求\"按推荐路线全部执行\"。\n- **网络暴露（维护者已决定）**：新增局域网 TCP 监听，作为另一个 inner mTLS 入口。认证不变（CA 签发的设备证书 + 每个请求按指纹重新授权），地址只在已授权的 `ping` 回复中给出。**维护者 2026-11-10 确认保持默认开启**，可用 `SCRY_REMOTE_LAN=0` 关闭。\n- **Relay 已部署**：经用户授权，本机 agent 已执行 `wrangler deploy`（当前 Version `beb062bc-29c2-42e5-98e5-49aef039550f`）。\n- **历史脱敏（维护者已决定）**：本分支独有的提交已改写并强制推送，去掉设备 UDID、relay 房间与会话 ID、账户名、签名身份（团队 ID、证书哈希）和公网 IP；两个测试改用同格式的假值。改写前的内容只保留在本地备份分支中，未推送。`main` 上早已存在的文件在本 PR 里改为脱敏版本；**`main` 的历史提交按维护者决定不改写**，旧值仍在 `main` 历史中。\n- **20KB 暂存文件门禁**：`RemoteRunStore.swift` 改动前就有 281KB；脱敏涉及的 6 个文档/测试文件（`docs/desktop-remote.md`、`docs/ios-execution-targets.md`、`docs/research/provider-handoff-technical-plan.md`、`perf-2026-10-22/reports/F.md`、`F2.md`、`src/main/providers/codex.test.ts`）改动前也已超过 20KB。涉及它们的提交无法通过门禁，是否拆分需要维护者决定；其余文件都已按职责拆分到预算以内。\n\n## 验证\n\n**CI**：Remote G0 transport（macOS `swift test`，含 `MuxTransportTests`、`PrewarmSettleTests`）、Remote G0 ios（ScryRemote 产品 App 编译）、Node unit/coverage、packaged-linux、cli-compat、Performance（所有场景在门限内）均通过。`packaged-electron` 的渲染层 UI 冒烟检查在本 PR 和 `main` 上都有偶发失败（详见 PR 评论），本 PR 不改渲染层代码。\n\n**真机（L2：iPhone 13 / iOS 26.5.2，Mac macOS 27.3，Mac 不在手机所在 Wi-Fi，全部走 relay，出口 PIT/EWR/ORD）**，三轮本机 agent 验证，最终一轮 `results/20261110T084031Z`：\n\n| 规则 | 结果 |\n|---|---|\n| R1 检查阶段 | 本分支未引入失败（`ios-checks` 4 条夹具失败在基线 `5760dd7` 上同样失败，不算通过） |\n| R2 无失败 / R3 复用 + 5 项能力 / R4 强制 relay | pass |\n| R5b 打开路径上无失败直连 | pass（第一轮每条隧道 2×900 ms 超时，已修复） |\n| R6 会话列表刷新被 host 确认未变化 | pass（3/3） |\n| R7 Mac 离线时 3 s 内得到\"不在线\" | pass（1.37 / 1.86 s；修复前约 24 s 超时） |\n| R5 局域网直连 | **blocked**：需要 Mac 与手机在同一 Wi-Fi，未验证 |\n\n冷开中位 / P90：`wifi-relay` 1717 / 3060 ms，`wifi-auto` 1958 / 3748 ms；热请求中位约 0.9–1.1 s（链路往返约 0.6 s）。\n\n三轮验证中本机 agent 修复的问题（各带回滚即失败的测试）：内层 TLS 截断掩盖 relay 的 4001、\"旧版 host\"判断被持久化导致永久串行回退、离线探测会话污染诊断等。\n\n**未验证 / 已知遗留**：局域网直连（R5）、蜂窝、Mac 合盖唤醒、大会话历史、Linux 宿主上的真实连接。验证中出现过两次\"冷开 5/5 约 31 s 失败\"后自行恢复：错误类型和时长与手机外层建连（TCP/外层 TLS/升级）的 10 s 看门狗 ×3 次重试一致，这是推断，卡在哪一段尚无证据；验证脚本已改为保留失败运行的分阶段计时，下次复现即可定位。\n\n## Agent 使用\n\nClaude Code（claude.ai/code 云端会话）编写改动；本机验证由维护者宿主上的另一个 Agent 按 `docs/handoff/ios-remote-verification/TASK.md` 执行。\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01UQCikyu9v4qCuaHoTWp1zG","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bingjiang0611/scry/issues/52/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bingjiang0611/scry/issues/52/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1236702,"client_id":"Iv23liqTIFEtdIu6Vn1r","slug":"claude","node_id":"A_kwHOBIuudM4AEt7e","owner":{"login":"anthropics","id":76263028,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjc2MjYzMDI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76263028?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics","html_url":"https://github.com/anthropics","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Claude","description":"Run Claude Code from your GitHub Pull Requests and Issues to respond to reviewer feedback, fix CI errors, or modify code, turning it into a virtual teammate that works alongside your development pipelines.\r\n\r\nThis is built on the publicly available Claude Code SDK.","external_url":"https://anthropic.com/claude-code","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","created_at":"2025-04-30T17:54:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T04:29:41Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","members":"read","merge_queues":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","repository_creation":"write","repository_hooks":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","discussion","discussion_comment","issues","issue_comment","merge_group","merge_queue_entry","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","push","release","repository_ruleset","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanikz/docker-infrastructure/issues/762","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanikz/docker-infrastructure","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanikz/docker-infrastructure/issues/762/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanikz/docker-infrastructure/issues/762/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanikz/docker-infrastructure/issues/762/events","html_url":"https://github.com/stanikz/docker-infrastructure/pull/762","id":6277264108,"node_id":"PR_kwDORmxVGs8AAAABNu1JPg","number":762,"title":"chore(deps): update databasus/databasus docker tag","user":{"login":"stanikz","id":58887532,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4ODg3NTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58887532?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz","html_url":"https://github.com/stanikz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10444547823,"node_id":"LA_kwDORmxVGs8AAAACbosm7w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanikz/docker-infrastructure/labels/renovate","name":"renovate","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"stanikz","id":58887532,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4ODg3NTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58887532?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz","html_url":"https://github.com/stanikz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-08T23:57:54Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:09:58Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"stanikz","id":58887532,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4ODg3NTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58887532?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz","html_url":"https://github.com/stanikz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanikz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanikz/docker-infrastructure/pulls/762","html_url":"https://github.com/stanikz/docker-infrastructure/pull/762","diff_url":"https://github.com/stanikz/docker-infrastructure/pull/762.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/stanikz/docker-infrastructure/pull/762.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Update | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| [databasus/databasus](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus) | minor | `v3.66.0` → `v3.68.0` |\n| fosrl/gerbil | minor | `1.5.1` → `1.6.0` |\n| [fosrl/pangolin](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin) | minor | `1.22.0` → `1.26.0` |\n| [getmeili/meilisearch](https://redirect.github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch) | patch | `v1.56.1` → `v1.56.2` |\n| [ghcr.io/lukegus/termix](https://redirect.github.com/Termix-SSH/Termix) | patch | `26.11.0` → `26.11.1` |\n\n---\n\n### Release Notes\n\n<details>\n<summary>databasus/databasus</summary>\n\n### [`v3.68.0`](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/releases/tag/v3.68.0)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/compare/v3.67.2...v3.68.0)\n\n### Changelog\n\n#### \\[3.68.0] - 2026-11-10\n\n##### ✨ Features\n\n- **physical-backups**: Verify schema and sequence recovery ([60a9481](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/60a9481d216a6c0c73f9e41a158d286d902cd60e))\n- **development**: Document AI reviews and streamline local setup ([9251cf8](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/9251cf8f0965dda967787d18ae6b4c182ecd00d4))\n- **deps**: Upgrade compatible major dependency versions ([ab729bc](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/ab729bcf97e8e004bb99e422da0645d685fe503f))\n- **deps**: Add dependency upgrade verification ([ef5e365](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/ef5e365394b4c597643f5814396d79c9f14a8e23))\n\n##### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n\n- **ci**: Resolve release security checks ([e35f4e0](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/e35f4e0783093744adfb4acfac0559f2a180d083))\n- **ci**: Resolve pnpm through the configured mise backend ([a4c76b6](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/a4c76b6655622b227ee59ed14d43f2ff791fbb72))\n- **deps**: Use supported Dependabot cooldown settings ([3ae90a3](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/3ae90a3a9c8ebe17d163013f14484df31563da5b))\n- **website**: Simplify homepage H1 across all locales ([d62f418](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/d62f4182aaa98ed79f32304230e1b3cf0cd8972f))\n\n##### 🔨 Refactoring\n\n- **deps**: Remove Dependabot configuration and documentation ([b184e6b](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/b184e6b7f6cb63eff2aea67e9f902516e80e4baa))\n\n##### 🐳 Docker\n\n- **Image**: `databasus/databasus:v3.68.0`\n- **Mirror**: `ghcr.io/databasus/databasus:v3.68.0`\n- **Platforms**: linux/amd64, linux/arm64\n\n### [`v3.67.2`](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/releases/tag/v3.67.2)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/compare/v3.67.1...v3.67.2)\n\n### Changelog\n\n#### \\[3.67.2] - 2026-11-09\n\n##### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n\n- **tests**: Verify storage writes through events instead of timing ([a42c2de](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/a42c2de691e10522c50edc0e5330b8d890dc4b22))\n\n##### 🔨 Refactoring\n\n- **storages**: Remove rclone support ([6b80632](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/6b80632ce500b0b95f772b99e59fc141b81f41c7))\n\n##### 🐳 Docker\n\n- **Image**: `databasus/databasus:v3.67.2`\n- **Mirror**: `ghcr.io/databasus/databasus:v3.67.2`\n- **Platforms**: linux/amd64, linux/arm64\n\n### [`v3.67.1`](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/releases/tag/v3.67.1)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/compare/v3.67.0...v3.67.1)\n\n### Changelog\n\n#### \\[3.67.1] - 2026-11-09\n\n##### 🔨 Refactoring\n\n- **storages**: Remove built-in Google Drive support ([58396bc](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/58396bcf2b37fb6cdc7f8123cf4f1a913eef3974))\n\n##### 🐳 Docker\n\n- **Image**: `databasus/databasus:v3.67.1`\n- **Mirror**: `ghcr.io/databasus/databasus:v3.67.1`\n- **Platforms**: linux/amd64, linux/arm64\n\n### [`v3.67.0`](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/releases/tag/v3.67.0)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/compare/v3.66.0...v3.67.0)\n\n### Changelog\n\n#### \\[3.67.0] - 2026-11-08\n\n##### ✨ Features\n\n- **frontend**: Add URL navigation for workspaces and database tabs ([da917f2](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/da917f20f181702bd1194b57484230355fb43d5d))\n- **docs**: Update docs ([30b15a6](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/30b15a6f5a4119c40e0d16ef74a84b6f9c274436))\n- **backups**: Show compact backup usage totals ([1baa792](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/1baa792b0857a88d8036570624ebdbcc506a6c92))\n- **archlint**: Enforce module contract usage ([47cc93a](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/47cc93a18541c580f24ac43c1170a549b9d4e245))\n\n##### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n\n- **e2e**: Check first administrator access through its settings URL ([81a8c0c](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/81a8c0c3ad8d0e536e1aedfe5ba4876438217996))\n- **frontend**: Restore CI coverage after form updates ([23d306e](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/23d306ec8f7885bd7eb748a352b115b18123c1d1))\n- **frontend**: Align settings forms and refine backup interfaces ([b8db16c](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/b8db16ce9d2f12c8a077afe092e5897a21eee23a))\n- **dev-seed**: Ensure the dev account is the bootstrap administrator ([fb343b7](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/fb343b73f7c9632dc1655fe436a8e1a4d2f71ef9))\n- **frontend**: Refine tabs, focus colors and form controls ([a8d575a](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/a8d575a7e24f472594e60fe355c91d7ee89a05ed))\n- **auth**: Explain specific sign-in failures ([5e471f4](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/5e471f43c9e46f7268428a2608c25cfec4501593))\n- **frontend**: Tighten form spacing and soften focus outlines ([dc0b281](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/dc0b28143001e3ff7476f3ab18438f06d8b0da55))\n- **ci**: Verify browser shards and archive parallelization ([3a7a73e](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/3a7a73eee2d5ce838f577487390b48ca196b20d5))\n- **ci**: Parallelize release test groups ([3172086](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/31720867d68f31edbcf39ec05cbe17c540d0e1ca))\n- **dev**: Allow seeding with stale verification agents ([97dabda](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/97dabdaa2148b53c40cb86ddea96115040f8434d))\n- **e2e**: Wait for workspace selection to persist ([b67abae](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/b67abaee952df6d21afdf2855f61de9bd0ba446e))\n- **ci**: Stabilize connection screenshots and test selectors ([f178811](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/f17881161198e0b5cf7beb9cbcb49619ae118d09))\n- **zed**: Disable Tailwind canonical class warnings ([6c77c70](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/6c77c70d6576e627b1d7b618ef86ba1b0cc58d6c))\n- **backups**: Preserve completed GFS periods during cleanup ([61feea0](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/61feea0bd2411f9c8cf32f7f7e2e8d1492191ef1))\n- **backend**: Preserve request and transaction contexts ([6ca2ce6](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/6ca2ce64f896c5e715cb38bdcb2ab64e9305f13f))\n\n##### 🔨 Refactoring\n\n- **frontend**: Group database page code by responsibility ([0df37c2](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/0df37c2e8d8c03f27392e20de0c44bc4148c93dc))\n- **frontend**: Centralize request lifecycles with TanStack Query ([adf923a](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/adf923ac9b05bae5ac21dc6af84bd8bd23aaf7db))\n- **frontend**: Replace Ant Design with Mantine ([49439f7](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/49439f79859ea1ae9592abe73a63c4882ce41c7d))\n- **agent**: Split verification job execution into domain steps ([903bb36](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/903bb3694cf04de48676076075d5ed822cee7d8c))\n- **frontend**: Share storage and notifier collection workflows ([1a4a77b](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/1a4a77bf1da7f6a38067c51daaad22f9451cb600))\n- **ci**: Reuse artifact transfers and backend preparation ([5274613](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/5274613b3ba317e9f16fd464f2c51dddcbd813e0))\n- **api**: Generate handlers with request contexts ([def83f4](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/def83f48b7f4569346d2d095b31be3e2eb1a9940))\n- **modules**: Remove unused contract declarations ([4d8435c](https://redirect.github.com/databasus/databasus/commit/4d8435c680e54bc19d60b9a7c99ef7372e14f879))\n\n##### 🐳 Docker\n\n- **Image**: `databasus/databasus:v3.67.0`\n- **Mirror**: `ghcr.io/databasus/databasus:v3.67.0`\n- **Platforms**: linux/amd64, linux/arm64\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>fosrl/pangolin</summary>\n\n### [`v1.26.0`](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/releases/tag/1.26.0)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.25.3...1.26.0)\n\n#### Read the Announcement\n\nRead the full announcement with discussion of new features: [Pangolin 1.26: Session Management, SSH Logs, and Auto Windows Updates](https://pangolin.net/news/1-26-release)\n\n### What’s Changed\n\n- Add option to add additional DNS records on delegated domains with Pangolin DNS (EE)\n- Add optional match on base wildcard domains\n- Add continuous session revalidation for OIDC IdPs using refresh tokens (EE)\n- Add SSH session logging when using Pangolin SSH (EE)\n- Add resource session management with ability to see and revoke active sessions (EE)\n- Add custom domain for org auth pages to self-hosted (EE)\n- Add opt-in CrowdSec bot detection\n- Fix failing Safari passkey registration\n- Fix the enabled/disabled filter on the private resources table\n- Fix IdP auto-provision not toggleable on a per org basis when using org-scoped IdP mode\n- Fix order same-second status events in status history\n- Fix duplicate header auth from blueprints\n- Fix Swagger API docs missing from container build\n- Fix missing API key permissions for integration API routes\n- Fix Bedrock cache token calculation\n- Dependency security updates\n- General UI improvements\n- Various other bug fixes\n\n#### New Contributors\n\n- [@&#8203;jnko266](https://redirect.github.com/jnko266) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3938](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3938)\n- [@&#8203;ASPCODES](https://redirect.github.com/ASPCODES) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3988](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3988)\n- [@&#8203;samirasidd](https://redirect.github.com/samirasidd) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3971](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3971)\n- [@&#8203;RishavTiwari25](https://redirect.github.com/RishavTiwari25) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3999](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3999)\n- [@&#8203;S-NoF3aR](https://redirect.github.com/S-NoF3aR) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;4027](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/4027)\n\n**Full Changelog**: <https://github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.25.3...1.26.0>\n\n#### How to Update\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> As of November 3, the Traefik team has fixed the bug that prevented Badger v1.8.0 from being pulled. You can now safely upgrade to Badger v1.8.0 to enable permanent redirects, introduced in Pangolin v1.25. The v1.26 migration will attempt to update Badger for you automatically. If it cannot find your Traefik config in the standard location, [manually update Badger](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update#:~:text=Increase%20the%20Badger%20version%20number).\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> SSH session logs with Pangolin SSH mode require an updated site agent. Upgrade to Pangolin CLI v0.2.0+ or Newt v1.20.0+ before enabling SSH logging.\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Always back up your config app-data before updating. This will allow you to easily roll back if the update breaks your configuration. You will not be able to easily downgrade otherwise.\n\n[View documentation](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update)\n\n### [`v1.25.3`](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/releases/tag/1.25.3)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.25.2...1.25.3)\n\n#### Read the Announcement\n\nRead the full announcement with discussion of new features: [Pangolin 1.25: Redirects, mTLS, and Machine Roles](https://pangolin.net/news/1-25-release)\n\n#### What's Changed\n\n- Update node to resolve Node2Shell CVE-2026-111497\n- Improve client connection speed with many sites\n- Fix agent and olm version separate in the database\n\n**Full Changelog**: <https://github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.25.2...1.25.3>\n\n#### How to Update\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> For all load balancing options to work, Treafik version 3.6 or greater must be used in your stack. Update accordingly.\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Redirects will work on older versions of Badger. In order to enable permanent redirects, update Badger to `v1.8.0` or greater. The migration will automatically do this if it can find the Traefik config in the standard location. Otherwise, [please ensure your Badger is up to date manually](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update#:~:text=Increase%20the%20Badger%20version%20number).\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Always back up your config app-data before updating. This will allow you to easily roll back if the update breaks your configuration. You will not be able to easily downgrade otherwise.\n\n[View documentation](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update)\n\n### [`v1.25.2`](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/releases/tag/1.25.2)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.25.1...1.25.2)\n\n#### Read the Announcement\n\nRead the full announcement with discussion of new features: [Pangolin 1.25: Redirects, mTLS, and Machine Roles](https://pangolin.net/news/1-25-release)\n\n#### What's Changed\n\n- Fix include optional name in blueprint health check\n- Fix mTLS hidden by enterprise feature flag on CE\n\n**Full Changelog**: <https://github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.25.1...1.25.2>\n\n#### How to Update\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> For all load balancing options to work, Treafik version 3.6 or greater must be used in your stack. Update accordingly.\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Redirects will work on older versions of Badger. In order to enable permanent redirects, update Badger to `v1.8.0` or greater. The migration will automatically do this if it can find the Traefik config in the standard location. Otherwise, [please ensure your Badger is up to date manually](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update#:~:text=Increase%20the%20Badger%20version%20number).\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Always back up your config app-data before updating. This will allow you to easily roll back if the update breaks your configuration. You will not be able to easily downgrade otherwise.\n\n[View documentation](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update)\n\n### [`v1.25.1`](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/releases/tag/1.25.1)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.25.0...1.25.1)\n\n#### Read the Announcement\n\nRead the full announcement with discussion of new features: [Pangolin 1.25: Redirects, mTLS, and Machine Roles](https://pangolin.net/news/1-25-release)\n\n#### What's Changed\n\n- Fix updated clients failing to relay\n- Fix credential generation not showing with EE features disabled\n\n**Full Changelog**: <https://github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.25.0...1.25.1>\n\n#### How to Update\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> For all load balancing options to work, Treafik version 3.6 or greater must be used in your stack. Update accordingly.\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Redirects will work on older versions of Badger. In order to enable permanent redirects, update Badger to `v1.8.0` or greater. The migration will automatically do this if it can find the Traefik config in the standard location. Otherwise, [please ensure your Badger is up to date manually](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update#:~:text=Increase%20the%20Badger%20version%20number).\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Always back up your config app-data before updating. This will allow you to easily roll back if the update breaks your configuration. You will not be able to easily downgrade otherwise.\n\n[View documentation](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update)\n\n### [`v1.25.0`](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/releases/tag/1.25.0)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.24.0...1.25.0)\n\n#### Read the Announcement\n\nRead the full announcement with discussion of new features: [Pangolin 1.25: Redirects, mTLS, and Machine Roles](https://pangolin.net/news/1-25-release)\n\n### What’s Changed\n\n- Add redirects\n- Add mTLS authentication method for public resources\n- Add support for assigning roles to machine clients (EE)\n- Add export resource to blueprint\n- Add support for configuring load balancing strategy\n- Add labels to the integration API\n- Add client identities for `Remote-*` headers on private HTTP\n- Add offline checking intervals configuration\n- Add site, machine client, and remote node credential regeneration to CE\n- Improve image size by pruning\n- Fix cluster license registration\n- Fix integration API organization delete\n- Fix allow underscores in health check hostnames\n- Fix pass relay port to Gerbil\n- Fix avoid exponential backtracking in `isPathAllowed`\n- Fix ensure more than one parts exists in signup page\n- Fix send missing error when clients registering\n- Fix clean up every site when deleting an org\n- Fix prevent overlapping exit node address selections\n- UI improvements\n\n**Full Changelog**: <https://github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.24.0...1.25.0>\n\n#### New Contributors\n\n- [@&#8203;kdcokenny](https://redirect.github.com/kdcokenny) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3838](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3838)\n- [@&#8203;mr-pmillz](https://redirect.github.com/mr-pmillz) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3830](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3830)\n- [@&#8203;TiltedTeapot](https://redirect.github.com/TiltedTeapot) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3870](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3870)\n- [@&#8203;choksi2212](https://redirect.github.com/choksi2212) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3895](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3895)\n\n#### How to Update\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> For all load balancing options to work, Treafik version 3.6 or greater must be used in your stack. Update accordingly.\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Redirects will work on older versions of Badger. In order to enable permanent redirects, update Badger to `v1.8.0` or greater. The migration will automatically do this if it can find the Traefik config in the standard location. Otherwise, [please ensure your Badger is up to date manually](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update#:~:text=Increase%20the%20Badger%20version%20number).\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Always back up your config app-data before updating. This will allow you to easily roll back if the update breaks your configuration. You will not be able to easily downgrade otherwise.\n\n[View documentation](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update)\n\n### [`v1.24.0`](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/releases/tag/1.24.0)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.23.0...1.24.0)\n\n#### Read the Announcement\n\nRead the full announcement with discussion of new features: [Pangolin 1.24: Exit Nodes and Improved Clients](https://pangolin.net/news/1-24-release)\n\n### What's New\n\n- Add exit node private resources\n- Add HTTP method matching to resource rules\n- Add Badger config overrides to config file\n- Add on-demand activation for iOS and macOS clients\n- Add always-on connections for Android clients\n- Add connect-at-login for Windows clients\n- Add response header customization\n- Add subnet routing to Linux CLI client for site to site networking\n- Significant UI improvements for all Pangolin clients (see release notes for each respective client for comprehensive list of changes)\n- Update iPhone and Mac client identifiers\n- Dependency security updates\n- General UI improvements\n- Various other bug fixes\n\n#### New Contributors\n\n- [@&#8203;Bolex80](https://redirect.github.com/Bolex80) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3790](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3790)\n- [@&#8203;m1handr](https://redirect.github.com/m1handr) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3616](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3616)\n- [@&#8203;kah-ja](https://redirect.github.com/kah-ja) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3750](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3750)\n- [@&#8203;Tyagiquamar](https://redirect.github.com/Tyagiquamar) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3785](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3785)\n- [@&#8203;breken-ai](https://redirect.github.com/breken-ai) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3738](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3738)\n- [@&#8203;moyaqoob](https://redirect.github.com/moyaqoob) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3585](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3585)\n- [@&#8203;Gulianrdgd](https://redirect.github.com/Gulianrdgd) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3172](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3172)\n- [@&#8203;MauryaQbit](https://redirect.github.com/MauryaQbit) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3797](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3797)\n- [@&#8203;Fra146](https://redirect.github.com/Fra146) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3811](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3811)\n\n**Full Changelog**: <https://github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.23.0...1.24.0>\n\n#### How to Update\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Private exit node resources require **Pangolin CLI v0.18.0+** or **Newt v1.18.0+**. Upgrade your site connector before deploying.\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Private exit node resources are exclusively compatible with the latest versions of all Pangolin clients. Support for exit node functionality was implemented in all client releases issued after September 29th, 2026. If your client's most recent release predates this date, exit nodes are not yet available.\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Always back up your config app-data before updating. This will allow you to easily roll back if the update breaks your configuration. You will not be able to easily downgrade otherwise.\n\n[View documentation](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update)\n\n### [`v1.23.0`](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/releases/tag/1.23.0)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.22.2...1.23.0)\n\n#### Read the Announcement\n\nRead the full announcement with discussion of new features: [Pangolin 1.23: High Availability and Clustering](https://pangolin.net/news/1-23-release)\n\n#### What's Changed\n\n- Add support for self-service high availability in Enterprise Edition\n- Add master list of all orgs to server admin panel\n- Add support for more than one server admin user; promote and demote via users table in server admin panel\n- Add sites widget to resource side panel in resource launcher\n- Add SSH commands to SSH private resources in resource side panel in resource launcher\n- Add Pangolin CLI commands to site install wizard as the preferred method and rename Newt to Pangolin Site\n- Dependency security updates\n- General UI improvements\n- Various other bug fixes\n\n**Full Changelog**: <https://github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.22.2...1.23.0>\n\n#### How to Update\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Always back up your config app-data before updating. This will allow you to easily roll back if the update breaks your configuration. You will not be able to easily downgrade otherwise.\n\n[View documentation](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update)\n\n### [`v1.22.2`](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/releases/tag/1.22.2)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.22.1...1.22.2)\n\n#### Read the Announcement\n\nRead the full announcement with discussion of new features: [Pangolin 1.22: AI Gateway for Cloud and Self-Hosted Models](https://pangolin.net/news/1-22-release)\n\n#### What's Changed\n\n- Add configurable tab title to branding (EE) and disable flag for AI keys\n- Fix js-yaml error in pangctl server commands\n- Fix form submissions resetting values on some pages\n\n**Full Changelog**: <https://github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.22.1...1.22.2>\n\n#### How to Update\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> AI gateway resources require the Badger Traefik plugin version `v1.6.0` or greater. The migration will automatically do this if it can find the Traefik config in the standard location. Otherwise, [please ensure your Badger is up to date](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update#:~:text=Increase%20the%20Badger%20version%20number).\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Private AI gateway resources require Gerbil to be on the latest version `1.5.0`. The migration will NOT automatically attempt to update Gerbil. Therefore, you must manually increment your Gerbil container version.\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Private AI gateway resources are exclusively compatible with the latest versions of all Pangolin clients. Support for gateway functionality was implemented in all client releases issued after August 19th, 2026. If your client's most recent release predates this date, private gateway access is not yet available.\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Always back up your config app-data before updating. This will allow you to easily roll back if the update breaks your configuration. You will not be able to easily downgrade otherwise.\n\n[View documentation](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update)\n\n### [`v1.22.1`](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/releases/tag/1.22.1)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.22.0...1.22.1)\n\n#### Read the Announcement\n\nRead the full announcement with discussion of new features: [Pangolin 1.22: AI Gateway for Cloud and Self-Hosted Models](https://pangolin.net/news/1-22-release)\n\n#### What's Changed\n\n- Add IP column filtering to tables by [@&#8203;Fredkiss3](https://redirect.github.com/Fredkiss3) in [#&#8203;3627](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3627)\n- Fix COUNTRY_IS_NOT rules to be created via Blueprints by [@&#8203;argueta-xyz](https://redirect.github.com/argueta-xyz) in [#&#8203;3647](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3647)\n- Fix domain namespaces and country is not in blueprints\n- Fix access token deletion for root API keys\n- Fix: License.check can fail silently by [@&#8203;shleeable](https://redirect.github.com/shleeable) in [#&#8203;3597](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3597)\n- Fix harden initial server-admin setup against duplicate users and races\n- Fix resolve security-key login only for a unique internal user\n- Fix add validation for health check hostname\n- Fix pull all matching users into blueprint instead of one\n- Improvement show warning when changing idp identifier mapping\n- Update dependencies\n\n**Full Changelog**: <https://github.com/fosrl/pangolin/compare/1.21.1...1.22.0>\n\n#### New Contributors\n\n- [@&#8203;argueta-xyz](https://redirect.github.com/argueta-xyz) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3647](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3647)\n- [@&#8203;iMord0](https://redirect.github.com/iMord0) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3654](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3654)\n- [@&#8203;moverq1337](https://redirect.github.com/moverq1337) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3655](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3655)\n- [@&#8203;aithal007](https://redirect.github.com/aithal007) made their first contribution in [#&#8203;3628](https://redirect.github.com/fosrl/pangolin/pull/3628)\n\n#### How to Update\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> AI gateway resources require the Badger Traefik plugin version `v1.6.0` or greater. The migration will automatically do this if it can find the Traefik config in the standard location. Otherwise, [please ensure your Badger is up to date](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update#:~:text=Increase%20the%20Badger%20version%20number).\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Private AI gateway resources require Gerbil to be on the latest version `1.5.0`. The migration will NOT automatically attempt to update Gerbil. Therefore, you must manually increment your Gerbil container version.\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Private AI gateway resources are exclusively compatible with the latest versions of all Pangolin clients. Support for gateway functionality was implemented in all client releases issued after August 19th, 2026. If your client's most recent release predates this date, private gateway access is not yet available.\n\n> \\[!IMPORTANT]\n> Always back up your config app-data before updating. This will allow you to easily roll back if the update breaks your configuration. You will not be able to easily downgrade otherwise.\n\n[View documentation](https://docs.pangolin.net/self-host/how-to-update)\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>meilisearch/meilisearch (getmeili/meilisearch)</summary>\n\n### [`v1.56.2`](https://redirect.github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/releases/tag/v1.56.2): 🐫\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/compare/v1.56.1...v1.56.2)\n\nMeilisearch v1.56.2 removes a leftover debug statement that could impede performance and was a regression from v1.56.1. Upgrading from previous versions of Meilisearch is strongly recommended.\n\nIt also updates several dependencies.\n\n### 🦋 Fixes\n\n- remove unwanted log & warn about future unwanted dbg by [@&#8203;dureuill](https://redirect.github.com/dureuill) in [#&#8203;6725](https://redirect.github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/pull/6725)\n\n### 🔩 Miscellaneous\n\n- Bump docker/build-push-action from 6.19.2 to 7.4.0 by [@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\\[bot] in [#&#8203;6712](https://redirect.github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/pull/6712)\n- Bump docker/login-action from 4.2.0 to 4.7.0 by [@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\\[bot] in [#&#8203;6714](https://redirect.github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/pull/6714)\n- Fix outdated CA certificates in the Docker images by [@&#8203;curquiza](https://redirect.github.com/curquiza) in [#&#8203;6705](https://redirect.github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/pull/6705)\n- Bump actions/download-artifact from 8.0.1 to 8.0.2 by [@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\\[bot] in [#&#8203;6713](https://redirect.github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/pull/6713)\n- Bump dart-lang/setup-dart from 1.7.2 to 1.8.1 by [@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\\[bot] in [#&#8203;6711](https://redirect.github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/pull/6711)\n- Bump mongodb to v9.0 in rails SDKs tests by [@&#8203;Strift](https://redirect.github.com/Strift) in [#&#8203;6716](https://redirect.github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/pull/6716)\n\n**Full Changelog**: <https://github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/compare/v1.56.1...v1.56.2>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Termix-SSH/Termix (ghcr.io/lukegus/termix)</summary>\n\n### [`v26.11.1`](https://redirect.github.com/Termix-SSH/Termix/blob/HEAD/CHANGELOG.md#26111)\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/Termix-SSH/Termix/compare/v26.11.0...v26.11.1)\n\n##### Added\n\n- Plugins in the desktop app can drag files out to Explorer or Finder\n- Termix actions: plugins can declare what they do once, and it works from the API with permission checks, dry runs, run history and approvals\n- API keys can be limited to reading or running actions, when an admin makes them\n- A click on a host can open its host page, when a plugin offers one\n- Plugins can build pages of tiles you drag and resize, and add many copies of one dashboard card, each with its own settings\n- A plugin a newer release ships is downloaded on its own when your image does not have it, and tried again on the next start when offline\n- Plugins can decide who may connect to a host, so a host can need approved access before an SSH or remote desktop session opens\n- When more than one plugin flags a host, its row shows one status dot with every reason in its tooltip\n- Plugins that issue SSH certificates can save them on the SSH key login they were issued for\n- Cmd+B shows or hides the sidebar, and can be changed in keybindings\n- The macOS menu bar icon can be monochrome (the default), in color or hidden, from the Termix menu\n- Browser back and forward, and the mouse back and forward buttons, move between the tabs you used instead of leaving Termix\n- Closing a tab goes back to the tab you used before it\n- Admin setting to stop anyone saving passwords and keys on hosts and credentials. Termix asks for them when connecting ([#&#8203;1753](https://redirect.github.com/Termix-SSH/Termix/issues/1753))\n- A signed in user can prove a second factor again, for plugins that ask before something sensitive\n- Desktop app: a credential can be kept on this device only, and used as a personal login for a shared host or folder. It is never sent to the server ([#&#8203;1749](https://redirect.github.com/Termix-SSH/Termix/issues/1749))\n\n##### Changed\n\n- Inputs, selects, tab groups and menus share one fill and one border color\n\n- Plugin cards and pages use the dashboard look everywhere, with shared lines between sections instead of separate boxes with gaps\n\n- The Plugins tab and plugin pages use the same look\n\n- List rows in plugins follow the host list status colors: accent for good, dark for offline or bad\n\n- Line charts that cover a few minutes show seconds in their times\n\n- Plugins a new release adds to the image start on only when they are recommended. The rest are installed and left off for an admin to turn on\n\n- Session tokens are stored as hashes, so a database copy holds no working logins ([#&#8203;1753](https://redirect.github.com/Termix-SSH/Termix/issues/1753))\n\n- Host status, import and export, and credential tools now start on for new installs\n\n- Sync now starts on in a new desktop app, so it can link to a server\n\n- The first run plugin picker leaves plugins you did not choose off instead of removing them\n\n- The Linux Flatpak now installs from flatpak.termix.site on x86_64 and arm64, and `flatpak update` keeps it current\n\n- Dropdowns and text areas are the same size as the text fields next to them\n\n- A page's own tabs sit above its search bar\n\n- A plugin view that is still starting shows the same loading spinner as the rest of Termix\n\n##### Fixed\n\n- Exporting hosts keeps each host status check setting and interval ([#&#8203;1787](https://redirect.github.com/Termix-SSH/Termix/issues/1787))\n- A linked desktop app now updates a plugin that came with the app when the server has a newer copy ([#&#8203;1785](https://redirect.github.com/Termix-SSH/Termix/issues/1785))\n- The first run plugin picker no longer sets the default layout and themes to Remove. They always stay on\n- Alerts with no icon no longer squeeze their text to one word per line\n- Password fields with the show button are the same height as the other fields next to them\n- Button groups next to tabs no longer touch the lines of the tab row\n- The Secure your account setup step no longer shows up empty when no passkey or authenticator plugin is on\n- An installed plugin update older than the copy in a newer image is removed at startup instead of logging an error every boot\n- Canceling a download to the desktop app right as it starts no longer leaves a partial file behind\n- Changing two interface settings at once, like resetting the dashboard, now saves both instead of only the last one\n- Release notes on a plugin's page are no longer cut off on the left\n- The Community badge in Browse is no longer missing its top border\n- Official plugin pages no longer show a stray divider before the author\n- The version picker on a plugin's page is no longer empty for a plugin installed from a local build\n- The plugin video no longer has a second border around it\n- The hint at the bottom of Browse and the stored data footer on plugin pages have the same padding as the rest of the page\n- Sign in methods on the Security page have a line between them\n- Chart axis labels with long units, like KiB/s, are no longer cut off\n- Filters, view toggles and small buttons in a toolbar are the same height as the search box next to them\n- Save and Cancel at the bottom of a form are the same height as other buttons\n- State badges in tables no longer stretch across the whole column\n- Text boxes, dropdowns, checkboxes and button groups share one border color\n- Small icons in buttons sit centered instead of half a pixel off\n- Installing Termix as an app works behind a proxy that needs a login cookie\n- The hosts Import / Export button and menu entry show their name again instead of a text key\n- SSH logins to servers that only offer group exchange no longer stall for up to a minute while checking a large key exchange group\n- Plugin views can open the host editor again, so the terminal's Edit host button works after a failed connection\n- The Linux arm64 and armv7l desktop builds start again instead of failing to load the image library\n- The terminal offers to fill a saved sudo or SSH password at a password prompt again\n- Closing the desktop app on GNOME, like Fedora Workstation, quits it instead of minimizing, since GNOME has no tray to bring it back from\n- A deleted or changed host no longer stays in the host list when a list refresh was already running ([#&#8203;1782](https://redirect.github.com/Termix-SSH/Termix/issues/1782))\n- Plugin connections to a shared host are no longer reused between people, so each person connects with their own login\n- A session that still has to set up a second factor can no longer open terminals or other live connections\n- A login still waiting on its second factor can no longer be used for desktop sync\n- Someone with time limited manage access can no longer share a host or credential so it outlasts their own access\n- Changing your password signs out your other sessions before it answers\n- A host setting that needs a permission can no longer be changed through host import, bulk edits, host defaults or desktop sync without it\n- Requests sent with no body get a clear error instead of a server error\n- On PostgreSQL and MySQL, a link with an invalid id finds nothing instead of failing with a server error\n- On MySQL, a plugin update that stopped halfway through its database changes finishes on the next start\n- Plugin host settings no longer show the previous host's values for a moment after you switch hosts\n- Switching layouts closes the old layout's tabs again when you sign in\n- A plugin panel beside a tab that fails no longer blanks every open tab\n- Scrolling with the pointer over a row of tabs scrolls the page again\n- A host list refresh that finishes late no longer puts an older list back on screen\n- Switches in settings and the host editor are named for screen readers\n- The show password button and the sign in fields are translated\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Configuration\n\n📅 **Schedule**: (UTC)\n\n- Branch creation\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n- Automerge\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n\n🚦 **Automerge**: Disabled by config. Please merge this manually once you are satisfied.\n\n♻ **Rebasing**: Whenever PR becomes conflicted, or you tick the rebase/retry checkbox.\n\n👻 **Immortal**: This PR will be recreated if closed unmerged. Get [config help](https://redirect.github.com/renovatebot/renovate/discussions) if that's undesired.\n\n---\n\n - [ ] <!-- rebase-check -->If you want to rebase/retry this PR, check this box\n\n---\n\nThis PR has been generated by [Mend Renovate CLI](https://redirect.github.com/renovatebot/renovate).\n<!--renovate-debug:eyJjcmVhdGVkSW5WZXIiOiI0NC4yMjIuNSIsInVwZGF0ZWRJblZlciI6IjQ0LjIyNi4zIiwidGFyZ2V0QnJhbmNoIjoibWFpbiIsImxhYmVscyI6WyJyZW5vdmF0ZSJdfQ==-->\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanikz/docker-infrastructure/issues/762/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanikz/docker-infrastructure/issues/762/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vdKolk/YouTubePlanner/issues/10","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vdKolk/YouTubePlanner","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vdKolk/YouTubePlanner/issues/10/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vdKolk/YouTubePlanner/issues/10/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vdKolk/YouTubePlanner/issues/10/events","html_url":"https://github.com