oogle-cloud-python/commit/8289d328f9a1eb2abb766644e4f6748198679c80))\n- update \\_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL_PATTERN to require .gserviceaccount.com    suffix   ([#&#8203;17748](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17748)) ([b60bb04](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/b60bb04a73eb35b15320c54bc3493132e6ba5706))\n\n### [`v2.56.1`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.56.1): google-auth: v2.56.1\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.56.0...google-auth-v2.56.1)\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- disable RAB lookup for Domain-Wide Delegation ([#&#8203;17763](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17763)) ([00eb128](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/00eb1284fb6081cd37b747d09366568490a6d9ad)), closes [#&#8203;17703](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17703)\n\n### [`v2.56.0`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.56.0): google-auth: v2.56.0\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.55.2...google-auth-v2.56.0)\n\n##### Features\n\n- **auth:** Implement python mtls helpers ([#&#8203;17495](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17495)) ([e7baed1](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/e7baed1a79677ca85f4dad7918a2f3e50a4fb9f2))\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- **google-auth:** add aiohttp bound for Python 3.14 ([#&#8203;17654](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17654)) ([b2ec761](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/b2ec76170d0550dc45e1b88cd66515e6dd9475cc))\n- **google-auth:** add bounds for urllib3 and packaging dependencies ([#&#8203;17647](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17647)) ([e9c6265](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/e9c626515efbcd5afefe1f6be40d0be068dac64f))\n- **google-auth:** add cryptography bound for Python 3.14 ([#&#8203;17649](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17649)) ([e9ca4c4](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/e9ca4c43029cffe1cc7386797a6477477fca218b))\n- **google-auth:** add gRPC extra and clean up obsolete TODOs ([#&#8203;17644](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17644)) ([6da41e8](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/6da41e83afd96e4719fc99a20c8fc6336de7da58)), closes [#&#8203;1735](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/1735) [#&#8203;1736](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/1736) [#&#8203;1739](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/1739)\n- **google-auth:** raise rsa extra lower bound to 4.0 ([#&#8203;17652](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17652)) ([4087828](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/40878283c3fd8838439880b0d0eece5692b3e325))\n\n### [`v2.55.2`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.55.2): google-auth: v2.55.2\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.55.1...google-auth-v2.55.2)\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- **auth:** Agentic Identites mTLS gaps fix \\_is_mtls and SslCredentials. ([#&#8203;17387](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17387)) ([7bfa41a](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/7bfa41a6746c43125f3534104aaaa7e8b18758ec))\n- **auth:** align mTLS discovery and enforce fail-fast transport configuration. ([#&#8203;17470](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17470)) ([f492d3d](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/f492d3d5e5a4b693caf7c9a8fbfdfc073a1bcda8))\n- **auth:** handle PermissionError on workload certificates to avoid startup hang and crash ([#&#8203;17568](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17568)) ([f538ad8](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/f538ad830631fa0a855c68b7cfb05788b31f03e3))\n\n### [`v2.55.1`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.55.1): google-auth: v2.55.1\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.55.0...google-auth-v2.55.1)\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- **auth:** lower regional access boundary logs from warning to debug. ([#&#8203;17571](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17571)) ([1ef4183](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/1ef418362c1a69e6bbe6f78741b53dc1f3e7b301)), closes [#&#8203;17515](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17515)\n\n### [`v2.55.0`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.55.0): google-auth: v2.55.0\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.54.0...google-auth-v2.55.0)\n\n##### Features\n\n- make RAB feature production ready ([#&#8203;17390](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17390)) ([af193931](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/af193931))\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- run async background boundary refresh on detached session ([#&#8203;17441](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17441)) ([56cbea85](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/56cbea85))\n\n### [`v2.54.0`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.54.0): google-auth: v2.54.0\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.53.0...google-auth-v2.54.0)\n\n##### Features\n\n- implement regional access boundary support for standalone JWT and async service accounts ([#&#8203;17025](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17025)) ([35af6168](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/35af6168))\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- configure mTLS for impersonated credentials ([#&#8203;17404](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17404)) ([57269d56](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/57269d56))\n\n- fail-fast on missing ECP config file to avoid 30s hang ([#&#8203;17377](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17377)) ([e0961270](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/e0961270))\n\n- Rename the &[#&#8203;39](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/39);seed&[#&#8203;39](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/39); argument for setting an initial regional access boundary for clarity ([#&#8203;17186](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17186)) ([e5c8cf92](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/e5c8cf92))\n\n- update incorrect urls in setup.py to point at monorepo vs splitrepo ([#&#8203;17237](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17237)) ([eaed04ba](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/eaed04ba))\n\n### [`v2.53.0`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.53.0): google-auth: v2.53.0\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.52.0...google-auth-v2.53.0)\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- allowlist agents-nonprod trust domains for agent identity ([#&#8203;17155](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17155)) ([44c93d2e](https://redirect.github.com/suztomo/google-cloud-python/commit/44c93d2e))\n\n- fail-fast on invalid or non-workload certificate configs in agent identity discovery ([#&#8203;17116](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17116)) ([f27a5461](https://redirect.github.com/suztomo/google-cloud-python/commit/f27a5461))\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Configuration\n\n📅 **Schedule**: (UTC)\n\n- Branch creation\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n- Automerge\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n\n🚦 **Automerge**: Disabled by config. Please merge this manually once you are satisfied.\n\n♻ **Rebasing**: Whenever PR becomes conflicted, or you tick the rebase/retry checkbox.\n\n🔕 **Ignore**: Close this PR and you won't be reminded about this update again.\n\n---\n\n - [ ] <!-- rebase-check -->If you want to rebase/retry this PR, check this box\n\n---\n\nThis PR was generated by [Mend Renovate](https://mend.io/renovate/). View the [repository job log](https://developer.mend.io/github/vdKolk/YouTubePlanner).\n<!--renovate-debug:eyJjcmVhdGVkSW5WZXIiOiI0My4xNzkuMyIsInVwZGF0ZWRJblZlciI6IjQ0LjIyMi41IiwidGFyZ2V0QnJhbmNoIjoibWFpbiIsImxhYmVscyI6W119-->\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vdKolk/YouTubePlanner/issues/10/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vdKolk/YouTubePlanner/issues/10/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RenruDall/TenantWise/issues/11","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RenruDall/TenantWise","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RenruDall/TenantWise/issues/11/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RenruDall/TenantWise/issues/11/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RenruDall/TenantWise/issues/11/events","html_url":"https://github.com/RenruDall/TenantWise/pull/11","id":6144826264,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU7J5FM8AAAABMFJEYg","number":11,"title":"Bump Microsoft.Identity.Client and Microsoft.Identity.Client.Broker","user":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12845864039,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU7J5FM8AAAAC_axUZw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RenruDall/TenantWise/labels/dependencies","name":"dependencies","color":"0366d6","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update a dependency file","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12845874727,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU7J5FM8AAAAC_ax-Jw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RenruDall/TenantWise/labels/.NET","name":".NET","color":"7121c6","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update .NET code","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-01T09:18:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:09:03Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T17:08:48Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RenruDall/TenantWise/pulls/11","html_url":"https://github.com/RenruDall/TenantWise/pull/11","diff_url":"https://github.com/RenruDall/TenantWise/pull/11.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/RenruDall/TenantWise/pull/11.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Updated [Microsoft.Identity.Client](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet) from 4.86.0 to 4.92.0.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n\n_Sourced from [Microsoft.Identity.Client's releases](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/releases)._\n\n## 4.92.0\n\n### New Features\n\n- Added `COSMIC_LOCATION` as a regional auto-detection source, after `REGION_NAME` and before IMDS. [#​6240](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6240)\n- Added `ITokenCacheSnapshotProvider` and `TokenCacheSnapshot` for process-local token-cache capture and restore without repeated JSON serialization. Use V3 serialization for persistence. [#​6229](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6229)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Fixed certificate private-key attachment on .NET Framework 4.7.2 to support non-exportable CNG keys. [#​6244](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6244)\n- Fixed managed identity KeyGuard attestation endpoint selection to use cloud-specific regional endpoints from IMDS compute metadata. [#​6238](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6238)\n- Fixed Android broker request serialization by registering `BrokerRequest` in the source-generated JSON serializer context. [#​6226](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6226)\n\n### Changes\n\n- Updated `Microsoft.Identity.Client.NativeInterop` from 0.20.6 to 0.20.7. [#​6230](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6230)\n- Reduced OpenTelemetry metric-tag allocations using `TagList` and cached canonical tag-key sets. Custom enrichers should use noncanonical tag names. [#​6227](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6227)\n\n\n## 4.91.1\n\n### Changes\n\n- Added opt-in reduced token-acquisition logging: set `MSAL_REDUCED_LOGGING=true` (or `1`) before application construction to move selected routine Information-level diagnostics to Verbose. Existing logging behavior is unchanged by default; acquisition summaries, warnings, and errors remain unchanged. [#​6208](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6208) [#​6224](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6224)\n\n**Full Changelog:** https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/compare/4.91.0...4.91.1\n\n## 4.91.0\n\n### New Features\n\n- Made the dynamic certificate provider and confidential-client callbacks (`OnMsalServiceFailure`, `OnCompletion`, and `OnBackgroundTokenRefreshCompleted`) generally available, removing the experimental feature opt-in requirement. [#​6216](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6216)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Fixed built-in mTLS `HttpClient` caching to use certificate object identity, ensuring a new certificate instance with a reacquired private-key handle receives a new handler even when its thumbprint is unchanged. [#​6217](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6217)\n- Fixed managed identity `WithForceRefresh(true)` to re-mint the MSI v2 binding certificate before acquiring a new token, while reusing a valid cached attestation token for the current key. [#​6215](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6215)\n- Fixed system-browser authentication callbacks in Linux containers by adding opt-in IPv4 port-forwarding support through `MSAL_ALLOW_SYSTEM_BROWSER_PORT_FORWARDING`, disabled by default. [#​6186](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6186)\n\n## 4.90.1\n\n### New Features\n- Added `IMsalWsTrustHttpClientFactory`, allowing custom HTTP client factories to provide redirect-disabled, credential-policy-aware clients for federation metadata (MEX) and WS-Trust requests. Added `MsalError.TooManyRedirects` and `MsalError.WsTrustCrossOriginRedirectNotSupported` for redirect failures. [#​6165](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6165)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n- Hardened federation metadata and WS-Trust requests by requiring HTTPS, securely validating redirects, rejecting credential-bearing cross-origin redirects, and limiting redirect chains. [#​6165](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6165)\n- Fixed instance discovery so a custom authority port is not forwarded to the global discovery host, while preserving the port when discovery uses the authority host. [#​6155](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6155)\n- Fixed KeyGuard attestation to send the tenant ID as the MAA `client_id` metadata value without changing managed-identity client-ID handling or attestation-cache partitioning. [#​6200](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6200)\n\n### Changes\n- Updated `Microsoft.Azure.Security.KeyGuardAttestation` from version 1.1.7 to 1.1.8. [#​6202](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6202)\n\n\n## 4.90.0\n\n### Changes\n- Updated the KeyGuardAttestation package version to 1.1.7. [#​6189](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6189)\n\n## 4.89.0\n\n## What's Changed\n* Add repository guidance for AI agents by @​bgavrilMS in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6158\n* Add Linux Attested Managed Identity Flow documentation by @​gladjohn in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6149\n* Remove internal authority example from API docs by @​bgavrilMS in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6170\n* Update SNI MTLS PoP Token Design documentation by @​bgavrilMS in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6171\n* Add SNI mTLS E2E coverage for a non-exportable VBS-protected certificate by @​gladjohn in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6167\n* Revise mTLS PoP acceptance-test matrix structure by @​gladjohn in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6161\n* Add ICloudConfiguration for cross-cloud metadata resolution by @​Avery-Dunn in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6104\n* Fix IMDSv2 SCHANNEL failures bypassing certificate re-mint retry by @​Robbie-Microsoft in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6173\n* Always record RawStsErrorCode on MsalFailure metric by @​ssmelov in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6175\n* Add MSAL_MI_DISABLE_IMDS_V2 kill switch for managed identity by @​Robbie-Microsoft in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6178\n* Add timeout for managed identity capability discovery by @​Robbie-Microsoft in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6181\n* Pin GitHub Actions to full-length commit SHAs by @​danfiedler-msft in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6182\n\n## New Contributors\n* @​danfiedler-msft made their first contribution in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6182\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/compare/4.88.0...4.89.0\n\n## 4.88.0\n\n### New Features\n- Added user-assigned managed identity support for Azure Arc, including selecting the identity by client ID and validating the identity returned in the token response. [#​6128](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6128)\n- Added `WithRequestOverMtls()` to managed identity token requests, enabling attested bearer-token acquisition over the IMDSv2 mTLS transport. [#​6086](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6086)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n- Fixed token-cache key collisions by length-prefixing additional cache-key components before hashing. [#​6137](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6137)\n- Populated authentication-result telemetry metadata on proactive background-refresh results. [#​6157](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6157)\n- Fixed mTLS PoP authority validation incorrectly rejecting sovereign-cloud aliases such as `login.chinacloudapi.cn` and `login.usgovcloudapi.net`. [#​6153](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6153)\n\n## 4.87.0\n\n## What's Changed\n\n* Expose `MsalServiceException.ErrorCodesForLogging` for diagnostics in #​6138\n* Expose `WithOtelTagsEnricher` for managed identity requests in #​6144\n* Forward OpenTelemetry tags enricher to the client-assertion callback in #​6142\n* Add client-side opaque-token log scrubber in #​6119\n* Populate `ExecutionResult.Exception` for non-MSAL failures in #​6139\n* Use PSS padding in KeyGuard liveness probe (CodeQL SM03799) in #​6141\n* Remove managed identity support from `WithClaimsFromClient` (confidential-client only) in #​6113\n* Remove experimental features from client setup in #​6143\n* Update Azure Arc managed identity API version from 2019-11-01 to 2020-06-01 in #​6130\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/compare/4.86.1...4.87.0\n\n\n## 4.86.1\n\n### Bug Fixes\n- Fixed the mTLS Proof-of-Possession token cache to key on the certificate's full DER (`x5t#S256`) instead of only the public key, preventing a stale token (and `AADSTS500181`) after a same-key certificate renewal. [#​6123](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6123)\n- Fell back to RS256 when a certificate's PSS signing operation is rejected by `RSACryptoServiceProvider`, rebuilding the client assertion so authentication can proceed. [#​6126](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6126)\n- Detect and reject symbolic links in the Unix cache-file write path (lstat pre-check plus `O_NOFOLLOW`), closing a TOCTOU window. [#​6115](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6115)\n- Corrected misleading \"region required\" error messages and doc comments in the mTLS PoP flow. [#​6127](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6127)\n\n\n\nCommits viewable in [compare view](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/compare/4.86.0...4.92.0).\n</details>\n\nUpdated [Microsoft.Identity.Client.Broker](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet) from 4.86.0 to 4.92.0.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n\n_Sourced from [Microsoft.Identity.Client.Broker's releases](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/releases)._\n\n## 4.92.0\n\n### New Features\n\n- Added `COSMIC_LOCATION` as a regional auto-detection source, after `REGION_NAME` and before IMDS. [#​6240](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6240)\n- Added `ITokenCacheSnapshotProvider` and `TokenCacheSnapshot` for process-local token-cache capture and restore without repeated JSON serialization. Use V3 serialization for persistence. [#​6229](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6229)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Fixed certificate private-key attachment on .NET Framework 4.7.2 to support non-exportable CNG keys. [#​6244](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6244)\n- Fixed managed identity KeyGuard attestation endpoint selection to use cloud-specific regional endpoints from IMDS compute metadata. [#​6238](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6238)\n- Fixed Android broker request serialization by registering `BrokerRequest` in the source-generated JSON serializer context. [#​6226](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6226)\n\n### Changes\n\n- Updated `Microsoft.Identity.Client.NativeInterop` from 0.20.6 to 0.20.7. [#​6230](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6230)\n- Reduced OpenTelemetry metric-tag allocations using `TagList` and cached canonical tag-key sets. Custom enrichers should use noncanonical tag names. [#​6227](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6227)\n\n\n## 4.91.1\n\n### Changes\n\n- Added opt-in reduced token-acquisition logging: set `MSAL_REDUCED_LOGGING=true` (or `1`) before application construction to move selected routine Information-level diagnostics to Verbose. Existing logging behavior is unchanged by default; acquisition summaries, warnings, and errors remain unchanged. [#​6208](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6208) [#​6224](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6224)\n\n**Full Changelog:** https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/compare/4.91.0...4.91.1\n\n## 4.91.0\n\n### New Features\n\n- Made the dynamic certificate provider and confidential-client callbacks (`OnMsalServiceFailure`, `OnCompletion`, and `OnBackgroundTokenRefreshCompleted`) generally available, removing the experimental feature opt-in requirement. [#​6216](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6216)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Fixed built-in mTLS `HttpClient` caching to use certificate object identity, ensuring a new certificate instance with a reacquired private-key handle receives a new handler even when its thumbprint is unchanged. [#​6217](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6217)\n- Fixed managed identity `WithForceRefresh(true)` to re-mint the MSI v2 binding certificate before acquiring a new token, while reusing a valid cached attestation token for the current key. [#​6215](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6215)\n- Fixed system-browser authentication callbacks in Linux containers by adding opt-in IPv4 port-forwarding support through `MSAL_ALLOW_SYSTEM_BROWSER_PORT_FORWARDING`, disabled by default. [#​6186](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6186)\n\n## 4.90.1\n\n### New Features\n- Added `IMsalWsTrustHttpClientFactory`, allowing custom HTTP client factories to provide redirect-disabled, credential-policy-aware clients for federation metadata (MEX) and WS-Trust requests. Added `MsalError.TooManyRedirects` and `MsalError.WsTrustCrossOriginRedirectNotSupported` for redirect failures. [#​6165](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6165)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n- Hardened federation metadata and WS-Trust requests by requiring HTTPS, securely validating redirects, rejecting credential-bearing cross-origin redirects, and limiting redirect chains. [#​6165](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6165)\n- Fixed instance discovery so a custom authority port is not forwarded to the global discovery host, while preserving the port when discovery uses the authority host. [#​6155](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6155)\n- Fixed KeyGuard attestation to send the tenant ID as the MAA `client_id` metadata value without changing managed-identity client-ID handling or attestation-cache partitioning. [#​6200](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6200)\n\n### Changes\n- Updated `Microsoft.Azure.Security.KeyGuardAttestation` from version 1.1.7 to 1.1.8. [#​6202](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6202)\n\n\n## 4.90.0\n\n### Changes\n- Updated the KeyGuardAttestation package version to 1.1.7. [#​6189](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6189)\n\n## 4.89.0\n\n## What's Changed\n* Add repository guidance for AI agents by @​bgavrilMS in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6158\n* Add Linux Attested Managed Identity Flow documentation by @​gladjohn in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6149\n* Remove internal authority example from API docs by @​bgavrilMS in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6170\n* Update SNI MTLS PoP Token Design documentation by @​bgavrilMS in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6171\n* Add SNI mTLS E2E coverage for a non-exportable VBS-protected certificate by @​gladjohn in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6167\n* Revise mTLS PoP acceptance-test matrix structure by @​gladjohn in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6161\n* Add ICloudConfiguration for cross-cloud metadata resolution by @​Avery-Dunn in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6104\n* Fix IMDSv2 SCHANNEL failures bypassing certificate re-mint retry by @​Robbie-Microsoft in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6173\n* Always record RawStsErrorCode on MsalFailure metric by @​ssmelov in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6175\n* Add MSAL_MI_DISABLE_IMDS_V2 kill switch for managed identity by @​Robbie-Microsoft in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6178\n* Add timeout for managed identity capability discovery by @​Robbie-Microsoft in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6181\n* Pin GitHub Actions to full-length commit SHAs by @​danfiedler-msft in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6182\n\n## New Contributors\n* @​danfiedler-msft made their first contribution in https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6182\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/compare/4.88.0...4.89.0\n\n## 4.88.0\n\n### New Features\n- Added user-assigned managed identity support for Azure Arc, including selecting the identity by client ID and validating the identity returned in the token response. [#​6128](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6128)\n- Added `WithRequestOverMtls()` to managed identity token requests, enabling attested bearer-token acquisition over the IMDSv2 mTLS transport. [#​6086](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6086)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n- Fixed token-cache key collisions by length-prefixing additional cache-key components before hashing. [#​6137](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6137)\n- Populated authentication-result telemetry metadata on proactive background-refresh results. [#​6157](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6157)\n- Fixed mTLS PoP authority validation incorrectly rejecting sovereign-cloud aliases such as `login.chinacloudapi.cn` and `login.usgovcloudapi.net`. [#​6153](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6153)\n\n## 4.87.0\n\n## What's Changed\n\n* Expose `MsalServiceException.ErrorCodesForLogging` for diagnostics in #​6138\n* Expose `WithOtelTagsEnricher` for managed identity requests in #​6144\n* Forward OpenTelemetry tags enricher to the client-assertion callback in #​6142\n* Add client-side opaque-token log scrubber in #​6119\n* Populate `ExecutionResult.Exception` for non-MSAL failures in #​6139\n* Use PSS padding in KeyGuard liveness probe (CodeQL SM03799) in #​6141\n* Remove managed identity support from `WithClaimsFromClient` (confidential-client only) in #​6113\n* Remove experimental features from client setup in #​6143\n* Update Azure Arc managed identity API version from 2019-11-01 to 2020-06-01 in #​6130\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/compare/4.86.1...4.87.0\n\n\n## 4.86.1\n\n### Bug Fixes\n- Fixed the mTLS Proof-of-Possession token cache to key on the certificate's full DER (`x5t#S256`) instead of only the public key, preventing a stale token (and `AADSTS500181`) after a same-key certificate renewal. [#​6123](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6123)\n- Fell back to RS256 when a certificate's PSS signing operation is rejected by `RSACryptoServiceProvider`, rebuilding the client assertion so authentication can proceed. [#​6126](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6126)\n- Detect and reject symbolic links in the Unix cache-file write path (lstat pre-check plus `O_NOFOLLOW`), closing a TOCTOU window. [#​6115](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6115)\n- Corrected misleading \"region required\" error messages and doc comments in the mTLS PoP flow. [#​6127](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/pull/6127)\n\n\n\nCommits viewable in [compare view](https://github.com/AzureAD/microsoft-authentication-library-for-dotnet/compare/4.86.0...4.92.0).\n</details>\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RenruDall/TenantWise/issues/11/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RenruDall/TenantWise/issues/11/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onyx-dot-app/onyx/issues/17533","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onyx-dot-app/onyx","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onyx-dot-app/onyx/issues/17533/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onyx-dot-app/onyx/issues/17533/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onyx-dot-app/onyx/issues/17533/events","html_url":"https://github.com/onyx-dot-app/onyx/pull/17533","id":6296362608,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJb7SK88AAAABN-Jviw","number":17533,"title":"feat(craft): guest daemon browser management with CDP over Dial (ENG-4573)","user":{"login":"justin-tahara","id":105671973,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkxtJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105671973?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justin-tahara","html_url":"https://github.com/justin-tahara","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justin-tahara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justin-tahara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justin-tahara/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justin-tahara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justin-tahara/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justin-tahara/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justin-tahara/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justin-tahara/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justin-tahara/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-11-09T22:54:56Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:08:54Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onyx-dot-app/onyx/pulls/17533","html_url":"https://github.com/onyx-dot-app/onyx/pull/17533","diff_url":"https://github.com/onyx-dot-app/onyx/pull/17533.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/onyx-dot-app/onyx/pull/17533.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Description\n\nAdds browser management to the Craft Firecracker guest daemon: headful Chromium on Xvfb with Chromium's own sandbox on. Everything stays behind `SANDBOX_RUNTIME=firecracker`. No change to the pod or Docker runtimes. No Alembic.\n\nLinear: [ENG-4573](https://linear.app/onyx-app/issue/ENG-4573)\n\n- **Proto:** `BrowserStart`, `BrowserStop`, `BrowserStatus` on `craft.sandboxd.v1`; reasons 20-22 (`BROWSER_NOT_AVAILABLE`, `BROWSER_START_FAILED`, `BROWSER_PROFILE_FAILED`).\n- **Supervisor** (`internal/guestd/browser`): Chromium runs as the non-root `sandbox` user, no GPU.\n  - States: stopped, starting, running, restarting, stopping, failed. Restart after a crash with a 1 s → 30 s backoff; 5 fast crashes → failed.\n  - Own cgroup `/sys/fs/cgroup/guestd-browser` (`memory.max` 2 GiB, `memory.oom.group`).\n  - Clean stop = CDP `Browser.close`, kill after 10 s. SIGTERM loses uncommitted cookies, so it is only a fallback.\n  - `--browser-bin` is a candidate list: `/opt/chrome/chrome`, then `/usr/bin/chromium`.\n- **CDP:** Chromium on `127.0.0.1:9222`, forwarded from guest vsock 9222 while it runs. The api_server reaches it with node agent `Dial` (needs `--dial-ports 3010,9222`).\n- **Profile:** Chromium runs on a live copy. A clean stop saves it without caches to `/workspace/.craft/browser-profile` (atomic swap, 256 MiB cap). A crash keeps the last saved profile.\n- **Fix:** the guest vsock listener returns `net.ErrClosed` after `Close` (accept loops spun before).\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n- `microvm/`: `go test -race ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `go vet -tags kvm ./...` pass after the rebase on main. `.pb.go` regenerated (protoc 36.2, protoc-gen-go v1.36.12, protoc-gen-go-grpc v1.6.2): byte-identical. New unit tests use a fake Xvfb/Chromium, plus forwarder and RPC gate tests.\n- pre-commit on all changed files.\n- Also deflakes `TestOutputGap` (merged in ENG-4571): a live stream could attach between the two writes; the test now checks the replay after the run ends. It failed in CI on this PR's first push.\n- KVM (`TestBrowserKVM`, m8i.4xlarge nested, 2 vCPU / 4 GiB VM, v5.1.0 rootfs, Chromium 156, agent over mTLS):\n  - BrowserStart: first in a new VM 0.74 s (2.17 s cold page cache); after a stop **219 ms p50**, 224 ms p95.\n  - CDP screenshot through `Dial`: 0.42-0.75 s.\n  - Renderer uid 1000, seccomp on, own user namespace; no `--no-sandbox`.\n  - Browser cgroup ~380 MiB after one page (2 GiB limit).\n  - BrowserStop 219 ms, clean; a cookie survives stop/start.\n  - `kill -9` of Chromium → running again in 1.24 s.\n  - Nothing left after the last stop. Torn down.\n\n## v1 choices (decided 2026-11-10)\n\n- **Profile stays in the VM.** It is saved on the VM's scratch disk only, and session saves do not include it. This matches the pod runtime. Revisit when P3 (saved logins) is decided.\n- **Dial port 9222 is allowed by default.** The Helm default is `3010,9222`, added in #17516.\n- **Chromium stays strict on Origin.** The api_server CDP client must send `Host: 127.0.0.1` and no `Origin` header. The daemon does not use `--remote-allow-origins`.\n\n## Docs\n\n- [ ] Customer-facing change: I updated `documentation/` (text and screenshots).\n- [x] No docs change needed (internal, tests, CI, or multi-tenant cloud only).\n\nThe runtime is not usable yet.\n\n## Additional Options\n\n- [ ] [Optional] Please cherry-pick this PR to the latest release version.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added controls to start, stop, and check the status of a Chromium browser running in a virtual machine.\n  * Browser sessions can save profiles, including cookies, after a clean stop and can recover automatically after crashes. Crashes and forced stops leave the saved profile unchanged.\n  * Browser DevTools access is available through the configured connection ports; add the browser port to the allowed ports to connect.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added guidance on browser setup, connection access, lifecycle, and saved profiles.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onyx-dot-app/onyx/issues/17533/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/onyx-dot-app/onyx/issues/17533/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nace-ai/kapitsa/issues/1156","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nace-ai/kapitsa","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nace-ai/kapitsa/issues/1156/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nace-ai/kapitsa/issues/1156/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nace-ai/kapitsa/issues/1156/events","html_url":"https://github.com/nace-ai/kapitsa/pull/1156","id":6310067960,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVLn4Ys8AAAABOJFNSw","number":1156,"title":"Nemotron-H KFlash trees: the verify after a tree cycle writes the accepted path into the Mamba conv ring (Bolt + LiLiCorr: 5 of 8 greedy answers equal to no drafter, was 2; #1150)","user":{"login":"alish-nace-23","id":350386894,"node_id":"U_kgDOFOJ6zg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/350386894?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alish-nace-23","html_url":"https://github.com/alish-nace-23","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alish-nace-23/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alish-nace-23/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alish-nace-23/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alish-nace-23/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alish-nace-23/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alish-nace-23/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alish-nace-23/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alish-nace-23/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alish-nace-23/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-11-10T15:31:34Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:07:38Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T17:07:35Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nace-ai/kapitsa/pulls/1156","html_url":"https://github.com/nace-ai/kapitsa/pull/1156","diff_url":"https://github.com/nace-ai/kapitsa/pull/1156.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nace-ai/kapitsa/pull/1156.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T17:07:35Z"},"body":"Refs #1150 (Bolt + LiLiCorr: answers unrelated to the prompt, fine with `--dflash none`): the conv ring cause we found. The remaining difference from `--dflash none` on Bolt (on topic, the verify's GEMM rows) is #1158.\n\n## What was wrong\n\nA KFlash tree verify keeps the accepted path's rows pending; the next verify commits them inside its Mamba scans (merged flush). With GEMM rows (the default), that commit writes the conv ring in the grouped norm, `nh_gnorm_half_ring` (#152). That kernel wrote rows `0 .. a` of the tree into the ring instead of the path's rows `pend_path[0 .. a]`. Whenever the accepted path was not the tree's first branch, three positions of every Mamba layer got a sibling draft's input. The target then decoded from a corrupted state, so its outputs changed only with the drafter on, and changed between identical requests as the tree shapes changed. `nh_conv_ring` (the other ring write) already read the path; this makes the grouped-norm one do the same.\n\nThis is also why `nh_tree_check`'s planted-branch cases had failed since `6cd6a11`, the merge that brought #152 into the tree branch (docs/kflash-map.md, item 3).\n\n## Changes\n\n- `nh_gnorm_half_ring`: with `ptree`, the ring takes pending row `pend_path[t]`, as `nh_conv_ring` does. The host passes `pend_tree` and `pend_path`.\n- `tools/nh_tree_check`: a \"pending tree path\" case. A tree whose accepted path is rows 0, 2, 3, 4; after the next verify's merged commit, the conv ring must equal the ring of a separate flush.\n- docs/kflash-map.md and docs/kflash.md: the failing check is explained; one gap on the M5 Pro stays open (below).\n\n## Results\n\nRuns: M5 Pro 48 GB, macOS 26.5.2 (25F84). Binaries built from f55b55b5 (main) and f55b55b5 + this change; the branch is rebased on dc244208 (no Nemotron changes in between). One run per build, greedy (temperature 0), `reasoning_effort: none`.\n\n`nh_tree_check` on the synthetic Nemotron-H model (`tools/nh_synth.py --dspark`):\n\n| case | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| pending tree path: ring equal to a separate flush | 0 of 3 Mamba layers | 3 of 3 |\n| planted-branch acceptance, sampled T 0.8 | FAIL: 83 of 112 cycles off the planted branch | PASS: 0 of 41 |\n| everything with `NI_NH_ROWS_GEMM=0` | PASS | PASS |\n\nBolt 24 GB + LiLiCorr, `kapitsa serve`, single slot. Answers identical to `--dflash none`:\n\n| | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| 8 different prompts | 2 of 8 | 5 of 8 |\n| the #1150 prompt 8 times, the reporter's flags (`--context 128k --slots 1 --private`) | 4 different answers among the 8 | the same answer 8 times |\n\nThe 3 answers that still differ are the three copies of the #1150 prompt. All of them, and all 8 copies in the second row (main and this PR alike), part from the no-drafter answer at answer token 7 (0-based): no drafter picks 24777 (碧水), the drafter run 40154 (碧波). In the no-drafter one-row decode those two are the top two, 0.20 logit apart (46.13 vs 45.93); every earlier position has a gap of at least 0.44. The drafter run's verify row had 40154 ahead by 0.145. Main splits at the same token, so this is not the ring bug; the ~0.35 logit move there comes from the verify's GEMM rows, not from trees: the issue prompt 8 times with the PR's build gave 0 of 8 answers identical to `--dflash none` by default, with `NI_KFLASH=0` (chains), `NI_NH_MERGE_FLUSH=0`, `NI_NH_ATTN_TV=0` and `NI_ANE=0`, and 8 of 8 with `NI_NH_ROWS_GEMM=0` (about 4x slower, so not a fix). An 8-row chain verify of the no-drafter tokens from position 41 keeps the no-drafter pick (gap +0.2026), so the move needs the server's cycle alignment or the state its earlier GEMM-row commits leave. That is a separate drafter-only difference, outside this PR: #1158.\n\nLightning (NVFP4) + DSpark, the same 8 prompts: 2 of 8 identical to `--dflash none` on main, 7 of 8 with this PR (the 8th parts at a 0.06-logit near-tie).\n\nPlain decoding is untouched: `--dflash none` gave the same 8 answers on both builds, and `logit_dump`'s prefill path does not run this kernel's tree case. Speed: one run per build, Bolt tok/s within run-to-run spread; not an A/B.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- The 0/8 off-topic answers of #1150 did not reproduce on this M5 Pro on either build: main's answers drift but stay on topic. The reporter's M5 Ultra on macOS 27.0.1 is not run. The report also shows one off-topic answer without the drafter, which this change does not touch.\n- Metal validation: `MTL_SHADER_VALIDATION=1 MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1` aborts before the changed kernel's tree case runs, on `nh_ssd_m` (20,480 B static threadgroup memory, read as 40,960) and with `NI_NH_SSD=0` on `nh_ssm1_tree` (17,024 B, read as 34,048), the layer's known doubling. The changed kernel reads `pend_path[t]` for `t < n_pend <= 8`; `pend_path` holds `kf::kPathWords` ints.\n- Still open on the M5 Pro: with GEMM rows a tree row's logits differ from the chain verify of its path by up to 2.5e-4 of the largest logit, so `nh_tree_check`'s greedy cases fail on the random synthetic model on both builds (they pass with `NI_NH_ROWS_GEMM=0`).\n- No other Mac.\n\n\n\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nace-ai/kapitsa/issues/1156/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nace-ai/kapitsa/issues/1156/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peiikai/LASRecomp/issues/238","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peiikai/LASRecomp","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peiikai/LASRecomp/issues/238/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peiikai/LASRecomp/issues/238/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peiikai/LASRecomp/issues/238/events","html_url":"https://github.com/peiikai/LASRecomp/pull/238","id":5942273550,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVBqNYc8AAAABJjlDsw","number":238,"title":"iOS port: the game on iPhone / iPad, built from the player's own files on any desktop","user":{"login":"ky1vstar","id":23170237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMTcwMjM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23170237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ky1vstar","html_url":"https://github.com/ky1vstar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ky1vstar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ky1vstar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ky1vstar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ky1vstar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ky1vstar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ky1vstar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ky1vstar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ky1vstar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ky1vstar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-20T13:12:03Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:02:58Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peiikai/LASRecomp/pulls/238","html_url":"https://github.com/peiikai/LASRecomp/pull/238","diff_url":"https://github.com/peiikai/LASRecomp/pull/238.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/peiikai/LASRecomp/pull/238.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"LAS Recomp runs natively on iOS (iPhone / iPad, arm64, iOS 16+). The Metal renderer, MetalFX, kernel, HLE and menus are shared with macOS; the game code is a dylib embedded as a framework; the randomizer's seed generator runs on the phone with its original Python packages. The Files app for game files, pause in the background, Home Screen quick actions.\n\nThis is the second half of the split from [the merge plan](https://github.com/peiikai/LASRecomp/pull/238#issuecomment-6713895321): the touch layer (on-screen controls, the menus for fingers, `PLAT_TOUCH`) went in with #634, and this PR is the iOS port on top of it - `PLAT_TOUCH` is 1 on iOS and `runtime/platform/ios_glue.m` / `ios_prompt.m` answer the layer's `plat_touch_*`. The guest window is upstream's `DYN_BASE`. Rebased on `beta_6` as of fc10aef7, two commits.\n\nTested on an iPhone 15 Pro (iOS 26 / 27): title and overworld at a steady 60 fps, 1.8–2.3 GB footprint, DualSense and touch, a seed generates in ~4 s and is byte-identical to the Mac's.\n\n## How a player gets it\n\nNo game code ships, and on iOS that means no public `.ipa` at all (iOS runs only code signed inside the bundle). Two ways, both from the player's own game files:\n\n- **From any desktop** (macOS, Linux, Windows x64 / ARM64): the release's **iOS kit** (`LAS Recomp-<version>-iOS.laskit`: the app without game code, a Mach-O linker for each desktop, the compiler's Darwin headers - one zip the runtime reads in place, nothing to unpack). The start screen's *Recomp for iOS* page (Settings > Prelaunch) takes the kit and the game files and writes an unsigned `.ipa` with the bundled zig + rust-lld (`lasrecomp --build-ios <kit.laskit> [game files]` from a terminal). A kit from another release is refused, naming both versions. The player signs and sideloads it (Sideloadly, AltStore, SideStore...).\n- **From source on a Mac**: `make PLATFORM=ios` + `make ipa` (signs with `TEAM_ID` / `PROFILE`).\n\nSigning needs only `increased-memory-limit`, which a free personal team can carry; the start screen says so when a signer dropped it.\n\n## What's in it\n\n**iOS port** - `PLATFORM=ios` (always `DYN_BASE`), `make deps-ios` (static SDL3 + LGPL FFmpeg, BeeWare's CPython 3.13 xcframework, keystone / oead / quicktex / Pillow cross-built, every input pinned by hash), `runtime/platform/ios*.{c,m}`, `PLAT_IOS`.\n- The guest window: `plat_place_guest` walks the process's map and takes a gap that holds the packed iOS layout (`runtime/rt.h`, 1 GB aligned; where an iOS process has room differs by device and iOS version). Game threads get 16 MB host stacks there (256 MB each doesn't fit next to the window).\n- `lasgame.dylib` as `Frameworks/LASGame.framework` (the executable holds no game code, checked in CI); the start screen refuses game files of another version than the app's code.\n- Randomizer: `plat_spawn` of a `.py` runs it in-process in a thread (same log file, exit codes, kill; the generator's modules reset between runs - the self-test generates twice and compares), so the Randomizer tab works unchanged. No symlink anywhere in the app (sideloading installs drop them).\n- Data: the app's Documents by default, or any folder in Files kept as a security-scoped bookmark; folders shown as Files names them; iCloud Drive warned about as OneDrive is on Windows, offloaded files named at launch.\n- Game Files page: `UIDocumentPickerViewController` behind SDL's dialogs (`platform/ios_sdl.h`); the setup clones the folder into the data root (APFS: seconds, no second copy). Open in Files for Show in Finder; Import fonts through the picker.\n- Background: iOS refuses GPU work there and kills without `exit()` - the game pauses at its next present, nothing is drawn, the hang watchdog sits it out, and settings are saved on the way out with the phones' atomic write (`settings.c`: Android's, now under `PLAT_TOUCH`).\n- Home Screen quick actions (`plat_touch_play_request` / `shortcuts_sync`): Play Vanilla, one per seed, Metal HUD. The system text prompt (`plat_touch_prompt`) is a `UIAlertController`; iPad is `plat_touch_tablet`.\n- The shipped fonts (BIZ UDPGothic, DejaVu) since iOS has no readable system fonts; a full-bleed app icon; the status bar hidden; `LARECOMP_IOS_PYTEST` self-test.\n\n**iOS export from the desktop** - the `.laskit` kit (`tools/ios_kit.sh`, five linkers from Rust's rust-lld, `version.txt`), `runtime/zipfile.c` over miniz, `runtime/iosexport.c` (the `.ipa` writer: the kit's entries cloned, the library deflated), the start screen page (`runtime/ui/ios_export_ui.mm`); the library's flags and id the same from every desktop host (tested against each OS's Makefile branch). `IOSEXPORT=0` leaves it out, as Android does.\n\n**CI / release** - the iOS game-code build tested on every desktop job including Linux aarch64 and Windows on ARM (`tools/test_gamebuild_ios.py`); the iOS app, the kit and a simulator build with the embedded Python's self-test in their own Mac job; the kit as a fifth release file, its layout and the executable's entitlement checked.\n\n**Shared changes outside iOS** - `rt_dispatch`'s cache slot from the address bits that vary (`(pc >> 4) ^ (pc >> 14)`: misses 2.7 → 1.7 % of the game thread); `romfs_find_game` shared by the setup and the export; rust-lld and miniz in the README's License section, with the iOS app's static FFmpeg and in-process oead / Keystone noted.\n\n## Docs\n\n`docs/ios-tech-debt.md`: every shortcut taken, with where it lives and the fix. Open:\n- `docs/ios.md` for players (the kit, the export, which sideloaders keep the entitlement).\n- Devices under 8 GB and iPad: not run. 4 GB devices and GPUs without BC (pre-A14: the same devices) are one problem - the design of where a loaded texture's BC bytes live comes first; measured options are in the doc.\n- The iOS strings are in the 11 languages' tables (appended after upstream's entries).\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peiikai/LASRecomp/issues/238/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peiikai/LASRecomp/issues/238/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/issues/48","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/issues/48/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/issues/48/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/issues/48/events","html_url":"https://github.com/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/pull/48","id":6265131014,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVX470s8AAAABNla80Q","number":48,"title":"Pick the CI iPad by iOS version; keep the dSYM; launch the Release build; smoke console as an artifact","user":{"login":"MarkPLacer","id":61635316,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNjM1MzE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61635316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarkPLacer","html_url":"https://github.com/MarkPLacer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarkPLacer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarkPLacer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarkPLacer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarkPLacer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarkPLacer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarkPLacer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarkPLacer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarkPLacer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarkPLacer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12844662492,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVX470s8AAAAC_Zn-3A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/labels/size:L","name":"size:L","color":"bfd4f2","default":false,"description":"This PR changes 100-499 lines, ignoring generated files","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2026-11-07T22:56:32Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:01:29Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T17:01:26Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/pulls/48","html_url":"https://github.com/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/pull/48","diff_url":"https://github.com/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/pull/48.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/pull/48.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T17:01:26Z"},"body":"## **User description**\nSkupina F (CI) iz revizije 7. 11. 2026: šest ugotovitev in štirje popravki po pregledu. Vsaka sprememba je v svoji zavezi. Spremenjeni so le `.github/workflows/build.yml`, korak »Pick the simulator« v `.github/workflows/screenshots.yml` in vrstica 88 v `scripts/screens.sh`. Koda aplikacije, del za izdajo (`latest-release`, objava oznake) in podpisovanje so nespremenjeni.\n\n## Kaj\n\n- **ci:0 – napaka izbirnika v Screenshots pokaže svojo sled klicev (traceback).**\n  - V koraku »Pick the simulator« se izpis izbirnika shrani v svoji vrstici, `PICK=$(xcrun simctl list devices available -j | python3 -c '…')`, nato sledi `read -r DEVICE RUNTIME DATA NAME <<< \"$PICK\"`.\n  - Napaka v Pythonu zdaj ustavi korak s svojim izpisom, ne z zavajajočim »No ipad simulator on this runner«. Preverjanje praznega `DEVICE` ostane.\n  - `scripts/screens.sh` pri neuspelem zagonu izpiše tudi vrstice z `Error:`, `error:` in `Traceback`.\n- **ci:4 – testi aplikacije tečejo na namenoma izbranem iPadu.**\n  - Nov korak »Pick the iPad simulator« (`id: simulator`) takoj za »Select Xcode«. Izbere najnovejši iOS, ki ima iPad, in na njem iPad Pro 13-inch (M5), sicer najbolje uvrščeni iPad. Različico prebere le iz vodilnih številk imena izvajalnega okolja, kot Screenshots.\n  - Izpiše `Using <ime> on <okolje> (<udid>)` in zapiše `DEVICE` v `$GITHUB_ENV`. Uporabita ga koraka za teste enot in za dimni test.\n  - Brez iPada posel pade z `::error::No iPad simulator on this runner`. Prej sta oba koraka le opozorila in končala z `exit 0`, zato bi `latest-release` lahko objavil build, na katerem ni tekel noben test aplikacije.\n  - Obe vgrajeni kopiji starega izbirnika sta odstranjeni. Opozorilo s preskokom ostane le za simulator, ki se ne zažene, in za neuspelo namestitev.\n- **ci:3 (del v CI) – konzola dimnega testa gre v artefakt in povzetek, ne v dnevnik posla.**\n  - Konzola gre v `build/smoke.log`. Dnevnik posla sproti kaže le vrstice `SMOKE …`. Ob neuspehu korak izpiše še zadnjih 200 vrstic konzole.\n  - Povzetek koraka (`$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY`) našteje 20 najpogostejših vrstic konzole (naslovi kot ADDR, številke kot N). Prešteje tudi vrstice »Metal API Validation Enabled« in »This may be a conflict«. Slednje izvirajo iz senčilnika sistemskega ogrodja, zato so le preštete, nikoli opozorilo ali napaka.\n  - Artefakt `smoke-log` se naloži vedno in ostane 7 dni. Vsi prehodi čez veliko datoteko uporabljajo `LC_ALL=C` in `grep -F`.\n  - Popravek v `ClassicEncoder` (Metal 3), od koder je večina vrstic, je naloga skupine C.\n- **ci:2 (delno) – build-ipa ne pusti več žetona za pisanje v `.git/config`.** Checkout v build-ipa ima `persist-credentials: false`. Noben korak tega posla ne potrebuje poverilnic za git: `git log` je lokalen, `gh` uporablja `GH_TOKEN`.\n- **critic:1 (del v CI) – dSYM vsakega builda ostane 90 dni.**\n  - Nov korak »Debug symbols (dSYM)« po gradnji Release zažene `xcrun dwarfdump --uuid` na binarni datoteki in na dSYM. Oba UUID-ja gresta v povzetek.\n  - Artefakt `AcuteCalc-<različica>-dSYM` ostane 90 dni, kolikor največ dovoli javni repozitorij. Ime nosi različico, ki jo poročilo o zrušitvi zapiše kot `app_version`.\n- **critic:3 – CI zažene build Release.**\n  - Ob pushu (main in oznake `v*`) in ob ročnem zagonu posel smoke-test zgradi še Release za simulator, preden se simulator zažene. Na PR ta dva koraka ne tečeta, ker je strežnikov xcode-27 malo.\n  - Po dimnem testu build Release namesti v nov vsebnik, ga zažene in počaka 30 s. Preverjanje pade, če proces ne živi več ali če je aplikacija zapisala napake (error ali fault). GPU timeoute obravnava enako kot dimni test. Če se simulator ne zažene ali namestitev ne uspe, sledi opozorilo s preskokom.\n  - `latest-release` čaka na smoke-test, zato build, ki se ne zažene, ne pride do naprav.\n- **Popravki po pregledu**\n  - Dimni test: ko `simctl launch` vrne napako (npr. 142, ko alarm po 300 s ustavi zastoj), se korak pod `bash -e` ne konča več takoj. Zapiše povzetek, izpiše `::error::` s statusom, zadnjih 200 vrstic konzole, dnevnik simulatorja in poročila o zrušitvah. Uspeh in neuspeh sta enaka kot na main.\n  - Posel smoke-test ima 45 minut namesto 25. Prvi pregled je omejitev dvignil na 30 minut, samodejni pregled (cubic) pa je pokazal, da to za počasen push ne zadošča (zaveza 44ff79c). Korak »Launch the Release build« ima 15 minut namesto 10, `simctl uninstall` v njem pa omejitev 60 s.\n  - Trije koraki, ki le zbirajo diagnostiko (»Debug symbols (dSYM)«, »Upload the debug symbols« in »Upload the smoke test's console«), imajo `continue-on-error: true`. Če kateri od njih ne uspe, gresta IPA in izdaja vseeno naprej.\n\n## Zakaj (viri)\n\n- **ci:0.** Nočni zagon 42362489908 je padel v izbirniku (`ValueError: … 'iPhone19'`), korak pa je javil le »No ipad simulator on this runner«. `read … <<< \"$(…)\"` namreč izgubi izhodni status cevovoda. PR #41 je zrušitev popravil, ta PR doda oba ostanka iz preverjanja ugotovitve.\n  - https://github.com/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/actions/runs/42362489908\n  - https://www.gnu.org/software/bash/manual/html_node/The-Set-Builtin.html\n  - https://www.gnu.org/software/bash/manual/html_node/Command-Substitution.html\n- **ci:4.** Stari izbirnik je imena izvajalnih okolij razvrstil kot besedilo in vzel zadnji iPad. Na obeh slikah strežnika je bil to iPad (A16), iOS pa se je z 27.0 na 27.2 premaknil brez zapisa v dnevniku (zagona 40966569673 in 42403152951). Apple za Xcode 27.x podpira simulatorje »iOS 17 or later«.\n  - https://developer.apple.com/support/xcode/\n  - https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/workflow-commands (`GITHUB_ENV`)\n  - https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/contexts (`steps.<id>.outcome`)\n- **ci:3.** V zagonu 42403152951 je imel dnevnik posla 741 447 vrstic (64 MB). Skoraj vse so opozorila preverjanja API-ja Metal (`MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1`, `MTL_DEBUG_LAYER_WARNING_MODE=nslog`). Korak je od tega izpisal le prvih pet vrstic z besedo »validation«, brez besedila opozoril. Štirje prehodi z grep so trajali okoli 2 min 14 s. Vrstice »This may be a conflict« (`coverage_tex[0]`) niso iz senčilnikov aplikacije.\n  - https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcode/validating-your-apps-metal-api-usage\n  - https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/workflow-commands (»Adding a job summary«)\n  - https://github.com/actions/upload-artifact (v7, ista glavna različica kot v #42)\n- **ci:2.** Posel build-ipa podeduje `contents: write` in poganja kodo iz PR (xcodebuild, `scripts/altsource.py`). Privzeti checkout pusti žeton v `.git/config` do konca posla.\n  - https://github.com/actions/checkout (`persist-credentials`)\n  - https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/github_token-reference\n- **critic:1.** Xcode je ustvaril `AcuteCalc.app.dSYM`, a ga noben korak ni shranil. Brez njega da poročilo o zrušitvi z naprave največ imena funkcij, brez datotek, vrstic in vgrajenih okvirjev. Nov build ga ne nadomesti: druga različica Xcode ali druge nastavitve dajo drug UUID.\n  - https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcode/building-your-app-to-include-debugging-information (»Keep the dSYM files for the specific builds you distribute«)\n  - https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcode/locating-a-missing-debug-symbol-file (`dwarfdump --uuid`)\n  - https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcode/adding-identifiable-symbol-names-to-a-crash-report\n- **critic:3.** CI je gradil in zaganjal le Debug. Samodejno preverjanje posodobitev ob zagonu in njegovo okno tečeta le v Release (`checksAutomatically` je v Debug `false`).\n  - https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcode/testing-a-release-build\n- **Popravki po pregledu.** GitHub zažene korak brez nastavitve `shell` kot `bash -e {0}`. Posla smoke-test sta na PR trajala 22,1 in 22,7 minute (zagona 42414751023 in 40963513835), samo testi enot v prvem 668 s. Gradnja Release za napravo v build-ipa je v zadnjih 38 zagonih trajala 2,0–4,9 minute, korak »Launch the Release build« pa sme z lastnimi mejami trajati do 13,5 minute. Push na počasnem strežniku zato traja okoli 30 minut, s počasnim simulatorjem okoli 41.\n  - https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/workflow-syntax (`shell`, `timeout-minutes`, `continue-on-error`)\n\n## Kako je preverjeno\n\n- CI tega PR je tekel na 7735010 in ab842cd (po spojitvi maina s `actions/checkout@v7`). Uspeli so AcuteCore tests, Build unsigned IPA (`persist-credentials: false`; dSYM in program imata isti UUID 3B2B2DF5-9814-3B3C-8130-DC865A912FEE; artefakta `AcuteCalc-2.0.337-dSYM` in `AcuteCalc-unsigned-ipa`), »Download the IPA as the release does« in na 7735010 tudi Smoke test (14,1 min, iPad Pro 13-inch (M5)). Gradnja Release in njen zagon na pull requestu namenoma ne tečeta. Koda Swift in Metal se ni spremenila. Novih ali spremenjenih testov ni.\n- YAML: vse različice obeh delovnih tokov (main, ta veja, poskusna združitev s #42) se razčlenijo z ruamel.yaml. ID-ji korakov so edinstveni.\n- Zaščiteni deli so bajt za bajtom enaki kot na main: `on`, `concurrency`, `env`, `permissions`, posel core-tests, koraka »Version« in »Build (Release, iphoneos, unsigned)« ter vse od »Package IPA« do konca (nalaganje IPA, objava oznake, `latest-release`). Vrstice `upload-artifact@v5` in `download-artifact@v5` so nespremenjene. Nova koraka za nalaganje uporabljata `@v7`, kot #42.\n- `bash -n` na vseh 30 blokih `run:`.\n- Ponovitve pod `bash -e`, kot na strežniku, z lažnim `xcrun`:\n  - dimni test, main proti tej veji, 18 primerov: prava konzola zagona 42403152951, zrušitev, neuspela trditev, statusi 134, 139 in 142, brez `SMOKE DONE`, prazna konzola, napake v dnevniku, 1 in 3 GPU timeouti. Uspeh in neuspeh sta povsod enaka. Dnevnik posla za pravo konzolo pade s 740 454 na 57 vrstic;\n  - »Launch the Release build«, 9 primerov: enaki rezultati kot pred popravki po pregledu;\n  - izbirnika (build.yml in Screenshots) na 98 datotekah JSON za obe sliki strežnika, med njimi vseh 24 vrstnih redov okolij nove slike: iPad Pro 13-inch (M5) na iOS-27-2 (na stari sliki iOS-27-0). Pri `-d iphone` na novi sliki iPhone 18 Pro Max, na stari iPhone Duo (glej »Opaženo, a ne spremenjeno«). Brez iPada `::error::`, pokvarjen JSON konča korak s sledjo klicev.\n- Poskusna združitev s #42 (`git merge-tree`) je brez sporov. Po njej so vsa nalaganja `@v7`.\n- `eol_check.py` je v redu: vse tri datoteke so ostale LF. `git diff --check` je čist.\n- Dva neodvisna pregleda (CI in vedenje) nista našla blokirajoče napake. Njune potrjene ugotovitve so v zavezah 5ccf077, 17b4ac7 in 7735010.\n- Samodejni pregled (cubic in Sourcery) je dal šest pripomb. Omejitev posla smoke-test je popravljena v 44ff79c, ki spremeni le vrednost `timeout-minutes` in komentar nad njo, zamiki so enaki. Ostalih pet pripomb ne spremeni ničesar:\n  - dve (neberljiv dnevnik v koraku »Launch the Release build« da le opozorilo) opisujeta namerno vedenje, enako kot pri dnevniku v dimnem testu;\n  - dve ne držita: korak dimnega testa ima `set -uo pipefail`, zato `SMOKE_STATUS` dobi status `simctl`; ponovni zagon pa artefakta z istim imenom ne zavrne, ampak ga naloži kot novega;\n  - ena (nezaščiten `simctl boot`) velja za vrstico, ki je enaka kot na main, in ostaja odločitev lastnika (glej »Opaženo, a ne spremenjeno«).\n\nKaj mora pokazati CI na tem PR:\n- **Smoke test (iPad simulator):**\n  - »Pick the iPad simulator« izpiše `Using iPad Pro 13-inch (M5) on iOS-27-2 (…)`.\n  - Testi aplikacije tečejo na tem iPadu, v enakem številu kot na osnovi (na e6300a8: 156 vrstic `✔`, 42 vrstic `Suite … passed after` in »Test Execute Succeeded«).\n  - Dimni test: v dnevniku posla le vrstice `SMOKE …` (okoli 60 vrstic), v povzetku razpredelnica »Smoke test console« s števili, največ 2 GPU timeouta.\n  - Artefakt `smoke-log`.\n  - »Build for the simulator (Release)« in »Launch the Release build« sta na PR namenoma preskočena.\n- **Build unsigned IPA (iOS 27 SDK):**\n  - Checkout izpiše `persist-credentials: false` in skupino »Removing auth«.\n  - Povzetek »Debug symbols of Acute Calc 2.0.<run>« z enakima UUID-jema binarne datoteke in dSYM.\n  - Artefakt `AcuteCalc-2.0.<run>-dSYM` z datoteko `AcuteCalc.app.dSYM/Contents/Resources/DWARF/AcuteCalc`.\n- **Screenshots (ipad):** zažene se sam, ker se je spremenil `screenshots.yml`. Izpiše `Using iPad Pro 13-inch (M5) (…)` in uspe.\n\nPred spojitvijo je potreben en ročni zagon na tej veji: `gh workflow run build.yml --ref pregled/ci`. V njem morata biti zelena »Build for the simulator (Release)« in »Launch the Release build«, z vrsticama `com.markplacer.acutecalc: <pid>` in »The Release build is still running after 30 s« ter brez napak. Posel smoke-test naj traja manj kot okoli 20 minut. Brez tega zagona tečeta koraka Release prvič šele na main, kjer bi napaka zadržala `latest-release`.\n\nLe napravi lahko pokažeta simbolizacijo prave zrušitve in build Release s potjo Metal 4 (glej »Ročni test na napravi«).\n\n## Tveganja\n\n- **Koraka Release.** Na PR ne tečeta. Napako v njiju pokaže šele ročni zagon ali push na main, kjer bi zadržala izdajo.\n- **Večji simulator.** iPad Pro 13-inch (M5) riše okoli 47 % več pikslov kot iPad (A16). Dimni test pade pri več kot dveh GPU timeoutih; v zagonu 42403152951 je bil eden. Če jih bo več, lahko lastnik namenoma izbere iPad (A16).\n- **Čas posla.** Ocena: na PR okoli 1–2 minuti hitreje kot doslej (hitrejši prehodi z grep), ob pushu okoli 13–19 minut. Na počasnem strežniku do okoli 30 minut, s počasnim simulatorjem v koraku Release do okoli 41 minut, zato je omejitev 45 minut. Posel, ki obvisi v koraku brez lastne omejitve (obe gradnji), pa zdaj zasede strežnik do 20 minut dlje kot na main.\n- **`continue-on-error`.** Po prehodni napaki storitve artefaktov ali `dwarfdump` je tak build izdan brez dSYM ali brez konzole v artefaktu. Če lastnik raje zadrži izdajo, naj odstrani tri vrstice `continue-on-error: true`.\n- **BSD namesto GNU.** Cevovod povzetka je preizkušen le z GNU sed, sort in grep. Razlika na macOS lahko vpliva le na besedilo povzetka (`|| true`), ne na uspeh ali neuspeh.\n- **Izhodni status.** Ko `simctl launch` vrne napako, se korak zdaj konča s statusom 1 namesto s statusom simctl. Status je v vrstici `::error::`.\n\n## Opaženo, a ne spremenjeno\n\n- **ci:0, izbira po rangu.** Pri `-d iphone` izbirnik v Screenshots vzame najboljši iPhone najnovejšega iOS. Če je najnovejše izvajalno okolje iOS samo za iPhone Duo in ima navadno ime, kot iOS 27.1 na sliki 20261026.0314.1, izbere iPhone Duo namesto iPhona Pro Max. Na današnji sliki izbere iPhone 18 Pro Max. Navodilo skupine je zajelo le dva ostanka ci:0, zato izbira po rangu (najprej naprava, nato najnovejši iOS) ostaja odločitev lastnika. Poti iPhone ni preveril še noben zagon: `gh workflow run screenshots.yml --ref pregled/ci -f device=iphone -f scenes=graphs`.\n- **Zagon simulatorja v dimnem testu.** `limit 120 xcrun simctl boot \"$DEVICE\"` ni zaščiten. Pod `bash -e` prvi zagon, daljši od 120 s, konča korak z napako, čeprav komentar obljublja opozorilo s preskokom. Z iPadom (A16) je zagon trajal 25–111 s. Popravek bi bil `|| true` (sledi `bootstatus -b`), a napako spremeni v preskok dimnega testa, zato odloči lastnik.\n- **ci:2, del za izdajo (odločitev lastnika):** `permissions: contents: read` na ravni delovnega toka, objava oznake v svojem poslu z `GH_REPO`, izrecni `contents: write` za `latest-release` in `persist-credentials: false` na njegovem checkoutu. Checkout v `screenshots.yml` (žeton le za branje) je zunaj koraka te skupine.\n- **ci:5:** pogoj `always() && …` za `latest-release`, da ga preklic ne prekine sredi objave (odločitev lastnika).\n- **critic:1:** dSYM kot zip ob izdaji (dlje kot 90 dni) ter MetricKit ali izvoz OSLogStore v aplikaciji (nove funkcije).\n- **critic:3, neobvezno:** odpiranje zavihkov z `acutecalc://…` v buildu Release in dimni test pod `-O`.\n- **critic:4:** zahtevana preverjanja v pravilih veje so odločitev lastnika. Imena poslov so ostala enaka.\n- Sporočilo zaveze 05973f6 ne navaja dokumentacije. Viri za ci:0 so zgoraj.\n\n## Ročni test na napravi\n\nTa PR ne spremeni aplikacije, IPA se gradi enako kot doslej. Na iPhonu 15 Pro Max in iPadu Pro 13 (M5):\n1. Po spojitvi in naslednji izdaji posodobi aplikacijo v AltStore, SideStore, Feather ali eSign. Aplikacija se odpre normalno. CI zažene build Release le na simulatorju, z Metal 3, zato pot Metal 4 preveri le naprava.\n2. Če se aplikacija kdaj zruši, preveri, ali se poročilo simbolizira:\n   - V Nastavitvah odpri Privacy & Security › Analytics & Improvements › Analytics Data (imena v angleščini) in poišči `AcuteCalc-….ips`.\n   - `app_version` (2.0.<run>) pove, kateri artefakt `AcuteCalc-2.0.<run>-dSYM` preneseš iz zagona Build. UUID slike AcuteCalc v `usedImages` se mora ujemati z UUID-jem v povzetku posla build-ipa. V poročilu je lahko zapisan z malimi črkami in brez vezajev.\n   - Na Windows z LLVM: `llvm-symbolizer --obj=AcuteCalc.app.dSYM/Contents/Resources/DWARF/AcuteCalc 0x…`, kjer je naslov 0x100000000 + `imageOffset` okvirja.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nHarden CI simulator validation and release verification while preserving diagnostics needed to investigate failures and symbolicate crashes.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add Release-build launch validation on push and manual CI runs to ensure the app remains running and does not emit application errors.\n- Provide retained smoke-test console artifacts and condensed job summaries for diagnosing simulator failures.\n- Preserve and publish per-build dSYM artifacts for crash-report symbolication.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Make iPad simulator selection deterministic on the newest available iOS and fail when no iPad is available instead of silently skipping app tests.\n- Surface simulator-picker Python tracebacks and relevant screen-test failure diagnostics instead of misleading fallback errors.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Reuse the selected iPad across unit and smoke tests and improve smoke-test failure handling, logging, and timeout behavior.\n\nBuild:\n- Disable persisted checkout credentials in the IPA build job.\n\nCI:\n- Extend smoke-test capacity for slower runners while keeping diagnostic uploads non-blocking.\n\n\n___\n\n## **CodeAnt-AI Description**\n**Make iPad CI checks reliable and verify Release launches**\n\n### What Changed\n- App tests use the same iPad on the newest available iOS version, and CI fails if no iPad simulator is available instead of silently skipping the tests.\n- Push and manual runs build and launch the Release app, failing if it exits early or logs app errors. Pull requests continue to run the Debug checks.\n- The full smoke-test console is saved as a 7-day artifact, while the job summary shows condensed output; failures include the end of the console for diagnosis.\n- Release debug symbols are saved for 90 days so crash reports from that build can be symbolicated.\n- Simulator-picker failures now show their traceback instead of a misleading “No iPad simulator” message.\n\n### Impact\n`✅ No silent app-test skips when an iPad simulator is unavailable`\n`✅ Release launch failures detected in push and manual runs`\n`✅ Crash reports can be symbolicated for 90 days`\n<details><summary><strong>💡 Usage Guide</strong></summary>\n\n### Checking Your Pull Request\nEvery time you make a pull request, our system automatically looks through it. We check for security issues, mistakes in how you're setting up your infrastructure, and common code problems. We do this to make sure your changes are solid and won't cause any trouble later.\n\n### Talking to CodeAnt AI\nGot a question or need a hand with something in your pull request? You can easily get in touch with CodeAnt AI right here. Just type the following in a comment on your pull request, and replace \"Your question here\" with whatever you want to ask:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Your question here</code>\n</pre>\nThis lets you have a chat with CodeAnt AI about your pull request, making it easier to understand and improve your code.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Can you suggest a safer alternative to storing this secret?</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Preserve Org Learnings with CodeAnt\nYou can record team preferences so CodeAnt AI applies them in future reviews. Reply directly to the specific CodeAnt AI suggestion (in the same thread) and replace \"Your feedback here\" with your input:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Your feedback here</code>\n</pre>\nThis helps CodeAnt AI learn and adapt to your team's coding style and standards.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Do not flag unused imports.</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Retrigger review\nAsk CodeAnt AI to review the PR again, by typing:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: review</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Check Your Repository Health\nTo analyze the health of your code repository, visit our dashboard at [https://app.codeant.ai](https://app.codeant.ai). This tool helps you identify potential issues and areas for improvement in your codebase, ensuring your repository maintains high standards of code health.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Improved automated app checks across available iPad simulators, with longer smoke-test and launch monitoring.\n  * Expanded failure reporting and saved diagnostic logs to help identify build, launch, and validation issues.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/issues/48/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarkPLacer/AcuteCalc/issues/48/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebookresearch/faiss/issues/5851","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebookresearch/faiss","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebookresearch/faiss/issues/5851/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebookresearch/faiss/issues/5851/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebookresearch/faiss/issues/5851/events","html_url":"https://github.com/facebookresearch/faiss/pull/5851","id":6236911849,"node_id":"PR_kwDOBNds_c8AAAABNO8rRQ","number":5851,"title":"Add MetalIndexIVFScalarQuantizer with GPU search and exact top-k selection","user":{"login":"Evandabest","id":145516605,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKxoPQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145516605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Evandabest","html_url":"https://github.com/Evandabest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Evandabest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Evandabest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Evandabest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Evandabest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Evandabest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Evandabest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Evandabest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Evandabest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Evandabest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":534246448,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1MzQyNDY0NDg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebookresearch/faiss/labels/CLA%20Signed","name":"CLA Signed","color":"009900","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-06T04:47:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:00:11Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebookresearch/faiss/pulls/5851","html_url":"https://github.com/facebookresearch/faiss/pull/5851","diff_url":"https://github.com/facebookresearch/faiss/pull/5851.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/facebookresearch/faiss/pull/5851.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds IVF scalar-quantizer search to the Metal backend.\n\n- Support `QT_8bit` and `QT_fp16`, L2/IP, and residual and non-residual encoding\n- Add exact GPU top-k selection through `k <= 512`, with ties ordered by 64-bit label\n- Support GPU scanning and eligible flat coarse-quantizer searches\n- Add CPU↔Metal cloning through the existing C++ and Python paths\n- Retain CPU training, encoding, reconstruction, and fallback\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add `MetalIndexIVFScalarQuantizer` and reusable, geometrically grown list/search buffers\n- Add parallel list/chunk scanning and exact GPU result merging in the compiled Metal kernels\n- Extend the Metal cloner, Python bridge, header installation, CMake, and CI targets\n- Add direct-GPU correctness, fallback, cloning, ownership, and fault-injection coverage\n\n## Scope and limitations\n\nGPU search requires nonnegative labels, representable kernel counts, and buffers within device limits. Unsupported codecs and search controls use CPU search with the original parameters. Failures after GPU execution is selected raise exceptions.\n\nRoot flat quantizers use GPU coarse search for `nlist >= 128` and `nprobe <= 512`; other coarse searches remain on CPU. Floating-point accumulation and coarse tie ordering can produce different labels from CPU search.\n\nCloning owns supported FlatCodes/HNSW quantizer storage, including PreTransform/IDMap wrappers. Unsupported quantizer structures and borrowed clustering dependencies are rejected. Search and mutation on an individual index must be serialized.\n\n## Planned follow-up PRs\n\nAdditional scalar formats (`QT_8bit_uniform`, `QT_8bit_direct`, `QT_4bit`, `QT_4bit_uniform`, and `QT_6bit`) and further scan/selection work remain follow-up scope.\n\n## Build and test\n\n```bash\ncmake -B build \\\n  -DFAISS_ENABLE_GPU=OFF \\\n  -DFAISS_ENABLE_METAL=ON \\\n  -DFAISS_ENABLE_PYTHON=ON \\\n  -DBUILD_TESTING=ON \\\n  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \\\n  -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=\"$(brew --prefix libomp)\" \\\n  .\n\ncmake --build build \\\n  --target faiss faiss_metal swigfaiss \\\n           TestMetalIndexIVFSQ TestMetalIVFSQFailures \\\n  -j$(sysctl -n hw.logicalcpu)\n\nOMP_NUM_THREADS=5 MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1 MTL_SHADER_VALIDATION=1 \\\n  ctest --test-dir build -R TestMetalIndexIVFSQ --output-on-failure\n```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebookresearch/faiss/issues/5851/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebookresearch/faiss/issues/5851/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlexaDeWit/Ecluse/issues/55","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlexaDeWit/Ec