y":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/atedeg/mdm/issues/21/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrossGL/crosstl/issues/1542","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrossGL/crosstl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrossGL/crosstl/issues/1542/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrossGL/crosstl/issues/1542/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrossGL/crosstl/issues/1542/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CrossGL/crosstl/issues/1542","id":4864461292,"node_id":"I_kwDOL2TxDs8AAAABIfHJ7A","number":1542,"title":"Represent source dispatch-grid extents on targets without a native builtin","user":{"login":"NripeshN","id":86844847,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2ODQ0ODQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86844847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NripeshN","html_url":"https://github.com/NripeshN","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NripeshN/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NripeshN/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NripeshN/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NripeshN/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NripeshN/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NripeshN/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NripeshN/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NripeshN/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NripeshN/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":6900563137,"node_id":"LA_kwDOL2TxDs8AAAABm048wQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrossGL/crosstl/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or improvement","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":7353768002,"node_id":"LA_kwDOL2TxDs8AAAABtlGYQg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrossGL/crosstl/labels/backend:hlsl","name":"backend:hlsl","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"DirectX HLSL","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12760416160,"node_id":"LA_kwDOL2TxDs8AAAAC-JR_oA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrossGL/crosstl/labels/area:runtime","name":"area:runtime","color":"1d76db","default":false,"description":"Native loaders, runtimes and execution checks","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2026-07-11T22:46:07Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T16:06:56Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T16:06:56Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\nSource compute entry points can request the total dispatch grid extent, but some target APIs expose only invocation, group, and local identifiers to shader code. The current translation path emits the source grid-extent parameter as an ordinary HLSL function parameter without a system semantic or host-supplied binding. The generated entry therefore has no valid value for that parameter.\n\nRepresentative source:\n\n```metal\nkernel void fill(\n    device uint* out [[buffer(0)]],\n    uint3 index [[thread_position_in_grid]],\n    uint3 grid [[threads_per_grid]]) {\n  out[index.x] = grid.x;\n}\n```\n\nThe total grid extent is part of the source execution contract. Deriving it from `SV_DispatchThreadID` or substituting a constant would be incorrect.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n- Represent total dispatch dimensions as a backend-neutral entry-point input distinct from invocation and workgroup size.\n- Map the value to a native shader builtin where one exists.\n- For targets such as Direct3D/HLSL without an equivalent builtin, materialize an explicit host-bound constant/uniform with deterministic binding metadata.\n- Populate runtime manifests and dispatch plans with the required grid dimensions so adapters can bind the exact values used for launch.\n- Preserve dimensionality and distinguish logical grid extent from group counts, local size, and rounded-up physical dispatch dimensions.\n- Emit a structured capability or missing-runtime-binding diagnostic when the required value cannot be supplied.\n- Never emit an unannotated entry parameter or infer the value from a single invocation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Reduced one-, two-, and three-dimensional fixtures compile with DXC and read the host-supplied total grid extent correctly.\n- Non-divisible logical extents with rounded-up dispatch groups preserve the logical source value.\n- Entry-point reflection records the synthetic binding, source builtin identity, type, and target register/location.\n- Runtime-test planning supplies the binding from dispatch geometry without source-specific logic.\n- Vulkan, OpenGL, Metal, CUDA, HIP, WGSL, and other targets use the same execution-input contract and either select a native builtin or the explicit binding path.\n- Missing or contradictory dispatch geometry produces a deterministic, source-located diagnostic.\n- A native execution/readback test verifies that the shader observes the expected grid extent.\n\n## Real-world impact\n\nAt MLX commit `968d264f2903d578e699c4452a4dbf48633921aa`, `random.metal` uses `threads_per_grid`. The generated DirectX artifact carries the grid extent as an ordinary entry parameter, so it is excluded from the DXC-validated frontier even though the rest of the kernel materializes.\n\n## Related work\n\n- #1388 covers general runtime dispatch metadata and binding contracts; this issue defines the missing source execution input and its target representation.\n- #1523 covers entry-point-scoped packaging after the required grid binding is represented.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrossGL/crosstl/issues/1542/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrossGL/crosstl/issues/1542/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Emaren/wolochain/issues/239","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Emaren/wolochain","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Emaren/wolochain/issues/239/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Emaren/wolochain/issues/239/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Emaren/wolochain/issues/239/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Emaren/wolochain/issues/239","id":6294867122,"node_id":"I_kwDOOxFNbM8AAAABdzQMsg","number":239,"title":"CENTRAL SCORECARD — close the final 7 real WoloChain production gates; no source-only PASS","user":{"login":"Emaren","id":15059910,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDU5OTEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15059910?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Emaren","html_url":"https://github.com/Emaren","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Emaren/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Emaren/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Emaren/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Emaren/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Emaren/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Emaren/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Emaren/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Emaren/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Emaren/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":39,"created_at":"2026-11-09T21:14:43Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T16:03:16Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# AoE2WAR — Seven-Gate Production Closure Scorecard (Central Command)\n\n**Owner: Central Command. Last physically checked: 2026-11-09 21:11 UTC.** This is a single short gate scoreboard rather than another open-ended engineering thread. Canonical detailed receipts stay in Chain #5 and App #1212. Only update this issue when evidence materially changes a gate or a next-action owner.\n\n**Formal release: 2/9 closed (C04, C08), seven OPEN. No funded deployment permission.** Work is substantial but source CI is not production gate closure. No chain reset, WOLO transfer, payout, legacy 8092/8093 fallback or imaginary second validator.\n\n## Latest GitHub and host anchors\n- Chain PR #238 (C05 private same-hash/cross-hash evidence classifiers) MERGED into held source branch at b7c86c05a185f21feb96d590a6ddb935c34ca606; all 11 listed CI checks passed. Root-only independent PG snapshot and private manifests exist. This is investigation tooling, not C05 financial acceptance.\n- App PR #1279 V18 retained R25 admission currently OPEN at b10ea7005d02c93746e5ef64ced0756bab0c4587, four listed CI checks PASS. Session B owns exact-head merge, physical retained cutover, Chrome auth role tests and accepted rollback.\n- Live HEL1: original restricted website port3032 PID378804; /api/bets HTTP500, /api/bets/public-live HTTP404, public-history HTTP200. Validator PID1009; both new C01 financial units inactive, both /etc/wolo-financial-c01/{custody,reviewer}.json absent; all 8092–8095 listeners closed. Old HD/DE roles retain 190/52 public table ownership from last independent census.\n\n## Binary gate decisions and next physical operations\n| Gate | Owner | Status | Exactly what must be physically accepted next |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| C01 custody | Chain Codex | OPEN | Exact two-role production config and credential enrollment, source-pinned immutable service authority, private network admission, wrong-key/nonce/expiry/revocation denial, off-host recovery. One HUMAN owner; technical reviewer role is not a second human. |\n| C02 transport | Chain + B | OPEN | Source-matched App→reviewer8095→Satchel8094 nonfunded original-operation journal, POST once, timeout/UNKNOWN GET-only, no duplicate credit, no 8092/8093 fallback; real bounded physical receipts. |\n| C03 exclusive writer | Chain + B | OPEN | B delivers physically retained authenticated 3032 R25 and reversible Steam V18 acceptance; Chain executes then proves live full HD 190 tables + 180 seq + 39 functions and DE 52 tables + 50 seq ownership/ACL writer fence, including preconnected old-role denials and rollback. |\n| C05 solvency | Chain Codex | OPEN | Consume PRIVATE two-manifest C05 adjudication (97 unindexed, reused same-hash and cross-hash cases, claim822 and UNKNOWN) without auto-waiver, sign disjoint economic liability scope, prove bank+real pledge+unencumbered new-vault control and margin at fixed height. Gross labeled wallet balances not collateral. |\n| C06 off-host backup | Chain Codex | OPEN | After coordinated financial-only writer freeze, capture complete consistent HD/DE+WAL+Chain+journals+nonce+role/authority state with encrypted Intel recipient and exact SHA/length/checkpoint proof; no permanent omission of large tables. |\n| C07 exact restore | Chain Codex | OPEN | Isolated Intel restore of the EXACT C06 ciphertext manifest; verify row counts, all ACLs/seq, native state/nonce/UNKNOWN, corrupt/partial archive denial and no public financial network exposure. |\n| C09 funded canary | Chain + human owner | OPEN | Only after other acceptance: fresh canonical ≤1 WOLO bounded operation permit, EXACT owner local signature for that recipient/amount/fee/nonce/expiry, one at-most-once broadcast via native reviewer/Satchel, chain finality + one ledger credit + replay denial. |\n\n## Work ownership and no-drifts\n- Chain Codex A: only financial source, services, DB ownership, private liability evidence, reserves, backup/restore and final signed canary. Temporary reversible controls are allowed for testing; final operational solution must be durable.\n- Session B: App R25/Steam V18, authenticated browser acceptance, website rollback, App-side C02 transport; no financial DML/owner or custody mutation.\n- Session C (user-operated): Kingdom Traders + frontend/watch only on separate branches, no shared financial credentials, no website runtime overlap with B's cutover.\n- Central Command: GitHub and HEL1 independent verification, this scoreboard, explicit handoff contract, next physical blocker. Avoid repeating tests/commments that do not change next-action decisions.\n\n## Exit rules\n1. An OPEN gate becomes CLOSED only when **source SHA + installed config/binary/role identity + real positive and negative physical receipts + rollback** are accepted in its owner lane.\n2. Observability is a permanent feature (systemd/timers, signed receipts, indexed operation IDs, backups, alerts), but do not insert unrelated work into the canary critical path.\n3. A standalone website/paper-only Kingdom Traders deployment may proceed while all seven Chain gates are held. No financial bet placement, bot exchange orders or wallet actions from a held release.\n4. For every substantial handoff, update just the exact rows changed and list a named next EXECUTION operation, not another PR-only status.\n\n## Current execution order\nB: physically retain b1ef R25 with V18 and prove authenticated rollback. In parallel A: C01 signer/reviewer restricted enrollment plus C05 liability and pledged-collateral evidence. After B handoff A: coordinated financial writer pause → C06 complete encrypted capture → C07 exact restore → C03 permanent live writer fence. A+B: C02 genuine native private transport. Last: C09 fresh-owner-signed bounded canary.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Emaren/wolochain/issues/239/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Emaren/wolochain/issues/239/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanleyrya/chunky-dad/issues/1936","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanleyrya/chunky-dad","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanleyrya/chunky-dad/issues/1936/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanleyrya/chunky-dad/issues/1936/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanleyrya/chunky-dad/issues/1936/events","html_url":"https://github.com/stanleyrya/chunky-dad/pull/1936","id":6310644737,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPIA9i88AAAABOJjD2w","number":1936,"title":"Keep bear and leather; strangers, junk and false gone cards out","user":{"login":"stanleyrya","id":8700100,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MDAxMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8700100?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanleyrya","html_url":"https://github.com/stanleyrya","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanleyrya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanleyrya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanleyrya/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanleyrya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanleyrya/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanleyrya/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanleyrya/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanleyrya/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stanleyrya/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T16:02:01Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T16:02:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanleyrya/chunky-dad/pulls/1936","html_url":"https://github.com/stanleyrya/chunky-dad/pull/1936","diff_url":"https://github.com/stanleyrya/chunky-dad/pull/1936.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/stanleyrya/chunky-dad/pull/1936.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What this is\n\nOne wave from the 2026-11-09 review of every scraped site against the calendar: what gets kept, why strangers' events were being kept as bear, and where the scrape itself was wrong. Seven fix clusters, each built and measured against run `20261109-053706` offline, merged here as one PR.\n\nState before this PR (run 20261109-053706): 1,304 kept, 1,945 dropped. Kept by reason: keyword 574, owner verdict 249, AI 219, tag only 195, none 66.\n\n## What is kept\n\n- **Only leather, bear-crowd and bear-run keep a not-bear event.** The other machine tags (kink, rubber, pup, drag, underwear, diaper) still describe an event but no longer keep it. About 110 events stop being kept.\n- **A bear run in a destination town keeps everything in its window.** `destination: true` on the city config. **Draft list, yours to correct:** palm-springs, sitges, ptown, pv, fire-island, gran-canaria. A bear run in a big city keeps nothing by itself.\n- **A leather night held for another crowd is not kept.** New `audience-check` AI question, asked only where the leather tag alone keeps the event.\n- **`gear` names leather only in a title.**\n- **An aggregator row the model itself is unsure about, with no bear evidence, goes to the Not-bear pile.**\n- **A stored bear verdict with no tags gets machine tags** (description only; stored not-bear and stored tagged are untouched).\n\n## Why strangers were kept as bear (promoter evidence)\n\n- A parser's promoter is inherited only by records read on the parser's own sites, or on the ticket page one of its rows led to. Two Tons of Fun: 265 of 273 records no longer inherit.\n- Every promoter stamp says how it was earned (`organizer`, `title`, `url`, `parser-site`).\n- **Prompt change, measured.** The bear check used to tell the model \"this event's own content names X\" for every stamp. It now says that only for a title or organizer match; a URL match reads \"page address or links belong to X\", an inherited stamp reads \"found through the website of X\". Replayed on the 211 cached events whose promoter is not named in their own text: 193 / 176 stay bear, 4 / 21 move to not-bear, all strangers' listings (12 Two Tons of Fun workshops and talks, 7 Toucans drag shows stamped Furball, 1 trans night stamped Bear it MTL, 1 Crown & Anchor drag show). No promoter's own party moved.\n- A listing's promoter is not an event's identity: Folsom Europe folds 110 to 108 records (was 110 to 86, 22 false folds).\n\n## Where the crawl went (crawl scope)\n\n- An off-site page reached by a link speaks for the source only when it names the source or links back. A ticket vendor's bare home page is never requested.\n- A ticket link is read only when the source's own allowlist would keep its page (whereto.party: 31 ticket links no longer followed).\n- **Social networks are never requested, not even at the end of a redirect.** The Mac adapter now walks redirects by hand (max 20) and refuses the hop. Found while fixing: `facebook.com/robots.txt` was requested on 2026-11-08 and an Instagram body was cached under another host. The phone adapter cannot see redirect hops yet.\n- Entity-encoded addresses are decoded; a relative or off-domain canonical is never an alias.\n- A crawled page that only the month-count guess calls a listing, that the model would not call one, and that read as no events hands the crawl nothing. Its links are the site's menu. Fired 6 times in the replay, all correct (a terms page, a plugin vendor, a JS library site, a builder temp domain, a widget-only events page, one detail page).\n- Known cost: the real \"Sitges BEAR WEEK Pool Party 2026\" on a bare off-site root is now withheld.\n\n## Finished events proposed as new (past records)\n\n- A record that is already over and would be NEW is withheld when it is an aggregator copy, kept only for a tag, or from a feed's own past list. 214 such proposals in today's run (Gathr 102, Folsom Europe 35, Bears of SF 29).\n- Saved runs now keep `siteRole`, so every aggregator rule also applies when the phone executes.\n- The ledger says how many new proposals are still to come.\n- The weekday check that pins a yearless date to its year no longer gives up when the same date is repeated elsewhere on the page with no weekday. A flyer's \"THU / JUNE 4TH\" held last June's Bear Jamboree parties in 2026; before, they rolled to a day in 2027 the page never names.\n\n## Feeds read wrong (feed fidelity)\n\n- Nights a feed cancelled or moved are not expanded (EXDATE / RECURRENCE-ID).\n- A street address typed after a row's name is the row's place (Lodge NY recovers 4 rows).\n- One calendar is read once per run; a page is the same page under http and https.\n- Nights of one party share its description: a blank night takes what the others agree on (73 in today's run), never a text two different parties share. **Watch the `📝 DESCRIPTION` lines on the next run.**\n- A bare calendar date is a day, not a midnight.\n\n## False \"gone\" cards (gone proof)\n\n- **The nine Eagle LA \"gone\" cards on the deck today are false.** Two month widgets shared one cache key since 2026-10-12. The key now names the widget.\n- \"Removed by the site\" needs proof: the event's own page answers 404/410, or a listing that covers that day no longer lists it. Otherwise the card is held.\n- A source the run could not read is \"not read\", never empty. A source that collapsed (5+ events down to 10%) holds its cards. Both show on /metrics.\n- Of today's removal cards, 3 are still raised and 16 are held.\n\n## Pages the reader gave up on (AI fallbacks)\n\n- The 500,000-character scan bound counts readable text, not template padding (GRUNT Season Closer: 0 events to 3; 166 of 177 oversized cached pages get their full body back).\n- A listing on the source's own site reached through a ticket link is read as a listing (Camp Out Poconos: 6 events were dropped as \"siblings\").\n- On a ticket page that lists several parties, a differently named party is a neighbour, never folded into the row (STANK.BK into Bear Belly).\n- A programme's day headings vote on its year, over the banner above them (Bears Sitges Week: last year's programme under a \"2027\" banner).\n- \"&\" and \"and\" are one word in place names; one night inside a saved multi-day event is that event and never rewrites its days (Bear Fuzz Fest).\n- Thirteen dates we made from one weekly feed row stay one series (The Bear Calendar \"Furry Friday\": 66 to 54 events).\n- Hours beside a weekday are not a date (\"TUE-SAT 4-6PM\" was pinned as a 2028 date).\n\n## Site furniture read as events (crawl junk)\n\n- The bear check and the tag match read the name the page stated, not only the trimmed title (`_statedTitles`).\n- A title tail is the bar only when it is the bar's name from its first word (\"Bears At The Beach\", \"Jocks at Jacques\" stay whole).\n- A city read from a word in a name yields to the curated door, the site and the page's home city. 12 kept records change city.\n- A lone crawl record with a guessed date never gives a field to a record whose page stated its date.\n- Menu labels, hours, bare numbers and byline fragments are not titles. A row's printed year is its stated year (13 Stud podcast rows from 2021 were walked forward).\n- `/form`, `/rsvp`, about-us, contact-us, team and staff pages are never followed. `currency` is a display selector like `lang`.\n- A row named only \"private event\" is a closure notice.\n- A sentence one venue prints word for word under three different parties is its standing line, never a tag candidate (149 records carry one; Dallas Eagle \"Our Leather Shop is Now Open!\").\n- Invisible marks are not part of a title. The Stud's site name is a lone direction mark, so 11 titles ended in \" — \" plus an invisible character. **A saved title that carries such a mark is rewritten to the clean name on the next merge, not withheld.**\n\n## Also\n\n- Browser route: the allowance is 20 pages per site with a run ceiling of 80 (it was 20 for the whole run; Folsom Europe starved Eagle Portland and Wilton Manors).\n\n## For the reviewer\n\n- **No new runtime files.** Existing phone files changed: `shared-core.js`, `ai-web-parser.js`, `normalizers.js`, `event-schema.js`, `scriptable-adapter.js`, `metrics-sections.js`, `bear-event-scraper-unified.js`.\n- The next run pays one-time AI cache misses (scan bound about 130 pages, Sitges about 37 windows, changed bear-check sentences).\n- The collapse hold is sticky until the source recovers; gone and date-moved cards become rare.\n- `npm test` flakes on Node 26.3 with \"Unable to deserialize cloned data\" on a random file, on main too. Every file passes when run directly: 35 files, 3,160 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## How it was checked\n\nAll 68 configured sources were replayed offline twice with the live local AI and the owner's verdict store: once on main, once on this branch. Main in the harness reproduces the real run (1,415 kept against 1,413), so the difference between the two replays is this PR. Counts are per-source records, before copies of one event from several sources fold, which is why they sit above the 1,304 in the run summary.\n\n| | kept | upcoming |\n|---|---|---|\n| real run 20261109-053706 | 1,413 | 935 |\n| main, replayed | 1,415 | 942 |\n| this branch, replayed | 1,055 | 725 |\n\nAbout 42 of the branch's drop is the harness, not the code: the Eagle LA month widget has a new cache key, so December onward is a cache miss and the offline guard blocks it. A live run reads those months.\n\nWhere the rest went: tag-only events for kink, rubber, pup, drag and underwear (Gathr 218 to 195, Dallas Eagle 15 to 9), leather nights for another crowd, strangers' events on promoter and venue pages (3 Dollar Bill 8 to 1, The Stud 15 to 7, Precinct 14 to 6), aggregator and past-list copies (Two Tons of Fun 119 to 4, whereto.party 47 to 5, Folsom Europe 46 to 23), and 35 Sitges Bears Week rows for 2027 that the page never stated.\n\nKnown gaps, not fixed here:\n\n- Bear Jamboree \"RED\" is dated June 2027 from a yearless \"JUNE 6\" on a page for the 2026 edition, and it lands in San Diego because \"House of Blues\" matches a curated bar by name alone. The page says Disney Springs.\n- An off-site bare root reached from a crawled page is still requested once to see whether it names the source (linktr.ee, a stats plugin vendor, a host's temp domain). Only a ticket vendor's bare home is never requested.\n- Precinct's calendar page now builds its events from the feed, so the crawl follows 12 of its 24 detail pages.\n- BLUF Toronto is not recognized as leather. One Crown & Anchor record has an empty title (styled Unicode letters are not normalized yet). Bear it MTL still reads sidebar dates.\n\n## Not built, owner calls\n\nBear-bar \"maybe\" path. Weak bear words deciding alone (daddy, jock, fat, beef, pup, pig). Venue-name-only keyword keeps. Stored verdicts are exact title + venue and per night. Extra tags (sportswear, country, naked, sex-party). Back-fill of first-party past nights (95 records, Two Tons of Fun 69). The 08:00 to 17:00 placeholder time. Candidate search window in the city's own timezone (85 \"creating override\" proposals per run). Restoring the corrupted festival rows for Bear Week Provincetown and Bear Pride Chicago. Cruises routed to a departure city. Article feeds read as one document (Bear World Magazine). Zero-event event pages after reclassification (74 today).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01QpPvhx88qaX3FdiLUqKKqP\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanleyrya/chunky-dad/issues/1936/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stanleyrya/chunky-dad/issues/1936/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector/issues/546","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector/issues/546/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector/issues/546/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector/issues/546/events","html_url":"https://github.com/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector/pull/546","id":5796909008,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEhr0ds8AAAABHwo6xQ","number":546,"title":"chore(deps): update dependency google-auth to v2.62.2","user":{"login":"renovate-bot","id":25180681,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MTgwNjgx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25180681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/renovate-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":2423000397,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNDIzMDAwMzk3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector/labels/kokoro:force-run","name":"kokoro:force-run","color":"C1FFB2","default":false,"description":"Add this label to force Kokoro to re-run the tests.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-11T01:20:21Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T16:01:40Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector/pulls/546","html_url":"https://github.com/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector/pull/546","diff_url":"https://github.com/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector/pull/546.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector/pull/546.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Change | [Age](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) | [Confidence](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [google-auth](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/tree/main/packages/google-auth) ([source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python)) | `==2.34.0` → `==2.62.2` | ![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/pypi/google-auth/2.62.2?slim=true) | ![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/pypi/google-auth/2.34.0/2.62.2?slim=true) |\n\n---\n\n### Release Notes\n\n<details>\n<summary>googleapis/google-cloud-python (google-auth)</summary>\n\n### [`v2.62.2`](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases/tag/google-auth-v2.62.2): google-auth: v2.62.2\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-auth-v2.62.1...google-auth-v2.62.2)\n\n##### Bug Fixes\n\n- **auth:** prevent