ned)\n- Automerge\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n\n🚦 **Automerge**: Disabled by config. Please merge this manually once you are satisfied.\n\n♻ **Rebasing**: Whenever PR becomes conflicted, or you tick the rebase/retry checkbox.\n\n🔕 **Ignore**: Close this PR and you won't be reminded about this update again.\n\n---\n\n - [ ] <!-- rebase-check -->If you want to rebase/retry this PR, check this box\n\n---\n\nThis PR was generated by [Mend Renovate](https://mend.io/renovate/). View the [repository job log](https://developer.mend.io/github/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector).\n<!--renovate-debug:eyJjcmVhdGVkSW5WZXIiOiI0NC4xMzQuMSIsInVwZGF0ZWRJblZlciI6IjQ0LjIyMi41IiwidGFyZ2V0QnJhbmNoIjoibWFpbiIsImxhYmVscyI6W119-->\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector/issues/546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/googleapis/proto-breaking-change-detector/issues/546/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2011","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2011/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2011/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2011/events","html_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/issues/2011","id":6289099331,"node_id":"I_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAABdtwKQw","number":2011,"title":"Ocarina of Time (0400486024DEC000 v131072, Mac M2 Pro): reproducible GPU hangs in NPC dialogue and the Impa escort — narrowed to Hi-Z task a5288d0a6c4971fd pipelines (mesh 3439aaa071d868ae / pixel bd09ab5fc4fd7680 light loop); c3[193] grid is sane","user":{"login":"pkimsey","id":4391552,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTE1NTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4391552?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pkimsey","html_url":"https://github.com/pkimsey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pkimsey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pkimsey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pkimsey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pkimsey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pkimsey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pkimsey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pkimsey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pkimsey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pkimsey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12938283270,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy6JBg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/mac","name":"mac","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"The Mac front end and app (dm/mac, front_mac.m)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12962853499,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADBKVyew","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/game:%200400486024DEC000","name":"game: 0400486024DEC000","color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"A game","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":12,"created_at":"2026-11-09T15:29:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T16:01:02Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T16:01:02Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"[vanilla-run2.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/34586002/vanilla-run2.log)\n[vanilla-impa.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/34586003/vanilla-impa.log)\n\n### Summary\nOn plain `main` (`eed7c42`) the game hangs the GPU (`kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorHang` → \"GPU access revoked\") **every time** at two story moments:\n1. **Kokiri Forest, early NPC conversation**: The girl sitting above the shop.  Right after the game prompts me to target her and I start talking, as the dialogue camera begins circling her. The frozen frame keeps the NPC drawn; the rest of the scene is gone.\n2. **Hyrule Castle, Impa escorting Link out after meeting Zelda.** Here the screen **flashes white a few seconds before the hang**.\n\nNot intermittent for me: 100% reproducible across ~20 runs and several builds. Related: #1843 (same pipeline found independently), #1830, #1326, #1756, #1788, #1690.\n\n### Setup\n- Apple M2 Pro (Mac14,12), macOS 26.6.2, Xcode 27.2, Metal compiler 32023.922\n- nxnative `eed7c42`, shader chain `094f939bfef9`, `build_ipa_from_nsp.py --platform mac-app --gpu g14s`, no env changes. Only local change: `shader_split.unzs` decompresses in-process, because the `zstd` subprocess pipe stalls the split at ~160,400 files under Python 3.15 on this Mac (doesn't change the app).\n- NUP: base v65536 + update v131072; all 203,786 `.zs` files checked (zstd signature + SHA-256), none damaged. (An earlier update-only NUP had 3 zero-filled textures; the clean dump hangs the same.)\n- Same hangs with `DM_UPSCALER=game` and `metalfx`, handheld mode.\n\n### Narrowing it down\nI added a small switch, `DM_NVN_SKIP_MESHKEYS=<key>[,…]`, in `mesh_tasks_draw` that drops task/mesh draws whose task, mesh or pixel key matches (`DM_NVN_SKIP_FS` doesn't apply to mesh draws, so #1756's planned test with it can't drop these).\n- `DM_NVN_SKIP_MESH=1` (all task/mesh draws off) → Kokiri conversation goes through.\n- Bisecting the task/mesh pipelines (49 in that scene) by key → **dropping only mesh `3439aaa071d868ae`** (task `a5288d0a6c4971fd`, pixel `bd09ab5fc4fd7680` / `7b0a886903a664b2`, `Model.Product.110 #BNSH@0x11543000`) prevents the Kokiri hang every time; every run that draws it hangs. That pipeline is first built a fraction of a second before the hang.\n- Dropping only `e8c667282ba7bd9b` + `d4171cf9adf0504b` (#1756's triple) → still hangs. Dropping only pixel `7b0a886903a664b2` → still hangs.\n- With only `3439aaa071d868ae` dropped, one session ran **88 minutes with zero GPU errors** (Deku Tree → Castle Town), then hung at the Impa escort. There, 11 *other* new `a5288d0a6c4971fd` pipelines were in the failed buffer (e.g. meshes `57ed4680e3042998`, `b903546b6b988e5f`, `d744d81c38c5831a`, `0c75c8aed6290acf`, `40a470bb5dbd8f2d`).\n- **`DM_NVN_SKIP_MESHKEYS=a5288d0a6c4971fd`** (every pipeline with that task) gets through **both** scenes, with nothing obviously missing on screen.\n\n### What the shaders show\n- Task `a5288d0a6c4971fd`: its tile loops are bounded by `c3[193].xy`. **I logged `S.ubo[3][0]` vec4 193 on the host for every a5288 draw: a sane `32 × 18` (and `1 × 1` for small passes) right up to the hang**, never garbage, so the Hi-Z scan in the task is bounded. (This is the suspect `DM_NVN_A5288_C3` in #1843 is built to check.) Some draws report `0 × 0`.\n- Mesh `3439aaa071d868ae`: no loops, barriers or SIMD ops in its body. Its index writes reach 1 word past the stage array when all 128 lanes write (`max_p 126`, the #1575 case).\n- Pixel `bd09ab5fc4fd7680`: a `do { … } while (true)` loop of `min(fp_s0[tile].count, fp_c6[113].x) + 1` iterations over lights. **Logged `fp_c6[113].x` = 1000** in every draw. So the hang implies the GPU-read per-tile counts in `fp_s0` are far too high during these scenes, giving up to ~1000 lighting iterations per pixel across the screen, enough to trip the watchdog. The white flash before the Impa hang fits overfull light/tile lists.\n\n### Ruled out on this machine\n- Batching (#1788's suggestion): `DM_NVN_CUT=4 DM_NVN_CUT_BUSY=0` still hangs (the failed segment is the main scene pass).\n- #1585 (task range pointer), #1616 (pool buffers after remap), the residency fix (now merged): each tested, still hangs.\n- Upscaler choice, damaged textures, memory (footprint ~4 GB at the Kokiri hang, ~11.7 GB peak in the long session).\n\n### Workaround\n`DM_NVN_SKIP_MESHKEYS=a5288d0a6c4971fd` (patch to `mesh_tasks_draw`, 13 lines; happy to open a PR). Logs from vanilla `eed7c42` runs of both scenes are available.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2011/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2011/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/issues/2394","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/issues/2394/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/issues/2394/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/issues/2394/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/pull/2394","id":6303064202,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUplEVs8AAAABODdolw","number":2394,"title":"feat: add OpenXR SteamVR support and independent Linux windows","user":{"login":"PigeonOuyang","id":33407430,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDA3NDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33407430?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PigeonOuyang","html_url":"https://github.com/PigeonOuyang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PigeonOuyang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PigeonOuyang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PigeonOuyang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PigeonOuyang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PigeonOuyang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PigeonOuyang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PigeonOuyang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PigeonOuyang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PigeonOuyang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-10T08:21:36Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:54:19Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/pulls/2394","html_url":"https://github.com/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/pull/2394","diff_url":"https://github.com/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/pull/2394.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/pull/2394.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\nThis PR adds a general Android OpenXR entry for SteamVR, selected through runtime capability detection. Android headsets exposing a compatible OpenXR runtime with Android instance creation and OpenGL ES support can use this entry. It also keeps the DroidDeck panel and independent Linux application windows accessible while SteamVR runs.\n\nOpenXR session startup and visible frame output are separate compatibility steps. This PR includes Android 10 DMA-BUF size-query and sRGB image-copy fixes for display interoperability issues on PICO 4 and Neo3.\n\nThe PICO-specific controller adaptation adds interaction profiles, bindings and render models for Neo3, PICO 4 and PICO 4 Ultra. Related to [#1267](https://github.com/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/issues/1267).\n\n**Feature acceptance and device regression validation are complete and have passed on the tested configurations. The rebuilt APK was regression-tested after both CodeRabbit review-fix batches, including the latest IME and touchpad fixes.**\n\n## Changes\n\n- **General OpenXR entry:** discover compatible runtimes through the Khronos Android loader and provide an immersive activity that starts SteamVR. Availability follows runtime capabilities rather than a headset-model whitelist.\n- **PICO controller adaptation:** add interaction profiles and bindings for Neo3, PICO 4 and PICO 4 Ultra, carrying grip/aim poses, trigger/grip clicks, touch state and haptics into SteamVR. Include licensed controller models, runtime-model fallback, and profile-specific pose alignment and animation.\n- **Android and runtime compatibility:** fix Android 10 DMA-BUF size-query and sRGB image-copy issues affecting PICO 4/Neo3 output, preserve the installed SteamVR tree during runtime upgrades and rollback, and add a one-time `statx` availability probe with a resolved-metadata fallback.\n- **Independent Linux windows:** map Wayland top-level windows to Android document tasks through KWin integration and AHB/SurfaceControl presentation. Synchronize sizes, presentation generations, titles and task icons, and restore presentation after surface recreation.\n- **Input and SteamVR coexistence:** add pointer gestures and Android/IBus IME routing, associate guest input with the selected window, and coordinate panel focus with XR/session ownership. Retain 2D presentation while SteamVR runs and provide return-to-VR and stop controls.\n- **Build and packaging:** build and stage the patched KWin runtime in local builds and CI, verify controller assets and their provenance/licenses, and include the new runtime inputs and imported store library in APK payload checks. Stage prepared Innoextract assets without duplicating source-tree copies.\n\n## Integration and review scope\n\nThe OpenXR activity retains desktop presentation, while the desktop and independent-window paths share compositor ticks, surface ownership, input focus and session visibility. KWin runtime staging and APK verification complete the window-presentation path. The complete integration is submitted together so these interfaces and lifecycle changes can be reviewed as a coherent implementation.\n\nThe original integration is organized into 10 feature commits:\n\n| Area | Commits |\n| --- | --- |\n| PRoot compatibility and SteamVR upgrade preservation | `f9cacdd59`, `85c6207aa` |\n| Android 10 graphics interoperability | `533b3b8c8` |\n| PICO controller models, bindings, poses and animation | `4b40fe156`, `d130a36e5` |\n| Linux pointer gestures and IME | `a3c6d1a25` |\n| Independent windows and task metadata | `0a2f03276`, `3c9d06ac0` |\n| OpenXR entry and SteamVR desktop-panel lifecycle | `cafc09ddf` |\n| Runtime build and packaging | `03b5651ba` |\n\nTwo merge commits incorporate upstream through `1ec2b696b75bfa401c61cb72850c3464fbf57d31`. The current head is `3694a5c490b1c7e894c240660299b4f0d8c56d76`, including the initial review fixes and follow-up input fixes below. The diff against that upstream revision changes 280 files; licensed controller GLB/OBJ assets, cgltf and generated Wayland protocol code account for much of its line count.\n\nThe additional `statx` probe supplements a path already addressed by upstream #2224. A separate remaining failure after that upstream fix has not been demonstrated; the necessity of the supplementary fallback remains an explicit review item.\n\n## Review fixes\n\n### Initial review fixes\n\nCommit [`7e1aa628d`](https://github.com/PigeonOuyang/DroidDeck/commit/7e1aa628dbf37652ec5934a34195373679ad4a57) addresses the 11 actionable comments from the initial CodeRabbit review:\n\n- Require the `xr-controller-reference.chord` diagnostics file before enabling the dual-stick reference-mode shortcut. Shortcut changes stay within the current session; explicit `.mode` file control remains available.\n- Select projection from active output ownership, preserve glasses rendering and saved Cardboard settings when a compatible OpenXR runtime is merely installed, and retain the Cardboard settings entry outside an active XR session.\n- Isolate WindowBridge loading, construction and startup failures so the existing agent continues answering requests; normalize its directory argument to `Path`.\n- Classify, build or verify, and stage all five required KWin assets in Windows runtime preparation. Reuse the pinned ARM64 Docker build recipe, validate source/output hashes and ELF architecture, record provenance, and expose `--rebuilt-kwin` for verified cached builds.\n- Add the partial-clone `merge-tree` workaround to the KWin CI job.\n- Allow AHB primary buffers to present directly without requiring or attempting Vulkan DMA-BUF import.\n- Schedule shared-scene retries only when a requested render fails or the shared layer is unavailable, including when independent-window presentation succeeds. Clean idle scenes no longer initiate the 16 ms retry loop.\n- Re-show a collapsed IME on API 28/29, correct horizontal Wayland wheel direction while preserving evdev output, serialize mapped mouse-button ownership changes and press/release events on the main thread, and classify `custom_shortcut` as an APP action.\n\nRegression coverage includes agent startup failures, KWin staging and stale-build rejection, actual native reference-control and AHB/pacing functions, glasses projection, older Android IME behavior, both mouse-wheel backends and background button ordering.\n\n### Follow-up input fixes\n\nCommit [`3694a5c49`](https://github.com/PigeonOuyang/DroidDeck/commit/3694a5c490b1c7e894c240660299b4f0d8c56d76) addresses two additional Major findings:\n\n- Preserve the latest composing text within its active IME connection and commit it once when composition finishes without an explicit commit. Clear pending text on explicit commit, cancellation, keyboard hiding/restart, focus loss, connection replacement and closure; reject late input from invalid connections. Unicode text callbacks and the existing key-event fallback remain available.\n- Cancel guest touchpad input before dispatching UI-owned touch and generic-motion events through the Android view hierarchy. Android 14 mouse-source events with a finger tool can reach drawer, keyboard and settings controls. Guest pointer input is retained when the app UI does not own the pointer.\n\nThe added automated cases cover composition completion/cancellation, stale connections, actual UI click callbacks, hover/scroll delivery, releasing guest button holds before UI input, and normal guest touchpad clicks on API 28 and 34. **Device regression of the rebuilt APK containing these fixes has also been completed and passed.**\n\n## Validation\n\n### Verified devices\n\n| Category | Device | Android version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| VR headset | PICO NEO3 | Android 10 |\n| VR headset | PICO 4 / PICO 4 Pro | Android 10 |\n| VR headset | PICO 4 Ultra | Android 14 |\n| Android tablet | Lenovo Legion Y700 | Android 16 |\n| Android phone | Xiaomi 14 Pro | Android 16 |\n\n### Completed feature acceptance and device regression\n\nDevice acceptance of the implemented features and regression validation after the CodeRabbit fixes are complete and have passed on the tested configurations:\n\n- [x] OpenXR entry and display compatibility, including SteamVR startup, stereo output, view orientation and Android 10 display fixes.\n- [x] Motion-controller detection, buttons, trigger/grip, thumbsticks, poses and haptics in SteamVR and a VR title.\n- [x] DroidDeck panel and independent Linux-window display, switching, presentation restoration and input routing during SteamVR.\n- [x] Native Android IME and external keyboard input, including window-to-window isolation.\n- [x] Window resizing, minimizing and repeated surface recreation.\n- [x] Long-running sessions, repeated startup/shutdown and clean session stop.\n- [x] Return to VR through the existing XR task, with focused stereo output restored.\n- [x] Regression of the rebuilt APK after both review-fix batches, including the IME composition lifecycle and touchpad routing between app UI and the Linux guest.\n\n### Automated tests and local build verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Android compilation and packaging | Updated Kotlin/Java and test classes compiled; signed `assembleRelease` and standard Release `lintVital` checks passed using the prepared native/runtime inputs |\n| Android unit tests | 225 tests in 13 classes passed on Linux Java 17 using freshly compiled code/tests and cached Robolectric SDKs; selected cases cover API 28/29/33/34; no failures or skips |\n| Related Linux/Python regression | 143 tests run with no failures; 4 JavaScript cases skipped because Node.js was unavailable in the compiler image |\n| Windows preparation and manifest tests | 16 preparation tests, 5 KWin build/verification tests and 22 runtime-input tests passed; these are included in the Linux/Python suite above |\n| APK verification | Latest APK signature matches the previous accepted build; ZIP alignment, package identity, version, ABI and both new input fixes verified. All 31 native libraries and 324 assets match the previous verified APK; the remaining generated DEX optimization profile matches the fresh build output |\n| Guest/native build inputs | Initial review preparation rebuilt vkBridge with the Windows NDK, ARM64 fakeinput/fastpath and x86_64/i386 fakeinput; x86 outputs retain Steam Linux Runtime glibc compatibility. These native inputs were reused unchanged for the follow-up input APK |\n| Submission checks | Personal authorship, whitespace, sensitive-marker and credential checks passed; device logs, APKs and local evidence are excluded from the commit |\n\nEarlier upstream-integration checks also passed: 3 Linux Java path/symlink tests, 181 related Linux/Python tests with 3 skips, and 9 final-sync Flatpak tests with one unrelated Snap case skipped. The counts above describe the recorded automated suites.\n\n## Build validation boundaries\n\n### Windows donor preparation\n\nThe KWin classification and missing-payload problem in `tools/prepare_windows_runtime.py` is fixed. Its older PR-732 donor-reuse flow still rejects other runtime changes made since `AUDITED_SOURCE` because those components have not been re-audited against that donor. The source-audit gate remains enabled.\n\nThe accepted APK uses prepared KWin, PRoot, VR and store-engine components, with modified scripts restaged and affected native inputs rebuilt during initial review preparation. A complete fresh build of every runtime component and a successful end-to-end run of the older Windows donor-preparation flow have not been established. Re-auditing or replacing that donor baseline remains necessary for that build path.\n\n### Full Android lint\n\nThe additional `lintRelease` run crashed in `androidx.compose.runtime.lint.ComposableStateFlowValueDetector` while analyzing `AddonPack.kt`: its metadata reader supports at most Kotlin metadata 2.0 but encountered version 2.1. The standard Release build and its `lintVital` checks passed. Full `lintRelease` is recorded as not completed.\n\n## Runtime prerequisite and upstream CI\n\nLinux/SteamVR sessions require disabling Android child-process restrictions in Developer options (“停止限制子进程” on the tested system). Session-stop and stability acceptance passed with this prerequisite enabled.\n\nThe PR remains Ready for review. For the current head, the [first Build validation run](https://github.com/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/actions/runs/42825597607) and [follow-up validation run](https://github.com/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/actions/runs/42825988450) passed, and the CodeRabbit check completed with `SUCCESS`. The [Build APK workflow](https://github.com/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/actions/runs/42825608281) is still `action_required`, with no build jobs run; it needs approval from a maintainer with write access to the upstream repository.\n\nLocal feature acceptance and device regression are complete. The remaining upstream steps are:\n\n- [ ] Approve and complete the upstream APK build.\n- [ ] Complete maintainer review.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/issues/2394/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/issues/2394/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/153","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/153/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/153/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/153/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/153","id":6280687993,"node_id":"I_kwDOVm1wds8AAAABdluxeQ","number":153,"title":"[问题] iPad mini 上三个浮层开关保存后重启不显示，启动前传参可显示 S2Arm 和 Metal HUD","user":{"login":"shengyifan","id":12181679,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTgxNjc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12181679?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan","html_url":"https://github.com/shengyifan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":13005656682,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVm1wds8AAAADBzKSag","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/labels/area:launcher","name":"area:launcher","color":"1d76db","default":false,"description":"Mac / Windows 启动器 / 环境检查 / 磁盘预算","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-11-09T05:44:43Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:50:58Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"在 iPad mini 上，游戏库「界面 → 性能浮层」和两个开发开关都能保存，但分别只开其中一项、完全退出 S2Arm 再启动游戏，标题画面都没有出现浮层。在同一台 iPad、同一个安装包上，从 Mac 在进程启动前传入相应环境变量，两个开发浮层都能显示。\n\n### 怎么复现\n\n1. 关闭「界面 → 性能浮层」「S2Arm 诊断浮层」「Metal HUD」，选定同一款游戏。本次用《塞尔达传说 旷野之息》，在标题画面观察，无需读档。\n2. 只开启下表一项，确认已保存，完全退出 S2Arm，重新打开并进入游戏。观察整屏画面，再恢复开关，继续下一项。两个开发开关用游戏内「设置 → 开发」切换，与 iPadOS 的 S2Arm 应用设置共用同一偏好。\n3. 三项都关闭，再用 Xcode 的 `devicectl` 冷启动同一个 App，分别在进程启动前传入 `S2A_HUD=1`、`MTL_HUD_ENABLED=1`，最后同时传入两项。每次都进入同一标题画面对照。\n\n### 实际结果\n\n| 唯一开启的选项 | 已确认保存或读取 | 冷启动后的游戏画面 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 游戏库「界面 → 性能浮层」 | `shell-settings` 中 `performanceHUD=true` | 没有浮层 |\n| 开发「S2Arm 诊断浮层」 | `S2ADevHUD=true`，且 `host.log` 记录了 `S2A_HUD=1（本 App 设置：开发浮层）` | 左上角没有 S2Arm 面板 |\n| 开发「Metal HUD」 | `MetalHUDForceEnabled=true`，且 `host.log` 记录了 `MTL_HUD_ENABLED=1（本 App 设置：Metal 性能浮层）` | 没有 Apple Metal HUD |\n\n**启动参数对照。** 提前传入 `S2A_HUD=1` 后，左上角出现 S2Arm 面板，日志出现 `开发浮层：开`。提前传入 `MTL_HUD_ENABLED=1` 后，右上角出现 Apple 面板，截图可读到 59.99 FPS、GPU 6.79 ms、帧间隔 16.67 ms。同时传入两项时，两个面板可以同屏显示。以上均为 iPad 系统整屏截图观察。\n\n![iPad mini 真机对照：分别在进程启动前传入参数后出现的 S2Arm 诊断面板和 Apple Metal HUD](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1d5c0a82-c5c0-48ed-99eb-e67d1183c0c8)\n\n### 预期结果\n\n按 [#69 中给出的 iPadOS 使用方式](https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/69#issuecomment-6730346287)，打开对应开发开关、完全退出并重开 App 后，应能在游戏中看到所选浮层。游戏库的「性能浮层」说明为“游戏未单独设置时使用”，也应能作为有效的默认设置。\n\n### 环境\n\n- iPad mini（A20 Pro），iPadOS 27.2（24B8120）。游戏为《塞尔达传说 旷野之息》1.9.0，Title ID `01007EF00011E000`。\n- iPad 上的 S2Arm 显示 0.1（构建 1），诊断面板显示「包 未记录」与「直连 NVN b-0be3f2」。本机成功打包并安装到这台 iPad 的任务记录中，启动器包号为 `ce81018d-38a4f5a5`，对应 [S2Arm v0.1.3](https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/releases/tag/v0.1.3)。与 #129 使用同一安装包。\n- 本次实测设备为 iPad mini。\n\n### 源码线索\n\n- 在 v0.1.3 对应的源码提交 `ce81018d9` 中，iOS 先创建游戏视图并尝试挂载诊断面板，再启动宿主线程读取用户偏好。`s2a_hud_on()` 会缓存第一次读取的值。这一顺序可解释 S2Arm 自有浮层的对照结果。[视图与线程的启动顺序](https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/blob/ce81018d96e136cbf5047075f533ed3164a8aabf/ios/app.m#L753-L774) · [开关缓存](https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/blob/ce81018d96e136cbf5047075f533ed3164a8aabf/runtime/src/ap_host.c#L17-L20) · [开发开关的读取](https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/blob/ce81018d96e136cbf5047075f533ed3164a8aabf/ios/settings.m#L154-L165)\n- 游戏库把 `performanceHUD` 转成 `DM_METAL_HUD`，在该提交的 S2Arm 游戏启动路径中未找到消费它的位置。[游戏库配置](https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/blob/ce81018d96e136cbf5047075f533ed3164a8aabf/shell/Sources/ShellUI/ShellSettingsStore.swift#L95-L103) · [游戏启动入口](https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/blob/ce81018d96e136cbf5047075f533ed3164a8aabf/shell/Sources/S2ArmShellHost/S2ArmShellHostModel.swift#L30-L38)\n- 对 Apple Metal HUD，实测确认了两种启用方式的结果不同。Apple 在该安装包上何时读取配置仍待核实。\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/153/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/153/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/171","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/171/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/171/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/171/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/171","id":6281170116,"node_id":"I_kwDOVm1wds8AAAABdmMMxA","number":171,"title":"[功能请求] 让 iPad 的 NVN 直连渲染实际支持 1.5× 和 2× 内部分辨率","user":{"login":"shengyifan","id":12181679,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTgxNjc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12181679?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan","html_url":"https://github.com/shengyifan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shengyifan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":13005656771,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVm1wds8AAAADBzKSww","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/labels/area:perf","name":"area:perf","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":"能耗 / 帧率 / 卡顿 / 画面","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-11-09T06:30:10Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:48:59Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"希望 iPad 玩家可以按需提高游戏的内部渲染分辨率。现在「设置 → App → S2Arm → 画面 → 渲染分辨率倍率」已经列出 **1.5×** 和 **2×**，但在《塞尔达传说 旷野之息》的 NVN 直连路径里，这两档最终都按 1× 绘制。玩家可以选中高倍率，却看不到预期的细节改善。\n\n### 希望实现的效果\n\n- 选择 1.5× 或 2× 后，下次启动游戏时，对支持缩放的 3D 渲染目标按所选倍率绘制，再采样到屏幕。以一块 1920×1080 的可缩放目标为例，1.5× 应实际使用 2880×1620，2× 应使用 3840×2160。最终显示区域可以保持现有尺寸。\n- 在高倍率支持落地前，或当前渲染路径需要回退时，希望设置页能提示实际生效的上限，例如「当前直连模式最高 1×」。这样玩家可以知道画质是否会随选择改变。\n\n### iPad mini 真机实测\n\n设备为 iPad mini（A20 Pro），iPadOS 27.2。游戏为《塞尔达传说 旷野之息》1.9.0（`01007EF00011E000`）。各档分别冷启动，使用同一存档的副本进入复苏神庙，在固定机位比较，保持主机模式、SMAA 高和双线性滤镜一致。0.5× 时日志确认一块 1920×1080 目标缩到 960×540，0.75× 时缩到 1440×810。1.5× 和 2× 时画面均未见比 1× 更多的细节，后端日志也明确记录了回退。\n\n```text\n[dm] [nvn-mtl] 内部分辨率：S2A_RES_SCALE=1.5 大于 1，直连只缩小不放大，按 1\n[dm] [nvn-mtl] 内部分辨率：S2A_RES_SCALE=2 大于 1，直连只缩小不放大，按 1\n```\n\n**建议验收**：选取一块可缩放的渲染目标，对照 1×、1.5×、2× 三档，核实 Metal 实际分配的宽高与倍率一致，再用同场景截图检查物体轮廓、HUD 和小地图是否正常。这样也能区分设置层“读到了 2×”和渲染器“实际按 2× 绘制”。\n\n相关的 Mac 画质需求见 #102。开发分支已有放开 Mac 高倍率、保留 iOS 上限的改动，可作为 iPad 端评估的起点。[分平台倍率改动](https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/commit/f6f58e79fde20ce9e628ce5c742f04d90fb3ede2) · [iOS 画面设置文档](https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/blob/34ff8d26c3d4680ee62f383ae18e9edb5725d4d9/docs/%E7%94%BB%E9%9D%A2%E8%AE%BE%E7%BD%AE.md#L7-L14)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/171/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jhaizhou-ops/S2Arm/issues/171/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodkie/v-show/issues/6","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodkie/v-show","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodkie/v-show/issues/6/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodkie/v-show/issues/6/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodkie/v-show/issues/6/events","html_url":"https://github.com/goodkie/v-show/issues/6","id":5651579964,"node_id":"I_kwDOT53X288AAAABUNxEPA","number":6,"title":"XPIDER AutoForm Sender Pro — Owner × ChatGPT × Antigravity Workspace","user":{"login":"goodkie","id":197914795,"node_id":"U_kgDOC8vwqw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/197914795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodkie","html_url":"https://github.com/goodkie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodkie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodkie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodkie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodkie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodkie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodkie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodkie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodkie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodkie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12834448352,"node_id":"LA_kwDOT53X288AAAAC_P4j4A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodkie/v-show/labels/audit-pending","name":"audit-pending","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1013,"created_at":"2026-09-30T19:03:15Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:40:31Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# XPIDER AutoForm Sender Pro — Owner × ChatGPT × Antigravity Workspace\n\n## Project Identity Declaration\n\n- **PROJECT NAME:** XPIDER AutoForm Sender Pro\n- **WORKSPACE TYPE:** Independent Project Workspace\n- **REPOSITORY:** goodkie/v-show\n- **LOCAL ISSUE / THREAD:** Issue #6\n- **ACTIVE BRANCH:** upgrade/phase-0-1\n- **CURRENT ACTIVE PHASE:** R6.9D Outcome Verifier false-failure remediation\n\n### Independence Declaration\n\nThis workroom is autonomous and project-local.\n\nThere is no central MASTER HUB.\n\nOnly XPIDER AutoForm Sender Pro directives, receipts, audits, owner feedback, runtime evidence, build state, and release gates belong here.\n\nNo other project may be mirrored, summarized, synchronized, or cross-posted here unless the Owner explicitly requests a scoped transfer.\n\nBefore posting or accepting any comment/Receipt, ChatGPT and Antigravity must verify:\n\n`PROJECT == XPIDER AutoForm Sender Pro`\n\nAnything else is OUT OF SCOPE.\n\n---\n\n## Workspace Boundary\n\nThis Issue is **only** for the XPIDER AutoForm Sender Pro workstream in the `goodkie/v-show` repository.\n\nIt is **not** a MASTER HUB and must not aggregate other projects.\n\n### In scope\n- XPIDER AutoForm Sender Pro\n- Contact-page discovery\n- inquiry-form classification\n- autofill / submit / outcome verification\n- CAPTCHA integration state\n- History & Ledger\n- live counters / diagnostics\n- Email Collector integrated tab\n- pause/resume/checkpoint/reset\n- tests, runtime evidence, build provenance, release gates for this extension\n\n### Out of scope\n- xpider-browser / Lite Chromium / LCW\n- Panorama / Issue #4\n- Gmail Sender\n- any unrelated application, browser, website, contract, marketing asset, or future project\n\n## No Cross-Posting Rule\n\nUnder OCA-DEV-1.0 Independent Workspace Model:\n\n- directives, audits, receipts, blockers, and gates posted here must relate only to XPIDER AutoForm Sender Pro;\n- ChatGPT must not post another project’s audit here;\n- Antigravity must not post another project’s Receipt here;\n- this Issue must not be used as a repository-wide or Owner-wide activity feed;\n- another project may be referenced only when the Owner explicitly requests a scoped transfer;\n- historical unrelated comments are non-authoritative for this workspace.\n\n## Roles\n\n### Owner\nProduct authority + real-use acceptance.\n\n### ChatGPT\nLead planner / architect / QA auditor / release gatekeeper **for this workspace only**.\n\n### Antigravity\nImplementation / testing / build / runtime evidence / rollback executor **for this workspace only**.\n\n## Current Operating Protocol\n\nOCA-DEV-1.0 — Independent Workspace Model.\n\nThe protocol document is Issue #7 and is a **policy reference only**, not a work-coordination hub.\n\n## Coordination Flow\n\n1. Owner provides goal or real-use feedback.\n2. ChatGPT converts it into a bounded local directive.\n3. Antigravity implements, tests, commits, pushes, and posts evidence here.\n4. ChatGPT audits actual repository/runtime evidence.\n5. Gate = PASS / PROVISIONAL PASS / HOLD / FAIL / OWNER SMOKE REQUIRED.\n6. Owner is involved only when a real-use acceptance step is genuinely required.\n\n## Message Prefixes\n\n- `[CHATGPT][DIRECTIVE][extension-form-sender][PHASE]`\n- `[CHATGPT][AUDIT][extension-form-sender][PHASE]`\n- `[CHATGPT][GATE][extension-form-sender][PHASE]`\n- `[ANTIGRAVITY][PROGRESS][extension-form-sender][PHASE]`\n- `[ANTIGRAVITY][RECEIPT][extension-form-sender][PHASE]`\n- `[ANTIGRAVITY][BLOCKER][extension-form-sender][PHASE]`\n- `[OWNER][REAL-DEVICE][extension-form-sender][PHASE]`\n\n## Security\n\nDo not post secrets, API keys, tokens, credentials, customer personal data, or other sensitive values in this public repository.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodkie/v-show/issues/6/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodkie/v-show/issues/6/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2037","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2037/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2037/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2037/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2037","id":6309036519,"node_id":"I_kwDOVNvIis8AAAABeAxB5w","number":2037,"title":"Ocarina of Time (Mac, M4 8-core GPU / 16 GB): slow-motion opening movie (GPU-bound), memory stays ~12 GB after dropping from 2K to 720p","user":{"login":"edsonlmancini","id":123320248,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1m3uA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123320248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/edsonlmancini","html_url":"https://github.com/edsonlmancini","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edsonlmancini/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edsonlmancini/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edsonlmancini/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edsonlmancini/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edsonlmancini/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edsonlmancini/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edsonlmancini/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edsonlmancini/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/edsonlmancini/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-10T14:36:47Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:38:36Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"> This report was written by Claude (an AI assistant, via Claude Code) from the game logs, at the request of the player (`edsonlmancini`), who did the play-testing. No code changes, just observations.\n\n**Setup:** MacBook Air M4 (`Mac16,12`, 8-core GPU), 16 GB RAM, macOS 27.2, plugged in. Packaged app built from `main` (`ca3c4ad6`), runtime updated to `2b2e0598` with `update_runtime.py`. Own dump (`.nup`, v131072). Player-style start (no `OOT_AUTO_SKIP_OPENING`). Debug log on.\n\nOverall it plays well: Kokiri Forest at 720p runs at 60–90 fps, and \"2K from 1080p\" docked looks great at ~40–50 fps. These are the three problems we hit.\n\n### 1. The title/opening AV1 movie plays in slow motion (GPU-bound at ~37 ms a frame)\n- During the movie (`Dm_Title_0005` and then the other AV1 stream, 9254 pictures, frames ~1000–10800), every frame takes **GPU p50 36.6 ms / frame time 38.3 ms** (~26 fps). The numbers barely move from start to end, and the `[负载]` line shows the GPU at 95% with the CPU mostly idle.\n- The frame is light: about 4 draws, 3 render passes and ~22 compute dispatches. The end-of-frame network is not detected during the movie (`net-bypass` first sees `aad7ea7e…` only when the 3D scene starts).\n- With `time step capped at 33.333 ms`, the movie runs at ~87% speed while the audio follows the wall clock. The player sees \"everything in slow motion with normal audio\".\n- After the movie, at the same 720p/handheld settings: frame p50 11–17 ms, GPU 10–15 ms.\n- Test runs set `OOT_AUTO_SKIP_OPENING=1`, so you probably never see this path on a slower GPU.\n\n```\n计时 至帧 3000： 帧时间 p50 38.24 / p95 39.32 ms； NVN 提交+出图 p50 1.50 ms； GPU p50 36.63 / p95 36.94 ms\n翻译 至帧 3000：…每帧绘制 4\n渲染通道 至帧 3000：每帧 3.0 个\n计时 至帧 12000： 帧时间 p50 12.00 / p95 13.18 ms； GPU p50 12.23 ms   (gameplay, after the movie)\n```\n\n### 2. Memory reaches ~12.5 GB at 2K, and does not come back when going back to 720p\n- **Session 3 (~12 min):** started at \"2K native\" (resolution 5).\n  - The footprint was **10.2 GB** after ~20 s and rose to **11.3–11.6 GB** with \"docked\" and \"2K from 1080p\".\n  - It reached **12.5 GB** after switching back to 2K native with the canvas-size network on (`net_copy = 0`). That gave ~60 ms frames.\n- The player then switched to **720p + handheld**. The footprint stayed at **12.0 GB**, and the game stayed stuck at **frame p50 62 ms / GPU p50 68 ms**, against 10–15 ms in a fresh 720p session.\n- After quitting, macOS still had ~3.1 GB of swap in use. Our reading is that the machine was paging, and the 2K allocations are not released when the resolution drops.\n- **Session 2:** same climb over a longer run, 5.5 GB at 720p in the movie → 7.8 → 10.2 → 12.6 GB after moving to 2K.\n- On a 16 GB Mac this is right at the ~12.3 GB limit mentioned in #1836. Releasing render targets or texture storage on a resolution or profile change, or a lower ceiling on 16 GB machines, would help a lot.\n\n```\n上屏 至帧 1200：footprint 10234 MiB      (2K native, start)\n上屏 至帧 18600：footprint 12542 MiB     (2K native + net_copy=0)\n[oot] resolution 0: canvas 1280x720, 3D scale 0.6667\n上屏 至帧 19200：footprint 12023 MiB\n计时 至帧 19200： 帧时间 p50 62.05 / p95 89.36 ms； GPU p50 67.92 / p95 87.15 ms\n【红】[net-bypass] MetalFX encode failed in frame 19075: the network ran on the previous C\n```\n\n### 3. Hitches entering new areas come from texture uploads, not pipelines\n- Of 608 long frames in session 3, only 1 built a new pipeline.\n- The big ones are 200–990 ms with long \"提交+出图\" (submit + present), while first-time texture uploads happen, up to 137 MB in one frame:\n\n```\n[长帧] 帧 971（22.64 s）整帧 328.9 ms，提交+出图 309.2 ms，GPU 13.4 ms；新建管线 0 条 …；上传贴图 首传 82 张 + 重传 2 次 136.8 MB / 57.0 ms\n[长帧] 帧 973（23.63 s）整帧 992.9 ms，提交+出图 229.8 ms，GPU 28.6 ms；新建管线 0 条 …\n```\n\nThe full logs (2.4 MB and 1 MB, home path removed) are available if useful. Just ask and we will attach them.\n\nMinor doc note: `games/oot/docs/install.md` lists `brew install dav1d libvpx opus python@3.14`, but the build also needed **`llvm@23`** (`structck.py`, `verify-rewrite-main`) and **`ffmpeg`/`ffprobe`** (opening overlay generation).\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2037/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2037/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/1971","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/1971/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/1971/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/1971/events","html_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/1971","id":6286102514,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAABN15k1A","number":1971,"title":"Ocarina of Time on an iPhone 17, an M1 iPad and in any window or screen shape: no freeze or paging over the guest's files, GPU-only textures share bytes under 8 GB, the title at full speed, and the picture and HUD follow the window","user":{"login":"stan69b","id":3304418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMDQ0MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3304418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stan69b","html_url":"https://github.com/stan69b","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stan69b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stan69b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stan69b/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stan69b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stan69b/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stan69b/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stan69b/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stan69b/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stan69b/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12938277381,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy5yBQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/docs","name":"docs","color":"0075ca","default":false,"description":"Documentation","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12938277884,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy5z_A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/ios","name":"ios","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"The iPhone and iPad app (dm/ios)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12938278094,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy50zg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/nvn","name":"nvn","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"NVN on Metal and its tests (dm/gfx/nvn, dm/gfx/tests)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12938278541,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy52jQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/tools","name":"tools","color":"bfdadc","default":false,"description":"Tools and scripts (dm/tools, scripts)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12938279457,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy56IQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/game:%2001007EF00011E000","name":"game: 01007EF00011E000","color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12938280714,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy5_Cg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/host","name":"host","color":"1d76db","default":false,"description":"The Horizon host: SVCs, services, threads, memory (dm/host)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12938283270,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy6JBg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/mac","name":"mac","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"The Mac front end and app (dm/mac, front_mac.m)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12938285310,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy6Q_g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/rewriter","name":"rewriter","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":"The NSO rewriter and per-build patches","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12944541838,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADA44Ijg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/game:%2001006F8002326000","name":"game: 01006F8002326000","color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"Animal Crossing: New Horizons","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12962853499,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADBKVyew","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/game:%200400486024DEC000","name":"game: 0400486024DEC000","color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"A game","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-11-09T12:31:32Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:38:06Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/pulls/1971","html_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/1971","diff_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/1971.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/1971.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Ocarina of Time now plays on an iPhone 17 and an M1 iPad Pro (both 8 GB), and on the Mac it fills any window shape, resized live: no bars, no stretching. The iPhone holds 27–30 fps in Kokiri Forest, and frames just over the 30 fps cap now show at the next vsync instead of waiting a full 33 ms tick. The iPad holds 20 fps where the views are light, but 5–12 fps, GPU-bound, in heavier rooms of the Great Deku Tree. Follows #1829.\n\n## What\n\n### iPhone and M1 iPad\n\n1. **Freeze over the guest's files** (`file_wire`, `t_file_wire`): the residency commit paged the guest file in from the GPU driver's path and hung on an APFS lock. File-backed buffers are now `mlock`ed before the commit. No change for anonymous memory (every Mac run by default). If growing the list of wired ranges fails, the new range is unlocked at once, so nothing writes through a null pointer (clang-tidy).\n2. **GPU-only textures share bytes under 8 GB of working set** (`window_texture`, `t_window_alias`): with 7f502220's per-target heaps the iPad ran out of GPU memory at an outdoor save load (5,184 of 5,461 MB). Placed per 32 MB span at the NVN offset × 9/8, no lossless compression. Only where `recommendedMaxWorkingSetSize` < 8 GB; `DM_NVN_WINDOW_ALIAS=0/1` forces it.\n   - #1453 found that sharing this pool corrupts the fog on a Mac. I don't claim this avoids that. On the iPad and the iPhone the picture looked clean (Kokiri Forest, Deku Tree), for reasons not known, and the alternative there is out of memory.\n3. **Shader-code pools stay out of the raw pool table** (`hle_nvn.c` `nvnMemoryPoolGetBufferAddress`, `nvn_mtl.m` `mtl_pool_addressed_by`, `t_addr_known`): the game asks for each shader-code pool's address to place its programs, so the raw pool table wired all 223 of them (317 MB), though the GPU never reads shader code here. On the 8 GB iPhone that left too little room for the guest's file pages, which were read back all the time: 14–17 fps, 117 ms frames on average with 27 ms of GPU. A shader-code pool's own address now keeps it out of the table, and a buffer made in such a pool still puts it in. Holds for every game.\n4. **Title in slow motion** (`nvn_fstep.h`, `hle_nvn.c`, `t_fstep`): the frame step took the boot screens' GPU time (0.4 ms) as its reference, so the title's 40 ms always read as a slowed GPU and probes of hold 1 never stopped. The step now calls the GPU slowed only against a reference that measured the same work: the same draws and, since the title is mostly compute, the same dispatches.\n5. **The title movie plays at its own speed** (`hle_codec_video.c`, `t_codec_video`): a movie the player reads one picture per game frame follows its own clock, so pictures behind it are dropped instead of the movie slowing with the frame step.\n6. **Clock waits in the power line** (`dm_clock_top`, `t_clockwait`): a diagnostic only. It shows Ocarina makes no clock waits, so 8bdfcb73 is not behind its slow motion. The cause is GPU time.\n7. **Game note**: \"For an iPhone or iPad build\", with the iPhone's results.\n\n### Any window or screen shape (`screen_aspect any`)\n\n8. **The present takes the crop's shape** (`nvn_mtl.m` `present_shape` / `present_fit`, `t_present_crop`): a crop whose width / height matches the shape the host asked for is shown in that shape instead of 16:9.\n9. **`screen_aspect any`** (`game.py`, `loader.c`, `hle_oe.c`, `front_mac.m`, `front_ios.m`, `settings.tsv`): a profile's stubs follow any shape from 0.25 to 6, portrait included, while the game runs. The loader writes the ratio, the size factors, a change count and the camera multipliers to the state page. The Mac reports the window's shape once a resize settles; iOS reports the space the picture has: the screen in landscape, and upright the whole screen or the part above the controls (item 12). The *Picture shape* setting defaults to auto. Front ends get two new calls, `front_view_aspect` and `dm_screen_view_changed`; until a front end provides them, these profiles render 16:9.\n10. **Ocarina's stubs**, all function-matched `others` of its frame-step rule:\n    - **Output size, window textures, camera, live resize:** the output size takes the shape, the window textures grow when the crop needs it, the cached camera matrix takes the shape every frame, and a live resize makes the game recompute its size.\n    - **HUD:** every layout file holds a 3840×2160 screen size, and each screen copies its 2D projection to the GPU every frame. The stub reshapes that copy at the HUD's pixel size, and the game's conversions between layout and screen get the same size.\n    - **The rule:** wider than 16:9 keeps the vertical angle, between 1:1 and 16:9 the horizontal one, and upright takes the scale of the same screen turned landscape.\n11. **Probe diagnostics** (`probe.c`), for values a game caches:\n    - `DM_PROBE_FP` prints float arguments.\n    - `DM_PROBE_FINDMAT` scans guest memory for perspective matrices, and `DM_PROBE_FINDF` for a pair of floats.\n    - `DM_PROBE_WATCH=@xN+<offset>` arms the write watch on an object a probe reaches.\n    - `DM_PROBE_XREG` dumps any register's memory.\n12. **Upright on the iPhone** (`front_ios.m`, `DmLayout.h`, `DmRotation.h`, `main.m`, `DmHostingController.swift`, `Launcher.swift`, `DmGamepad.m`, `settings.tsv`, `settings.py`):\n    - *Rotation* (Automatic / Landscape / Portrait, `DM_ROTATION`), on the settings screen and in the in-game menu, locks the orientation, so an iPhone can be played upright.\n    - *Portrait layout* (`DM_PORTRAIT_LAYOUT`, only for `screen_aspect any` profiles): *Full screen* (the default) fills the screen with the touch controls over the picture; *Picture above controls* fills the space above them. Either way the game renders that shape.\n    - Other games keep a 16:9 picture above the controls. With a controller and no touch controls shown, the picture takes the whole screen.\n13. **Upright cap** (`loader.c`, `DM_SCREEN_UPRIGHT_FOV`, default 1): an upright picture shows no more height than a square would (79° against about 90° without the cap), so a phone no longer looks up into parts of the world the game never builds. `0` turns it off.\n14. **Docs:**\n    - The game note gets a \"Screen shape\" section.\n    - `memory.md`: shader-code pools wired by the raw pool table. `rendering.md`: a camera that caches its projection. `movies.md`: the movie's own clock.\n    - The `screen_aspect` key, `DM_SCREEN_ASPECT`'s any range, and the new switches.\n    - `game-patches.md` regenerated: `docs_patches.py`'s dry run spaced a rule's other functions 16 MB apart, so the ninth was out of a branch's reach; now 4 MB.\n\n### Frame pacing at the 30 fps cap\n\n15. **#1942's frame step is carried here** (uncraftablexd's commit, unchanged from #1942 except one conflict resolved in `fstep_tick`): late frames with the GPU idle do not step up, and a longer hold the GPU does not explain is probed. The pacing below builds on it. If #1942 merges first, drop that commit from this PR.\n16. **Late frames at a 30 fps cap are shown at the next vsync** (`nvn_fstep.h` `fine`, `hle_nvn.c` `nvn_game_fps`, `t_fstep`): at a 30 fps cap the hold is at most 2 vsyncs, and the display link runs at 30 Hz. A frame a little over 33.3 ms (the iPhone's 36.5 ms in Kokiri Forest) missed its tick and waited for the next one, so about 1 frame in 10 stayed 66.7 ms on screen. When frames are late at the longest hold the cap allows (the same 3 late frames in a row that would otherwise step up), the 60 Hz link runs instead: each frame is still held its two vsyncs, and a late one shows at the next vsync, 50 ms. It is never faster than 30. The 30 Hz link comes back after 8 s with no late frame. Both switches are logged.\n17. **That 60 Hz link runs at frame latency 2** (`nvn_mtl.m` `link_latency`): at latency 1 on a ProMotion screen it took frames whose GPU work was still running, and held the iPad's 40 ms title frames at 50 ms. Latency 2 gives the same lead the 30 Hz link has at latency 1, so input lag is unchanged.\n18. **The frame step's log lines name the cap**, the longest hold it allows and why, and the `on-screen` lines count gaps at the hold, one vsync longer, and two or more longer.\n19. **Docs:** a `frame-rate.md` entry, \"Late frames at a 30 fps cap on the 30 Hz display link\", with the measurements, and a pacing bullet in the game note.\n20. **A smoke route for Ocarina** (`dm/games/0400486024DEC000/smoke.tsv`), so `regress.py check` boots it: an empty save to the title, no input, 400 s. Quick mode pays the cold pipeline prepare, 130–270 s for 14,748 pipelines on an M4, before the first frame.\n\n### The iPhone 17 frame on the GPU\n\n21. **A submission's end no longer waits for the encode thread** (`nvn_mtl.m` `mtl_sub_commit`, `t_sub_overlap`): with Metal encoding on its own thread (the iOS default), each submission waited for the encode thread to finish the previous one. Ocarina makes about 30 submissions a frame, so on the iPhone 17 frame 3600 spanned 34.9 ms for 20.2 ms of GPU work, 13.6 ms of it gaps before a submission's first encoder, and the replay waited 36 times a frame (10 ms). The records now go to the encode thread with a note of their fence, and the replay goes on; a present still waits for the submissions before it. `DM_NVN_SUB_DRAIN=1` restores the old wait. Holds for every game with the encode thread on. On the iPhone it halved the GPU's idle gaps; the frame rate did not change, because gameplay there is CPU-bound (16–20 fps at thermal state 2, GPU p50 21–24 ms).\n22. **`DM_NVN_GPUPROF` logs the host's CPU timeline** beside a profiled frame's encoders (`nvn_mtl.m`, `nvn_queue.inc`, `t_gpuprof`): each submission's encoding, each commit, every blocking CPU wait for the GPU by its site, and the NVN queue worker's parks, on the encoders' clock. A diagnostic, off by default.\n23. **#1751's `DM_NVN_GPUPROF_GEOM` is carried here** (`nvn_mtl.m`, `gpuprof.py`): item 22 builds on it. Off by default. If #1751 merges first, drop that commit from this PR.\n\n## Checked\n\n- **iPhone 17** (A19, 8 GB, iOS 26.6.1), on 04811a63 (chain `39eb2f781d07`), the owner playing from a save in Kokiri Forest, the launcher's 30 fps cap and Dynamic resolution on. For testing, the build also held #1842, #1901, #1942 and #1751.\n  - Before item 3: 14–17 fps, 6,000–15,600 page-ins every 10 s, 122 of 300 frames dropped. An earlier build without these fixes ended in a kernel panic after the save loaded.\n  - With it: 27 fps standing, 27–30 walking, frame p50 36.5 / p95 40 ms, GPU p50 32 ms, 100–400 page-ins every 10 s, about 30 of 300 frames dropped. The title holds 30 fps with its movie at full speed.\n- **iPad Pro 11\" 3rd gen** (M1, 8 GB, iPadOS 27.0.1), on 7ffa63cc (chain `dedc9391c30b`), no switches needed. Two 32-minute runs at the Deku Tree's entrance: 20.0 fps in every window, GPU 34–35 ms, game speed 0.97–1.00, residency 3.2 GB, headroom ≥ 5.87 GB. No crash, hang, GPU error or panic.\n- **Screen shape on an M4 Pro Mac**, at chain `dedc9391c30b`:\n  - six window shapes resized live while playing: iPhone and iPad, upright and landscape; 1700×478; 16:9;\n  - the pause menu, the \"A Open\" prompt, and the Kokiri Forest cutscene with its location card, at 2.2.\n- **On this branch** (04811a63, chain `39eb2f781d07`; its shader libraries now exist, built with no compile failures):\n  - items 3–5: the host builds; `t_addr_known` 20/20 (fails without item 3), `t_fstep` 84/84, `test_docs.py`; `t_codec_video` passed on the test build that carries the same change;\n  - before items 3–5 (16f5a3d2): every host test passed;\n  - `test_oot_aspect.py` 18/18 (unicorn), plus the rewriter tests and `test_patches.py`;\n  - `t_present_crop` 120/120, `t_file_wire`, `t_window_alias`, `t_image_alias`, `t_clockwait`;\n  - Python lint and clang-tidy (LLVM 21; CI uses 23) on 16f5a3d2: 0 new findings; not re-run for items 3–5.\n- **Upright on the iPhone 17:** six 3-minute runs into Kokiri Forest, no crash. Full screen rendered 1200x2600, capped; Picture above controls 1.07:1; landscape 2.18:1. The frame rate was the same upright and in landscape. Duo harness on the Simulator: 42 tests, 0 failures, including a real rotation to portrait. `test_oot_aspect` 20/20, `test_launcher_settings`, `test_docs`.\n- **Pacing at the 30 fps cap, M1 iPad Pro** (Deku Tree save, Dynamic resolution on, 9,000 frames of camera turns per run):\n\n  | Build | fps | gaps of 33 / 42 / 50 / 67 ms | 66.7 ms gaps per 300 | on-screen p99 |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | 30 Hz link (before) | 27.9 | 88.6 / 3.8 / 0 / 7.5 % | 22.8 | 66.7 ms |\n  | 60 Hz link, latency 2 (this PR) | 27.7 | 81.0 / 2.3 / 16.7 / 0.1 % | 0.2 | 50.0 ms |\n\n  Game time stayed at 1.000 of real time.\n- **Pacing at the 30 fps cap, iPhone 17** (Kokiri Forest, camera turns): first gameplay at thermal state 1 showed 1,098 / 997 / 1 gaps at the hold / one vsync longer / two or more (p99 45.8–50 ms, game time 0.999), where before about 30 of every 300 frames had a 66.7 ms gap. Later, at thermal state 2, gameplay ran CPU-bound at 13–22 fps and game time fell to 0.73. Those frames are longer than the 3 vsyncs a frame step can carry, so no hold changes that.\n- Tests on the rebased head: `t_fstep` 106/106, `t_nvn` 277/277, `t_copy_alias` 126/126, `t_sub_overlap` 8/8, `test_docs`; earlier `t_thermal` 21/21, `present_rescue` 101/101.\n- **Regress:** `scripts/regress.py check --quick --games 0400486024DEC000` on an M4 Mac (macOS 27.2, Xcode 27.2). Baseline: upstream main `c4ffb9df`. Candidate: `404a6dd3`, which is this PR's content before its last rebase onto three newer main commits and its two lint fixes, plus the route below.\n  - **Games:** `regress.py impact` names Breath of the Wild, Pokémon Scarlet and Tears of the Kingdom as affected, and Hades through a broad rule. None of them has a Mac build here, so they are unchecked. Ocarina of Time is the game this PR is about, and the only one booted. It boots with a new smoke route, `dm/games/0400486024DEC000/smoke.tsv`: an empty save to the title, no input.\n  - **Result:** `regress.py` reports REGRESSION, from two screenshots only, and it is not one. Both show the title rendered correctly. They differ in the title movie's position: at 385 s the candidate is at the field shot and main still at the forest shot, because the movie now follows its own clock.\n    - Shaders: 42,848 / 42,848 on both, no MSL change, no interface finding, no new `[RED]`.\n    - Frames: 19.8 → 33.1 fps, frame p50 / p99 49.96 / 114.64 → 33.27 / 34.67 ms.\n    - Game time: 0.955 → 1.000 of real time. Main holds 3 vsyncs most of the time with 26 probes and 30 failed trials; the candidate holds 1–2.\n    - Peak footprint: 2,778 → 2,765 MB. Cold pipeline prepare: 128 → 142 s.\n    - These are single runs, with replay noise not measured.\n  - **The movie:** main reads one picture per game frame, so at 20 fps the title movie plays at about a third of its speed. The candidate drops pictures behind the movie's clock instead (`600 pictures dropped to the movie's clock, 780 put in`), so it plays at its own speed. Both runs recorded `frames.tsv` the same way, and nothing else ran on the Mac.\n  - **Setup:** OoT's local Mac build folders hold a shader package split before records carried keys, so the harness ran from a folder that links the build to its keyed re-split.\n\n## Related PRs, to merge with this one\n\nNone of them is needed for this PR to build or work, and this PR is not needed for them. The iPhone 17 build above carried the first four.\n\n| PR | What | Measured gain | In the iPhone build | Merging after this PR |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| #1901 | The game's compute dispatches with no game barrier between them run side by side (`dispatch_overlap`, on for Ocarina) | Kokiri Forest GPU p50 15.63 → 14.76 ms (Mac) | yes | one conflict in `nvn_mtl.m` `dispatch_enc`: keep #1901's body and this PR's `g_stat_disp++` beside `g_gp_disp++` |\n| #1942 | Frame step: late frames with the GPU idle do not step up; a longer hold the GPU does not explain is probed | after a warm start, no more ~1,470 presents held at 20 fps or below (Mac) | yes | **carried in this PR** (the pacing builds on it); drop it here if #1942 merges first |\n| #1842 | Opt-in task isolation (`DM_NVN_ISOLATE_TASK`) for the Hi-Z task a5288 | the M1 GPU hangs after an area change (about 15 of 16 walks without it) did not happen with it; off by default, a workaround | yes, off | clean |\n| #1751 | `DM_NVN_GPUPROF_GEOM`: a render pass's GPU time split into geometry and pixels | diagnostic: Ocarina's colour pass with its 11 mesh draws is 5.8 ms of geometry, 0.2 ms after | yes, off | **carried in this PR** (item 22 builds on it); drop it here if #1751 merges first |\n| #1903 | Ocarina takes the launcher's Render scale | Kokiri Forest docked at 0.75: GPU p50 15.77 → 14.31 ms, 60 fps held (Mac) | no | not tried |\n| #1752 | Raw global memory loads through one pointer resolve their pool once (chain change) | the colour-pass mesh shaders: frame p50 22.1 → 18.8 ms, p95 38.9 → 22.6 ms | no | needs a full shader build |\n| #1833 (draft) | Raw global memory at Metal's own GPU addresses, opt-in per game | Kokiri Forest at 854x480: GPU 39.4 → 27.4 ms, frame 33.2 → 23.6 ms (M1 Pro) | no | needs a full shader build |\n\n#1906 (iOS builds link without `IOBluetooth`) is already in main as 9983d659.\n\n## Open\n\n- **iPhone stutter at the 30 fps cap:** fixed for frames just over 33 ms (above). Still open: the iPad's title shows uneven 29–50 ms gaps, its movie gets a new picture on only about 210 of 300 frames, and the power cost of 60 link callbacks a second while late frames are paced is not measured.\n- **GPU time in heavy views** on the iPad (54–67 ms a frame). Next to try: #1901, #1752, #1903 (above).\n- **More memory headroom on 8 GB devices:** about 1.2 GB of pools are wired only because the raw pool table lists them; smaller textures where the working set is under 6 GB. For a later PR.\n- **A GPU hang on an earlier build**, in the draws of #1842's M1 hangs (`a5288d0a6c4971fd`).\n- **The HUD's edges:**\n  - The UI system places every pane relative to the screen's centre and doesn't anchor anything to the edges. So the HUD keeps its 16:9 arrangement in the middle: in wide shapes the hearts sit at the edge of the 16:9 band, and upright the HUD sits around mid-height, smaller (in Full screen, under the touch controls).\n  - Full-screen panes (fades, the menu backdrop) cover only the 16:9 middle.\n  - Moving the edge groups and stretching those panes needs the UI's per-frame pane transform, not found yet.\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/1971/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/1971/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8752","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8752/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8752/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8752/events","html_url":"https://github.com/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8752","id":6309876238,"node_id":"I_kwDOR4Nb7s8AAAABeBkSDg","number":8752,"title":"AI_MEMORY_REQUIRE_ENTERPRISE_FEDERATION_POSTURE with an unrecognised value (e.g. \"enforce\", \"required\", \"enabled\") silently disarms the enterprise-federation boot gate with no warning","user":{"login":"alphaonedev","id":29924871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI0ODcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29924871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev","html_url":"https://github.com/alphaonedev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10592868577,"node_id":"LA_kwDOR4Nb7s8AAAACd2JY4Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10976466978,"node_id":"LA_kwDOR4Nb7s8AAAACjj-YIg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/labels/auto-filed-by-agent","name":"auto-filed-by-agent","color":"FBCA04","default":false,"description":"Issue was filed autonomously by an AI agent per the track-and-fix global rule","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/milestones/12","html_url":"https://github.com/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/milestone/12","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/milestones/12/labels","id":18388138,"node_id":"MI_kwDOR4Nb7s4BGJSq","number":12,"title":"v1.0.0 GA","description":"GA-blocking work packages for v1.0.0","creator":{"login":"alphaonedev","id":29924871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI0ODcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29924871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev","html_url":"https://github.com/alphaonedev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":690,"closed_issues":1048,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-10-07T15:53:59Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T18:11:32Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-10T15:21:22Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:33:50Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"> **Evidence status at filing.** Found by a P4 review lane of the GA dogfood audit (#8741) and filed on the conductor's order before the audit's release build had finished. The evidence below is what the review lane recorded: where it is a file:line chain rather than a command with output, it has not yet been reproduced against a running process. The executed reproduction against the audit build at the target sha will be added as a comment on this issue; if it does not reproduce, that comment says so and the issue is closed as not reproduced.\n\n**Severity:** LOW · **Phase:** P4 · **Target sha:** `dacf8f2c3ba72ae485be06b6b59d9d247a1e4aed`\n\n## Root cause\nThe opt-in gate parses its value with the strict truthy grammar, so anything outside that grammar silently reads as \"off\":\n- `src/enterprise_federation_posture.rs:818-822` `enterprise_federation_posture_required()` returns `is_truthy(&v)`, with `unwrap_or(false)` when the variable is unset.\n- `src/security_profile.rs:222-226` `is_truthy` accepts only `1`, `true`, `yes` and `on`.\n- Every other set value (`enforce`, `required`, `enabled`, `y`, a typo) therefore returns `false`.\n\nWhen that happens, `enforce_at_boot_pre_runtime` (`src/enterprise_federation_posture.rs:843-846`) returns `Ok(())` and the daemon boots without the certified posture gate. The other callers branch the same way:\n- `src/daemon_runtime.rs:1341`\n- `src/daemon_runtime.rs:1483`\n- `src/checkpoints/mod.rs:120`\n- `src/cli/doctor.rs:3476`\n\nNo warning is emitted. An operator who believes they deployed the certified enterprise-federation posture runs with none of the boot refusals it promises.\n\nSibling resolvers in the same area fail closed on an unknown token:\n- `src/federation/signing.rs:240-248` `require_sig` and `require_nonce` use `env_flag_default_on`, where only an exact falsy token disables.\n- `src/mtls_agent_binding.rs:115` `AgentBindingMode::resolve` bails on an unknown token.\n- `security_profile::SecurityPosture::resolve` errors on an unknown token (`src/enterprise_federation_posture.rs:222-226` relies on that).\n\nrust-1-98: ERRORS (no permissive default on a parse failure), SEC fail-closed.\n\n## Evidence\nevidence: static (binary not available). File:line at the target sha:\n- `src/enterprise_federation_posture.rs:819-821` `std::env::var(ENV_REQUIRE_ENTERPRISE_FEDERATION_POSTURE).map(|v| is_truthy(&v)).unwrap_or(false)`\n- `src/enterprise_federation_posture.rs:844-846` `if !enterprise_federation_posture_required() { return Ok(()); }`\n- `src/security_profile.rs:225` `\"1\" | \"true\" | \"yes\" | \"on\"`\n\n## Reproduction\n1. On a node whose federation posture fails at least one certified control (for example, no mTLS allowlist), run `AI_MEMORY_REQUIRE_ENTERPRISE_FEDERATION_POSTURE=1 ai-memory serve ...`. Boot is refused and the failing controls are listed.\n2. Repeat with `AI_MEMORY_REQUIRE_ENTERPRISE_FEDERATION_POSTURE=enforce`. Boot succeeds with no refusal and no warning.\n\n## Proposed fix\n- `src/enterprise_federation_posture.rs` (~20 lines): make it a tri-state resolver. Truthy arms the gate, unset or an exact falsy token disarms it, and any other value is an `Err` that `enforce_at_boot_pre_runtime` returns, so boot is refused and the error names the accepted tokens. The precedent is `security_profile::is_falsy` and the #3200 tri-state resolvers, so no vote is needed.\n- Adapt the four callers listed above (~8 lines), which keep their bool via the resolved value.\n- Test (~40 lines): `enforce` refuses boot with the exact message, `1` arms the gate, `0` and unset disarm it.\n\n## Found by\nGA dogfood audit, lane p4-a1-sec, sha dacf8f2c3ba72ae485be06b6b59d9d247a1e4aed.\n\nFull title: AI_MEMORY_REQUIRE_ENTERPRISE_FEDERATION_POSTURE with an unrecognised value (e.g. \"enforce\", \"required\", \"enabled\") silently disarms the enterprise-federation boot gate with no warning\n\nRefs #8741\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8752/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8752/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8751","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8751/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8751/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8751/events","html_url":"https://github.com/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8751","id":6309874974,"node_id":"I_kwDOR4Nb7s8AAAABeBkNHg","number":8751,"title":"AI_MEMORY_FED_CERT_PEER_BINDING with an unrecognised value (e.g. \"enforced\") silently runs as warn under the standard posture instead of refusing boot, unlike its sibling AI_MEMORY_MTLS_AGENT_BINDING","user":{"login":"alphaonedev","id":29924871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI0ODcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29924871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev","html_url":"https://github.com/alphaonedev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10592868577,"node_id":"LA_kwDOR4Nb7s8AAAACd2JY4Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10976466978,"node_id":"LA_kwDOR4Nb7s8AAAACjj-YIg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/labels/auto-filed-by-agent","name":"auto-filed-by-agent","color":"FBCA04","default":false,"description":"Issue was filed autonomously by an AI agent per the track-and-fix global rule","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/milestones/12","html_url":"https://github.com/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/milestone/12","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/milestones/12/labels","id":18388138,"node_id":"MI_kwDOR4Nb7s4BGJSq","number":12,"title":"v1.0.0 GA","description":"GA-blocking work packages for v1.0.0","creator":{"login":"alphaonedev","id":29924871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI0ODcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29924871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev","html_url":"https://github.com/alphaonedev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alphaonedev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":690,"closed_issues":1048,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-10-07T15:53:59Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T18:11:32Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-10T15:21:17Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:33:49Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"> **Evidence status at filing.** Found by a P4 review lane of the GA dogfood audit (#8741) and filed on the conductor's order before the audit's release build had finished. The evidence below is what the review lane recorded: where it is a file:line chain rather than a command with output, it has not yet been reproduced against a running process. The executed reproduction against the audit build at the target sha will be added as a comment on this issue; if it does not reproduce, that comment says so and the issue is closed as not reproduced.\n\n**Severity:** LOW · **Phase:** P4 · **Target sha:** `dacf8f2c3ba72ae485be06b6b59d9d247a1e4aed`\n\n## Root cause\n`src/tls.rs:472-486` `cert_peer_binding_mode()`: when the env var is set but does not parse, it logs `tracing::error!` and returns `CertPeerBindingMode::Warn`. In Warn, a certificate / `X-Peer-Id` mismatch is logged and allowed (`src/handlers/federation_receive.rs:130`, which reads the mode on every request).\n\nAn operator who types `enforced`, `Enforce `, `on` or `true` therefore believes the binding is enforced while every mismatching peer is admitted. That is a fail-open on parse failure.\n\nThe doc comment at `tls.rs:466-470` records this as deliberate (#3289 A1/A5: \"rather than silently tightening to Enforce\"). The new fact is that the sibling control does the opposite:\n- `src/mtls_agent_binding.rs:103-120` `AgentBindingMode::resolve` `bail!`s on an unrecognised token.\n- `src/mtls_agent_binding.rs:618` `resolve_boot` propagates that with `?`, so boot is refused.\n\nOnly `asi-hard` catches the cert-peer case (`src/security_profile.rs:536`, exact `enforce` floor). At boot, `daemon_runtime.rs:8474-8481` feeds the already-defaulted Warn into `cert_peer_binding_boot_warnings`, so the boot warning describes a Warn posture rather than the typo.\n\nrust-1-98: ERRORS (a parse failure propagated as `Result`, never mapped to a permissive default), SEC fail-closed. Engineering standard North Star: never fail open.\n\n## Evidence\nevidence: static (binary not available). File:line at the target sha:\n- `src/tls.rs:476` `Ok(v) => match CertPeerBindingMode::parse(&v) {`\n- `src/tls.rs:478-483` `Err(e) => { tracing::error!(... \"invalid AI_MEMORY_FED_CERT_PEER_BINDING; holding standard default warn (#3289)\"); CertPeerBindingMode::Warn }`\n- `src/mtls_agent_binding.rs:115-118` `other => bail!(\"unrecognised {MTLS_AGENT_BINDING_ENV} value {other:?} ...\")`\n\n## Reproduction\n1. Start `ai-memory serve` with TLS, an mTLS allowlist and a cert-peer binding map, under the default (standard) security profile, and set `AI_MEMORY_FED_CERT_PEER_BINDING=enforced`.\n2. Boot succeeds and logs one ERROR line.\n3. A peer presenting an allowlisted certificate bound to peer `p1` POSTs `/api/v1/sync/push` with `X-Peer-Id: p2`. The request proceeds past `enforce_cert_peer_binding`. With the value `enforce`, the same request is refused with 403.\n\n## Proposed fix\n- `src/tls.rs` (~15 lines): make `cert_peer_binding_mode()` return `Result<CertPeerBindingMode>`, keeping unset mapped to Warn.\n- `src/daemon_runtime.rs` (~10 lines): resolve once at boot and refuse to start on `Err`, mirroring `mtls_agent_binding::resolve_boot`.\n- Cache the resolved mode in `AppState` for `federation_receive.rs:130`, instead of reading the env on every request.\n- `src/security_profile.rs:1618` (~3 lines): adapt the call.\n- Test (~40 lines): `enforced` refuses boot with the exact error text, unset gives Warn, and `enforce` gives Enforce.\n- Update the `tls.rs:466-470` doc comment and `docs/federation.md`.\n\n## Found by\nGA dogfood audit, lane p4-a1-sec, sha dacf8f2c3ba72ae485be06b6b59d9d247a1e4aed.\n\nFull title: AI_MEMORY_FED_CERT_PEER_BINDING with an unrecognised value (e.g. \"enforced\") silently runs as warn under the standard posture instead of refusing boot, unlike its sibling AI_MEMORY_MTLS_AGENT_BINDING\n\nRefs #8741\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8751/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alphaonedev/ai-memory-mcp/issues/8751/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EKvargas/episteck_home/issues/125","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EKvargas/episteck_home","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EKvargas/episteck_home/issues/125/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EKvargas/episteck_home/issues/125/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EKvargas/episteck_home/issues/125/events","html_url":"https://github.com/EKvargas/episteck_home/pull/125","id":6296423674,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUag0ZM8AAAABN-M5Ng","number":125,"title":"fix(kap2): correct attempt 03 A6 root cause and run blockers","user":{"login":"EKvargas","id":125833890,"node_id":"U_kgDOB4ASog","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125833890?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EKvargas","html_url":"https://github.com/EKvargas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EKvargas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EKvargas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EKvargas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EKvargas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EKvargas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EKvargas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EKvargas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EKvargas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EKvargas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-09T22:59:19Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:33:13Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T15:33:13Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EKvargas/episteck_home/pulls/125","html_url":"https://github.com/EKvargas/episteck_home/pull/125","diff_url":"https://github.com/EKvargas/episteck_home/pull/125.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/EKvargas/episteck_home/pull/125.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T15:33:13Z"},"body":"## Summary\nThis PR corrects the root cause of two-host attempt 03's A6 failure, plus two further defects that would have stopped the next remote run. It is **stacked on #124**: merge #124 first, then retarget this PR to `main`.\n\nThe code changes are confined to the disconnected spike packages. No `apps/` file changes, so merging deploys nothing new to the Home bench. **It authorizes no remote run.** It also records an open latency-gate decision that needs Erick before attempt 04.\n\n## Root cause (reproduced, then fixed under TDD)\n- **Trigger:** PyMySQL 1.2 negotiates *unverified* TLS whenever the server offers it (\"PREFERRED\" mode). MariaDB 11.4+ offers TLS by default; 10.11 doesn't. So on Nuremberg's 11.8.6, the witness gateway's pinned unix-socket sessions were TLS sessions.\n- **Failure:** A5's expected writer loss on the serving HTTP thread left that thread unable to use the next recovery's fresh reader. Its first read failed with a spurious `BrokenPipe`, PyMySQL dropped the socket, and the gateway failed closed, giving A6's 503.\n- **Masked earlier:** A5's last check hit the same failure but expected a deny anyway.\n- **Not the Python version:** Python 3.12 on 11.8 fails the same way.\n\n**Reproduction:** `spike/knowledge-kap2-two-host/replica/` rebuilds the witness host with podman (Ubuntu 26.04.1, Python 3.14.4, `mariadb-server 1:11.8.6-5ubuntu0.1`, PyMySQL 1.2.3). At `be46ade` it reproduced attempt 03 exactly: A6 FAIL at 112 requests, `Aborted_clients=3`, `Com_kill=1`. The MariaDB error log, which the remote cleanup had deleted, shows `Aborted connection … gw_reader … (Got an error writing communication packets)`.\n\n## Changes\n| Defect | Fix | Test (failed first) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Gateway sessions silently used TLS on MariaDB 11.4+ | `gateway.py`: `ssl_disabled=True` | `test_serving_thread_survives_writer_loss_and_later_recovery`, `test_pinned_sessions_never_negotiate_tls` (fail in replica) |\n| Witness reply header/body writes stalled behind Nagle and delayed ACK: ~45 ms per loopback call, roughly 1 RTT + 40 ms across hosts | `witness_runner.py`: `disable_nagle_algorithm = True` | `test_warm_rpc_has_no_small_write_stall` |\n| 2 s client timeout on A9 witness DB restarts (1.9–2.5 s on 11.8) | `transport.py`: 30 s **only** for `snapshot`/`restore`; all other calls keep 2 s | `test_disposable_restarts_outlast_the_serving_timeout` |\n\nNo pass criterion, request cap, path, port, credential route or retry rule changed.\n\n## Topology decided (Erick, 2026-11-10): attempt 04 uses a dedicated Ashburn witness host\nA read-only ping from Ashburn to `100.81.4.57` (direct Tailscale path) measured an RTT of **min 95.6 / avg 99.3 ms**. A10 times one witness round trip per call, and every cold pair opens TCP and TLS first (≥3 RTT ≈ 290 ms). So even with all fixes, the ratified gate could not be met on Ashburn↔Nuremberg.\n\n**Decision (commit `6c8dd18`, docs only):** keep the gate and move the witness to a **new dedicated host in Hetzner Ashburn**, separate from Home. Attempt 04 then needs no Mealie stop and no Nuremberg account.\n- **Host preparation, proven locally:** `replica/fresh_host_acquisition.sh` pins the apt source to the `20261109T000000Z` snapshot and installs five runtime libraries. The reviewed `acquire_mariadb.sh` then passes **unmodified** on a fresh Ubuntu 26.04. The snapshot pin also removes the A0 timing risk.\n- **Next:** Erick creates the host, then read-only RTT and capacity checks, then a new exact-SHA authorization naming the host.\n- **This PR authorizes neither the host nor any run.**\n\n## Follow-ups (not in this PR)\n- **Home side, same latent defect:** Home's pinned sessions in `integrated.py` and `lane.py` lack `ssl_disabled=True`. They're harmless while Home runs MariaDB 10.11, which offers no TLS. This is flagged for R4.\n- **Certificates:** `certs.py`'s CA has no KeyUsage, so Python ≥3.13 clients reject it. The real Home client is Python 3.12, so the run is unaffected. It does stop the transport tests from running inside the replica.\n\n## Review (high effort) and follow-up\n**Fixed in `05298d6` / `83547a5`:**\n- **Witness probe sessions also took TLS.** The runner's `PrivateDB.connect` is now socket-only.\n- **The new tests passed vacuously on stock 10.11.** The gateway test fixture now makes any MariaDB offer TLS, with a guard test proving it. Without the gateway fix, `test_pinned_sessions_never_negotiate_tls` now fails on 10.11.\n- **`loopback_matrix.sh` always exited 0** and could leave the container and keys behind. It now has an exit trap and propagates the exit status.\n- **The replica would stop building** once Ubuntu superseded 11.8.6. The base is now pinned by digest and apt uses the 2026-11-09 snapshot archive.\n- **Fixed `sleep` in the timeout test.** It now waits on the handler's evidence write.\n\n**Declined:**\n- **Home `integrated.py` / `lane.py` TLS:** that's app code, left to R4. It's harmless on 10.11.\n- **Nagle test's absolute threshold:** kept. The stall is ≥40 ms against ~1–3 ms when fixed.\n- **A shared mTLS server helper:** it would refactor the reviewed runner's `serve()` for tests only.\n\n**Surfaced risk:** `acquire_mariadb.sh` still pins 11.8.6 from the *live* archive. A newer Ubuntu MariaDB update would stop attempt 04 at A0. This is resolved for attempt 04 by the dedicated host's snapshot-pinned apt source (see above).\n\n## Testing (code head `83547a5`, run strictly in sequence; `6c8dd18` adds docs and a test script only)\n- **Local, Python 3.12 / MariaDB 10.11:** the four KAP-2 spike packages pass 106/106. The Home contracts, policy, authority and inertness tests pass 55/55.\n- **Replica (pinned image):**\n  - Gateway suite: 33/33.\n  - `replica/loopback_matrix.sh`: all 11 executed steps PASS, 329/400 requests, exit 0, no leftovers. Loopback warm call p50/p95 is 3.1/5.8 ms, against about 50 ms before. A forced failure exits 1 and cleans up.\n- **Overlap failure:** an earlier run that overlapped a replica matrix gave one environmental setup error (a host `mariadb-install-db` `/tmp` collision). It passes alone.\n- **Fresh host (2026-11-10):** `replica/fresh_host_acquisition.sh` passes, exit 0, MariaDB 11.8.6.\n- `git diff --check` is clean.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EKvargas/episteck_home/issues/125/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EKvargas/episteck_home/issues/125/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/issues/1069","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/issues/1069/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/issues/1069/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/issues/1069/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/pull/1069","id":5355381171,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQ9ieqs8AAAABCSeZvA","number":1069,"title":"JEP-0015: Multi-Exporter Leases and Inter-Exporter Port Forwarding","user":{"login":"kirkbrauer","id":14915766,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTE1NzY2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14915766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kirkbrauer","html_url":"https://github.com/kirkbrauer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kirkbrauer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kirkbrauer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kirkbrauer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kirkbrauer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kirkbrauer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kirkbrauer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kirkbrauer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kirkbrauer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kirkbrauer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10029158514,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQ9ieqs8AAAACVcjQcg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true,"description":"Improvements or additions to documentation","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12070045062,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQ9ieqs8AAAACz25Fhg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/labels/jep","name":"jep","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"Jumpstarter Enhancement Proposals","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/milestones/3","html_url":"https://github.com/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/milestone/3","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/milestones/3/labels","id":16475859,"node_id":"MI_kwDOQ9ieqs4A-2bT","number":3,"title":"0.10.0","description":"","creator":{"login":"mangelajo","id":1176434,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzY0MzQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1176434?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mangelajo","html_url":"https://github.com/mangelajo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mangelajo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mangelajo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mangelajo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mangelajo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mangelajo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mangelajo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mangelajo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mangelajo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mangelajo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":31,"closed_issues":20,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-06-23T11:37:19Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T15:08:28Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-09-05T03:53:19Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:28:21Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/pulls/1069","html_url":"https://github.com/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/pull/1069","diff_url":"https://github.com/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/pull/1069.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/pull/1069.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Multi-device tests currently need separate exporter leases and manually configured connections. This JEP extends the existing `Lease` so a test can acquire a complete bench, such as a phone and head unit, and connect its devices even when their exporters run on different hosts.\n\nAn optional `spec.members[]` assigns roles such as `phone` and `headunit` to exporter selections. The controller selects distinct exporters and commits all required member claims in one status update, so a waiting lease holds no partial bench. Members share expiry and release, and each must pass the client's existing access policy. If a member fails after binding, the lease reports degradation and retains the surviving devices for diagnostics.\n\nDrivers declare named ports as `provides` or `requires`. An optional `spec.forwards[]` connects those ports—for example, `headunit.rootcanal` to `phone.controller`—while addresses stay in exporter configuration. Exporters establish authenticated connections directly within a network zone when possible, falling back to the existing router. The client is outside the forwarding data path. The controller validates port direction and compares protocol tags when both endpoints supply them. Direct mode uses mTLS; Kubernetes 1.37 Pod Certificates and ClusterTrustBundles are recorded as a future workload-identity source, along with broader mTLS-based exporter authentication.\n\nThe proposal adds fields and one controller RPC without introducing a new lease resource or changing the `RouterService` protobuf. Router token validation is strengthened to pair only reciprocal endpoint claims under a unique per-forward subject. Existing single-exporter workflows remain supported; multi-member clients select devices by role through the CLI and Python API. A Mobly testbed export is also proposed for existing test suites.\n\nDelivery is phased:\n\n1. Bluetooth pairing between virtual devices in separate Pods.\n2. Virtual phone projection over a forwarded TCP connection.\n3. Physical phone and head unit testing across exporter hosts, with radio peers still within RF range.\n4. Simulated Wi-Fi association and the full Bluetooth-to-Wi-Fi projection handover.\n\nThe early projection phase exercises the projection session but does not simulate the radio handover. Mixed physical/virtual radio benches are deferred. Atomic member claims do not fix the existing scheduling race between separate leases, and reconnecting a forward can still require protocol-specific recovery. Optional-member forwards now become explicitly `Disabled` when their endpoint is omitted, and an explicit one-member lease uses member status and the role-mapping client shape. Remaining review questions include launch/readiness ordering, listener allocation, synchronization, and Mobly endpoint lifetime.\n\nThe JEP includes design decisions, Mermaid diagrams, recorded prototype results, and acceptance criteria for these phases.\n\nValidation: spelling, whitespace, YAML/Python example syntax, and local links checked. Sphinx/MyST parsed and rendered the JEP successfully; the repository-wide warnings-as-errors build remains blocked by an unrelated pre-existing broken authentication-document link.\n\nAI Generated, Human Reviewed\n\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/issues/1069/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jumpstarter-dev/jumpstarter/issues/1069/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LNPANDY/NX2Apple/issues/1139","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LNPANDY/NX2Apple","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LNPANDY/NX2Apple/issues/1139/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LNPANDY/NX2Apple/issues/1139/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LNPANDY/NX2Apple/issues/1139/events","html_url":"https://github.com/LNPANDY/NX2Apple/issues/1139","id":6309935111,"node_id":"I_kwDOVRRpkc8AAAABeBn4Bw","number":1139,"title":"When the time-reversal skill is used, a yellow mosaic pattern appears over the highlighted area on screen.","user":{"login":"Sunny7777777777","id":234089466,"node_id":"U_kgDODfPr-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234089466?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sunny7777777777","html_url":"https://github.com/Sunny7777777777","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sunny7777777777/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sunny7777777777/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sunny7777777777/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sunny7777777777/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sunny7777777777/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sunny7777777777/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sunny7777777777/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sunny7777777777/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sunny7777777777/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12875203012,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVRRpkc8AAAAC_2wBxA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LNPANDY/NX2Apple/labels/game","name":"game","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"A game fails, crashes or misbehaves","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12875203275,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVRRpkc8AAAAC_2wCyw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LNPANDY/NX2Apple/labels/mac","name":"mac","color":"BFD4F2","default":false,"description":"Mac","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T15:24:30Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:25:47Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Game and title ID\n\nThe Legend of Zelda: Tears of The Kindom  0100F2C0115B6000\n\n### Base game and update versions\n\nbase v1.4.3\n\n### Where it runs\n\nMac app (built for This Mac)\n\n### Device, chip and RAM\n\nMacbook Pro, M1 Pro, 16GB\n\n### macOS or iOS / iPadOS version\n\nmacOS 27.2\n\n### How it was installed\n\ndeepseek\n\n### NX2Apple version\n\nv1.1.7\n\n### What happens, and when\n\n\n1.When the time-reversal skill is used, a yellow mosaic pattern appears over the highlighted area on screen.\n2.Inside the temple, FPS dropped very low, like 7~16fps, while it's 60fps outside.\n\n### What you expected\n\nA solution from upstream\n\n### Launch options changed from the defaults\n\nrender scale 100%, frame rate 60\n\n### Copy diagnostics\n\n```markdown\n### NX2Apple diagnostics\n\n- App: NX2Apple 1.3.0\n- macOS: 27.2.1\n- Chip: Apple M1 Pro\n- Engine: stable 1.3.0 (c78d7375bea9c862679ec294a6a69ff3e22e18d0-66e8bc624c49)\n- Python: /Applications/NX2Apple.app/Contents/Resources/python/bin/python3 (3.13.18)\n- .NET: ~/.dotnet/dotnet (10.0.403)\n- Dependencies: all present\n  - ok xcode\n  - ok metal\n  - ok brew:xcodegen: dep.bundled\n  - ok brew:zstd: dep.bundled\n  - ok brew:spirv-cross: dep.bundled\n  - ok brew:glslang: dep.bundled\n  - ok dotnet: ~/.dotnet/dotnet\n  - ok python: dep.bundled\n- Fork patches: 64\n- Xcode: /Applications/Xcode.app (Xcode 27.2, Build version 27B52)\n- Metal compiler (macOS): Apple metal version 32023.922 (metalfe-32023.922.4)\n- Metal compiler (iOS): Apple metal version 32023.922 (metalfe-32023.922.4)\n- iOS SDK: /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Platforms/iPhoneOS.platform/Developer/SDKs/iPhoneOS27.2.sdk\n\n#### Selected game\n\n- Name: The Legend of Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom\n- Title ID: 0100F2C0115B6000\n- Built with shader chain: e047be1b6829\n- App version: 1.4.3\n- Built: 2026-11-04T07:24:28\n```\n\n### Game profile lines from the build log\n\n```text\nnone\n```\n\n### The game's log\n\nfork patches: none\nlauncher: The Legend of Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom (0100F2C0115B6000)